window.TURATH_DATA.hadith.push(...[{"num":16179,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أنس قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((يجمع اللّٰه الناس يوم القيامة، فيقولون: لو استشفعنا على ربنا حتى يريحنا من مكاننا، فيأتون آدم فيقولون: أنت الذي خلقك اللّٰه بيده، ونفخ فيك من روحه، وأمر الملائكة فسجدوا لك، فاشفع لنا عند ربنا. فيقول: لست هناكم، ويذكر خطيئته، ويقول: ائتوا نوحًا، أول رسول بعثه الله، فيأتونه فيقول: لست هناكم، ويذكر خطيئته، ائتوا إبراهيم الذي اتخذه اللّٰه خليلًا، فيأتونه فيقول: لست هناكم، ويذكر خطيئته، ائتوا موسى الذي كلمه اللّٰه، فيأتونه فيقول: لست هناكم، فيذكر خطيئته، ائتوا عيسى، فيأتونه، فيقول: لست هناكم، ائتوا محمدًا ﷺ فقد غفر له ما تقدم من ذنبه وما تأخر، فيأتوني، فأستأذن على ربي، فإذا رأيته وقعت ساجدًا، فيدعني ما شاء الله، ثم يقال: ارفع رأسك: سل تعطه، وقل يسمع، واشفع تشفع، فأرفع رأسي، فأحمد ربي بتحميد يعلمني، ثم أشفع فيحد لي حدًا، ثم أخرجهم من النار، وأدخلهم الجنة، ثم أعود فأقع ساجدًا مثله في الثالثة، أو الرابعة، حتى ما بقي في النار إلا من حبسه القرآن)).","وكان قتادة، يقول عند هذا: “أي وجب عليه الخلود”."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٦٥٦٥)، ومسلم (٣٢٢:١٩٣). واللفظ للبخاري.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في الشفاعة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6565) and Muslim (322:193). The wording is al-Bukhārī’s.","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning Intercession","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":23,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah will gather the people on the Day of Resurrection, and they will say: ‘If only we could seek someone to intercede with our Lord so that He might relieve us from this place.’ They will go to Ādam and say: ‘You are the one whom Allah created with His hand, breathed into you from His spirit, and commanded the angels to prostrate to you. So intercede for us with your Lord.’ He will say: ‘I am not fit for that,’ and he will mention his sin. He will say: ‘Go to Nūḥ, the first Messenger Allah sent.’","They will go to him, but he will say: ‘I am not fit for that,’ and he will mention his sin. He will say: ‘Go to Ibrāhīm, whom Allah took as an intimate friend.’ They will go to him, but he will say: ‘I am not fit for that,’ and he will mention his sin. He will say: ‘Go to Mūsā, to whom Allah spoke directly.’ They will go to him, but he will say: ‘I am not fit for that,’ and he will mention his sin. He will say: ‘Go to ʿĪsā.’ They will go to him, but he will say: ‘I am not fit for that. Go to Muḥammad ﷺ, for Allah has forgiven his past and future sins.’","They will come to me, and I will seek permission to enter upon my Lord. When I see Him, I will fall down in prostration. He will leave me for as long as Allah wills. Then it will be said: ‘Raise your head. Ask and you will be given. Speak and you will be heard. Intercede and your intercession will be accepted.’ I will raise my head and praise my Lord with a form of praise that He will teach me. Then I will intercede, and He will set a limit for me. I will bring them out of the Fire and admit them into Paradise.","Then I will return and fall in prostration again, similarly, on the third or fourth occasion, until no one remains in the Fire except those whom the Qurʾān has confined there.” Qatādah used to say regarding this: “Meaning: those for whom eternal residence in the Fire has become obligatory.”"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["٢- شفاعة النبي ﷺ في دخول من لا حساب عليهم الجنة"],"en":["2 – The Intercession of the Prophet ﷺ for Those Who Will Enter Paradise without Reckoning"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6565},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":322}]},{"num":16180,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة قال: أتي رسول اللّٰه ﷺ يومًا بلحم، فرفع إليه الذراع، وكانت تعجبه، فنهس منها نهسة فقال:","((أنا سيد الناس يوم القيامة، وهل تدرون بم ذاك؟ يجمع اللّٰه يوم القيامة الأولين والآخرين في صعيد واحد، فيسمعهم الداعي، وينفذهم البصر، وتدنو الشمس فيبلغ الناس من الغم والكرب ما لا يطيقون، وما لا يحتملون، فيقول بعض الناس لبعض: ألا ترون ما أنتم فيه؟ ألا ترون ما قد بلغكم؟ ألا تنظرون من يشفع لكم إلى ربكم؟ فيقول بعض الناس لبعض: ائتوا آدم، فيأتون آدم، فيقولون: يا آدم، أنت أبو البشر، خلقك اللّٰه بيده، ونفخ فيك من روحه، وأمر الملائكة فسجدوا لك، اشفع لنا إلى ربك، ألا ترى إلى ما نحن فيه؟ ألا ترى إلى ما قد بلغنا؟ فيقول آدم: إن ربي غضب اليوم غضبًا لم يغضب قبله مثله، ولن يغضب بعده مثله، وإنه نهاني عن الشجرة، عصيته، نفسي نفسي، اذهبوا إلى غيري، اذهبوا إلى نوح، فيأتون نوحًا، فيقولون: يا نوح، أنت أول الرسل إلى الأرض، وسماك اللّٰه عبدًا شكورًا، اشفع لنا إلى ربك، ألا ترى ما نحن فيه؟ ألا ترى ما قد بلغنا؟ فيقول لهم: إن ربي قد غضب اليوم غضبًا لم يغضب قبله مثله، ولن يغضب بعده مثله، وإنه قد كانت لي دعوة دعوت بها على قومي، نفسي نفسي، اذهبوا إلى إبراهيم، فيأتون إبراهيم، فيقولون: أنت نبي اللّٰه وخليله من أهل الأرض، اشفع لنا إلى ربك، ألا ترى إلى ما نحن فيه؟ ألا ترى إلى ما قد بلغنا؟ فيقول لهم إبراهيم: إن ربي قد غضب اليوم غضبًا لم يغضب قبله مثله، ولا يغضب بعده مثله، وذكر كذباته، نفسي نفسي، اذهبوا إلى غيري، اذهبوا إلى موسى، فيأتون موسى ﷺ، فيقولون: يا موسى، أنت رسول الله، فضلك اللّٰه برسالاته، وبتكليمه على الناس، اشفع لنا إلى ربك، ألا ترى إلى ما نحن فيه؟ ألا ترى ما قد بلغنا؟ فيقول لهم موسى ﷺ: إن ربي قد غضب اليوم غضبًا لم يغضب قبله مثله، ولن يغضب بعده مثله، وإني قتلت نفسًا لم أؤمر بقتلها، نفسي نفسي، اذهبوا إلى عيسى ﷺ، فيأتون عيسى، فيقولون: يا عيسى أنت رسول الله، وكلمت الناس في المهد، وكلمة منه ألقاها إلى مريم، وروح منه، فاشفع لنا إلى ربك، ألا ترى ما نحن فيه؟ ألا ترى ما قد بلغنا؟ فيقول لهم عيسى ﷺ: إن ربي قد غضب اليوم غضبًا لم يغضب قبله مثله، ولن يغضب بعده مثله، ولم يذكر له ذنبًا، نفسي نفسي، اذهبوا إلى غيري، اذهبوا إلى محمد ﷺ، فيأتوني فيقولون: يا محمد، أنت رسول الله، وخاتم الأنبياء، وغفر اللّٰه لك ما تقدم من ذنبك، وما تأخر، اشفع لنا إلى ربك، ألا ترى ما نحن فيه؟ ألا ترى ما قد بلغنا؟ فأنطلق، فآتي تحت العرش، فأقع ساجدًا لربي، ثم يفتح اللّٰه علي ويلهمني من محامده وحسن الثناء عليه شيئًا لم يفتحه لأحد قبلي، ثم يقال: يا محمد، ارفع رأسك، سل تعطه، اشفع تشفع، فأرفع رأسي، فأقول: يا رب، أمتي أمتي، فيقال: يا محمد، أدخل الجنة من أمتك من لا حساب عليه من الباب الأيمن من أبواب الجنة، وهم شركاء الناس فيما سوى ذلك من الأبواب، والذي نفس محمد بيده، إن ما بين المصراعين من مصاريع الجنة لكما بين مكة وهجر، أو كما بين مكة وبصرى))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٤٧١٢)، ومسلم (١٩٤). واللفظ لمسلم.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في الشفاعة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4712) and Muslim (194). The wording is Muslim’s.","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning Intercession","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":23,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated: One day some meat was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The foreleg was presented to him, and he liked it, so he took a bite from it and said: “I will be the master of mankind on the Day of Resurrection. Do you know why that is? Allah will gather the first and the last generations on one plain, so that the caller can make them all hear and eyesight can encompass them all. The sun will draw near, and the people will be overcome by such distress and anguish that they will neither be able to bear nor endure it.","Some of them will say to others: ‘Do you not see what condition you are in? Do you not see what has befallen you? Will you not look for someone to intercede for you with your Lord?’ Some will say: ‘Go to Ādam.’ They will come to Ādam and say: ‘O Ādam, you are the father of mankind. Allah created you with His hand, breathed into you from His spirit, and commanded the angels to prostrate to you. Intercede for us with your Lord. Do you not see what condition we are in and what has befallen us?’","Ādam will say: ‘Indeed, my Lord is angry today with an anger unlike any anger He had before, and unlike any anger He will have afterward. He forbade me from the tree, but I disobeyed Him. Myself! Myself! Go to someone else. Go to Nūḥ.’ They will come to Nūḥ and say: ‘O Nūḥ, you were the first Messenger sent to the people of the earth, and Allah called you a grateful servant. Intercede for us with your Lord. Do you not see what condition we are in and what has befallen us?’","He will say: ‘Indeed, my Lord is angry today with an anger unlike any anger He had before and unlike any anger He will have afterward. I had a supplication that I invoked against my people. Myself! Myself! Go to Ibrāhīm.’ They will come to Ibrāhīm and say: ‘You are the Prophet of Allah and His intimate friend among the people of the earth. Intercede for us with your Lord. Do you not see what condition we are in and what has befallen us?’ Ibrāhīm will say: ‘Indeed, my Lord is angry today with an anger unlike any anger He had before and unlike any anger He will have afterward.’ He will mention his statements, then say: ‘Myself! Myself! Go to someone else. Go to Mūsā.’","They will come to Mūsā, peace be upon him, and say: ‘O Mūsā, you are the Messenger of Allah. Allah favored you over the people with His messages and by speaking directly to you. Intercede for us with your Lord. Do you not see what condition we are in and what has befallen us?’ Mūsā will say: ‘Indeed, my Lord is angry today with an anger unlike any anger He had before and unlike any anger He will have afterward. I killed a person whom I had not been commanded to kill. Myself! Myself! Go to ʿĪsā.’","They will come to ʿĪsā and say: ‘O ʿĪsā, you are the Messenger of Allah. You spoke to the people in the cradle, you are a Word from Him which He cast to Maryam, and a spirit from Him. Intercede for us with your Lord. Do you not see what condition we are in and what has befallen us?’ ʿĪsā will say: ‘Indeed, my Lord is angry today with an anger unlike any anger He had before and unlike any anger He will have afterward.’ He will not mention any sin. ‘Myself! Myself! Go to someone else. Go to Muḥammad ﷺ.’","They will come to me and say: ‘O Muḥammad, you are the Messenger of Allah and the Seal of the Prophets. Allah has forgiven your past and future sins. Intercede for us with your Lord. Do you not see what condition we are in and what has befallen us?’ I will go and come beneath the Throne, then fall down in prostration before my Lord. Allah will open for me and inspire me with praises and beautiful words of glorification of Him that He had not opened for anyone before me.","Then it will be said: ‘O Muḥammad, raise your head. Ask and you will be given. Intercede and your intercession will be accepted.’ I will raise my head and say: ‘My Lord, my Ummah! My Ummah!’ It will be said: ‘O Muḥammad, admit into Paradise from your Ummah those upon whom there is no reckoning through the right-hand gate of the gates of Paradise. They will also share with the rest of the people in the other gates.’ By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muḥammad, the distance between the two sides of a gate of Paradise is like the distance between Makkah and Hajar, or like the distance between Makkah and Buṣrā.”"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["٣- شفاعة النبي ﷺ في فتح باب الجنة لأهلها"],"en":["3 – The Intercession of the Prophet ﷺ for the Opening of the Gate of Paradise for Its People"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":4712},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":194}]},{"num":16181,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أنس بن مالك، قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((أنا أول الناس يشفع في الجنة، وأنا أكثر الأنبياء تبعًا)).","وفي رواية:","((أنا أكثر الأنبياء تبعًا يوم القيامة، وأنا أول من يقرع باب الجنة)).","وفي رواية أخرى:","((أنا أول شفيع في الجنة، لم يصدق نبي من الأنبياء ما صدقت، وإن من الأنبياء نبيًا ما يصدقه من أمته إلا رجل واحد))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (١٩٦).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في الشفاعة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (196).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning Intercession","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":23,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I will be the first of the people to intercede concerning Paradise, and I will have the greatest number of followers among the Prophets.”","In another narration: “I will have the greatest number of followers among the Prophets on the Day of Resurrection, and I will be the first to knock at the gate of Paradise.”","And in another narration: “I will be the first intercessor concerning Paradise. No Prophet was believed by as many people as believed me, while among the Prophets there is even a Prophet whom only one man from his nation believed.”"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["٤- شفاعة النبي ﷺ في تخفيف العذاب عن بعض أهل النار"],"en":["4 – The Intercession of the Prophet ﷺ to Lessen the Punishment of Some of the People of the Fire"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":196}]},{"num":16182,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي سعيد، أنه سمع النبي ﷺ وذكر عنده عمه فقال:","((لعله تنفعه شفاعتي يوم القيامة، فيجعل في ضحضاح من النار يبلغ كعبيه، يغلي منه دماغه))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٣٨٨٥)، ومسلم (٢١٠).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في الشفاعة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3885) and Muslim (210).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning Intercession","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":23,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd narrated that he heard the Prophet ﷺ, when his uncle was mentioned in his presence, say: “Perhaps my intercession will benefit him on the Day of Resurrection, so that he will be placed in a shallow part of the Fire reaching his ankles, from which his brain will boil.”"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["قوله: ((ضحضاح)) هو ما رق من الماء على وجه الأرض إلى نحو الكعبين، واستعير في النار.","٥- شفاعة النبي ﷺ في إخراج أرباب الكبائر من أهل التوحيد من النار"],"en":["The word “ḍaḥḍāḥ” refers to shallow water spread over the ground to approximately ankle depth. Here it is used figuratively to describe a shallow level of the Fire.","5 – The Intercession of the Prophet ﷺ to Bring the Major Sinners among the People of Tawḥīd Out of the Fire"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":3885},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":210}]},{"num":16183,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أنس بن مالك، عن النبي ﷺ قال:","((شفاعتي لأهل الكبائر من أمتي))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود (٤٧٣٩)، والترمذي (٢٤٣٥)، وأحمد (١٣٢٢٢)، وابن خزيمة في التوحيد (٥٢٧).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في الشفاعة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (4739), al-Tirmidhī (2435), Aḥmad (13222), and Ibn Khuzaymah in al-Tawḥīd (527).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning Intercession","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":23,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “My intercession is for those among my Ummah who committed major sins.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"abudawud","label":"أبو داود","number":4739},{"key":"tirmidhi","label":"الترمذي","number":2435},{"key":"ابن_خزیمہ/التوحید","label":"ابن خزيمة في التوحيد","number":527},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":13222,"n":13222}]},{"num":16184,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر، قال: سمعت رسول اللّٰه ﷺ يقول:","((إن شفاعتي يوم القيامة لأهل الكبائر من أمتي))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه ابن ماجه (٤٣١٠)، وابن خزيمة في التوحيد (٥٣١)، وابن حبان (٦٤٦٧)، والحاكم (٦٩/١).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في الشفاعة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Ibn Mājah (4310), Ibn Khuzaymah in al-Tawḥīd (531), Ibn Ḥibbān (6467), and al-Ḥākim (1/69).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning Intercession","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":23,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Indeed, my intercession on the Day of Resurrection is for those among my Ummah who committed major sins.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ibnmajah","label":"ابن ماجه","number":4310},{"key":"ابن_خزیمہ/التوحید","label":"ابن خزيمة في التوحيد","number":531},{"key":"ibnhibban","label":"ابن حبان","number":6467},{"key":"hakim","label":"الحاكم","number":69}]},{"num":16185,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر، أن النبي ﷺ قال:","((يخرج من النار بالشفاعة كأنهم الثعارير)).","قلت: ما الثعارير؟ قال: الضغابيس، وكان قد سقط فمه. فقلت لعمرو بن دينار: أبا محمد، سمعت جابر بن عبدالله يقول: سمعت النبي ﷺ يقول:","((يخرج بالشفاعة من النار))؟","قال: نعم."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٦٥٥٨)، ومسلم (٣١٨ :١٩١).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في الشفاعة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6558) and Muslim (318 :191).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning Intercession","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":23,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “People will be brought out of the Fire through intercession looking like thaʿārīr.” The narrator asked: “What are thaʿārīr?” He replied: “Ḍaghābīs.” His teeth had fallen out, affecting his pronunciation. I said to ʿAmr ibn Dīnār: “O Abū Muḥammad, did you hear Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh say that he heard the Prophet ﷺ say, ‘People will be brought out of the Fire through intercession’?” He replied: “Yes.”"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["((الضغابيس)) هي صغار القثاء، واحدها ضغبوس وقيل غير ذلك."],"en":["The word “ḍaghābīs” refers to small cucumbers; the singular is ḍaghbūs. Other explanations have also been given."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6558},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":318}]},{"num":16186,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عمران بن حصين، عن النبي ﷺ قال:","((يخرج قوم من النار بشفاعة محمد ﷺ فيدخلون الجنة يسمون الجهنميين))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (٦٥٦٦).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في الشفاعة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6566).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning Intercession","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":23,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “A people will be brought out of the Fire through the intercession of Muḥammad ﷺ and will enter Paradise. They will be called the Jahannamiyyūn.”"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["وهؤلاء الجهنميون الذين يخرجون من النار بالشفاعة هم أهل الكبائر من أهل التوحيد.","وهذه الشفاعة يشارك فيها الملائكة والنبيون والصديقون والمؤمنون:"],"en":["The author says that these Jahannamiyyūn, who are brought out of the Fire through intercession, are those among the people of Tawḥīd who committed major sins.","The angels, Prophets, truthful believers, and other believers will also participate in this intercession:"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6566}]},{"num":16187,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي سعيد الخدري، قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((… حتى إذا خلص المؤمنون من النار، فوالذي نفسي بيده ما منكم من أحد بأشد مناشدة لله في استقصاء الحق من المؤمنين لله يوم القيامة لإخوانهم الذين في النار، يقولون: ربنا كانوا يصومون معنا، ويصلون ويحجون، فيقال لهم: أخرجوا من عرفتم، فتحرم صورهم على النار. فيخرجون خلقًا كثيرًا قد أخذت النار إلى نصف ساقيه وإلى ركبتيه، ثم يقولون: ربنا ما بقي فيها أحد ممن أمرتنا به. فيقول: ارجعوا فمن وجدتم في قلبه مثقال دينار من خير فأخرجوه. فيخرجون خلقًا كثيرًا، ثم يقولون: ربنا لم نذر فيها أحدًا ممن أمرتنا. ثم يقول: ارجعوا فمن وجدتم في قلبه مثقال نصف دينار من خير فأخرجوه. فيخرجون خلقًا كثيرًا، ثم يقولون: ربنا لم نذر فيها ممن أمرتنا أحدًا. ثم يقول: ارجعوا فمن وجدتم في قلبه مثقال ذرة من خير فأخرجوه، فيخرجون خلقًا كثيرًا، ثم يقولون: ربنا لم نذر فيها أحدًا)).","وكان أبو سعيد يقول: إن لم تصدقوني بهذا الحديث فاقرؤوا إن شئتم:","﴿إِنَّ اللَّهَ لَا يَظْلِمُ مِثْقَالَ ذَرَّةٍ وَإِنْ تَكُ حَسَنَةً يُضَاعِفْهَا وَيُؤْتِ مِنْ لَدُنْهُ أَجْرًا عَظِيمًا﴾ [سورة النساء: ٤٠].","فيقول اللّٰه عز وجل: ((شفعت الملائكة، وشفع النبيون، وشفع المؤمنون، ولم يبق إلا أرحم الراحمين، فيقبض قبضة من النار، فيخرج منها قومًا لم يعملوا خيرًا قط، قد عادوا حممًا، فيلقيهم في نهر في أفواه الجنة يقال له: نهر الحياة، فيخرجون كما تخرج الحبة في حميل السيل…)).","الحديث."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٧٤٣٩)، ومسلم (١٨٣).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في الشفاعة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (7439) and Muslim (183).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning Intercession","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":23,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “…When the believers have been delivered from the Fire, then by the One in whose hand is my soul, none of you is more persistent in pleading with Allah for the full restoration of his rights than the believers will be on the Day of Resurrection in pleading with Allah on behalf of their brothers who are in the Fire. They will say: ‘Our Lord, they used to fast with us, pray with us, and perform Ḥajj with us.’","It will be said to them: ‘Bring out those whom you recognize.’ Their forms will then be forbidden to the Fire. They will bring out a great many people, some of whom the Fire had reached halfway up their shins and others up to their knees. Then they will say: ‘Our Lord, no one remains therein from among those whom You commanded us to bring out.’ He will say: ‘Go back, and whoever you find in whose heart there is goodness equal to the weight of a dinar, bring him out.’","They will bring out a great many people. Then they will say: ‘Our Lord, we have not left therein anyone whom You commanded us to bring out.’ Then He will say: ‘Go back, and whoever you find in whose heart there is goodness equal to half the weight of a dinar, bring him out.’ They will bring out a great many people. Then they will say: ‘Our Lord, we have not left therein anyone whom You commanded us to bring out.’ Then He will say: ‘Go back, and whoever you find in whose heart there is goodness equal to the weight of an atom, bring him out.’","They will bring out a great many people, and then say: ‘Our Lord, we have not left anyone therein.’” Abū Saʿīd used to say: “If you do not believe me concerning this hadith, then recite, if you wish: ‘Indeed, Allah does not wrong even by the weight of an atom. If there is a good deed, He multiplies it and gives from Himself a tremendous reward.’ [al-Nisāʾ 4:40]” Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will say: “The angels have interceded, the Prophets have interceded, and the believers have interceded. None remains except the Most Merciful of those who show mercy.","Then He will take a handful from the Fire and bring out from it people who had never done any good whatsoever and who had become charred like coal. He will cast them into a river at the entrances of Paradise called the River of Life. They will emerge from it just as a seed grows in the silt carried by a flood…” The hadith continues."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":7439},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":183}]},{"num":16188,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي بكرة، عن النبي ﷺ قال:","((يحمل الناس على الصراط يوم القيامة، فتقادع بهم جنبتا الصراط تقادع الفراش في النار)).","قال:","((فينجي اللّٰه برحمته من يشاء)).","قال:","((ثم يؤذن للملائكة والنبيين والشهداء أن يشفعوا، فيشفعون ويخرجون، ويشفعون ويخرجون، ويشفعون ويخرجون - وزاد عفان مرة، فقال أيضًا: ويشفعون ويخرجون - من كان في قلبه ما يزن ذرة من إيمان))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (٢٠٤٤٠)، والبزار (٣٦٧١)، وابن أبي عاصم في السنة (٨٣٨).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في الشفاعة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (20440), al-Bazzār (3671), and Ibn Abī ʿĀṣim in al-Sunnah (838).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning Intercession","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":23,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Bakrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The people will be brought onto the Ṣirāṭ on the Day of Resurrection, and the two sides of the Ṣirāṭ will cause them to fall one after another just as moths tumble into a fire.” He said: “Allah will save by His mercy whomever He wills.” He then said: “After that, permission will be given to the angels, the Prophets, and the martyrs to intercede. They will intercede and people will be brought out; they will intercede and people will be brought out; and they will intercede and people will be brought out.”","ʿAffān once added: “They will intercede and bring out whoever has in his heart faith weighing as much as an atom.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"البزار","label":"البزار","number":3671},{"key":"ابن_ابی_عاصم/السنہ","label":"ابن أبي عاصم في السنة","number":838},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":20440,"n":20440},{"key":"sh12862","label":"كشف الأستار عن زوائد البزار","number":3467,"n":3468}]},{"num":16189,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أنس بن مالك، أن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال:","((يخرج من النار أربعة، فيعرضون على الله، فيلتفت أحدهم فيقول: أي رب، إذ أخرجتني منها فلا تعدني فيها، فينجيه اللّٰه منها))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (١٩٢).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب يخرج من النار أربعة بالشفاعة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (192).","chapter_en":"Four People Will Be Brought Out of the Fire through Intercession","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":24,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Four people will be brought out of the Fire and presented before Allah. One of them will turn and say: ‘My Lord, since You have brought me out of it, do not return me to it.’ So Allah will save him from it.”"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["وهؤلاء الأربعة ذكر منهم الثلاثة أنس بن مالك في الحديث الآتي:"],"en":["Of these four, Anas ibn Mālik mentioned three in the following hadith:"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":192}]},{"num":16190,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أنس، عن النبي ﷺ قال:","((يخرج من النار من قال: لا إله إلا الله، وفي قلبه وزن شعيرة من خير، ويخرج من النار من قال: لا إله إلا اللّٰه، وفي قلبه وزن برة من خير، ويخرج من النار من قال: لا إله إلا اللّٰه وفي قلبه وزن ذرة من خير))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٤٤)، ومسلم (٣٢٥ :١٩٣).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب يخرج من النار أربعة بالشفاعة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (44) and Muslim (325 :193).","chapter_en":"Four People Will Be Brought Out of the Fire through Intercession","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":24,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever said, ‘There is no deity except Allah,’ while there was in his heart goodness equal to the weight of a grain of barley will be brought out of the Fire. Whoever said, ‘There is no deity except Allah,’ while there was in his heart goodness equal to the weight of a grain of wheat will be brought out of the Fire. And whoever said, ‘There is no deity except Allah,’ while there was in his heart goodness equal to the weight of an atom will be brought out of the Fire.”"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["والرابع من الناس ما ذكره الحسن البصري عن أنس بن مالك وهو الآتي:"],"en":["As for the fourth, it is what al-Ḥasan al-Baṣrī related from Anas ibn Mālik in the following report:"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":44},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":325}]},{"num":16191,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن معبد بن هلال العنزي قال: انطلقنا إلى أنس بن مالك وتشفعنا بثابت، فأتيناه وهو يصلي الضحى، فاستأذن لنا ثابت فدخلنا عليه، وأجلس ثابتًا معه على سريره، فقال له: يا أبا حمزة، إن إخوانك من أهل البصرة يسألونك أن تحدثهم حديث الشفاعة. قال: حدثنا محمد ﷺ قال:","((فذكر من كان في قلبه مثقال حبة من برة أو شعير من إيمان، ثم من كان في قلبه مثقال حبة من خردل، ثم ذكر من كان في قلبه أدنى أدنى من مثقال من خردل من إيمان)).","هذا حديث أنس الذي أنبأنا به، فخرجنا من عنده، فلما كنا بظهر الجبان قلنا: لو ملنا إلى الحسن، سلمنا عليه، وهو مستخف في دار أبي خليفة. قال: فدخلنا عليه فسلمنا عليه، فقلنا: يا أبا سعيد جئنا من عند أخيك أبي حمزة فلم نسمع مثل حديث حدثناه في الشفاعة. قال: هيه! فحدثناه الحديث فقال: هيه! قلنا: ما زادنا. قال: قد حدثنا به منذ عشرين سنة وهو يومئذ جميع، ولقد ترك شيئًا ما أدري أنسي الشيخ أو كره أن يحدثكم فتتكلوا. قلنا له: حدثنا، فضحك وقال: ﴿خُلِقَ الْإِنْسَانُ مِنْ عَجَلٍ﴾ [الأنبياء: ٣٧]. ما ذكرت لكم هذا إلا وأنا أريد أن أحدثكموه:","((ثم أرجع إلى ربي في الرابعة فأحمده بتلك المحامد ثم أخر له ساجدًا، فيقال لي: يا محمد ارفع رأسك، وقل يسمع لك، وسل تعطه، واشفع تشفع. فأقول: يا رب ائذن لي فيمن قال: لا إله إلا الله. قال: ليس ذاك لك - أو قال ليس ذاك إليك - ولكن وعزتي وكبريائي وعظمتي وجبريائي لأخرجن من قال: لا إله إلا الله))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٧٥١٠)، ومسلم (٣٢٦ :١٩٣).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب يخرج من النار أربعة بالشفاعة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (7510) and Muslim (326 :193).","chapter_en":"Four People Will Be Brought Out of the Fire through Intercession","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":24,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Maʿbad ibn Hilāl al-ʿAnazī narrated: We went to Anas ibn Mālik and asked Thābit to intercede for us with him. We came to him while he was praying Ṣalāt al-Ḍuḥā. Thābit sought permission for us, so we entered. Anas seated Thābit with him upon his couch. Thābit said: “O Abū Ḥamzah, your brothers from the people of Baṣrah are asking you to narrate to them the hadith of intercession.” Anas said: “Muḥammad ﷺ narrated to us…” He then mentioned: “Whoever had in his heart faith equal to the weight of a grain of wheat or barley, then whoever had in his heart faith equal to a mustard seed, and then whoever had in his heart even less and less than the weight of a mustard seed of faith.”","This was the hadith of Anas that he narrated to us. We left him, and when we reached the open desert, we said: “Why do we not go to al-Ḥasan and greet him?” At that time he was hiding in the house of Abū Khalīfah. We entered and greeted him, then said: “O Abū Saʿīd, we have just come from your brother Abū Ḥamzah, and we have never heard anything like the hadith he narrated to us concerning intercession.” He said: “Go on!” So we narrated the hadith to him.","He said: “Go on!” We replied: “He did not add anything beyond that.” Al-Ḥasan said: “He narrated this to us twenty years ago when he was still young, strong, and possessed of full memory. He left out something. I do not know whether the old man forgot it or whether he disliked narrating it to you out of fear that you might become complacent.” We said: “Then narrate it to us.” He laughed and said: “‘Man was created of haste.’” [al-Anbiyāʾ 21:37] He continued: “I only mentioned this because I intended to narrate it to you.”","Then he narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Then I will return to my Lord for the fourth time and praise Him with those praises. Then I will fall down before Him in prostration. It will be said to me: ‘O Muḥammad, raise your head. Speak and you will be heard. Ask and you will be given. Intercede and your intercession will be accepted.’ I will say: ‘My Lord, permit me concerning those who said: There is no deity except Allah.’ He will say: ‘That is not for you’—or: ‘That is not up to you’—‘but by My Might, My Majesty, My Greatness, and My Supremacy, I will surely bring out everyone who said: There is no deity except Allah.’”"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["قوله: ((جبان وجبانة)) هما الصحراء. وجميع معناه شاب مجتمع القوة والحفظ.","ويؤيده حديث أبي سعيد الخدري الآتي:"],"en":["The expression “jabān” or “jabānah” means an open desert or plain.","The word “jamīʿ” here means a young man whose strength and memory are fully developed.","This is also supported by the following hadith of Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī:"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":7510},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":326}]},{"num":16192,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي سعيد الخدري قال: وفيه: ثم يقول: ارجعوا فمن وجدتم في قلبه مثقال ذرة من خير، فأخرجوه فيخرجون خلقًا كثيرًا، فذكر الحديث… ثم يقول: ربنا لم نذر فيها أحدًا.","وكان أبو سعيد يقول: فإن لم تصدقوني بهذا الحديث فاقرؤوا:","﴿إِنَّ اللَّهَ لَا يَظْلِمُ مِثْقَالَ ذَرَّةٍ وَإِنْ تَكُ حَسَنَةً يُضَاعِفْهَا وَيُؤْتِ مِنْ لَدُنْهُ أَجْرًا عَظِيمًا﴾ [النساء: ٤٠].","فيشفع النبيون والملائكة والمؤمنون فيقول الجبار: بقيت شفاعتي، فيقبض قبضة من النار، فيخرج أقوامًا قد امتحشوا، فيلقون في نهر بأفواه الجنة يقال له: ماء الحياة، فينبتون في حافتيه كما تنبت الحبة في حميل السيل، قد رأيتموها إلى جانب الصخرة، وإلى جانب الشجرة، فما كان إلى الشمس منها كان أخضر، وما كان منها إلى الظل كان أبيض، فيخرجون كأنهم اللؤلؤ، فيجعل في رقابهم الخواتيم، فيدخلون الجنة، فيقول أهل الجنة: هؤلاء عتقاء الرحمن، أدخلهم الجنة بغير عمل عملوه ولا خير قدموه، فيقال لهم: لكم ما رأيتم، ومثله معه."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٧٤٣٩)، ومسلم (١٨٣).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب يخرج من النار أربعة بالشفاعة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (7439) and Muslim (183).","chapter_en":"Four People Will Be Brought Out of the Fire through Intercession","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":24,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated, within the hadith: “Then He will say: ‘Go back, and whoever you find in whose heart there is goodness equal to the weight of an atom, bring him out.’ So they will bring out a great many people.” He then continued the hadith until they say: “Our Lord, we have not left anyone therein.” Abū Saʿīd used to say: “If you do not believe me concerning this hadith, then recite: ‘Indeed, Allah does not wrong even by the weight of an atom. If there is a good deed, He multiplies it and gives from Himself a tremendous reward.’","[al-Nisāʾ 4:40]” Then: “The Prophets, the angels, and the believers will intercede. Then the Almighty will say: ‘My intercession remains.’ He will take a handful from the Fire and bring out people who have been completely charred. They will be cast into a river at the entrances of Paradise called the Water of Life. They will grow along its banks just as a seed grows in the silt carried by a flood. You have seen such seeds beside a rock and beside a tree: the part exposed to the sun is green, while the part in the shade is white.","They will emerge looking like pearls, and seals will be placed around their necks. Then they will enter Paradise. The people of Paradise will say: ‘These are those whom the Most Merciful has set free. He admitted them into Paradise without any deed they performed or any good they sent ahead.’ It will then be said to them: ‘You will have everything you see, and an equal amount besides it.’”"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["والخلاصة: أنه وقع في حديث أبي سعيد الخدري تقديم وتأخير، واختصار وتفصيل، كما روي حديث أنس بالمعنى، وحاصله أن النبي ﷺ يشفع ثلاث مرات، وفي المرة الرابعة يقول: يا رب ائذن لي فيمن قال: “لا إله إلا الله” فيقول اللّٰه عز وجل: ((ليس ذاك إليك، ولكن عزتي وكبريائي، وعظمتي وجبريائي لأخرجن من قال: لا إله إلا اللّه)).","يعني أن اللّه عز وجل يخرج برحمته وفضله من النار كل من أقر بالتوحيد، ولو لم يعمل عملًا قط - وهذا شامل لجميع الأمم - مثل الرجل الذي أوصى بإحراقه بعد موته لكثرة ذنوبه إلا أنه خاف من اللّه تعالى بأنه يعذبه عذابًا شديدًا.","ثم يخبر النبي ﷺ بأنه لم يبق في النار أحد بعده إلا من حبسه القرآن أي وجب عليه الخلود كما في تفسير قتادة، وهم الكفار والمشركون والمنافقون. كما في قوله تعالى:","﴿إِنَّ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا وَمَاتُوا وَهُمْ كُفَّارٌ أُولَٰئِكَ عَلَيْهِمْ لَعْنَةُ اللَّهِ وَالْمَلَائِكَةِ وَالنَّاسِ أَجْمَعِينَ ۝ خَالِدِينَ فِيهَا لَا يُخَفَّفُ عَنْهُمُ الْعَذَابُ وَلَا هُمْ يُنْظَرُونَ﴾ [البقرة: ١٦١-١٦٢].","﴿إِنَّهُ مَنْ يُشْرِكْ بِاللَّهِ فَقَدْ حَرَّمَ اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ الْجَنَّةَ وَمَأْوَاهُ النَّارُ وَمَا لِلظَّالِمِينَ مِنْ أَنْصَارٍ﴾ [المائدة: ٧٢].","﴿إِنَّ اللَّهَ لَا يَغْفِرُ أَنْ يُشْرَكَ بِهِ وَيَغْفِرُ مَا دُونَ ذَٰلِكَ لِمَنْ يَشَاءُ وَمَنْ يُشْرِكْ بِاللَّهِ فَقَدْ ضَلَّ ضَلَالًا بَعِيدًا﴾ [سورة النساء: ١١٦].","وقال في المنافقين:","﴿إِنَّ الْمُنَافِقِينَ فِي الدَّرْكِ الْأَسْفَلِ مِنَ النَّارِ وَلَنْ تَجِدَ لَهُمْ نَصِيرًا﴾ [النساء: ١٤٥].","وأما ما جاء في حديث أنس: فلا أدري في الثالثة أو الرابعة قال: ((فأقول: يا ربي ما بقي في النار إلا من حبسه القرآن))، فقوله في “الرابعة” أي بعد الرابعة.","وبعد بعثة النبي ﷺ فلا بد من الإيمان برسالته مع الإقرار بالتوحيد، كما صح عن النبي ﷺ أنه قال: ((لو كان موسى حيًا ما وسعه إلا أن يتبعني)). والحمد لله على توفيقه."],"en":["In summary, the author says that the hadith of Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī contains some variation in order, abbreviation, and elaboration, just as the hadith of Anas was narrated according to its meaning.","Its overall meaning is that the Prophet ﷺ will intercede three times. On the fourth occasion he will say:","“My Lord, permit me concerning those who said: ‘There is no deity except Allah.’”","Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will say:","“That is not up to you. But by My Might, My Majesty, My Greatness, and My Supremacy, I will surely bring out whoever said: ‘There is no deity except Allah.’”","That is, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will by His mercy and grace bring out of the Fire everyone who affirmed Tawḥīd, even if he had never performed any good deed. According to the author, this applies to all nations.","An example is the man who instructed that his body be burned after his death because of the enormity of his sins, yet he feared Allah, the Exalted, fearing that He would punish him severely.","Then the Prophet ﷺ informs that afterward no one will remain in the Fire except those “whom the Qurʾān has confined there,” meaning those upon whom eternal residence therein has become obligatory, as Qatādah explained.","They are the disbelievers, polytheists, and hypocrites, as in the statement of Allah, the Exalted:","“Indeed, those who disbelieve and die while they are disbelievers—upon them is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all mankind. They will remain therein forever. The punishment will not be lightened for them, nor will they be given respite.”","[al-Baqarah 2:161-162]","“Indeed, whoever associates partners with Allah, Allah has forbidden Paradise to him, and his refuge is the Fire. The wrongdoers will have no helpers.”","[al-Māʾidah 5:72]","“Indeed, Allah does not forgive associating partners with Him, but He forgives what is less than that for whomever He wills. Whoever associates partners with Allah has certainly strayed far away.”","[al-Nisāʾ 4:116]","And regarding the hypocrites, He says:","“Indeed, the hypocrites will be in the lowest depths of the Fire, and you will never find for them any helper.”","[al-Nisāʾ 4:145]","As for what occurs in the hadith of Anas:","“I do not know whether it was on the third or fourth occasion that he said: ‘My Lord, no one remains in the Fire except those whom the Qurʾān has confined there,’”","the author explains that the phrase “on the fourth” means after the fourth intercession.","After the mission of the Prophet ﷺ, belief in his Messengership is required together with affirming Tawḥīd, as it is authentically reported from the Prophet ﷺ that he said:","“If Mūsā were alive, he would have no choice but to follow me.”","And all praise belongs to Allah for granting success."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":7439},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":183}]},{"num":16193,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عدي بن حاتم قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((ما منكم أحد إلا سيكلمه ربه ليس بينه وبينه ترجمان، فينظر أيمن منه فلا يرى إلا ما قدم من عمله، وينظر أشأم منه فلا يرى إلا ما قدم، وينظر بين يديه فلا يرى إلا النار تلقاء وجهه، فاتقوا النار ولو بشق تمرة)).","زاد في رواية:","((ولو كلمة طيبة))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٧٥١٢)، ومسلم (٦٧ :١٠١٦).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب أن الله يكلم الناس يوم القيامة ليس بينه وبينهم ترجمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (7512) and Muslim (67 :1016).","chapter_en":"Allah Will Speak to the People on the Day of Resurrection with No Interpreter between Him and Them","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":25,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAdī ibn Ḥātim narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is none among you except that his Lord will speak to him directly, with no interpreter between him and Him. He will look to his right and see nothing except the deeds he sent ahead. He will look to his left and see nothing except the deeds he sent ahead. Then he will look in front of himself and see nothing except the Fire directly before his face. So protect yourselves from the Fire, even if only by giving half of a date in charity.”","Another narration adds: “Even if only by a good word.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":7512},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":67}]},{"num":16194,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن ابن عباس، أن النبي ﷺ قال:","((نحن آخر الأمم، وأول من يحاسب، يقال: أين الأمة الأمية، ونبيها؟ فنحن الآخرون الأولون))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه ابن ماجه (٤٢٩٠).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أمة محمد ﷺ هم أول الناس حسابًا يوم القيامة مع أنهم آخر الأمم","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Ibn Mājah (4290).","chapter_en":"The Ummah of Muḥammad ﷺ Will Be the First People Reckoned on the Day of Resurrection, Though They Are the Last of the Nations","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":26,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿAbbās narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “We are the last of the nations, yet the first to be brought to account. It will be said: ‘Where is the unlettered nation and its Prophet?’ So we are the last, yet the first.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ibnmajah","label":"ابن ماجه","number":4290}]},{"num":16195,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عائشة أن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال:","((ليس أحد يحاسب يوم القيامة إلا هلك)).","فقلت: يا رسول الله، أليس قد قال اللّٰه تعالى:","﴿فَأَمَّا مَنْ أُوتِيَ كِتَابَهُ بِيَمِينِهِ ۝ فَسَوْفَ يُحَاسَبُ حِسَابًا يَسِيرًا﴾ [الانشقاق: ٧-٨].","فقال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((إنما ذلك العرض، وليس أحد يناقش الحساب يوم القيامة إلا عذب))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٦٥٣٧)، ومسلم (٨٠ :٢٨٧٦).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب من نوقش الحساب عذب","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6537) and Muslim (80 :2876).","chapter_en":"Whoever Is Scrutinized in the Reckoning Will Be Punished","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":27,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀ’ishah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No one will be brought to account on the Day of Resurrection except that he will be ruined.” I said: “O Messenger of Allah, has Allah not said: ʿAs for the one who is given his record in his right hand, he will receive an easy reckoning.’ [al-Inshiqāq 84:7-8]” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “That only refers to the presentation of the deeds. No one will have his reckoning scrutinized on the Day of Resurrection except that he will be punished.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6537},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":80}]},{"num":16196,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عائشة قالت: سمعت النبي ﷺ يقول في بعض صلاته:","((اللهم حاسبني حسابًا يسيرًا)).","فلما انصرف، قلت: يا نبي الله، ما الحساب اليسير؟ قال:","((أن ينظر في كتابه فيتجاوز عنه، إنه من نوقش الحساب يومئذ يا عائشة هلك، وكل ما يصيب المؤمن، يكفر اللّٰه عز وجل به عنه، حتى الشوكة تشوكه))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (٢٤٢١٥)، وصححه ابن خزيمة (٨٤٩) والحاكم (٥٧ ،٢٥٥/١).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب من نوقش الحساب عذب","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (24215), authenticated by Ibn Khuzaymah (849) and al-Ḥākim (57, 255/1).","chapter_en":"Whoever Is Scrutinized in the Reckoning Will Be Punished","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":27,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀ’ishah narrated: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say during one of his prayers: “O Allah, call me to an easy reckoning.” When he finished, I asked: “O Prophet of Allah, what is an easy reckoning?” He replied: “That his record is looked at and then he is pardoned. Indeed, whoever has his reckoning scrutinized on that Day, O ʿĀ’ishah, will be ruined. And whatever affliction befalls a believer, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, expiates sins through it—even a thorn that pricks him.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"صححہ_ابن_خزیمہ","label":"صححه ابن خزيمة","number":849},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":24215,"n":24215},{"key":"hakim","label":"المستدرك على الصحيحين","number":936,"n":930}]},{"num":16197,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن سليمان بن يسار قال: تفرق الناس عن أبي هريرة، فقال له ناتل أهل الشام: أيها الشيخ حدثنا حديثًا سمعته من رسول اللّٰه ﷺ، قال: نعم، سمعت رسول اللّٰه ﷺ يقول:","((إن أول الناس يقضى يوم القيامة عليه رجل استشهد، فأتي به، فعرفه نعمه، فعرفها، قال: فما عملت فيها؟ قال: قاتلت فيك حتى استشهدت، قال: كذبت، ولكنك قاتلت لأن يقال: جريء، فقد قيل، ثم أمر به، فسحب على وجهه، حتى ألقي في النار، ورجل تعلم العلم، وعلمه، وقرأ القرآن، فأتي به، فعرفه نعمه فعرفها، قال: فما عملت فيها؟ قال: تعلمت العلم وعلمته، وقرأت فيك القرآن، قال: كذبت، ولكنك تعلمت العلم ليقال: عالم، وقرأت القرآن، ليقال: هو قارئ، فقد قيل، ثم أمر به، فسحب على وجهه حتى ألقي في النار، ورجل وسع اللّٰه عليه، وأعطاه من أصناف المال كله، فأتي به، فعرفه نعمه فعرفها، قال: فما عملت فيها؟ قال: ما تركت من سبيل تحب أن ينفق فيها إلا أنفقت فيها لك، قال: كذبت، ولكنك فعلت ليقال: هو جواد، فقد قيل، ثم أمر به، فسحب على وجهه، ثم ألقي في النار))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (١٥٢ :١٩٠٥).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب مناقشة المرائين من الشهداء والقراء والأثرياء","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (152 :1905).","chapter_en":"The Scrutiny of Those Who Showed Off among the Martyrs, Reciters, and Wealthy","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":28,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Sulaymān ibn Yasār narrated: When the people had dispersed from Abū Hurayrah, Nātil of the people of al-Shām said to him: “O shaykh, narrate to us a hadith that you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” He replied: “Yes. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ʿThe first person whose case will be judged on the Day of Resurrection will be a man who was martyred. He will be brought, and Allah will make him recognize His blessings, and he will recognize them.","Allah will ask: “What did you do with them?” He will say: “I fought for Your sake until I was martyred.” Allah will say: “You have lied. Rather, you fought so that it would be said: ‘He is courageous,’ and that was said.” Then he will be ordered to be dragged on his face until he is thrown into the Fire. Then a man who learned knowledge, taught it, and recited the Qurʾān will be brought. Allah will make him recognize His blessings, and he will recognize them.","Allah will ask: “What did you do with them?” He will say: “I learned knowledge, taught it, and recited the Qurʾān for Your sake.” Allah will say: “You have lied. Rather, you learned knowledge so that it would be said: ‘He is a scholar,’ and you recited the Qurʾān so that it would be said: ‘He is a reciter,’ and that was said.” Then he will be ordered to be dragged on his face until he is thrown into the Fire. Then a man upon whom Allah had bestowed abundance and given every kind of wealth will be brought. Allah will make him recognize His blessings, and he will recognize them.","Allah will ask: “What did you do with them?” He will say: “I did not leave any path in which You love wealth to be spent except that I spent in it for Your sake.” Allah will say: “You have lied. Rather, you did that so that it would be said: ‘He is generous,’ and that was said.” Then he will be ordered to be dragged on his face and thrown into the Fire.’”"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["وقوله: “ناتل أهل الشام” وهو ناتل بن قيس الخزاعي، وكان ناتل كبير قومه."],"en":["The phrase “Nātil of the people of al-Shām” refers to Nātil ibn Qays al-Khuzāʿī, who was a leading man among his people."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":152}]},{"num":16198,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن شفي الأصبحي أنه دخل المدينة، فإذا هو برجل قد اجتمع عليه الناس، فقال: من هذا؟ فقالوا: أبو هريرة، فدنوت منه حتى قعدت بين يديه وهو يحدث الناس، فلما سكن وخلا قلت له: أسألك بحق وبحق لما حدثتني حديثًا سمعته من رسول اللّٰه ﷺ عقلته وعلمته، فقال أبو هريرة: أفعل، لأحدثنك حديثًا حدثنيه رسول اللّٰه ﷺ عقلته وعلمته، ثم نشغ أبو هريرة نشغة، مكث قليلًا، ثم أفاق، فقال: لأحدثنك حديثًا حدثنيه رسول اللّٰه ﷺ في هذا البيت، ما معنا أحد غيري وغيره، ثم نشغ أبو هريرة نشغة أخرى، ثم أفاق، فمسح وجهه، فقال: لأحدثنك حديثًا حدثنيه رسول اللّٰه ﷺ، وأنا وهو في هذا البيت ما معنا أحد غيري وغيره، ثم نشغ أبو هريرة نشغة أخرى، ثم أفاق ومسح وجهه، فقال: أفعل لأحدثنك حديثًا حدثنيه رسول اللّٰه ﷺ، وأنا معه في هذا البيت ما معه أحد غيري وغيره، ثم نشغ أبو هريرة نشغة شديدة، ثم مال خارًا على وجهه، فأسندته علي طويلًا، ثم أفاق، فقال: حدثني رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((أن اللّٰه تبارك وتعالى إذا كان يوم القيامة ينزل إلى العباد ليقضي بينهم وكل أمة جاثية، فأول من يدعو به رجل جمع القرآن، ورجل قتل في سبيل اللّٰه، ورجل كثير المال، فيقول اللّٰه للقارئ: ألم أعلمك ما أنزلت على رسولي؟ قال: بلى يا رب. قال: فماذا عملت فيما علمت؟ قال: كنت أقوم به آناء الليل وآناء النهار، فيقول اللّٰه له: كذبت. وتقول له الملائكة: كذبت. ويقول اللّٰه: بل أردت أن يقال: إن فلانًا قارئ، فقد قيل ذاك. ويؤتى بصاحب المال فيقول اللّٰه له: ألم أوسع عليك حتى لم أدعك تحتاج إلى أحد؟ قال: بلى يا رب. قال: فماذا عملت فيما آتيتك؟ قال: كنت أصل الرحم وأتصدق، فيقول اللّٰه له: كذبت. وتقول له الملائكة: كذبت. ويقول اللّٰه تعالى: بل أردت أن يقال: فلان جواد، فقد قيل ذاك. ويؤتى بالذي قتل في سبيل اللّٰه فيقول اللّٰه له: فيماذا قتلت؟ فيقول: أمرت بالجهاد في سبيلك، فقاتلت حتى قتلت، فيقول اللّٰه تعالى له: كذبت. وتقول له الملائكة: كذبت. ويقول الله: بل أردت أن يقال: فلان جريء، فقد قيل ذاك)).","ثم ضرب رسول اللّٰه ﷺ على ركبتي، فقال:","((يا أبا هريرة، أولئك الثلاثة أول خلق اللّٰه تسعر بهم النار يوم القيامة))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الترمذي (٢٣٨٢)، وصححه ابن خزيمة (٢٤٨٢)، وابن حبان (٤٠٨).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب مناقشة المرائين من الشهداء والقراء والأثرياء","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (2382), authenticated by Ibn Khuzaymah (2482) and Ibn Ḥibbān (408).","chapter_en":"The Scrutiny of Those Who Showed Off among the Martyrs, Reciters, and Wealthy","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":28,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Shufayy al-Aṣbaḥī narrated: I entered Madinah and saw a man surrounded by people. I asked: “Who is this?” They replied: “Abū Hurayrah.” I drew near until I sat directly in front of him while he was narrating to the people. When the people became quiet and he was alone, I said to him: “I ask you by what is sacred and binding upon you to narrate to me a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, understood, and learned well.” Abū Hurayrah said: “I will. I will narrate to you a hadith that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ narrated to me, which I understood and learned well.”","Then Abū Hurayrah gasped deeply and remained that way for a short while before recovering. He said: “I will narrate to you a hadith that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ narrated to me in this very house, when there was no one here except him and me.” Then he gasped again and recovered. He wiped his face and repeated that he would narrate the hadith. Then he gasped a third time, recovered, and wiped his face. Then he said again: “I will narrate to you a hadith that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ narrated to me while I was with him in this house and no one else was with us.”","Then Abū Hurayrah gave a severe gasp and collapsed forward onto his face. I supported him against myself for a long time until he recovered. He then said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ told me: “When the Day of Resurrection comes, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will descend to the servants to judge between them while every nation is kneeling. The first people He will summon will be a man who had memorized the Qurʾān, a man who was killed in the path of Allah, and a man of great wealth.","Allah will say to the reciter: ‘Did I not teach you what I revealed to My Messenger?’ He will reply: ‘Yes, my Lord.’ Allah will ask: ‘Then what did you do with what you learned?’ He will say: ‘I used to stand reciting it throughout the night and throughout the day.’ Allah will say to him: ‘You have lied.’ And the angels will say to him: ‘You have lied.’ Allah will say: ‘Rather, you wanted it to be said: “So-and-so is a reciter,” and that was indeed said.’","Then the wealthy man will be brought. Allah will say to him: ‘Did I not grant you such abundance that I left you in need of no one?’ He will reply: ‘Yes, my Lord.’ Allah will ask: ‘What did you do with what I gave you?’ He will say: ‘I maintained ties of kinship and gave charity.’ Allah will say: ‘You have lied.’ And the angels will say: ‘You have lied.’ Allah, the Exalted, will say: ‘Rather, you wanted it to be said: “So-and-so is generous,” and that was indeed said.’","Then the man who was killed in the path of Allah will be brought. Allah will ask him: ‘For what were you killed?’ He will reply: ‘I was commanded to fight in Your path, so I fought until I was killed.’ Allah, the Exalted, will say to him: ‘You have lied.’ And the angels will say to him: ‘You have lied.’ Allah will say: ‘Rather, you wanted it to be said: “So-and-so is courageous,” and that was indeed said.’” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ struck my knee and said: “O Abū Hurayrah, these three are the first of Allah’s creation with whom the Fire will be kindled on the Day of Resurrection.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"tirmidhi","label":"الترمذي","number":2382},{"key":"صححہ_ابن_خزیمہ","label":"صححه ابن خزيمة","number":2482},{"key":"ibnhibban","label":"صحيح ابن حبان (التقاسيم والأنواع)","number":2961,"n":2958}]},{"num":16199,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن تميم الداري، عن النبي ﷺ قال:","((أول ما يحاسب به العبد يوم القيامة صلاته، فإن أكملها كتبت له نافلة، فإن لم يكن أكملها، قال اللّٰه سبحانه لملائكته: انظروا، هل تجدون لعبدي من تطوع؟ فأكملوا بها ما ضيع من فريضته، ثم تؤخذ الأعمال على حسب ذلك))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه ابن ماجه (١٤٢٦)، وأبو داود (٨٦٦)، والحاكم (٢٦٣-٢٦٢/١).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أول ما يحاسب به العبد من حقوق الله يوم القيامة الصلاة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Ibn Mājah (1426), Abū Dāwūd (866), and al-Ḥākim (1/262-263).","chapter_en":"The First of Allah’s Rights for Which the Servant Will Be Reckoned on the Day of Resurrection Is the Prayer","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":29,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Tamīm al-Dārī narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The first thing for which the servant will be brought to account on the Day of Resurrection will be his prayer. If he completed it, voluntary prayer will be recorded for him. But if he did not complete it, Allah, Glorified is He, will say to His angels: ‘Look and see whether My servant has any voluntary prayers. Complete through them whatever he neglected from his obligatory prayer.’ Then the rest of his deeds will be dealt with in the same manner.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ibnmajah","label":"ابن ماجه","number":1426},{"key":"abudawud","label":"أبو داود","number":866},{"key":"hakim","label":"الحاكم","number":263}]},{"num":16200,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبد اللّٰه بن مسعود قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((أول ما يقضى بين الناس يوم القيامة في الدماء))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٦٥٣٣)، ومسلم (٢٨:١٦٧٨).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب أول ما يقضى بين الناس يوم القيامة من حقوقهم في الدماء","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6533) and Muslim (28:1678).","chapter_en":"The First Disputes among the People to Be Judged on the Day of Resurrection Will Concern Bloodshed","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":30,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The first matters to be judged between the people on the Day of Resurrection will concern bloodshed.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6533},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":28}]},{"num":16201,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عقبة بن عامر قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((أول خصمين يوم القيامة جاران))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (١٧٣٧٢)، والطبراني في الكبير (٣٠٩/١٧).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب أول خصمين يوم القيامة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (17372) and al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Kabīr (17/309).","chapter_en":"The First Two Litigants on the Day of Resurrection","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":31,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The first two disputants on the Day of Resurrection will be two neighbors.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"الطبرانی/الکبیر","label":"الطبراني في الكبير","number":309},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":17372,"n":17372}]},{"num":16202,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((إن أول ما يسأل عنه يوم القيامة - يعني العبد - من النعيم أن يقال له: ألم نصح لك جسمك، ونرويك من الماء البارد))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الترمذي (٣٣٥٨)، والبزار (٩٤٠٨)، وعبد اللّٰه بن أحمد في زوائد الزهد (ص ٣١).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في السؤال عن النعيم","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (3358), al-Bazzār (9408), and ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad in Zawāʾid al-Zuhd (p. 31).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning Being Questioned about Blessings","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":32,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The first blessing about which the servant will be questioned on the Day of Resurrection will be that it is said to him: ‘Did We not give you a healthy body and give you cold water to drink?’”"]},"intro":{"ar":["قال تعالى:","﴿ثُمَّ لَتُسْأَلُنَّ يَوْمَئِذٍ عَنِ النَّعِيمِ﴾ [سورة التكاثر: ٨]."],"en":["Allah, the Exalted, says:","“Then, on that Day, you will surely be questioned about the blessings.”","[al-Takāthur 102:8]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"tirmidhi","label":"الترمذي","number":3358},{"key":"البزار","label":"البزار","number":9408},{"key":"عبد_اللہ_بن_احمد/زواید_الزہد","label":"عبد اللّٰه بن أحمد في زوائد الزهد","number":31}]},{"num":16203,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة قال: خرج رسول اللّٰه ﷺ ذات يوم أو ليلة فإذا هو بأبي بكر وعمر، فقال:","((ما أخرجكما من بيوتكما هذه الساعة؟)).","قالا: الجوع يا رسول الله، قال:","((وأنا والذي نفسي بيده لأخرجني الذي أخرجكما، قوموا)).","فقاموا معه، فأتى رجلًا من الأنصار، فإذا هو ليس في بيته، فلما رأته المرأة قالت: مرحبًا وأهلًا. فقال لها رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((أين فلان؟)).","قالت: ذهب يستعذب لنا من الماء.","إذ جاء الأنصاري فنظر إلى رسول اللّٰه ﷺ وصاحبيه، ثم قال: الحمد لله ما أحد اليوم أكرم أضيافًا مني، قال: فانطلق، فجاءهم بعذق فيه بسر وتمر ورطب. فقال: كلوا من هذه، وأخذ المدية، فقال له رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((إياك والحلوب)).","فذبح لهم فأكلوا من الشاة، ومن ذلك العذق وشربوا، فلما أن شبعوا ورووا قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ لأبي بكر وعمر:","((والذي نفسي بيده لتسألن عن هذا النعيم يوم القيامة، أخرجكم من بيوتكم الجوع، ثم لم ترجعوا حتى أصابكم هذا النعيم)).","وفي رواية:","((لا تذبحن ذات در))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (١٤٠ :٢٠٣٨).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في السؤال عن النعيم","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (140 :2038).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning Being Questioned about Blessings","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":32,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out one day—or one night—and found Abū Bakr and ʿUmar. He asked: “What brought you out of your homes at this hour?” They replied: “Hunger, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, the same thing that brought you out brought me out as well. Get up.” So they went with him to the home of a man from the Anṣār, but he was not at home. When his wife saw them, she said: “Welcome and greetings.”","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked her: “Where is so-and-so?” She replied: “He has gone to fetch sweet water for us.” Then the Anṣārī man arrived. When he saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his two companions, he said: “All praise is due to Allah. No one today has more honored guests than I do.” He went and brought them a cluster of dates containing unripe, ripe, and fresh dates and said: “Eat from these.” Then he took up a knife. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “Do not slaughter a milk-giving animal.”","He slaughtered an animal for them, and they ate from the sheep and from the dates and drank. When they had eaten their fill and quenched their thirst, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Abū Bakr and ʿUmar: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, you will surely be questioned about this blessing on the Day of Resurrection. Hunger brought you out of your homes, and you did not return until this blessing had reached you.”","In another narration: “Do not slaughter an animal that gives milk.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":140}]},{"num":16204,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي برزة الأسلمي قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((لا تزول قدما عبد يوم القيامة حتى يسأل عن عمره فيما أفناه، وعن علمه فيم فعل، وعن ماله من أين اكتسبه وفيم أنفقه، وعن جسمه فيم أبلاه))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (٢٤١٧).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب يسأل العبد يوم القيامة عن أربع: عن عمره، وعلمه، وماله، وجسمه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (2417).","chapter_en":"The Servant Will Be Questioned on the Day of Resurrection about Four Things: His Life, His Knowledge, His Wealth, and His Body","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":33,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Barzah al-Aslamī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The feet of a servant will not move on the Day of Resurrection until he is questioned about his life and how he spent it, about his knowledge and what he did with it, about his wealth—where he earned it and how he spent it—and about his body and how he wore it out.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"tirmidhi","label":"الترمذي","number":2417}]},{"num":16205,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي سعيد الخدري قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((يدعى نوح يوم القيامة، فيقول: لبيك وسعديك يا رب، فيقول: هل بلغت؟ فيقول: نعم، فيقال لأمته: هل بلغكم؟ فيقولون: ما أتانا من نذير، فيقول: من يشهد لك؟ فيقول: محمد وأمته، فتشهدون أنه قد بلغ: ﴿وَيَكُونَ الرَّسُولُ عَلَيْكُمْ شَهِيدًا﴾، فذلك قوله جل ذكره: ﴿وَكَذَٰلِكَ جَعَلْنَاكُمْ أُمَّةً وَسَطًا لِتَكُونُوا شُهَدَاءَ عَلَى النَّاسِ وَيَكُونَ الرَّسُولُ عَلَيْكُمْ شَهِيدًا﴾ [البقرة: ١٤٣])).","والوسط: العدل.","وفي لفظ:","((يجيء النبي يوم القيامة، ومعه الرجل، والنبي ومعه الرجلان، وأكثر من ذلك، فيدعى قومه، فيقال لهم: هل بلغكم هذا؟ فيقولون: لا. فيقال له: هل بلغت قومك؟ فيقول: نعم. فيقال له: من يشهد لك؟ فيقول: محمد وأمته. فيدعى محمد وأمته، فيقال لهم: هل بلغ هذا قومه؟ فيقولون: نعم. فيقال: وما علمكم؟ فيقولون: جاءنا نبينا، فأخبرنا أن الرسل قد بلغوا، فذلك قوله: ﴿وَكَذَٰلِكَ جَعَلْنَاكُمْ أُمَّةً وَسَطًا﴾ قال: يقول: عدلًا ﴿لِتَكُونُوا شُهَدَاءَ عَلَى النَّاسِ وَيَكُونَ الرَّسُولُ عَلَيْكُمْ شَهِيدًا﴾))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (٤٤٨٧)، واللفظ الثاني رواه أحمد (١١٥٥٨).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب شهادة النبي ﷺ وأمته على الأمم","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4487). The second wording was narrated by Aḥmad (11558).","chapter_en":"The Testimony of the Prophet ﷺ and His Ummah against the Nations","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":34,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Nūḥ will be summoned on the Day of Resurrection and will say: ‘At Your service and ready to obey, my Lord.’ Allah will ask: ‘Did you convey the message?’ He will reply: ‘Yes.’ His nation will then be asked: ‘Did he convey the message to you?’ They will say: ‘No warner came to us.’ It will be said to Nūḥ: ‘Who will testify for you?’ He will reply: ‘Muḥammad and his Ummah.’ So you will testify that he conveyed the message, and the Messenger will be a witness over you. This is the meaning of the statement of Allah, Glorious is His remembrance: ‘Thus We have made you a just and balanced nation so that you may be witnesses over mankind and the Messenger may be a witness over you.’","[al-Baqarah 2:143]” The word “wasaṭ” means just.","In another wording: “A Prophet will come on the Day of Resurrection accompanied by one man, another Prophet accompanied by two men, and another by more than that. His people will be summoned and asked: ‘Did this man convey the message to you?’ They will say: ‘No.’ The Prophet will be asked: ‘Did you convey the message to your people?’ He will reply: ‘Yes.’ It will be asked: ‘Who will testify for you?’ He will say: ‘Muḥammad and his Ummah.’ Muḥammad and his Ummah will then be summoned and asked: ‘Did this Prophet convey the message to his people?’","They will reply: ‘Yes.’ It will be asked: ‘How do you know?’ They will say: ‘Our Prophet came to us and informed us that the Messengers had conveyed their messages.’ That is the meaning of His statement: ‘Thus We have made you a wasaṭ nation’—meaning just—‘so that you may be witnesses over mankind and the Messenger may be a witness over you.’”"]},"intro":{"ar":["قال تعالى:","﴿وَكَذَٰلِكَ جَعَلْنَاكُمْ أُمَّةً وَسَطًا لِتَكُونُوا شُهَدَاءَ عَلَى النَّاسِ وَيَكُونَ الرَّسُولُ عَلَيْكُمْ شَهِيدًا﴾ [البقرة: ١٤٣]."],"en":["Allah, the Exalted, says:","“Thus We have made you a just and balanced nation so that you may be witnesses over mankind and the Messenger may be a witness over you.”","[al-Baqarah 2:143]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":4487},{"key":"اللفظ_الثانی_رواہ_احمد","label":"اللفظ الثاني رواه أحمد","number":11558},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":11558,"n":11558}]},{"num":16206,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن يحنس مولى الزبير بن العوام، أنه أخبره أنه كان جالسًا عند عبد اللّٰه بن عمر في الفتنة، فأتته مولاة له تسلم عليه، فقالت: إني أريد الخروج، يا أبا عبد الرحمن، اشتد علينا الزمان، فقال لها عبد الله: اقعدي لكاع، فإني سمعت رسول الله ﷺ يقول:","((لا يصبر على لأوائها وشدتها أحد، إلا كنت له شهيدًا أو شفيعًا يوم القيامة))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مالك في الجامع (٣) ومسلم (٤٨٢:١٣٧٧).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب شهادة النبي ﷺ وشفاعته لمن صبر على لأواء المدينة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Mālik in al-Jāmiʿ (3) and Muslim (482:1377).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s ﷺ Testimony and Intercession for Whoever Patiently Endures the Hardships of Madinah","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":35,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Yaḥnas, the freedman of al-Zubayr ibn al-ʿAwwām, narrated that he was sitting with ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar during a time of tribulation when a female servant of his came to greet him. She said: “I want to leave, O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān. Times have become difficult for us.” ʿAbdullāh said to her: “Remain here, foolish woman, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘No one patiently endures the hardships and severity of Madinah except that I will be a witness or an intercessor for him on the Day of Resurrection.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"malik/الجامع","label":"مالك في الجامع","number":3},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":482}]},{"num":16207,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي سعيد مولى المهري أنه جاء أبا سعيد الخدري ليالي الحرة، فاستشاره في الجلاء من المدينة، وشكا إليه أسعارها وكثرة عياله، وأخبره أن لا صبر له على جهد المدينة ولأوائها، فقال له: ويحك لا آمرك بذلك، إني سمعت رسول اللّٰه ﷺ يقول:","((لا يصبر أحد على لأوائها، فيموت، إلا كنت له شفيعًا أو شهيدًا يوم القيامة إذا كان مسلمًا))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٤٧٧:١٣٧٤).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب شهادة النبي ﷺ وشفاعته لمن صبر على لأواء المدينة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (477:1374).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s ﷺ Testimony and Intercession for Whoever Patiently Endures the Hardships of Madinah","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":35,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd, the freedman of al-Mahrī, came to Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī during the nights of al-Ḥarrah and consulted him about leaving Madinah. He complained about its high prices and his large family and told him that he could no longer endure the hardship and difficulty of life in Madinah. Abū Saʿīd said: “Woe to you! I will not advise you to do that. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘No Muslim patiently endures the hardships of Madinah until he dies except that I will be an intercessor or a witness for him on the Day of Resurrection.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":477}]},{"num":16208,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ - في حديث رؤية الرب يوم القيامة -:","((ثم يقال له: الآن نبعث شاهدنا عليك، ويتفكر في نفسه: من ذا الذي يشهد علي؟ فيختم على فيه، ويقال لفخذه ولحمه وعظامه: انطقي، فتنطق فخذه ولحمه وعظامه بعمله، وذلك ليعذر من نفسه، وذلك المنافق، وذلك الذي يسخط اللّٰه عليه))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٢٩٦٨).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما يشهد يوم القيامة من أعضاء الإنسان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2968).","chapter_en":"The Parts of the Human Body That Will Testify on the Day of Resurrection","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":36,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, in the hadith concerning seeing the Lord on the Day of Resurrection: “Then it will be said to him: ‘Now We will bring Our witness against you.’ He will think to himself: ‘Who could testify against me?’ His mouth will then be sealed, and his thigh, flesh, and bones will be told: ‘Speak.’ His thigh, flesh, and bones will then speak about his deeds. This will be so that every excuse is removed from him.","That is the hypocrite, and that is the one with whom Allah is angry.”"]},"intro":{"ar":["قال تعالى:","﴿يَوْمَ تَشْهَدُ عَلَيْهِمْ أَلْسِنَتُهُمْ وَأَيْدِيهِمْ وَأَرْجُلُهُمْ بِمَا كَانُوا يَعْمَلُونَ﴾ [النور: ٢٤].","وقال تعالى:","﴿حَتَّىٰ إِذَا مَا جَاءُوهَا شَهِدَ عَلَيْهِمْ سَمْعُهُمْ وَأَبْصَارُهُمْ وَجُلُودُهُمْ بِمَا كَانُوا يَعْمَلُونَ ۝ وَقَالُوا لِجُلُودِهِمْ لِمَ شَهِدْتُمْ عَلَيْنَا قَالُوا أَنْطَقَنَا اللَّهُ الَّذِي أَنْطَقَ كُلَّ شَيْءٍ وَهُوَ خَلَقَكُمْ أَوَّلَ مَرَّةٍ وَإِلَيْهِ تُرْجَعُونَ﴾ [فصلت: ٢٠-٢١]."],"en":["Allah, the Exalted, says:","“On the Day when their tongues, their hands, and their feet will testify against them concerning what they used to do.”","[al-Nūr 24:24]","And He, the Exalted, says:","“Until, when they reach it, their hearing, their sight, and their skins will testify against them concerning what they used to do. They will say to their skins: ‘Why did you testify against us?’ They will reply: ‘Allah, who gives speech to everything, has made us speak. He created you the first time, and to Him you are being returned.’”","[Fuṣṣilat 41:20-21]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2968}]},{"num":16209,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أنس بن مالك قال: كنا عند رسول اللّٰه ﷺ فضحك، فقال:","((هل تدرون مم أضحك؟)).","قال: قلنا: اللّٰه ورسوله أعلم، قال:","((من مخاطبة العبد ربه، يقول: يا رب ألم تجرني من الظلم؟ قال: يقول: بلى، قال: فيقول: فإني لا أجيز على نفسي إلا شاهدًا مني، قال: فيقول: كفى بنفسك اليوم عليك شهيدًا، وبالكرام الكاتبين شهودًا، قال: فيختم على فيه، فيقال لأركانه: انطقي. قال: فتنطق بأعماله، قال: ثم يخلى بينه وبين الكلام، قال: فيقول: بعدًا لكن وسحقًا، فعنكن كنت أناضل))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٢٩٦٨).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما يشهد يوم القيامة من أعضاء الإنسان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2968).","chapter_en":"The Parts of the Human Body That Will Testify on the Day of Resurrection","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":36,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik narrated: We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he laughed. He asked: “Do you know what made me laugh?” We replied: “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said: “It is because of the conversation between a servant and his Lord. The servant will say: ‘My Lord, did You not protect me from injustice?’ Allah will say: ‘Yes.’ The servant will say: ‘Then I will accept no witness against myself except one from myself.’ Allah will say: ‘Today you are sufficient as a witness against yourself, and the noble recording angels are sufficient as witnesses.’","Then his mouth will be sealed, and his limbs will be told: ‘Speak.’ They will speak about his deeds. Then he will be allowed to speak again, and he will say to his limbs: ‘Away with you! Woe to you! It was on your behalf that I was arguing!’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2968}]},{"num":16210,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن بهز بن حكيم، عن أبيه، عن جده قال: أتيت النبي ﷺ، فقال في حديث طويل:","((ما لي أمسك بحجزكم عن النار؟ ألا إن ربي داعي وإنه سائلي: هل بلغت عباده؟ وإني قائل: رب إني قد بلغتهم، فليبلغ الشاهد منكم الغائب، ثم إنكم مدعوون مفدمة أفواهكم بالفدام، ثم إن أول ما يبين عن أحدكم لفخذه وكفه)).","قلت: يا نبي اللّه: هذا ديننا؟ قال:","((هذا دينكم، وأينما تحسن يكفك))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (٢٠٠٤٣).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما يشهد يوم القيامة من أعضاء الإنسان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (20043).","chapter_en":"The Parts of the Human Body That Will Testify on the Day of Resurrection","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":36,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Bahz ibn Ḥakīm narrated from his father, from his grandfather: I came to the Prophet ﷺ, and in a lengthy hadith he said: “Why am I holding you back by your waistbands from the Fire? Indeed, my Lord will call me and ask me: ‘Did you convey My message to My servants?’ I will say: ‘My Lord, I conveyed it to them.’ So let those who are present convey it to those who are absent. Then you will be summoned with your mouths restrained by a muzzle, and the first part of one of you to speak will be his thigh and his hand.”","I asked: “O Prophet of Allah, is this our religion?” He replied: “This is your religion, and wherever you do good, it will suffice you.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":20043,"n":20043}]},{"num":16211,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي سعيد الخدري أنه قال لعبد اللّه بن عبد الرحمن بن أبي صعصعة الأنصاري ثم المازني: إني أراك تحب الغنم والبادية، فإذا كنت في غنمك، أو باديتك، فأذنت بالصلاة فارفع صوتك بالنداء، فإنه:","((لا يسمع مدى صوت المؤذن جن ولا إنس ولا شيء، إلا شهد له يوم القيامة)).","قال أبو سعيد: سمعته من رسول اللّٰه ﷺ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: أخرجه مالك في الصلاة (٥) والبخاري (٦٠٩).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب شهادة الإنس والجن وكل رطب ويابس للمؤذن","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Mālik in al-Ṣalāh (5) and al-Bukhārī (609).","chapter_en":"The Testimony of Humans, Jinn, and Every Living and Inanimate Thing for the Muʾadhdhin","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":37,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī said to ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Ṣaʿṣaʿah al-Anṣārī al-Māzinī: “I see that you love sheep and the open countryside. When you are with your sheep or out in the desert and call the adhān for prayer, raise your voice with the call, for: ‘No jinn, human being, or anything else within the range of the muʾadhdhin’s voice hears it except that it will testify for him on the Day of Resurrection.’” Abū Saʿīd said: “I heard this from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"malik/الصلاہ","label":"مالك في الصلاة","number":5},{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":609}]},{"num":16212,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة، عن النبي ﷺ، قال:","((المؤذن يغفر له مدى صوته، ويشهد له كل رطب ويابس، وشاهد الصلاة يكتب له خمس وعشرون صلاة، ويكفر عنه ما بينهما))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (٥١٥) واللفظ له، والنسائي (٦٤٥) وابن ماجه (٧٢٤).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب شهادة الإنس والجن وكل رطب ويابس للمؤذن","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (515), whose wording this is, al-Nasā’ī (645), and Ibn Mājah (724).","chapter_en":"The Testimony of Humans, Jinn, and Every Living and Inanimate Thing for the Muʾadhdhin","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":37,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The mu’adhdhin will be forgiven to the extent reached by his voice, and every living and inanimate thing will testify for him. Whoever attends the prayer will have the reward of twenty-five prayers recorded for him, and the sins committed between the two prayers will be expiated.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"abudawud","label":"أبو داود","number":515},{"key":"nasai","label":"النسائي","number":645},{"key":"ibnmajah","label":"ابن ماجه","number":724}]},{"num":16213,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن ابن عباس قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ في الحجر:","((والله ليبعثنه اللّٰه يوم القيامة، له عينان يبصر بهما، ولسان ينطق به، يشهد على من استلمه بحق))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (٩٦١)، وابن ماجه (٢٩٤٤)، وأحمد (٢٦٤٣، ٣٣٩٨، ٢٢١٥)، وصححه ابن خزيمة (٢٧٣٥)، وابن حبان (٣٧١٢)، والحاكم (١/٦٦٤).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب شهادة الحجر الأسود لمن استلمه بحق","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (961), Ibn Mājah (2944), and Aḥmad (2643, 3398, 2215), and authenticated by Ibn Khuzaymah (2735), Ibn Ḥibbān (3712), and al-Ḥākim (1/664).","chapter_en":"The Black Stone Will Testify for Whoever Touched It Rightfully","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":38,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿAbbās narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said concerning the Black Stone: “By Allah, Allah will surely resurrect it on the Day of Resurrection with two eyes by which it will see and a tongue by which it will speak, testifying for whoever touched it rightfully.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"tirmidhi","label":"الترمذي","number":961},{"key":"ibnmajah","label":"ابن ماجه","number":2944},{"key":"صححہ_ابن_خزیمہ","label":"صححه ابن خزيمة","number":2735},{"key":"ibnhibban","label":"ابن حبان","number":3712},{"key":"hakim","label":"الحاكم","number":1},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":2643,"n":2643}]},{"num":16214,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن صفوان بن محرز قال: قال رجل لابن عمر: كيف سمعت رسول اللّٰه ﷺ يقول في النجوى؟ قال: سمعته يقول:","((يدنى المؤمن يوم القيامة من ربه عز وجل، حتى يضع عليه كنفه، فيقرره بذنوبه، فيقول: هل تعرف؟ فيقول: أي رب أعرف، قال: فإني قد سترتها عليك في الدنيا، وإني أغفرها لك اليوم، فيعطى صحيفة حسناته، وأما الكفار والمنافقون، فينادى بهم على رؤوس الخلائق: هؤلاء الذين كذبوا على اللّٰه))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٤٦٨٥)، ومسلم (٢٧٦٨). واللفظ لمسلم.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب يقرر الله المؤمن بذنوبه يوم القيامة ثم يغفرها له","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4685) and Muslim (2768). The wording is Muslim’s.","chapter_en":"Allah Will Make the Believer Acknowledge His Sins on the Day of Resurrection and Then Forgive Him","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":40,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ṣafwān ibn Muḥriz narrated: A man asked Ibn ʿUmar: “How did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ describe the private conversation?” He replied: I heard him say: “The believer will be brought near to his Lord, Mighty and Majestic, on the Day of Resurrection until He places His covering over him. He will make him acknowledge his sins and ask: ‘Do you recognize them?’ He will say: ‘Yes, my Lord, I recognize them.’ Allah will say: ‘I concealed them for you in the world, and today I forgive them for you.’","Then he will be given the record of his good deeds. As for the disbelievers and hypocrites, it will be proclaimed before all creation: ‘These are the ones who lied about Allah.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":4685},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2768}]},{"num":16215,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أنس بن مالك قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((إن اللّه لا يظلم مؤمنًا حسنة، يعطى بها في الدنيا ويجزى بها في الآخرة، وأما الكافر فيطعم بحسنات ما عمل بها لله في الدنيا، حتى إذا أفضى إلى الآخرة، لم تكن له حسنة يجزى بها)).","وفي رواية عنده مرفوعًا بلفظ:","((إن الكافر إذا عمل حسنة أطعم بها طعمة من الدنيا، وأما المؤمن، فإن اللّه يدخر له حسناته في الآخرة ويعقبه رزقًا في الدنيا على طاعته))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٢٨٠٨).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب جزاء المؤمن بحسناته في الدنيا والآخرة، وتعجيل حسنات الكافر في الدنيا","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2808).","chapter_en":"The Believer Is Rewarded for His Good Deeds in This World and the Hereafter, While the Disbeliever’s Reward for Good Deeds Is Hastened for Him in This World","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":41,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah does not wrong a believer regarding any good deed. He is given something for it in this world and rewarded for it in the Hereafter. As for the disbeliever, he is given worldly provision in return for the good deeds he performed for Allah, until when he reaches the Hereafter, he has no good deed remaining for which he will be rewarded.” In another marfūʿ narration recorded by Muslim: “When a disbeliever performs a good deed, he is given some worldly benefit because of it. As for the believer, Allah stores his good deeds for him in the Hereafter and also grants him provision in this world because of his obedience.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2808}]},{"num":16216,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة قال: قالوا: يا رسول الله، هل نرى ربنا يوم القيامة؟ قال:","((هل تضارون في رؤية الشمس في الظهيرة، ليست في سحابة؟)).","قالوا: لا، قال:","((فهل تضارون في رؤية القمر ليلة البدر، ليس في سحابة؟)).","قالوا: لا، قال:","((فوالذي نفسي بيده لا تضارون في رؤية ربكم إلا كما تضارون في رؤية أحدهما، قال: فيلقى العبد، فيقول: أي فل، ألم أكرمك، وأسودك، وأزوجك، وأسخر لك الخيل والإبل، وأذرك ترأس وتربع؟ فيقول: بلى، قال: فيقول: أفظننت أنك ملاقي؟ فيقول: لا، فيقول: فإني أنساك كما نسيتني، ثم يلقى الثاني فيقول: أي فل، ألم أكرمك، وأسودك، وأزوجك، وأسخر لك الخيل والإبل، وأذرك ترأس وتربع؟ فيقول: بلى، أي رب، فيقول: أفظننت أنك ملاقي؟ فيقول: لا، فيقول: فإني أنساك كما نسيتني، ثم يلقى الثالث، فيقول له مثل ذلك، فيقول: يا رب آمنت بك، وبكتابك، وبرسلك، وصليت، وصمت، وتصدقت، ويثني بخير ما استطاع، فيقول: هاهنا إذًا، قال: ثم يقال له: الآن نبعث شاهدنا عليك، ويتفكر في نفسه: من ذا الذي يشهد علي؟ فيختم على فيه، ويقال لفخذه ولحمه وعظامه: انطقي، فتنطق فخذه ولحمه وعظامه بعمله، وذلك ليعذر من نفسه، وذلك المنافق وذلك الذي يسخط اللّٰه عليه))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٢٩٦٨).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب مصير من نسي لقاء ربه يوم القيامة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2968).","chapter_en":"The Fate of Those Who Forgot the Meeting with Their Lord on the Day of Resurrection","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":42,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated: They asked: “O Messenger of Allah, will we see our Lord on the Day of Resurrection?” He replied: “Do you have difficulty seeing the sun at midday when there is no cloud?” They said: “No.” He asked: “Do you have difficulty seeing the full moon on a cloudless night?” They replied: “No.” He said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, you will have no more difficulty seeing your Lord than you have seeing either of those.","A servant will then meet Him, and Allah will say: ‘O so-and-so, did I not honor you, make you a leader, give you a spouse, subject horses and camels to you, and allow you to lead and enjoy a quarter share of the spoils?’ He will reply: ‘Yes.’ Allah will ask: ‘Did you think that you would meet Me?’ He will reply: ‘No.’ Allah will say: ‘Then today I forget you just as you forgot Me.’ Then He will meet a second person and say the same to him. He will likewise reply that he did not think he would meet Allah, so Allah will say: ‘Today I forget you just as you forgot Me.’","Then He will meet a third person and say the same to him. The man will say: ‘My Lord, I believed in You, Your Book, and Your Messengers. I prayed, fasted, and gave charity,’ and he will praise himself with as much good as he can. Allah will say: ‘Then remain here.’ Then it will be said to him: ‘Now We will bring Our witness against you.’ He will think to himself: ‘Who could testify against me?’ His mouth will then be sealed, and his thigh, flesh, and bones will be told: ‘Speak.’","His thigh, flesh, and bones will speak about his deeds. This will be so that no excuse remains for him. That is the hypocrite, and that is the one with whom Allah is angry.”"]},"intro":{"ar":["قال تعالى:","﴿وَبَدَا لَهُمْ سَيِّئَاتُ مَا عَمِلُوا وَحَاقَ بِهِمْ مَا كَانُوا بِهِ يَسْتَهْزِئُونَ ۝ وَقِيلَ الْيَوْمَ نَنْسَاكُمْ كَمَا نَسِيتُمْ لِقَاءَ يَوْمِكُمْ هَذَا وَمَأْوَاكُمُ النَّارُ وَمَا لَكُمْ مِنْ نَاصِرِينَ﴾ [سورة الجاثية: ٣٣-٣٤]."],"en":["Allah, the Exalted, says:","“The evil consequences of what they did will become apparent to them, and what they used to mock will surround them. And it will be said: ‘Today We will forget you just as you forgot the meeting of this Day of yours. Your refuge is the Fire, and you will have no helpers.’”","[al-Jāthiyah 45:33-34]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2968}]},{"num":16217,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة، وأبي سعيد، قالا: قال رسول الله ﷺ:","((يؤتى بالعبد يوم القيامة فيقول اللّٰه له: ألم أجعل لك سمعًا وبصرًا ومالًا وولدًا، وسخرت لك الأنعام والحرث، وتركتك ترأس وتربع، فكنت تظن أنك ملاقي يومك هذا؟ فيقول: لا، فيقول له: اليوم أنساك كما نسيتني))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (٢٤٢٨).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب مصير من نسي لقاء ربه يوم القيامة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (2428).","chapter_en":"The Fate of Those Who Forgot the Meeting with Their Lord on the Day of Resurrection","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":42,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah and Abū Saʿīd narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A servant will be brought on the Day of Resurrection, and Allah will say to him: ‘Did I not give you hearing, sight, wealth, and children? Did I not subject livestock and cultivated land to you and allow you to lead and enjoy a share of the spoils? Did you think that you would meet this Day of yours?’ He will reply: ‘No.’ Allah will say to him: ‘Today I forget you just as you forgot Me.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"tirmidhi","label":"الترمذي","number":2428}]},{"num":16218,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن ثوبان، عن النبي ﷺ أنه قال:","((لأعلمن أقوامًا من أمتي يأتون يوم القيامة بحسنات أمثال جبال تهامة بيضًا، فيجعلها اللّٰه عز وجل هباء منثورًا)).","قال ثوبان: يا رسول الله، صفهم لنا، جلهم لنا أن لا نكون منهم، ونحن لا نعلم، قال:","((أما إنهم إخوانكم، ومن جلدتكم، ويأخذون من الليل كما تأخذون، ولكنهم أقوام إذا خلوا بمحارم اللّٰه انتهكوها))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه ابن ماجه (٤٢٤٥)، والروياني في مسنده (٦٥٨)، والطبراني في الأوسط (٤٦٣٢).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب مصير من ينتهك محارم الله في الخلوة يوم القيامة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Ibn Mājah (4245), al-Rūyānī in his Musnad (658), and al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Awsaṭ (4632).","chapter_en":"The Fate on the Day of Resurrection of Those Who Violate Allah’s Sacred Limits in Private","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":43,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Thawbān narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “I certainly know of people from my Ummah who will come on the Day of Resurrection with good deeds as great and white as the mountains of Tihāmah, but Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will turn them into scattered dust.” Thawbān said: “O Messenger of Allah, describe them to us and make them clear to us so that we do not unknowingly become among them.” He replied: “Indeed, they are your brothers and are from your own people. They take a portion of the night for worship just as you do. But they are people who, when alone with what Allah has forbidden, violate it.”"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["قوله: ((إذا خلوا بمحارم اللّٰه انتهكوها)) أي استحلوها.","وقيل من أهل العلم: إنه خاص بالمنافقين لقوله تعالى:","﴿يَسْتَخْفُونَ مِنَ النَّاسِ وَلَا يَسْتَخْفُونَ مِنَ اللَّهِ وَهُوَ مَعَهُمْ إِذْ يُبَيِّتُونَ مَا لَا يَرْضَىٰ مِنَ الْقَوْلِ وَكَانَ اللَّهُ بِمَا يَعْمَلُونَ مُحِيطًا﴾ [النساء: ١٠٨].","وقال بعضهم: إنه منسوخ بعد قول النبي ﷺ:","((كل أمتي معافى إلا المجاهرين، وإن من المجاهرة أن يعمل الرجل بالليل عملًا، ثم يصبح وقد ستره اللّٰه عليه، فيقول: يا فلان، عملت البارحة كذا وكذا، وقد بات يستره ربه، ويصبح يكشف ستر اللّٰه عنه)).","رواه البخاري ومسلم."],"en":["The author explains that the statement:","“When they are alone with what Allah has forbidden, they violate it”","means that they treat those prohibitions as permissible.","Some scholars said that this specifically refers to hypocrites, based on the statement of Allah, the Exalted:","“They seek to hide from people, but they do not seek to hide from Allah, while He is with them when they plot by night words with which He is not pleased. Allah encompasses all that they do.”","[al-Nisāʾ 4:108]","Others said that this was abrogated after the statement of the Prophet ﷺ:","“All of my Ummah may be pardoned except those who openly publicize their sins. Among publicizing sins is that a man does something at night, then wakes in the morning after Allah had concealed it for him and says: ‘O so-and-so, last night I did such-and-such.’ His Lord had concealed him throughout the night, yet in the morning he removes Allah’s concealment from himself.”","Narrated by al-Bukhārī and Muslim."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ibnmajah","label":"ابن ماجه","number":4245},{"key":"الرویانی/مسندہ","label":"الروياني في مسنده","number":658},{"key":"الطبرانی/الاوسط","label":"الطبراني في الأوسط","number":4632},{"key":"sh28171","label":"المعجم الأوسط للطبراني","number":4632,"n":4620}]},{"num":16219,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي سعيد الخدري قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((يخلص المؤمنون من النار، فيحبسون على قنطرة بين الجنة والنار، فيقتص لبعضهم من بعض مظالم كانت بينهم في الدنيا، حتى إذا هذبوا ونقوا أذن لهم في دخول الجنة، فوالذي نفس محمد بيده، لأحدهم أهدى بمنزله في الجنة منه بمنزله كان في الدنيا))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (٦٥٣٥).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب اقتصاص المظالم بين الخلق يوم القيامة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6535).","chapter_en":"Settling Wrongs between Created Beings on the Day of Resurrection","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":44,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When the believers have been delivered from the Fire, they will be held on a bridge between Paradise and the Fire. There, the wrongs that occurred between them in this world will be settled. When they have been purified and cleansed, they will be given permission to enter Paradise. By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muḥammad, each of them will know his dwelling in Paradise better than he knew his dwelling in this world.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6535}]},{"num":16220,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة: أن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال:","((من كانت عنده مظلمة لأخيه فليتحلل منها، فإنه ليس ثم دينار ولا درهم، من قبل أن يؤخذ لأخيه من حسناته، فإن لم يكن له حسنات أخذ من سيئات أخيه فطرحت عليه))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (٦٥٣٤).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب اقتصاص المظالم بين الخلق يوم القيامة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6534).","chapter_en":"Settling Wrongs between Created Beings on the Day of Resurrection","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":44,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever has wronged his brother should seek to be absolved by him now, for there will be neither dinars nor dirhams there. Before that Day comes, some of his good deeds will be taken and given to his brother. If he has no good deeds, then some of his brother’s sins will be taken and cast upon him.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6534}]},{"num":16221,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة، أن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال:","((أتدرون ما المفلس؟)).","قالوا: المفلس فينا من لا درهم له ولا متاع، فقال:","((إن المفلس من أمتي يأتي يوم القيامة بصلاة، وصيام، وزكاة، ويأتي قد شتم هذا، وقذف هذا، وأكل مال هذا، وسفك دم هذا، وضرب هذا، فيعطى هذا من حسناته، وهذا من حسناته، فإن فنيت حسناته قبل أن يقضى ما عليه أخذ من خطاياهم فطرحت عليه، ثم طرح في النار))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٢٥٨١).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب اقتصاص المظالم بين الخلق يوم القيامة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2581).","chapter_en":"Settling Wrongs between Created Beings on the Day of Resurrection","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":44,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked: “Do you know who the bankrupt person is?” They replied: “The bankrupt among us is the one who has neither money nor possessions.” He said: “The bankrupt person from my Ummah is the one who comes on the Day of Resurrection with prayer, fasting, and zakāh, but he also comes having insulted this person, falsely accused that person, consumed another’s wealth, shed another’s blood, and struck another.","This person will be given from his good deeds, and that person will be given from his good deeds. If his good deeds run out before all that he owes has been settled, some of their sins will be taken and cast upon him, then he will be cast into the Fire.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2581}]},{"num":16222,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبدالله بن أنيس، قال: سمعت رسول اللّٰه ﷺ يقول:","((يحشر الناس يوم القيامة - أو قال: العباد - عراة غرلا بهما)).","قال: قلنا: وما بهما؟ قال:","((ليس معهم شيء، ثم يناديهم بصوت يسمعه من بعد كما يسمعه من قرب: أنا الملك، أنا الديان، ولا ينبغي لأحد من أهل النار أن يدخل النار، وله عند أحد من أهل الجنة حق، حتى أقصه منه، ولا ينبغي لأحد من أهل الجنة أن يدخل الجنة ولأحد من أهل النار عنده حق، حتى أقصه منه حتى اللطمة)).","قال: قلنا: كيف وإنا إنما نأتي اللّٰه عز وجل عراة غرلا بهما؟ قال:","((بالحسنات والسيئات))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (١٦٠٤٢)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (٩٧٠)، وابن أبي عاصم في السنة (٥١٤)، وصححه الحاكم (٣٦٣٨).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب اقتصاص المظالم بين الخلق يوم القيامة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (16042), al-Bukhārī in al-Adab al-Mufrad (970), Ibn Abī ʿĀṣim in al-Sunnah (514), and authenticated by al-Ḥākim (3638).","chapter_en":"Settling Wrongs between Created Beings on the Day of Resurrection","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":44,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn Unays narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The people—or he said, the servants—will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection naked, uncircumcised, and possessing nothing.” We asked: “What does ‘possessing nothing’ mean?” He replied: “They will have nothing with them. Then He will call them with a voice heard by the distant just as the near hear it: ʿI am the King. I am the One who gives full recompense. No one from the people of the Fire should enter the Fire while someone from the people of Paradise has a right against him until I settle it from him.","And no one from the people of Paradise should enter Paradise while someone from the people of the Fire has a right against him until I settle it from him—even for a slap.’” We asked: “How can that be when we come before Allah, Mighty and Majestic, naked, uncircumcised, and possessing nothing?” He replied: “Through good deeds and bad deeds.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari/الادب_المفرد","label":"البخاري في الأدب المفرد","number":970},{"key":"ابن_ابی_عاصم/السنہ","label":"ابن أبي عاصم في السنة","number":514},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":16042,"n":16042},{"key":"hakim","label":"المستدرك على الصحيحين","number":3638,"n":3625}]},{"num":16223,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن سلمان وغيره من أصحاب محمد ﷺ قالوا: إن الرجل يجيء يوم القيامة قد عمل عملًا يرجو أن ينجو به، قال: فما يزال الرجل يأتيه فيشتكي مظلمة فيؤخذ من حسناته فيعطاها حتى ما تبقى له حسنة، ويجيء المشتكي يشتكي مظلمة فيؤخذ من سيئاته فتوضع على سيئاته، ثم يكب في النار أو يلقى في النار."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه ابن أبي شيبة في المصنف (٣٥٨١٤) والحاكم (٥٧٠/٤).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب اقتصاص المظالم بين الخلق يوم القيامة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah in al-Muṣannaf (35814) and al-Ḥākim (4/570).","chapter_en":"Settling Wrongs between Created Beings on the Day of Resurrection","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":44,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Salmān and others among the Companions of Muḥammad ﷺ said: A man will come on the Day of Resurrection having performed deeds by which he hopes to be saved. But one person after another will come to him complaining of wrongs committed against them. Some of his good deeds will be taken and given to them until he has no good deeds left. Then another claimant will come complaining of a wrong. Some of that person’s sins will be taken and added to his sins.","Then he will be thrown face-first into the Fire—or cast into the Fire."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ابن_ابی_شیبہ/المصنف","label":"ابن أبي شيبة في المصنف","number":35814},{"key":"hakim","label":"الحاكم","number":570},{"key":"sh9944","label":"المصنف لابن أبي شيبة","number":34669,"n":34649}]},{"num":16224,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي أمامة الباهلي قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((يجيء الظالم يوم القيامة حتى إذا كان على جسر جهنم بين الظلمة والوعرة، لقيه المظلوم، فعرفه وعرف ما ظلمه به، فما يبرح الذين ظلموا يقضون من الذين ظلموا، حتى ينزعوا ما في أيديهم من الحسنات، فإن لم يكن لهم حسنات أدرك عليهم من سيئاتهم مثل ما ظلموا، حتى يوردوا الدرك الأسفل من النار))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الطبراني في الأوسط (٥٩٧٣) - والسياق له -، والبخاري في التاريخ الكبير (٢٢٨/٢).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب اقتصاص المظالم بين الخلق يوم القيامة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Awsaṭ (5973), whose wording this is, and al-Bukhārī in al-Tārīkh al-Kabīr (2/228).","chapter_en":"Settling Wrongs between Created Beings on the Day of Resurrection","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":44,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Umāmah al-Bāhilī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The wrongdoer will come on the Day of Resurrection until, when he reaches a bridge over Hell between darkness and rugged terrain, the one he wronged will meet him. The wronged person will recognize him and recognize the wrong he committed against him. Those who were wronged will continue taking their due from those who wronged them until all the good deeds in their hands have been taken away.","If they have no good deeds, then sins equal to the amount of their wrongdoing will be placed upon them, until they are brought to the lowest depth of the Fire.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"الطبرانی/الاوسط","label":"الطبراني في الأوسط","number":5973},{"key":"bukhari/التاریخ_الکبیر","label":"البخاري في التاريخ الكبير","number":228},{"key":"sh28171","label":"المعجم الأوسط للطبراني","number":5976,"n":5963}]},{"num":16225,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة، عن النبي ﷺ قال:","((من ضرب ضربًا ظلمًا اقتص منه يوم القيامة))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه البخاري في الأدب المفرد (١٨٦) والبزار (٩٥٣٥).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب اقتصاص المظالم بين الخلق يوم القيامة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Adab al-Mufrad (186) and al-Bazzār (9535).","chapter_en":"Settling Wrongs between Created Beings on the Day of Resurrection","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":44,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever strikes another person unjustly will have retaliation exacted from him on the Day of Resurrection.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari/الادب_المفرد","label":"البخاري في الأدب المفرد","number":186},{"key":"البزار","label":"البزار","number":9535},{"key":"adab","label":"الأدب المفرد","number":186,"n":186}]},{"num":16226,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة، أن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال:","((لتؤدن الحقوق إلى أهلها يوم القيامة، حتى يقاد للشاة الجلحاء من الشاة القرناء))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٢٥٨٢).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب اقتصاص المظالم بين الخلق يوم القيامة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2582).","chapter_en":"Settling Wrongs between Created Beings on the Day of Resurrection","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":44,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Rights will certainly be restored to those entitled to them on the Day of Resurrection, to the extent that retaliation will be taken for the hornless sheep from the horned sheep.”"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["ورواه أحمد (٨٧٥٦) من طريق آخر نحوه، وزاد فيه:","((وحتى للذرة من الذرة))."],"en":["Aḥmad (8756) narrated a similar report through another chain and added:","“Even for one tiny ant from another tiny ant.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2582}]},{"num":16227,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي ذر، أن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ كان جالسًا، وشاتان تعتلفان، فنطحت إحداهما الأخرى، فأجهضتها، قال: فضحك رسول اللّٰه ﷺ، فقيل له: ما يضحكك يا رسول اللّٰه؟ قال:","((عجبت لها، والذي نفسي بيده، ليقادن لها يوم القيامة))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه عبدالله بن أحمد في مسند أبيه (٢١٥١١).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب اقتصاص المظالم بين الخلق يوم القيامة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad in his father’s Musnad (21511).","chapter_en":"Settling Wrongs between Created Beings on the Day of Resurrection","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":44,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Dharr narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting while two sheep were feeding. One of them butted the other and caused it to miscarry. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed. He was asked: “What makes you laugh, O Messenger of Allah?” He replied: “I am amazed at it. By the One in whose hand is my soul, retaliation will certainly be taken for it on the Day of Resurrection.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"عبداللہ_بن_احمد/مسند_ابیہ","label":"عبدالله بن أحمد في مسند أبيه","number":21511}]},{"num":16228,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة، عن النبي ﷺ قال:","((كلمتان خفيفتان على اللسان، ثقيلتان في الميزان، حبيبتان إلى الرحمن: سبحان اللّٰه وبحمده، سبحان اللّٰه العظيم))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٦٤٠٦)، ومسلم (٢٦٩٤).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في الميزان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6406) and Muslim (2694).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Scale","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":45,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Two phrases are light upon the tongue, heavy in the Scale, and beloved to the Most Merciful: ‘Glory and praise be to Allah; glory be to Allah, the Magnificent.’”"]},"intro":{"ar":["قال تعالى:","﴿وَنَضَعُ الْمَوَازِينَ الْقِسْطَ لِيَوْمِ الْقِيَامَةِ فَلَا تُظْلَمُ نَفْسٌ شَيْئًا وَإِنْ كَانَ مِثْقَالَ حَبَّةٍ مِنْ خَرْدَلٍ أَتَيْنَا بِهَا وَكَفَىٰ بِنَا حَاسِبِينَ﴾ [سورة الأنبياء: ٤٧].","وقال تعالى:","﴿وَالْوَزْنُ يَوْمَئِذٍ الْحَقُّ فَمَنْ ثَقُلَتْ مَوَازِينُهُ فَأُولَٰئِكَ هُمُ الْمُفْلِحُونَ ۝ وَمَنْ خَفَّتْ مَوَازِينُهُ فَأُولَٰئِكَ الَّذِينَ خَسِرُوا أَنْفُسَهُمْ بِمَا كَانُوا بِآيَاتِنَا يَظْلِمُونَ﴾ [سورة الأعراف: ٨-٩].","وقال تعالى:","﴿فَأَمَّا مَنْ ثَقُلَتْ مَوَازِينُهُ ۝ فَهُوَ فِي عِيشَةٍ رَاضِيَةٍ ۝ وَأَمَّا مَنْ خَفَّتْ مَوَازِينُهُ ۝ فَأُمُّهُ هَاوِيَةٌ ۝ وَمَا أَدْرَاكَ مَا هِيَهْ ۝ نَارٌ حَامِيَةٌ﴾ [سورة القارعة: ٦-١١]."],"en":["Allah, the Exalted, says:","“We will set up the scales of justice for the Day of Resurrection, so no soul will be wronged in the least. Even if a deed is the weight of a mustard seed, We will bring it forth. And sufficient are We as Reckoners.”","[al-Anbiyāʾ 21:47]","And He, the Exalted, says:","“The weighing on that Day will be the truth. Those whose scales are heavy—it is they who will be successful. And those whose scales are light—it is they who will have lost themselves because they used to wrongfully reject Our signs.”","[al-Aʿrāf 7:8-9]","And He, the Exalted, says:","“As for the one whose scales are heavy, he will be in a pleasant life. But as for the one whose scales are light, his refuge will be the Abyss. And what can make you know what it is? A blazing Fire.”","[al-Qāriʿah 101:6-11]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6406},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2694}]},{"num":16229,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي مالك الأشعري قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((الطهور شطر الإيمان، والحمد لله تملأ الميزان، وسبحان اللّٰه والحمد لله تملآن - أو تملأ - ما بين السماوات والأرض…)).","الحديث."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٢٢٣).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في الميزان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (223).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Scale","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":45,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Mālik al-Ashʿarī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Purification is half of faith. ‘Al-ḥamdu lillāh’ fills the Scale, and ‘subḥān Allah’ and ‘al-ḥamdu lillāh’ fill—or one of them fills—what is between the heavens and the earth…” The hadith continues."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":223}]},{"num":16230,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة قال: قال النبي ﷺ:","((من احتبس فرسًا في سبيل اللّٰه إيمانًا بالله، وتصديقًا بوعده؛ فإن شبعه وريه، وروثه وبوله في ميزانه يوم القيامة))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (٢٨٥٣).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في الميزان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (2853).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Scale","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":45,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever keeps a horse for the sake of Allah, out of faith in Allah and belief in His promise, then its food, drink, dung, and urine will all be placed in his Scale on the Day of Resurrection.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":2853}]},{"num":16231,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبدالله بن عمرو بن العاص قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((إنّ اللّٰه سيخلّص رجلًا من أمتي على رؤوس الخلائق يوم القيامة، فينشر عليه تسعة وتسعين سجلًا، كل سجل مثل مدّ البصر، ثم يقول: أتنكر من هذا شيئًا؟ أظلمك كتبتي الحافظون؟ فيقول: لا يا رب. فيقول: أفلك عذر؟ فيقول: لا يا رب. فيقول: بلى، إن لك عندنا حسنة، فإنه لا ظلم عليك اليوم، فتخرج بطاقة فيها: أشهد أن لا إله إلا الله، وأشهد أن محمدًا عبده ورسوله. فيقول: احضر وزنك. فيقول: يا رب، ما هذه البطاقة مع هذه السجلات؟ فقال: إنك لا تظلم، قال: فتوضع السجلات في كفة، والبطاقة في كفة، فطاشت السجلات وثقلت البطاقة، فلا يثقل مع اسم اللّٰه شيء))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الترمذي (٢٦٣٩) - واللفظ له -، وابن ماجه (٤٣٠٠).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في الميزان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (2639), whose wording this is, and Ibn Mājah (4300).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Scale","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":45,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah will single out a man from my Ummah before all creation on the Day of Resurrection. Ninety-nine records will be spread out before him, each record extending as far as the eye can see. Then Allah will say: ‘Do you deny anything in these? Have My recording angels wronged you?’ He will reply: ‘No, my Lord.’ Allah will ask: ‘Do you have any excuse?’ He will reply: ‘No, my Lord.’","Allah will say: ‘Rather, you have one good deed with Us, and there will be no injustice against you today.’ Then a card will be brought out upon which is written: ‘I testify that there is no deity except Allah, and I testify that Muḥammad is His servant and Messenger.’ Allah will say: ‘Come and witness your weighing.’ The man will say: ‘My Lord, what is this card compared with all these records?’ He will say: ‘You will not be wronged.’ The records will then be placed on one side of the Scale and the card on the other. The records will become light and the card will outweigh them, for nothing can outweigh the Name of Allah.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"tirmidhi","label":"الترمذي","number":2639},{"key":"ibnmajah","label":"ابن ماجه","number":4300}]},{"num":16232,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن ابن مسعود أنه كان يجتني سواكًا من الأراك، وكان دقيق الساقين، فجعلت الريح تكفؤه، فضحك القوم منه، فقال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((مم تضحكون؟)).","قالوا: يا نبي اللّٰه، من دقة ساقيه، فقال:","((والذي نفسي بيده لهما أثقل في الميزان من أحد))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (٣٩٩١) وأبو يعلى (٥٣١٠) والبزار - كشف الأستار - (٢٦٧٨) والطبراني في الكبير (٨٤٥٢) كلهم من طريق عاصم، عن زر بن حبيش، عن ابن مسعود فذكره. وصححه ابن حبان (٧٠٦٩) فرواه من هذا الوجه.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في الميزان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (3991), Abū Yaʿlā (5310), al-Bazzār in Kashf al-Astār (2678), and al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Kabīr (8452), all through ʿĀṣim, from Zirr ibn Ḥubaysh, from Ibn Masʿūd. Ibn Ḥibbān authenticated it (7069) through this route.","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Scale","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":45,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn Masʿūd was gathering siwāk sticks from an arāk tree. His legs were very thin, and the wind began causing him to sway. The people laughed at him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked: “What are you laughing at?” They replied: “O Prophet of Allah, at the thinness of his legs.” He said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, they are heavier in the Scale than Mount Uḥud.”"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["ومجموع هذه الأحاديث تدل على أن الذي يوزن في الميزان يوم القيامة هو العمل والعامل وصحيفة عمله."],"en":["Taken together, these hadiths indicate that what will be weighed in the Scale on the Day of Resurrection includes the deed, the person who performed it, and the record of his deeds."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ابو_یعلی","label":"أبو يعلى","number":5310},{"key":"البزار_کشف_الاستار","label":"البزار - كشف الأستار -","number":2678},{"key":"الطبرانی/الکبیر","label":"الطبراني في الكبير","number":8452},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":3991,"n":3991}]},{"num":16233,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة، عن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال:","((إنه ليأتي الرجل العظيم السمين يوم القيامة، لا يزن عند اللّٰه جناح بعوضة)).","وقال: اقرؤوا:","﴿فَلَا نُقِيمُ لَهُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ وَزْنًا﴾ [الكهف: ١٠٥]."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٤٧٢٩)، ومسلم (٢٧٨٥).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب لا يقيم الله للكافر وزنًا يوم القيامة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4729) and Muslim (2785).","chapter_en":"Allah Will Assign No Weight to the Disbeliever on the Day of Resurrection","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":46,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A huge, corpulent man will come on the Day of Resurrection, yet with Allah he will not weigh as much as the wing of a mosquito.” Then he said: “Recite: ‘We will assign no weight to them on the Day of Resurrection.’ [al-Kahf 18:105]”"]},"intro":{"ar":["قال تعالى:","﴿قُلْ هَلْ نُنَبِّئُكُمْ بِالْأَخْسَرِينَ أَعْمَالًا ۝ الَّذِينَ ضَلَّ سَعْيُهُمْ فِي الْحَيَاةِ الدُّنْيَا وَهُمْ يَحْسَبُونَ أَنَّهُمْ يُحْسِنُونَ صُنْعًا ۝ أُولَٰئِكَ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا بِآيَاتِ رَبِّهِمْ وَلِقَائِهِ فَحَبِطَتْ أَعْمَالُهُمْ فَلَا نُقِيمُ لَهُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ وَزْنًا﴾ [سورة الكهف: ١٠٣-١٠٥]."],"en":["Allah, the Exalted, says:","“Say: Shall We inform you of those who are the greatest losers in their deeds? They are those whose efforts in the life of this world have gone astray while they thought they were doing good. Those are the ones who disbelieved in the signs of their Lord and in meeting Him, so their deeds became worthless, and We will assign no weight to them on the Day of Resurrection.”","[al-Kahf 18:103-105]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":4729},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2785}]},{"num":16234,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبد الله بن عمرو قال: قال النبي ﷺ:","((حوضي مسيرة شهر، ماؤه أبيض من اللبن، وريحه أطيب من المسك، وكيزانه كنجوم السماء، من شرب منها فلا يظمأ أبدًا)).","وفي لفظ:","((حوضي مسيرة شهر، وزواياه سواء، وماؤه أبيض من الورق)).","والباقي مثله."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٦٥٧٧) ومسلم (٢٢٩٢).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب في الحوض","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6577) and Muslim (2292).","chapter_en":"Concerning the Ḥawḍ","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":47,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “My Ḥawḍ is a month’s journey in length. Its water is whiter than milk, its fragrance is more pleasant than musk, and its drinking vessels are like the stars of the sky. Whoever drinks from it will never thirst again.”","In another wording: “My Ḥawḍ is a month’s journey, its sides are equal, and its water is whiter than silver.” The remainder is similar."]},"intro":{"ar":["قال تعالى:","﴿إِنَّا أَعْطَيْنَاكَ الْكَوْثَرَ﴾ [الكوثر: ١]."],"en":["Allah, the Exalted, says:","“Indeed, We have granted you al-Kawthar.”","[al-Kawthar 108:1]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6577},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2292}]},{"num":16235,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي ذر قال: قلت: يا رسول الله، ما آنية الحوض؟ قال:","((والذي نفس محمد بيده لآنيته أكثر من عدد نجوم السماء وكواكبها، ألا في الليلة المظلمة المصحية، آنية الجنة، من شرب منها لم يظمأ آخر ما عليه، يشخب فيه ميزابان من الجنة، من شرب منه لم يظمأ، عرضه مثل طوله، ما بين عمان إلى أيلة، ماؤه أشد بياضًا من اللبن، وأحلى من العسل))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٢٣٠٠).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب في الحوض","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2300).","chapter_en":"Concerning the Ḥawḍ","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":47,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Dharr narrated: I asked: “O Messenger of Allah, what are the vessels of the Ḥawḍ like?” He replied: “By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muḥammad, its vessels are more numerous than the stars and planets of the sky on a dark, clear night. They are vessels from Paradise. Whoever drinks from them will never thirst again. Two channels from Paradise pour into it. Whoever drinks from it will never thirst. Its width is equal to its length, extending from ʿAmmān to Aylah. Its water is whiter than milk and sweeter than honey.”"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["قوله: ((ألا في الليلة المظلمة المصحية)) تخفيف وهي للاستفتاح، وخص الليلة المظلمة؛ لأن النجوم ترى فيها أكثر، والمراد بالمظلمة: التي لا قمر فيها مع أن النجوم طالعة، فإن وجود القمر يستر كثيرًا من النجوم.","وقوله: ((يشخب فيه ميزابان)) الشخب: السيلان، وأصله ما يخرج من تحت يد الحالب عند كل غمزة وعصرة لضرع الشاة."],"en":["Regarding the phrase “on a dark, clear night,” the author explains that it introduces and emphasizes the description. A dark night is specifically mentioned because more stars can be seen when there is no moon, since moonlight obscures many stars.","Regarding the phrase “two channels pour into it,” shakhb means flowing or streaming. Its original usage refers to the stream of milk that comes from an animal’s udder each time it is squeezed during milking."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2300}]},{"num":16236,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أنس بن مالك، عن النبي ﷺ قال:","((بينما أنا أسير في الجنة، إذا أنا بنهر، حافتاه قباب الدر المجوف، قلت: ما هذا يا جبريل؟ قال: هذا الكوثر، الذي أعطاك ربك، فإذا طينه - أو طيبه - مسك أذفر))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (٦٥٨١).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب في الحوض","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6581).","chapter_en":"Concerning the Ḥawḍ","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":47,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “While I was walking in Paradise, I came upon a river whose banks were domes of hollow pearls. I asked: ‘What is this, O Jibrīl?’ He replied: ‘This is al-Kawthar, which your Lord has granted you.’ Its mud—or its fragrance—was intensely fragrant musk.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6581}]},{"num":16237,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة قال: قال النبي ﷺ:","((والذي نفسي بيده لأذودن رجالًا عن حوضي كما تذاد الغريبة من الإبل عن الحوض))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٢٣٦٧)، ومسلم (٢٣٠٢).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب في الحوض","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (2367) and Muslim (2302).","chapter_en":"Concerning the Ḥawḍ","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":47,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, I will certainly drive certain men away from my Ḥawḍ just as stray camels are driven away from a watering place.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":2367},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2302}]},{"num":16238,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة، أن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال:","((إن حوضي أبعد من أيلة من عدن، لهو أشد بياضًا من الثلج، وأحلى من العسل باللبن، ولآنيته أكثر من عدد النجوم، وإني لأصد الناس عنه كما يصد الرجل إبل الناس عن حوضه)).","قالوا: يا رسول الله، أتعرفنا يومئذ؟ قال:","((نعم، لكم سيما ليست لأحد من الأمم، تردون علي غرًا محجلين من أثر الوضوء)).","وفي رواية:","((ترد علي أمتي الحوض، وأنا أذود الناس عنه كما يذود الرجل إبل الرجل عن إبله)).","قالوا: يا نبي الله، أتعرفنا؟ قال:","((نعم، لكم سيما ليست لأحد غيركم. تردون علي غرًا محجلين من آثار الوضوء. وليصدن عني طائفة منكم فلا يصلون، فأقول: يا رب، هؤلاء من أصحابي، فيجيبني ملك فيقول: وهل تدري ما أحدثوا بعدك؟))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٢٤٧).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب في الحوض","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (247).","chapter_en":"Concerning the Ḥawḍ","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":47,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “My Ḥawḍ is farther in extent than the distance from Aylah to ʿAdan. It is whiter than snow and sweeter than honey mixed with milk. Its vessels are more numerous than the stars. I will keep people away from it just as a man keeps other people’s camels away from his own watering place.” They asked: “O Messenger of Allah, will you recognize us on that Day?” He replied: “Yes. You will have a distinguishing mark that no other nation has. You will come to me with radiant faces and limbs from the traces of wuḍūʾ.”","In another narration: “My Ummah will come to me at the Ḥawḍ, while I drive other people away from it just as a man drives another man’s camels away from his own camels.” They asked: “O Prophet of Allah, will you recognize us?” He replied: “Yes. You will have a distinguishing mark that no one else has. You will come to me with radiant faces and limbs from the traces of wuḍūʾ. Yet a group from among you will certainly be kept away from me and will not reach me. I will say: ‘My Lord, these are from my Companions.’","An angel will answer me: ‘Do you know what they introduced after you?’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":247}]},{"num":16239,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبدالله بن مسعود قال: قال النبي ﷺ:","((أنا فرطكم على الحوض، ليرفعن إلي رجال منكم، حتى إذا أهويت لأناولهم اختلجوا دوني، فأقول: أي رب أصحابي، يقول: لا تدري ما أحدثوا بعدك))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٧٠٤٩)، ومسلم (٢٢٩٧).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب في الحوض","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (7049) and Muslim (2297).","chapter_en":"Concerning the Ḥawḍ","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":47,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “I will precede you to the Ḥawḍ. Men from among you will be brought toward me, but when I reach out to give them water, they will be snatched away before reaching me. I will say: ‘My Lord, my Companions!’ He will say: ‘You do not know what they introduced after you.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":7049},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2297}]},{"num":16240,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن حذيفة، أن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال:","((ليردن على الحوض أقوام فيختلجون دوني فأقول: رب أصيحابي، رب أصيحابي، فيقال لي: إنك لا تدري ما أحدثوا بعدك))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٢٢٩٧) وأحمد (٢٣٢٩٠).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب في الحوض","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2297) and Aḥmad (23290).","chapter_en":"Concerning the Ḥawḍ","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":47,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ḥudhayfah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Certain people will come to the Ḥawḍ but will be snatched away before reaching me. I will say: ‘My Lord, my Companions! My Lord, my Companions!’ It will be said to me: ‘You do not know what they introduced after you.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2297},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":23290,"n":23290}]},{"num":16241,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي حازم قال: سمعت سهل بن سعد يقول: سمعت النبي ﷺ يقول:","((أنا فرطكم على الحوض، من ورد شرب منه، ومن شرب منه لم يظمأ بعده أبدًا، ليرد علي أقوام أعرفهم ويعرفوني، ثم يحال بيني وبينهم)).","قال أبو حازم: فسمعني النعمان بن أبي عياش، وأنا أحدثهم هذا، فقال: هكذا سمعت سهلًا؟ فقلت: نعم، قال: وأنا أشهد على أبي سعيد الخدري لسمعته يزيد فيه، قال:","((إنهم مني، فيقال: إنك لا تدري ما بدلوا بعدك، فأقول: سحقًا سحقًا لمن بدل بعدي))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٧٠٥١ ،٧٠٥٠)، ومسلم (٢٢٩٠).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب في الحوض","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (7051, 7050) and Muslim (2290).","chapter_en":"Concerning the Ḥawḍ","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":47,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Ḥāzim narrated: I heard Sahl ibn Saʿd say: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “I will precede you to the Ḥawḍ. Whoever comes to it will drink from it, and whoever drinks from it will never thirst again. Certain people whom I recognize and who recognize me will come to me, but then a barrier will be placed between me and them.” Abū Ḥāzim said: Al-Nuʿmān ibn Abī ʿAyyāsh heard me narrating this and asked: “Is this how you heard Sahl narrate it?”","I replied: “Yes.” He said: “And I testify that I heard Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī add to it that the Prophet ﷺ said: ‘They are from me.’ Then it will be said: ‘You do not know what they changed after you.’ So I will say: ‘Away with them! Away with those who changed after me!’”"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["فوائد هذا الباب","١- الحوض هو المكان الذي يجتمع فيه الماء، وهذا الماء مصدره نهر الجنة، كما جاء في صحيح مسلم (٤٠٠) عن أنس قال:","بينا رسول اللّٰه ﷺ ذات يوم بين أظهرنا إذ أغفى إغفاءة، ثم رفع رأسه مبتسمًا، فقلنا: ما أضحكك يا رسول الله؟ قال:","((أنزلت علي آنفًا سورة)).","فقرأ:","﴿إِنَّا أَعْطَيْنَاكَ الْكَوْثَرَ ۝ فَصَلِّ لِرَبِّكَ وَانْحَرْ ۝ إِنَّ شَانِئَكَ هُوَ الْأَبْتَرُ﴾.","ثم قال:","((أتدرون ما الكوثر؟)).","فقلنا: اللّٰه ورسوله أعلم. قال:","((فإنه نهر وعدنيه ربي عز وجل، عليه خير كثير، هو حوض ترد عليه أمتي يوم القيامة، آنيته عدد النجوم، فيختلج العبد منهم، فأقول: رب إنه من أمتي. فيقول: ما تدري ما أحدث بعدك)).","٢- إخبار من النبي ﷺ بأن الردة تقع بعده، وقد وقعت بعد موت النبي ﷺ، فيقال: ما من مسجد غير مسجد مكة والمدينة إلا وقع فيه الردة.","٣- حديث الحوض متواتر، ومن جملة إيمان أهل السنة الإيمان بالحوض.","٤- عظم قدر الحوض:","أ- مسيرة شهر.","ب- بين صنعاء والمدينة.","ج- بين جرباء وأذرح، قريتان في الشام.","د- بين المدينة وعمان.","هـ- بين أيلة والجحفة.","وغيرها.","وهذا ليس فيه اضطراب، بل خاطب النبي ﷺ في أوقات مختلفة، وروت كل طائفة بما كانت تعرف من مسافات بين البلدان.","٥- وفيه معجزة النبي ﷺ أنه ذكر هذه المدن، مع أنه لم يزرها ولم يرها."],"en":["Benefits and Lessons from This Chapter","The Ḥawḍ is the place in which water gathers, and its water comes from a river of Paradise.","As narrated in Ṣaḥīḥ Muslim (400), Anas said:","One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was among us when he dozed briefly. Then he raised his head smiling.","We asked:","“What made you smile, O Messenger of Allah?”","He replied:","“A sūrah was just revealed to me.”","Then he recited:","“Indeed, We have granted you al-Kawthar. So pray to your Lord and sacrifice. Indeed, the one who hates you is the one cut off.”","Then he asked:","“Do you know what al-Kawthar is?”","We replied:","“Allah and His Messenger know best.”","He said:","“It is a river that my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, has promised me. It contains abundant good. It is a Ḥawḍ to which my Ummah will come on the Day of Resurrection. Its vessels are as numerous as the stars.","A servant from among them will be pulled away, and I will say: ‘My Lord, he is from my Ummah.’","He will say: ‘You do not know what he introduced after you.’”","The Prophet ﷺ informed that apostasy would occur after him, and it indeed occurred after the death of the Prophet ﷺ.","It is said that there was no mosque, apart from the mosques of Makkah and Madinah, in which apostasy did not occur.","The hadiths concerning the Ḥawḍ are mutawātir, and belief in the Ḥawḍ is part of the creed of Ahl al-Sunnah.","4 – The Vast Size of the Ḥawḍ","Its dimensions have been described as:","a journey of one month;","the distance between Ṣanʿāʾ and Madinah;","the distance between Jarbāʾ and Adhruḥ, two villages in al-Shām;","the distance between Madinah and ʿAmmān;","the distance between Aylah and al-Juḥfah;","and other descriptions.","There is no contradiction in these reports. Rather, the Prophet ﷺ spoke at different times, and each group of narrators transmitted comparisons using distances between places familiar to them.","Among the miracles of the Prophet ﷺ is that he mentioned these cities even though he had neither visited nor seen them."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":7051},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2290}]},{"num":16242,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جرير بن عبد اللّٰه قال: كنا جلوسًا عند النبي ﷺ إذ نظر إلى القمر ليلة البدر، قال:","((أما إنكم سترون ربكم كما ترون هذا القمر، لا تضامون في رؤيته، فإن استطعتم أن لا تغلبوا على صلاة قبل طلوع الشمس، وصلاة قبل غروب الشمس، فافعلوا))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٧٤٣٤)، ومسلم (٦٣٣).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب رؤية المؤمنين ربهم يوم القيامة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (7434) and Muslim (633).","chapter_en":"The Believers Will See Their Lord on the Day of Resurrection","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":48,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jarīr ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: We were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when he looked at the moon on the night of the full moon and said: “Indeed, you will see your Lord just as you see this moon, without crowding or difficulty in seeing Him. So if you are able not to be overcome in performing a prayer before sunrise and a prayer before sunset, then do so.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":7434},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":633}]},{"num":16243,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أنس، أن رجلًا قال: يا رسول اللّٰه كيف يحشر الكافر على وجهه يوم القيامة؟ قال:","((أليس الذي أمشاه على رجليه في الدنيا، قادرًا على أن يمشيه على وجهه يوم القيامة؟)).","قال قتادة: بلى، وعزة ربنا."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٦٥٢٣)، ومسلم (٢٨٠٦).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب يحشر الكافر إلى النار على وجهه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6523) and Muslim (2806).","chapter_en":"The Disbeliever Will Be Gathered to the Fire upon His Face","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":49,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas narrated: A man asked: “O Messenger of Allah, how will the disbeliever be gathered upon his face on the Day of Resurrection?” He replied: “Is not the One who made him walk upon his two feet in this world able to make him walk upon his face on the Day of Resurrection?” Qatādah said: “Yes, by the Might of our Lord.”"]},"intro":{"ar":["قال تعالى:","﴿الَّذِينَ يُحْشَرُونَ عَلَىٰ وُجُوهِهِمْ إِلَىٰ جَهَنَّمَ أُولَٰئِكَ شَرٌّ مَكَانًا وَأَضَلُّ سَبِيلًا﴾ [سورة الفرقان: ٣٤]."],"en":["Allah, the Exalted, says:","“Those who will be gathered upon their faces toward Hell—those are in the worst place and are furthest astray from the path.”","[al-Furqān 25:34]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6523},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2806}]},{"num":16244,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عائشة قالت: سألت رسول اللّٰه ﷺ عن قوله عز وجل:","﴿يَوْمَ تُبَدَّلُ الْأَرْضُ غَيْرَ الْأَرْضِ وَالسَّمَاوَاتُ﴾ [إبراهيم: ٤٨]","فأين يكون الناس يومئذ يا رسول الله؟ فقال:","((على الصراط))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٢٧٩١).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب المرور على الصراط يوم القيامة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2791).","chapter_en":"Crossing the Ṣirāṭ on the Day of Resurrection","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":50,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀ’ishah narrated: I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ concerning the statement of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: “On the Day the earth will be replaced by another earth, and the heavens as well.” [Ibrāhīm 14:48] I asked: “Where will the people be at that time, O Messenger of Allah?” He replied: “Upon the Ṣirāṭ.”"]},"intro":{"ar":["قال تعالى:","﴿يَوْمَ تَرَى الْمُؤْمِنِينَ وَالْمُؤْمِنَاتِ يَسْعَىٰ نُورُهُمْ بَيْنَ أَيْدِيهِمْ وَبِأَيْمَانِهِمْ بُشْرَاكُمُ الْيَوْمَ جَنَّاتٌ تَجْرِي مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْأَنْهَارُ خَالِدِينَ فِيهَا ذَٰلِكَ هُوَ الْفَوْزُ الْعَظِيمُ ۝ يَوْمَ يَقُولُ الْمُنَافِقُونَ وَالْمُنَافِقَاتُ لِلَّذِينَ آمَنُوا انْظُرُونَا نَقْتَبِسْ مِنْ نُورِكُمْ قِيلَ ارْجِعُوا وَرَاءَكُمْ فَالْتَمِسُوا نُورًا فَضُرِبَ بَيْنَهُمْ بِسُورٍ لَهُ بَابٌ بَاطِنُهُ فِيهِ الرَّحْمَةُ وَظَاهِرُهُ مِنْ قِبَلِهِ الْعَذَابُ ۝ يُنَادُونَهُمْ أَلَمْ نَكُنْ مَعَكُمْ قَالُوا بَلَىٰ وَلَٰكِنَّكُمْ فَتَنْتُمْ أَنْفُسَكُمْ وَتَرَبَّصْتُمْ وَارْتَبْتُمْ وَغَرَّتْكُمُ الْأَمَانِيُّ حَتَّىٰ جَاءَ أَمْرُ اللَّهِ وَغَرَّكُمْ بِاللَّهِ الْغَرُورُ ۝ فَالْيَوْمَ لَا يُؤْخَذُ مِنْكُمْ فِدْيَةٌ وَلَا مِنَ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا مَأْوَاكُمُ النَّارُ هِيَ مَوْلَاكُمْ وَبِئْسَ الْمَصِيرُ﴾ [سورة الحديد: ١٢-١٥].","وقال تعالى:","﴿يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا تُوبُوا إِلَى اللَّهِ تَوْبَةً نَصُوحًا عَسَىٰ رَبُّكُمْ أَنْ يُكَفِّرَ عَنْكُمْ سَيِّئَاتِكُمْ وَيُدْخِلَكُمْ جَنَّاتٍ تَجْرِي مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْأَنْهَارُ يَوْمَ لَا يُخْزِي اللَّهُ النَّبِيَّ وَالَّذِينَ آمَنُوا مَعَهُ نُورُهُمْ يَسْعَىٰ بَيْنَ أَيْدِيهِمْ وَبِأَيْمَانِهِمْ يَقُولُونَ رَبَّنَا أَتْمِمْ لَنَا نُورَنَا وَاغْفِرْ لَنَا إِنَّكَ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرٌ﴾ [التحريم: ٨]."],"en":["Allah, the Exalted, says:","“On the Day you will see the believing men and believing women, their light proceeding before them and on their right: ‘Glad tidings for you today—Gardens beneath which rivers flow, remaining therein forever. That is the tremendous success.’","On that Day the hypocrite men and hypocrite women will say to those who believed: ‘Wait for us so that we may take some of your light.’ It will be said: ‘Go back behind you and seek light.’ Then a wall containing a gate will be placed between them. Inside it will be mercy, while outside it will be punishment.","They will call to them: ‘Were we not with you?’ They will reply: ʿYes, but you put yourselves into temptation, waited, doubted, and false hopes deceived you until the command of Allah came, and the deceiver deceived you concerning Allah.","So today no ransom will be accepted from you or from those who disbelieved. Your refuge is the Fire. It is your proper abode, and what a wretched destination.’”","[al-Ḥadīd 57:12-15]","And He, the Exalted, says:","“O you who believe, turn to Allah in sincere repentance. Perhaps your Lord will remove your sins from you and admit you into Gardens beneath which rivers flow, on the Day when Allah will not disgrace the Prophet and those who believed with him. Their light will proceed before them and on their right. They will say: ‘Our Lord, perfect our light for us and forgive us. Indeed, You are capable of all things.’”","[al-Taḥrīm 66:8]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2791}]},{"num":16245,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي سعيد الخدري، أن ناسًا في زمن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قالوا: يا رسول الله! هل نرى ربنا يوم القيامة؟ قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((نعم)).","في حديث طويل، وجاء فيه:","((ثم يضرب الجسر على جهنم، وتحل الشفاعة، ويقولون: اللهم سلم سلم)).","قيل: يا رسول الله، وما الجسر؟ قال:","((دحض مزلة، فيه خطاطيف وكلاليب وحسك تكون بنجد فيها شويكة يقال لها: السعدان، فيمر المؤمنون كطرف العين، وكالبرق، وكالريح، وكالطير، وكأجاويد الخيل والركاب، فناج مسلم، ومخدوش مرسل، ومكدوس في نار جهنم. حتى إذا خلص المؤمنون من النار، فوالذي نفسي بيده ما منكم من أحد بأشد مناشدة لله في استقصاء الحق من المؤمنين لله يوم القيامة لإخوانهم الذين في النار))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٤٥٨١)، ومسلم (١٨٣)، واللفظ لمسلم.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب المرور على الصراط يوم القيامة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4581) and Muslim (183). The wording is Muslim’s.","chapter_en":"Crossing the Ṣirāṭ on the Day of Resurrection","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":50,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated: Some people during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked: “O Messenger of Allah, will we see our Lord on the Day of Resurrection?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “Yes.” In the lengthy hadith, he said: “Then the bridge will be placed over Hell, and intercession will be permitted. They will say: ‘O Allah, grant safety! Grant safety!’” It was asked: “O Messenger of Allah, what is the bridge?” He replied: “It is slippery and causes feet to slip. Upon it are hooks, grappling irons, and thorns like the thorny plant found in Najd called al-Saʿdān.","The believers will cross like the blink of an eye, like lightning, like the wind, like birds, and like the finest horses and riding animals. Some will cross safely and unharmed, some will be scratched but released, and some will be thrown into the Fire of Hell. When the believers have been delivered from the Fire, then by the One in whose hand is my soul, none of you will plead more intensely with Allah for the complete restoration of a right than the believers will plead with Allah on the Day of Resurrection for their brothers who are in the Fire.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":4581},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":183}]},{"num":16246,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة وحذيفة في حديث الشفاعة الطويل:","((فيأتون محمدًا ﷺ فيقوم فيؤذن له، وترسل الأمانة والرحم، فتقومان جنبتي الصراط يمينًا وشمالًا، فيمر أولكم كالبرق)).","قال: قلت: بأبي أنت وأمي أي شيء كمر البرق؟ قال:","((ألم تروا إلى البرق كيف يمر ويرجع في طرفة عين؟ ثم كمر الريح، ثم كمر الطير وشد الرجال، تجري بهم أعمالهم، ونبيكم قائم على الصراط يقول: رب سلم سلم، حتى تعجز أعمال العباد، حتى يجيء الرجل فلا يستطيع السير إلا زحفًا)).","قال:","((وفي حافتي الصراط كلاليب معلقة مأمورة بأخذ من أمرت به، فمخدوش ناج، ومكدوس في النار)).","والذي نفس أبي هريرة بيده، إن قعر جهنم لسبعون خريفًا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (١٩٥).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب المرور على الصراط يوم القيامة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (195).","chapter_en":"Crossing the Ṣirāṭ on the Day of Resurrection","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":50,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah and Ḥudhayfah narrated in the lengthy hadith of intercession: “They will come to Muḥammad ﷺ, and he will stand, and permission will be granted to him. Then the Trust and the ties of kinship will be sent forth, and they will stand on the two sides of the Ṣirāṭ, one on the right and one on the left. The first of you will pass over it like lightning.” The narrator said: I asked: “May my father and mother be sacrificed for you—what is passing like lightning?”","He replied: “Have you not seen how lightning passes and returns in the blink of an eye? Then some will pass like the wind, then like birds, and then like men running swiftly. Their deeds will carry them along. Your Prophet will stand upon the Ṣirāṭ saying: ‘My Lord, grant safety! Grant safety!’ This will continue until the deeds of the servants become too weak to carry them swiftly, until a man comes who can only move by crawling.” He continued: “On the two sides of the Ṣirāṭ are suspended hooks commanded to seize those whom they are commanded to seize. Some will be scratched but saved, while others will be piled into the Fire.”","By the One in whose hand is the soul of Abū Hurayrah, the depth of Hell is a journey of seventy years."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":195}]},{"num":16247,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن ابن مسعود أن رسول الله ﷺ قال:","((آخر من يدخل الجنة رجل، فهو يمشي مرة ويكبو مرة، وتسفعه النار مرة، فإذا ما جاوزها التفت إليها، فقال: تبارك الذي نجاني منك، لقد أعطاني اللّٰه شيئًا ما أعطاه أحدًا من الأولين والآخرين…)).","الحديث."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (١٨٧).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب المرور على الصراط يوم القيامة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (187).","chapter_en":"Crossing the Ṣirāṭ on the Day of Resurrection","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":50,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn Masʿūd narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The last person to enter Paradise will be a man who walks at one time, stumbles at another, and is scorched by the Fire at another. When he finally passes beyond it, he will turn toward it and say: ‘Blessed is the One who saved me from you! Allah has given me something that He has not given anyone among the first or the last…’” The hadith continues."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":187}]},{"num":16248,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي أسماء: أنه دخل على أبي ذر، وهو بالربذة، وعنده امرأة سوداء مشبعة ليس عليها أثر المجاسد والخلوق، قال: فقال: ألا تنظرون إلى ما تأمرني به هذه السويداء؟ تأمرني أن آتي العراق، فإذا أتيت العراق مالوا علي بدنياهم، وإن النبي ﷺ، خليلي، عهد إلي أن دون جسر جهنم طريقًا ذا دحض ومزلة، وإنا نأتي عليه وفي أحمالنا اقتدار - وحدث مطر أيضًا بالحديث أجمع، في قول أحدهما: أن نأتي عليه وفي أحمالنا اقتدار. وقال الآخران: نأتي عليه وفي أحمالنا اضطمار - أحرى أن ننجو من أن نأتي عليه ونحن مواقير."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (٢١٤١٦) والحارث بن أبي أسامة كما في بغية الباحث (١٠٨٧).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب المرور على الصراط يوم القيامة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (21416) and al-Ḥārith ibn Abī Usāmah, as cited in Bughyat al-Bāḥith (1087).","chapter_en":"Crossing the Ṣirāṭ on the Day of Resurrection","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":50,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Asmāʾ narrated: He entered upon Abū Dharr while he was at al-Rabadhah. With him was a dark-skinned woman who was not adorned and bore no traces of perfume or cosmetic coloring. Abū Dharr said: “Do you not see what this woman is telling me to do? She tells me to go to Iraq. But if I go to Iraq, they will incline toward me with their worldly possessions. The Prophet ﷺ, my close friend, entrusted me with the knowledge that before the bridge over Hell there is a path that is slippery and causes feet to slip.","For us to come to it while our burdens are light is more likely to save us than to come to it heavily laden.” Maṭar also narrated the complete report. In one wording: “That we come to it while we are able to carry our loads…” And in the other two versions: “That we come to it with our burdens reduced…” is more likely to lead to salvation than coming to it while heavily burdened."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"الحارث_بن_ابی_اسامہ_کما/بغیہ_الباحث","label":"الحارث بن أبي أسامة كما في بغية الباحث","number":1087},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":21416,"n":21416}]},{"num":16249,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي سعيد الخدري قال: سمعت رسول اللّٰه ﷺ يقول:","((يوضع الصراط بين ظهري جهنم، عليه حسك كحسك السعدان، ثم يستجيز الناس، فناج مسلم، ومجروح به، ثم ناج، ومحتبس به فمنكوس فيها…)).","الحديث بطوله."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (١١٠٨١) واللفظ له، وابن خزيمة في التوحيد (٦٤٨)، وابن ماجه (٤٢٨٠) مختصرًا، والحاكم (٥٨٥-٥٨٦/٤) - وصححه -.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب المرور على الصراط يوم القيامة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (11081), whose wording this is, Ibn Khuzaymah in al-Tawḥīd (648), Ibn Mājah (4280) in abbreviated form, and al-Ḥākim (4/585-586), who authenticated it.","chapter_en":"Crossing the Ṣirāṭ on the Day of Resurrection","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":50,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The Ṣirāṭ will be placed over Hell. Upon it are thorns like the thorns of al-Saʿdān. Then the people will attempt to cross. Some will be saved unharmed, some will be wounded by it and then saved, while others will be caught by it and overturned into the Fire…” The hadith continues at length."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ابن_خزیمہ/التوحید","label":"ابن خزيمة في التوحيد","number":648},{"key":"ibnmajah","label":"ابن ماجه","number":4280},{"key":"hakim","label":"الحاكم","number":585},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":11081,"n":11081}]},{"num":16250,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي بكرة، عن النبي ﷺ قال:","((يحمل الناس على الصراط يوم القيامة، فتقادع بهم جنبتا الصراط تقادع الفراش في النار. قال: فينجي الله برحمته من يشاء)).","الحديث."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (٢٠٤٤٠)، والبزار (٣٦٧١)، وابن أبي عاصم في السنة (٨٣٨).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب المرور على الصراط يوم القيامة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (20440), al-Bazzār (3671), and Ibn Abī ʿĀṣim in al-Sunnah (838).","chapter_en":"Crossing the Ṣirāṭ on the Day of Resurrection","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":50,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Bakrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The people will be brought onto the Ṣirāṭ on the Day of Resurrection, and the two sides of the Ṣirāṭ will cause them to fall one after another just as moths fall into a fire. Then Allah will save by His mercy whomever He wills.” The hadith continues."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"البزار","label":"البزار","number":3671},{"key":"ابن_ابی_عاصم/السنہ","label":"ابن أبي عاصم في السنة","number":838},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":20440,"n":20440},{"key":"sh12862","label":"كشف الأستار عن زوائد البزار","number":3467,"n":3468}]},{"num":16251,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي سعيد الخدري، أن ناسًا في زمن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قالوا: يا رسول الله! هل نرى ربنا يوم القيامة؟ قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((نعم)).","قال:","((هل تضارون في رؤية الشمس بالظهيرة صحوًا ليس معها سحاب؟ وهل تضارون في رؤية القمر ليلة البدر صحوًا ليس فيها سحاب؟)).","قالوا: لا يا رسول الله، قال:","((ما تضارون في رؤية اللّٰه تبارك وتعالى يوم القيامة إلا كما تضارون في رؤية أحدهما. إذا كان يوم القيامة آذن مؤذن ليتبع كل أمة ما كانت تعبد، فلا يبقى أحد كان يعبد غير الله سبحانه من الأصنام والأنصاب إلا يتساقطون في النار، حتى إذا لم يبق إلا من كان يعبد اللّٰه من بر وفاجر، وغبر أهل الكتاب، فيدعى اليهود، فيقال لهم: ما كنتم تعبدون؟ قالوا: كنا نعبد عزير ابن الله، فيقال: كذبتم، ما اتخذ اللّه من صاحبة ولا ولد، فماذا تبغون؟ قالوا: عطشنا يا ربنا، فاسقنا، فيشار إليهم: ألا تردون؟ فيحشرون إلى النار كأنها سراب يحطم بعضها بعضًا، فيتساقطون في النار، ثم يدعى النصارى، فيقال لهم: ما كنتم تعبدون؟ قالوا: كنا نعبد المسيح ابن الله، فيقال لهم: كذبتم ما اتخذ اللّٰه من صاحبة ولا ولد، فيقال لهم: ماذا تبغون؟ فيقولون: عطشنا يا ربنا، فاسقنا، قال: فيشار إليهم: ألا تردون؟ فيحشرون إلى جهنم كأنها سراب يحطم بعضها بعضًا، فيتساقطون في النار، حتى إذا لم يبق إلا من كان يعبد اللّٰه تعالى من بر وفاجر، أتاهم رب العالمين سبحانه وتعالى في أدنى صورة من التي رأوه فيها، قال: فما تنتظرون؟ تتبع كل أمة ما كانت تعبد، قالوا: يا ربنا، فارقنا الناس في الدنيا أفقر ما كنا إليهم، ولم نصاحبهم، فيقول: أنا ربكم، فيقولون: نعوذ بالله منك، لا نشرك بالله شيئًا، مرتين أو ثلاثًا، حتى إن بعضهم ليكاد أن ينقلب، فيقول: هل بينكم وبينه آية فتعرفونه بها؟ فيقولون: نعم، فيكشف عن ساق، فلا يبقى من كان يسجد لله من تلقاء نفسه إلا أذن اللّٰه له بالسجود، ولا يبقى من كان يسجد اتقاء ورياء إلا جعل اللّٰه ظهره طبقة واحدة، كلما أراد أن يسجد خر على قفاه، ثم يرفعون رؤوسهم وقد تحول في صورته التي رأوه فيها أول مرة، فقال: أنا ربكم، فيقولون: أنت ربنا. ثم يضرب الجسر على جهنم، وتحل الشفاعة، ويقولون: اللهم سلم، سلم)).","قيل: يا رسول الله، وما الجسر؟ قال:","((دحض مزلة، فيه خطاطيف وكلاليب وحسك تكون بنجد فيها شويكة يقال لها: السعدان، فيمر المؤمنون كطرف العين، وكالبرق، وكالريح، وكالطير، وكأجاويد الخيل والركاب، فناج مسلم، ومخدوش مرسل، ومكدوس في نار جهنم.","حتى إذا خلص المؤمنون من النار، فوالذي نفسي بيده، ما منكم من أحد بأشد مناشدة لله في استقصاء الحق من المؤمنين لله يوم القيامة لإخوانهم الذين في النار، يقولون: ربنا كانوا يصومون معنا ويصلون ويحجون، فيقال لهم: أخرجوا من عرفتم، فتحرم صورهم على النار، فيخرجون خلقًا كثيرًا قد أخذت النار إلى نصف ساقيه، وإلى ركبتيه، ثم يقولون: ربنا ما بقي فيها أحد ممن أمرتنا به، فيقول: ارجعوا فمن وجدتم في قلبه مثقال دينار من خير فأخرجوه، فيخرجون خلقًا كثيرًا، ثم يقولون: ربنا لم نذر فيها أحدًا ممن أمرتنا، ثم يقول: ارجعوا فمن وجدتم في قلبه مثقال نصف دينار من خير فأخرجوه، فيخرجون خلقًا كثيرًا، ثم يقولون: ربنا لم نذر فيها ممن أمرتنا أحدًا، ثم يقول: ارجعوا فمن وجدتم في قلبه مثقال ذرة من خير فأخرجوه، فيخرجون خلقًا كثيرًا ثم يقولون: ربنا لم نذر فيها خيرًا)).","وكان أبو سعيد الخدري يقول: إن لم تصدقوني بهذا الحديث فاقرؤوا إن شئتم:","﴿إِنَّ اللَّهَ لَا يَظْلِمُ مِثْقَالَ ذَرَّةٍ وَإِنْ تَكُ حَسَنَةً يُضَاعِفْهَا وَيُؤْتِ مِنْ لَدُنْهُ أَجْرًا عَظِيمًا﴾ [النساء: ٤٠].","((فيقول اللّٰه عز وجل: شفعت الملائكة، وشفع النبيون، وشفع المؤمنون، ولم يبق إلا أرحم الراحمين، فيقبض قبضة من النار، فيخرج منها قومًا لم يعملوا خيرًا قط قد عادوا حممًا، فيلقيهم في نهر في أفواه الجنة يقال له: نهر الحياة، فيخرجون كما تخرج الحبة في حميل السيل، ألا ترونها تكون إلى الحجر، أو إلى الشجر، ما يكون إلى الشمس أصيفر وأخيضر، وما يكون منها إلى الظل يكون أبيض؟)).","فقالوا: يا رسول الله، كأنك كنت ترعى بالبادية، قال:","((فيخرجون كاللؤلؤ في رقابهم الخواتم، يعرفهم أهل الجنة، هؤلاء عتقاء اللّٰه الذين أدخلهم اللّٰه الجنة بغير عمل عملوه، ولا خير قدموه، ثم يقول: ادخلوا الجنة فما رأيتموه فهو لكم، فيقولون: ربنا، أعطيتنا ما لم تعط أحدًا من العالمين، فيقول: لكم عندي أفضل من هذا، فيقولون: يا ربنا، أي شيء أفضل من هذا؟ فيقول: رضاي، فلا أسخط عليكم بعده أبدًا)).","وفي رواية بعد قوله: ((بغير عمل عملوه، ولا خير قدموه)):","((لكم ما رأيتم ومثله معه)).","وقال أبو سعيد: “بلغني أن الجسر أدق من الشعرة وأحد من السيف”."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٧٤٣٩)، ومسلم (١٨٣). واللفظ لمسلم.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب جامع في ذكر عدد من مشاهد يوم القيامة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (7439) and Muslim (183). The wording is Muslim’s.","chapter_en":"A Comprehensive Chapter Mentioning a Number of the Scenes of the Day of Resurrection","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":51,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated: Some people during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked: “O Messenger of Allah, will we see our Lord on the Day of Resurrection?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “Yes.” He then asked: “Do you have any difficulty seeing the sun at midday on a clear day when there are no clouds? And do you have any difficulty seeing the full moon on a clear night when there are no clouds?” They replied: “No, O Messenger of Allah.”","He said: “You will have no more difficulty seeing Allah, Blessed and Exalted, on the Day of Resurrection than you have seeing either of those. When the Day of Resurrection comes, a caller will announce that every nation should follow what it used to worship. No one who worshipped anything besides Allah—idols or objects of worship—will remain except that they will fall into the Fire. When none remain except those who worshipped Allah, both the righteous and the sinful, along with the remnants of the People of the Book, the Jews will be summoned.","They will be asked: ‘What did you worship?’ They will reply: ‘We used to worship ʿUzayr, the son of Allah.’ It will be said: ‘You have lied. Allah has taken neither a wife nor a son. What do you seek?’ They will say: ‘Our Lord, we are thirsty, so give us drink.’ They will be directed: ‘Will you not go to drink?’ Then they will be gathered toward the Fire, which will appear like a mirage, its parts crashing into one another, and they will fall into the Fire.","Then the Christians will be summoned. They will be asked: ‘What did you worship?’ They will say: ‘We used to worship the Messiah, the son of Allah.’ It will be said: ‘You have lied. Allah has taken neither a wife nor a son.’ They will be asked: ‘What do you seek?’ They will reply: ‘Our Lord, we are thirsty, so give us drink.’ They will be directed: ‘Will you not go to drink?’ Then they will be gathered toward Hell, which will appear like a mirage, its parts crashing into one another, and they will fall into the Fire.","When none remain except those who worshipped Allah, the righteous among them and the sinful, the Lord of the worlds, Glorified and Exalted, will come to them in a form less recognizable than the form in which they had seen Him before. He will say: ‘What are you waiting for? Every nation has followed what it used to worship.’ They will say: ‘Our Lord, we separated ourselves from the people in the world at the time when we were most in need of them, and we did not accompany them.’","He will say: ‘I am your Lord.’ They will say: ‘We seek refuge in Allah from you! We do not associate anything with Allah,’ repeating this two or three times, until some of them will almost turn back. He will ask: ‘Is there a sign between you and Him by which you will recognize Him?’ They will reply: ‘Yes.’ Then the Shin will be uncovered. Everyone who used to prostrate to Allah sincerely of his own accord will be permitted by Allah to prostrate. As for anyone who used to prostrate merely out of fear of people or to show off, Allah will make his back into a single rigid piece. Whenever he tries to prostrate, he will fall backward onto his neck.","Then they will raise their heads, and He will have returned to the form in which they had recognized Him the first time. He will say: ‘I am your Lord.’ They will say: ‘You are our Lord.’ Then the bridge will be placed over Hell, intercession will be permitted, and they will say: ‘O Allah, grant safety! Grant safety!’” It was asked: “O Messenger of Allah, what is the bridge?” He replied: “It is slippery and causes feet to slip. Upon it are hooks, grappling irons, and thorns like a thorny plant found in Najd called al-Saʿdān.","The believers will cross like the blink of an eye, like lightning, like the wind, like birds, and like the finest horses and riding animals. Some will pass safely and unharmed, some will be scratched but released, and some will be piled into the Fire of Hell. When the believers have been delivered from the Fire, then by the One in whose hand is my soul, none of you will plead with Allah more intensely for the full restoration of a right than the believers will plead with Allah on the Day of Resurrection on behalf of their brothers who are in the Fire.","They will say: ‘Our Lord, they used to fast with us, pray with us, and perform Ḥajj with us.’ It will be said to them: ‘Bring out those whom you recognize.’ Their forms will be made forbidden to the Fire. They will bring out a great many people, some of whom the Fire had reached halfway up their shins and others up to their knees. Then they will say: ‘Our Lord, no one remains therein from among those whom You commanded us to bring out.’ He will say: ‘Go back, and whoever you find in whose heart there is goodness equal to the weight of a dinar, bring him out.’","They will bring out a great many people. Then they will say: ‘Our Lord, we have not left therein anyone whom You commanded us to bring out.’ Then He will say: ‘Go back, and whoever you find in whose heart there is goodness equal to half a dinar, bring him out.’ They will bring out a great many people. Then they will say: ‘Our Lord, we have not left therein anyone whom You commanded us to bring out.’ Then He will say: ‘Go back, and whoever you find in whose heart there is goodness equal to the weight of an atom, bring him out.’","They will bring out a great many people, then say: ‘Our Lord, we have left no good therein.’” Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī used to say: “If you do not believe me concerning this hadith, then recite, if you wish: ‘Indeed, Allah does not wrong even by the weight of an atom. If there is a good deed, He multiplies it and gives from Himself a tremendous reward.’ [al-Nisāʾ 4:40]” Then the Prophet ﷺ continued: “Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will say: ‘The angels have interceded, the Prophets have interceded, and the believers have interceded. None remains except the Most Merciful of those who show mercy.’","Then He will take a handful from the Fire and bring out from it people who had never done any good whatsoever and who had become charred like coal. He will cast them into a river at the entrances of Paradise called the River of Life. They will emerge just as a seed sprouts in the silt carried by a flood. Have you not seen how such a seed grows beside a rock or tree—the portion exposed to the sun being yellowish and greenish, while the portion in the shade is white?”","They said: “O Messenger of Allah, it is as though you used to herd animals in the desert.” He continued: “They will emerge looking like pearls, with seals around their necks by which the people of Paradise will recognize them. These are those whom Allah has set free, whom Allah admitted into Paradise without any deed they had performed or any good they had sent ahead. Then He will say: ‘Enter Paradise. Whatever you see is yours.’ They will say: ‘Our Lord, You have given us what You have not given anyone among all creation.’","He will say: ‘I have something better than this for you.’ They will ask: ‘Our Lord, what could be better than this?’ He will say: ‘My pleasure. I will never be angry with you after this.’”","In another narration, after the words: “Without any deed they had performed or any good they had sent ahead,” it adds: “You will have whatever you see and an equal amount with it.” Abū Saʿīd said: “It has reached me that the bridge is finer than a hair and sharper than a sword.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":7439},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":183}]},{"num":16252,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عطاء بن يزيد الليثي، أن أبا هريرة أخبره، أن ناسًا قالوا لرسول اللّٰه ﷺ: يا رسول اللّه، هل نرى ربنا يوم القيامة؟ فقال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((هل تضارون في رؤية القمر ليلة البدر؟)).","قالوا: لا يا رسول الله. قال:","((هل تضارون في الشمس ليس دونها سحاب؟)).","قالوا: لا يا رسول الله. قال:","((فإنكم ترونه كذلك. يجمع الله الناس يوم القيامة، فيقول: من كان يعبد شيئًا فليتبعه، فيتبع من كان يعبد الشمس الشمس، ويتبع من كان يعبد القمر القمر، ويتبع من كان يعبد الطواغيت الطواغيت، وتبقى هذه الأمة فيها منافقوها، فيأتيهم الله تبارك وتعالى في صورة غير صورته التي يعرفون. فيقول: أنا ربكم، فيقولون: نعوذ بالله منك! هذا مكاننا حتى يأتينا ربنا، فإذا جاء ربنا عرفناه، فيأتيهم الله تعالى في صورته التي يعرفون فيقول: أنا ربكم. فيقولون: أنت ربنا، فيتبعونه.","ويضرب الصراط بين ظهري جهنم، فأكون أنا وأمتي أول من يجيز، ولا يتكلم يومئذ إلا الرسل، ودعوى الرسل يومئذ: اللهم سلم، سلم. وفي جهنم كلاليب مثل شوك السعدان، هل رأيتم سعدان؟)).","قالوا: نعم، يا رسول الله. قال:","((فإنها مثل شوك السعدان، غير أنه لا يعلم ما قدر عظمها إلا الله، تخطف الناس بأعمالهم. فمنهم المؤمن بقي بعمله، ومنهم المجازى حتى ينجى. حتى إذا فرغ الله من القضاء بين العباد، وأراد أن يخرج برحمته من أراد من أهل النار، أمر الملائكة أن يخرجوا من النار من كان لا يشرك بالله شيئًا ممن أراد الله تعالى أن يرحمه ممن يقول: لا إله إلا الله، فيعرفونهم في النار، يعرفونهم بأثر السجود، تأكل النار من ابن آدم إلا أثر السجود، حرم الله على النار أن تأكل أثر السجود، فيخرجون من النار قد امتحشوا، فيصب عليهم ماء الحياة فينبتون تحته كما تنبت الحبة في حميل السيل.","ثم يفرغ الله تعالى من القضاء بين العباد، ويبقى رجل مقبل بوجهه على النار - وهو آخر أهل الجنة دخولًا الجنة - فيقول: أي رب، اصرف وجهي عن النار، فإنه قد قشبني ريحها وأحرقني ذكاؤها. فيدعو الله ما شاء الله أن يدعوه، ثم يقول الله تبارك وتعالى: هل عسيت إن فعلت ذلك بك أن تسأل غيره؟ فيقول: لا أسألك غيره، ويعطي ربه من عهود ومواثيق ما شاء الله، فيصرف الله وجهه عن النار، فإذا أقبل على الجنة ورآها سكت ما شاء الله أن يسكت. ثم يقول: أي رب، قدمني إلى باب الجنة. فيقول الله له: أليس قد أعطيت عهودك ومواثيقك لا تسألني غير الذي أعطيتك؟ ويلك يا ابن آدم ما أغدرك! فيقول: أي رب، ويدعو الله حتى يقول له: فهل عسيت إن أعطيتك ذلك أن تسأل غيره؟ فيقول: لا وعزتك. فيعطي ربه ما شاء الله من عهود ومواثيق، فيقدمه إلى باب الجنة، فإذا قام على باب الجنة انفهقت له الجنة، فرأى ما فيها من الخير والسرور، فيسكت ما شاء الله أن يسكت، ثم يقول: أي رب، أدخلني الجنة. فيقول الله تبارك وتعالى له: أليس قد أعطيت عهودك ومواثيقك أن لا تسأل غير ما أعطيت؟! ويلك يا ابن آدم ما أغدرك! فيقول: أي رب، لا أكون أشقى خلقك، فلا يزال يدعو الله حتى يضحك الله تبارك وتعالى منه، فإذا ضحك الله منه قال: ادخل الجنة، فإذا دخلها قال الله له: تمنه، فيسأل ربه ويتمنى، حتى إن الله ليذكره من كذا وكذا، حتى إذا انقطعت به الأماني، قال الله تعالى: ذلك لك ومثله معه)).","قال عطاء بن يزيد: وأبو سعيد الخدري مع أبي هريرة لا يرد عليه من حديثه شيئًا، حتى إذا حدث أبو هريرة: ((إن الله قال لذلك الرجل: ومثله معه)). قال أبو سعيد: ((وعشرة أمثاله معه)) يا أبا هريرة. قال أبو هريرة: ما حفظت إلا قوله ذلك: ((ذلك لك ومثله معه)). قال أبو سعيد: أشهد أني حفظت من رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قوله ذلك: ((ذلك لك وعشرة أمثاله)). قال أبو هريرة: وذلك الرجل آخر أهل الجنة دخولًا الجنة."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٧٤٣٧)، ومسلم (١٨٢).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب جامع في ذكر عدد من مشاهد يوم القيامة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (7437) and Muslim (182).","chapter_en":"A Comprehensive Chapter Mentioning a Number of the Scenes of the Day of Resurrection","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":51,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yazīd al-Laythī narrated that Abū Hurayrah informed him that some people asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “O Messenger of Allah, will we see our Lord on the Day of Resurrection?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do you have any difficulty seeing the full moon?” They replied: “No, O Messenger of Allah.” He asked: “Do you have any difficulty seeing the sun when there is no cloud before it?” They replied: “No, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “You will see Him in the same way. Allah will gather the people on the Day of Resurrection and say: ‘Whoever used to worship something, let him follow it.’","Those who worshipped the sun will follow the sun, those who worshipped the moon will follow the moon, and those who worshipped false deities will follow those false deities. This Ummah will remain, including its hypocrites. Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will come to them in a form other than the form they recognize. He will say: ‘I am your Lord.’ They will say: ‘We seek refuge in Allah from you! We will remain here until our Lord comes to us. When our Lord comes, we will recognize Him.’","Then Allah, the Exalted, will come to them in the form they recognize and say: ‘I am your Lord.’ They will reply: ‘You are our Lord,’ and they will follow Him. Then the Ṣirāṭ will be placed across the middle of Hell. I and my Ummah will be the first to cross it. No one will speak on that Day except the Messengers, and the supplication of the Messengers on that Day will be: ‘O Allah, grant safety! Grant safety!’ In Hell there will be hooks like the thorns of al-Saʿdān. Have you seen al-Saʿdān?”","They replied: “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “They are like the thorns of al-Saʿdān, except that no one knows the enormity of their size except Allah. They will seize people according to their deeds. Among them will be the believer who remains safe because of his deeds, and among them will be one who is punished until he is eventually saved. When Allah has finished judging between the servants and wishes by His mercy to bring out from the Fire whomever He wills, He will command the angels to bring out of the Fire those whom He wishes to have mercy upon among those who did not associate anything with Allah and who used to say: ‘There is no deity except Allah.’","The angels will recognize them in the Fire by the marks of prostration. The Fire consumes every part of the son of Ādam except the marks of prostration; Allah has forbidden the Fire from consuming the marks of prostration. They will be brought out of the Fire completely charred, and the Water of Life will be poured over them. They will grow beneath it just as a seed grows in the silt carried by a flood. Then Allah, the Exalted, will finish judging between the servants, and one man will remain with his face turned toward the Fire. He will be the last of the people of Paradise to enter Paradise.","He will say: ‘My Lord, turn my face away from the Fire, for its wind has poisoned me and its blaze has burned me.’ He will continue supplicating to Allah for as long as Allah wills. Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will say: ‘If I do that for you, perhaps you will ask Me for something else?’ He will reply: ‘I will ask You for nothing else,’ and he will give his Lord whatever pledges and covenants Allah wills. So Allah will turn his face away from the Fire. When he faces Paradise and sees it, he will remain silent for as long as Allah wills.","Then he will say: ‘My Lord, bring me nearer to the gate of Paradise.’ Allah will say to him: ‘Did you not give Me your pledges and covenants that you would ask for nothing beyond what I gave you? Woe to you, son of Ādam! How treacherous you are!’ He will say: ‘My Lord…’ and continue supplicating until Allah says to him: ‘If I give you that, perhaps you will ask for something else?’ He will say: ‘No, by Your Might.’ He will give his Lord whatever pledges and covenants Allah wills, so Allah will bring him to the gate of Paradise.","When he stands at the gate of Paradise, Paradise will open wide before him and he will see the goodness and joy within it. He will remain silent for as long as Allah wills. Then he will say: ‘My Lord, admit me into Paradise.’ Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will say: ‘Did you not give Me your pledges and covenants that you would ask for nothing beyond what I gave you? Woe to you, son of Ādam! How treacherous you are!’ He will say: ‘My Lord, do not make me the most miserable of Your creation.’","He will continue supplicating to Allah until Allah, Blessed and Exalted, laughs at him. When Allah laughs at him, He will say: ‘Enter Paradise.’ When he enters it, Allah will say to him: ‘Wish.’ He will ask his Lord and continue wishing, and Allah will remind him to ask for such-and-such, until all his wishes are exhausted. Then Allah, the Exalted, will say: ‘All of that is yours, and the like of it with it.’” ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yazīd said: Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī was present with Abū Hurayrah and did not object to anything in his narration until Abū Hurayrah narrated that Allah said to the man: “And the like of it with it.”","Then Abū Saʿīd said: “And ten times the like of it with it, O Abū Hurayrah.” Abū Hurayrah replied: “I only memorized the wording: ‘That is yours, and the like of it with it.’” Abū Saʿīd said: “I testify that I memorized from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ the wording: ‘That is yours, and ten times the like of it with it.’” Abū Hurayrah said: “That man is the last of the people of Paradise to enter Paradise.”"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["قوله: ((تبقى هذه الأمة فيها منافقوها)) أي يبقى المنافقون مع المؤمنين كما كانوا في الدنيا متسترين معهم.","وقوله: ((فيأتيهم الله في صورة غير صورته التي يعرفون)) أي بصورة المخلوق، وقد علموا من قوله تعالى:","﴿لَيْسَ كَمِثْلِهِ شَيْءٌ وَهُوَ السَّمِيعُ الْبَصِيرُ﴾ [الشورى: ١١]","أي أنه منزه عن صفات هذه الصورة.","وقوله: ((فيأتيهم اللّه في صورته التي يعرفون)) فقال المؤمنون: أنت ربنا فيتبعونه.","وأما المنافقون: فيضرب الصراط بين ظهري جهنم فيبقى المنافقون وراء الصراط، ولا يرون اللّٰه تعالى لأن نور المؤمنين قد حجب عنهم.","وقوله: ((فأكون أنا وأمتي أول من يجيز)) أي بدون المنافقين لأنهم قد وقعوا في قعر جهنم كما قال تعالى:","﴿إِنَّ الْمُنَافِقِينَ فِي الدَّرْكِ الْأَسْفَلِ مِنَ النَّارِ﴾ [النساء: ١٤٥].","وبهذا يحرم المنافقون من رؤية اللّٰه تعالى إلى الأبد كما هو مذهب أهل السنة والجماعة."],"en":["Regarding the statement:","“This Ummah will remain, including its hypocrites,”","the author explains that the hypocrites will remain among the believers, just as they concealed themselves among them in this world.","Regarding the statement:","“Allah will come to them in a form other than the form they recognize,”","the author explains this as a form resembling that of created beings, while they know from the statement of Allah:","“There is nothing like Him, and He is the All-Hearing, the All-Seeing.”","[al-Shūrā 42:11]","that Allah is exalted above the attributes of such a form.","Regarding the statement:","“Then Allah will come to them in the form they recognize,”","the believers will say:","“You are our Lord,”","and they will follow Him.","As for the hypocrites, when the Ṣirāṭ is placed across Hell, they will remain behind the Ṣirāṭ and will not see Allah, the Exalted, because the light of the believers will have been withheld from them.","Regarding the statement:","“I and my Ummah will be the first to cross,”","the author explains that this does not include the hypocrites, because they will have fallen into the lowest depth of Hell, as Allah, the Exalted, says:","“Indeed, the hypocrites will be in the lowest depth of the Fire.”","[al-Nisāʾ 4:145]","Accordingly, the author says that the hypocrites will be permanently deprived of seeing Allah, the Exalted, as held by Ahl al-Sunnah wa-l-Jamāʿah."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":7437},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":182}]},{"num":16253,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة، أن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال:","((يجمع اللّٰه الناس يوم القيامة في صعيد واحد، ثم يطلع عليهم رب العالمين فيقول: ألا يتبع كل إنسان ما كانوا يعبدونه، فيمثل لصاحب الصليب صليبه، ولصاحب التصاوير تصاويره، ولصاحب النار ناره، فيتبعون ما كانوا يعبدون، ويبقى المسلمون، فيطلع عليهم رب العالمين فيقول: ألا تتبعون الناس؟ فيقولون: نعوذ بالله منك، نعوذ بالله منك، اللّٰه ربنا، وهذا مكاننا حتى نرى ربنا، وهو يأمرهم ويثبتهم، ثم يتوارى ثم يطلع فيقول: ألا تتبعون الناس؟ فيقولون: نعوذ بالله منك، نعوذ بالله منك، الله ربنا، وهذا مكاننا حتى نرى ربنا، وهو يأمرهم ويثبتهم)).","قالوا: وهل نراه يا رسول اللّه؟ قال:","((وهل تضارون في رؤية القمر ليلة البدر؟)).","قالوا: لا يا رسول الله. قال:","((فإنكم لا تضارون في رؤيته تلك الساعة. ثم يتوارى، ثم يطلع فيعرفهم نفسه، ثم يقول: أنا ربكم فاتبعوني، فيقوم المسلمون، ويوضع الصراط فيمرون عليه مثل جياد الخيل والركاب، وقولهم عليه: سلم سلم، ويبقى أهل النار فيطرح منهم فيها فوج، فيقال: هل امتلأت؟ فتقول: هل من مزيد، ثم يطرح فيها فوج، فيقال: هل امتلأت؟ فتقول: هل من مزيد، حتى إذا أوعوا فيها وضع الرحمن قدمه فيها، وأزوي بعضها إلى بعض، ثم قال: قط، قالت: قط قط، فإذا أدخل اللّٰه أهل الجنة الجنة وأهل النار النار، قال: أتي بالموت ملببًا، فيوقف على السور الذي بين أهل الجنة وأهل النار، ثم يقال: يا أهل الجنة، فيطلعون خائفين، ثم يقال: يا أهل النار، فيطلعون مستبشرين يرجون الشفاعة، فيقال لأهل الجنة وأهل النار: هل تعرفون هذا؟ فيقولون هؤلاء وهؤلاء: قد عرفناه، هو الموت الذي وكل بنا، فيضجع فيذبح ذبحًا على السور الذي بين الجنة والنار، ثم يقال: يا أهل الجنة خلود لا موت، ويا أهل النار خلود لا موت))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (٢٥٥٧)، وابن خزيمة في التوحيد (١٥٠).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب جامع في ذكر عدد من مشاهد يوم القيامة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (2557) and Ibn Khuzaymah in al-Tawḥīd (150).","chapter_en":"A Comprehensive Chapter Mentioning a Number of the Scenes of the Day of Resurrection","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":51,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah will gather the people on the Day of Resurrection upon a single plain. Then the Lord of the worlds will appear to them and say: ‘Let every person follow what he used to worship.’ The cross will be represented to the one who worshipped the cross, images will be represented to the one who worshipped images, and fire will be represented to the one who worshipped fire. They will then follow what they used to worship.","The Muslims will remain. Then the Lord of the worlds will appear to them and say: ‘Will you not follow the people?’ They will say: ‘We seek refuge in Allah from you! We seek refuge in Allah from you! Allah is our Lord, and this is our place until we see our Lord.’ He will command them and keep them firm. Then He will withdraw and appear again, saying: ‘Will you not follow the people?’ They will say: ‘We seek refuge in Allah from you! We seek refuge in Allah from you! Allah is our Lord, and this is our place until we see our Lord.’”","They asked: “Will we see Him, O Messenger of Allah?” He replied: “Do you have difficulty seeing the full moon?” They said: “No, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “You will likewise have no difficulty seeing Him at that time. Then He will withdraw and appear again, making Himself known to them, and say: ‘I am your Lord, so follow Me.’ The Muslims will rise, and the Ṣirāṭ will be placed. They will pass over it like fine horses and riding animals, saying while upon it: ‘Safety! Safety!’","The people of the Fire will remain, and a group of them will be thrown into it. It will be asked: ‘Are you full?’ It will reply: ‘Are there any more?’ Then another group will be thrown into it, and it will again be asked: ‘Are you full?’ It will reply: ‘Are there any more?’ When they have all been placed into it, the Most Merciful will place His Foot upon it, and its parts will contract toward one another. Then He will say: ‘Enough.’ It will say: ‘Enough! Enough!’","When Allah has admitted the people of Paradise into Paradise and the people of the Fire into the Fire, death will be brought restrained and placed upon the wall separating the people of Paradise from the people of the Fire. Then it will be said: ‘O people of Paradise!’ They will look up fearfully. Then it will be said: ‘O people of the Fire!’ They will look up joyfully, hoping for intercession. It will be said to the people of Paradise and the people of the Fire: ‘Do you recognize this?’","Both groups will say: ‘We recognize it. It is death, which had been appointed over us.’ Then it will be laid down and slaughtered upon the wall between Paradise and the Fire. Then it will be said: ‘O people of Paradise, eternity with no death! O people of the Fire, eternity with no death!’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"tirmidhi","label":"الترمذي","number":2557},{"key":"ابن_خزیمہ/التوحید","label":"ابن خزيمة في التوحيد","number":150}]},{"num":16254,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبدالله بن مسعود، عن النبي ﷺ قال:","((يجمع اللّٰه الأولين والآخرين لميقات يوم معلوم قيامًا أربعين سنة شاخصة أبصارهم إلى السماء ينتظرون فصل القضاء، قال: وينزل اللّٰه عز وجل في ظلل من الغمام من العرش إلى الكرسي، ثم ينادي مناد: أيها الناس ألم ترضوا من ربكم الذي خلقكم ورزقكم وأمركم أن تعبدوه ولا تشركوا به شيئًا أن يولي كل ناس منكم ما كانوا يتولون ويعبدون في الدين؟ أليس ذلك عدلًا من ربكم؟ قالوا: بلى. قال: فلينطلق كل قوم إلى ما كانوا يعبدون في الدنيا. قال: فينطلقون، ويمثل لهم أشياء ما كانوا يعبدون؛ فمنهم من ينطلق إلى الشمس، ومنهم من ينطلق إلى القمر، وإلى الأوثان من الحجارة، وأشباه ما كانوا يعبدون، قال: ويمثل لمن كان يعبد عيسى شيطان عيسى، ويمثل لمن كان يعبد عزيرًا شيطان عزير، ويبقى محمد ﷺ وأمته. قال: فيتمثل الرب عز وجل فيأتيهم فيقول: ما لكم لا تنطلقون كما انطلق الناس؟ قال: فيقولون: إن لنا لإلهًا ما رأيناه بعد. فيقول: هل تعرفونه إن رأيتموه؟ فيقولون: إن بيننا وبينه علامة إذا رأيناها عرفناها. قال: فيقول: ما هي؟ فيقولون: يكشف عن ساقه. قال: فعند ذلك يكشف عن ساق، فيخر كل من كان بظهره طبق، ويبقى قوم ظهورهم كصياصي البقر يريدون السجود فلا يستطيعون، وقد كانوا يدعون إلى السجود وهم سالمون، ثم يقول: ارفعوا رؤوسكم، فيرفعون رؤوسهم، فيعطيهم نورهم على قدر أعمالهم، فمنهم من يعطى نوره مثل الجبل العظيم يسعى بين يديه، ومنهم من يعطى نوره أصغر من ذلك، ومنهم من يعطى نورًا مثل النخلة بيمينه، ومنهم من يعطى نورًا أصغر من ذلك، حتى يكون آخرهم رجلًا يعطى نوره على إبهام قدمه يضيء مرة ويطفأ مرة، فإذا أضاء قدم قدمه فمشى، وإذا طفئ قام. قال: والرب عز وجل أمامهم حتى يمر في النار فيبقى أثره كحد السيف دحض مزلة. قال: ويقول: مروا، فيمرون على قدر نورهم، منهم من يمر كطرف العين، ومنهم من يمر كالبرق، ومنهم من يمر كالسحاب، ومنهم من يمر كانقضاض الكوكب، ومنهم من يمر كالريح، ومنهم من يمر كشد الفرس، ومنهم من يمر كشد الرجل، حتى يمر الذي أعطي نوره على إبهام قدميه يحبو على وجهه ويديه ورجليه، تخر يد وتعلق يد، وتخر رجل وتعلق رجل، ويصيب جوانبه النار، فلا يزال كذلك حتى يخلص، فإذا خلص وقف عليها، ثم قال: الحمد لله لقد أعطاني اللّٰه ما لم يعط أحدًا أن نجاني منها بعد إذ رأيتها. قال: فينطلق به إلى غدير عند باب الجنة، فيغتسل، فيعود إليه ريح أهل الجنة وألوانهم، فيرى ما في الجنة من خلال الباب، فيقول: رب أدخلني الجنة. فيقول اللّٰه له: أتسأل الجنة وقد نجيتك من النار؟ فيقول: رب اجعل بيني وبينها حجابًا لا أسمع حسيسها. قال: فيدخل الجنة. قال: فيرى أو يرفع له منزلًا أمام ذلك كأنما هو فيه إليه حلم. فيقول: رب أعطني ذلك المنزل. فيقول له: فلعلك إن أعطيتكه تسأل غيره؟ فيقول: لا وعزتك لا أسألك غيره، وأي منزل يكون أحسن منه؟ فيعطيه فينزله، ويرى أمام ذلك منزلًا كأنما هو فيه إليه حلم، قال: رب أعطني ذلك المنزل، فيقول اللّٰه عز وجل له: فلعلك إن أعطيتكه تسأل غيره؟ فيقول: لا وعزتك لا أسألك غيره، وأي منزل يكون أحسن منه؟ قال: فيعطى منزله، قال: ويرى أو يرفع له أمام ذلك منزل آخر كأنما هو إليه حلم، فيقول: أعطني ذلك المنزل. فيقول اللّٰه جل جلاله: فلعلك إن أعطيتكه تسأل غيره؟ قال: لا وعزتك لا أسألك غيره، وأي منزل يكون أحسن منه؟ قال: فيعطاه فينزله، ثم يسكت، فيقول اللّٰه عز وجل: ما لك لا تسأل؟ فيقول: رب لقد سألتك حتى استحييتك، وأقسمت لك حتى استحييتك. فيقول اللّٰه تعالى: ألم ترض أن أعطيك مثل الدنيا منذ خلقتها إلى يوم أفنيتها وعشرة أضعافه؟ فيقول: أتستهزئ بي وأنت رب العزة؟ فيضحك الرب عز وجل من قوله)).","قال: فرأيت عبدالله بن مسعود إذا بلغ هذا المكان من هذا الحديث ضحك. فقال له رجل: يا أبا عبد الرحمن قد سمعتك تحدث هذا الحديث مرارًا، كلما بلغت هذا المكان ضحكت؟ فقال: إني سمعت رسول اللّه ﷺ يحدث هذا الحديث مرارًا، كلما بلغ هذا المكان من هذا الحديث ضحك حتى تبدو أضراسه. قال:","((فيقول الرب عز وجل: لا، ولكني على ذلك قادر، سل، فيقول: ألحقني بالناس، فيقول: الحق الناس. قال: فينطلق يرمل في الجنة حتى إذا دنا من الناس، رفع له قصر من درة فيخر ساجدًا. فيقال له: ارفع رأسك، مالك؟ فيقول: رأيت ربي أو تراءى لي ربي! فيقال له: إنما هو منزل من منازلك. قال: ثم يلقى رجلًا فيتهيأ للسجود له، فيقال له: مه مالك؟ فيقول: رأيت أنك ملك من الملائكة، فيقول: إنما أنا خازن من خزانك، عبد من عبيدك، تحت يدي ألف قهرمان على مثل ما أنا عليه. قال: فينطلق أمامه حتى يفتح له القصر. قال: وهو في درة مجوفة سقائفها وأبوابها وأغلاقها ومفاتيحها منها، تستقبله جوهرة، جوهرة خضراء مبطنة بحمراء، كل جوهرة تفضي إلى جوهرة على غير لون الأخرى، في كل جوهرة سرر وأزواج ووصائف، أدناهن حوراء عيناء عليها سبعون حلة، يرى مخ ساقها من وراء حللها، كبدها مرآته وكبده مرآتها، إذا أعرض عنها إعراضة ازدادت في عينه سبعين ضعفًا عما كانت قبل ذلك، وإذا أعرضت عنه إعراضة ازداد في عينها سبعين ضعفًا عما كان قبل ذلك. فيقول لها: والله لقد ازددت في عيني سبعين ضعفًا! وتقول له: وأنت والله لقد ازددت في عيني سبعين ضعفًا! فيقال له: أشرف. قال: فيشرف، فيقال له: ملكك مسيرة مائة عام ينفذه بصرك)).","قال: فقال عمر: ألا تسمع ما يحدثنا ابن أم عبد يا كعب عن أدنى أهل الجنة منزلًا، فكيف أعلاهم؟ فقال كعب: يا أمير المؤمنين، ما لا عين رأت ولا أذن سمعت، إن اللّٰه عز وجل جعل دارًا، فجعل فيها ما شاء من الأزواج والثمرات والأشربة، ثم أطبقها، ثم لم يرها أحد من خلقه لا جبريل ولا غيره من الملائكة، ثم قرأ كعب:","﴿فَلَا تَعْلَمُ نَفْسٌ مَا أُخْفِيَ لَهُمْ مِنْ قُرَّةِ أَعْيُنٍ جَزَاءً بِمَا كَانُوا يَعْمَلُونَ﴾ [السجدة: ١٧].","قال: وخلق دون ذلك جنتين وزينهما بما شاء، وأراهما من شاء من خلقه. ثم قال: من كان كتابه في عليين نزل تلك الدار التي لم يرها أحد، حتى إن الرجل من أهل عليين ليخرج فيسير في ملكه، فما تبقى خيمة من خيم الجنة إلا دخلها من ضوء وجهه فيستبشرون بريحه، فيقولون: واها لهذه الريح! هذا رجل من أهل عليين قد خرج يسير في ملكه. فقال: ويحك يا كعب! إن هذه القلوب قد استرسلت فاقبضها. فقال كعب: والذي نفسي بيده إن لجهنم يوم القيامة لزفرة، ما من ملك مقرب ولا نبي مرسل إلا يخر لركبتيه حتى إن إبراهيم خليل اللّٰه ليقول: رب نفسي نفسي، حتى لو كان لك عمل سبعين نبيًا إلى عملك لظننت أنك لا تنجو."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه محمد بن نصر المروزي في تعظيم قدر الصلاة (٢٧٨)، وعبد اللّٰه بن أحمد في السنة (١٢٠٣)، والطبراني في الكبير (٤١٦-٤٢١/٩)، والدارقطني في الرؤية (١٦١)، وابن منده في التوحيد (٥٣١)، وصححه الحاكم (٥٨٩-٥٩٢/٤).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب جامع في ذكر عدد من مشاهد يوم القيامة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Muḥammad ibn Naṣr al-Marwazī in Taʿẓīm Qadr al-Ṣalāh (278), ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad in al-Sunnah (1203), al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Kabīr (9/416-421), al-Dāraquṭnī in al-Ruʾyah (161), Ibn Mandah in al-Tawḥīd (531), and authenticated by al-Ḥākim (4/589-592).","chapter_en":"A Comprehensive Chapter Mentioning a Number of the Scenes of the Day of Resurrection","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة يوم القيامة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Day of Judgment","part_no":66,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":51,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Allah will gather the first and the last generations at the appointed time of a known Day. They will remain standing for forty years, their eyes fixed toward the sky, awaiting the decisive judgment. Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will descend in canopies of cloud from the Throne to the Kursī. A caller will proclaim: ‘O people, are you not content that your Lord—the One who created you, provided for you, and commanded you to worship Him without associating anything with Him—should place every group with whatever they used to follow and worship in the world? Is that not justice from your Lord?’","They will say: ‘Yes.’ Then every group will go toward what it used to worship in the world. Things resembling their objects of worship will be represented to them. Some will go toward the sun, some toward the moon, some toward stone idols, and others toward whatever they used to worship. For those who used to worship ʿĪsā, the devil of ʿĪsā will be represented, and for those who used to worship ʿUzayr, the devil of ʿUzayr will be represented. Muḥammad ﷺ and his Ummah will remain.","Then the Lord, Mighty and Majestic, will appear to them and say: ‘Why do you not depart as the other people departed?’ They will reply: ‘We have a deity whom we have not yet seen.’ He will ask: ‘Will you recognize Him if you see Him?’ They will say: ‘There is a sign between us and Him. If we see it, we will recognize Him.’ He will ask: ‘What is it?’ They will say: ‘He will uncover His Shin.’ At that point the Shin will be uncovered. Everyone whose back had remained flexible will fall in prostration, while some people’s backs will become like the horns of cattle. They will want to prostrate but will be unable to do so, though they had previously been called to prostrate while they were sound.","Then He will say: ‘Raise your heads.’ They will raise their heads, and He will give them light in proportion to their deeds. Some will be given a light like a tremendous mountain proceeding before them. Some will receive less than that. Some will be given a light like a palm tree on their right. Others will receive less than that, until the last of them will be a man whose light is upon the big toe of his foot, shining at one time and going out at another.","When it shines, he will move his foot forward and walk; when it goes out, he will stop. The Lord, Mighty and Majestic, will be before them until He passes over the Fire, and His path will remain like the edge of a sword—slippery and causing feet to slip. He will say: ‘Pass over.’ They will cross according to the amount of their light. Some will pass like the blink of an eye, some like lightning, some like clouds, some like a falling star, some like the wind, some like the running of a horse, and some like the running of a man.","Eventually the man whose light is only on the big toes of his feet will cross crawling upon his face, hands, and feet. One hand will slip while the other clings; one foot will slip while the other clings. The Fire will strike his sides. He will remain like this until he is finally delivered. When he is delivered, he will stand over it and say: ‘All praise belongs to Allah! Allah has given me something He has given no one else—He saved me from it after I had seen it.’","He will then be taken to a pool near the gate of Paradise and bathe in it. The fragrance and complexion of the people of Paradise will return to him. Through the gate he will see what is inside Paradise and say: ‘My Lord, admit me into Paradise.’ Allah will say to him: ‘You ask for Paradise after I have saved you from the Fire?’ He will say: ‘My Lord, place a barrier between me and it so that I no longer hear its sound.’ Then he will enter Paradise.","A dwelling will be shown to him beyond that, appearing so wonderful that what he already has seems like a dream beside it. He will say: ‘My Lord, give me that dwelling.’ Allah will say: ‘Perhaps if I give it to you, you will ask for another?’ He will reply: ‘No, by Your Might. I will ask for nothing else. What dwelling could be better than it?’ So Allah will give it to him and settle him there. Then another dwelling beyond it will be shown to him, and what he has will seem like a dream beside it.","He will say: ‘My Lord, give me that dwelling.’ Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will say: ‘Perhaps if I give it to you, you will ask for another?’ He will say: ‘No, by Your Might. I will ask for nothing else. What dwelling could be better than it?’ So it will be given to him. Then another dwelling beyond that will be shown to him, and he will ask for it as before. It will be given to him and he will settle there. Then he will become silent. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will say: ‘Why do you not ask?’","He will say: ‘My Lord, I have asked You until I became ashamed before You. I have sworn to You until I became ashamed before You.’ Allah, the Exalted, will say: ‘Would you be satisfied if I gave you the equivalent of the world from the day I created it until the day I destroy it, and ten times as much?’ He will say: ‘Are You mocking me while You are the Lord of Might?’ The Lord, Mighty and Majestic, will laugh at his statement.” The narrator said: I saw ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd laugh whenever he reached this part of the hadith.","A man asked him: “O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, I have heard you narrate this hadith many times, and every time you reach this point you laugh. Why?” He replied: “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ narrate this hadith many times, and whenever he reached this part, he laughed until his molar teeth became visible.” The Prophet ﷺ continued: “The Lord, Mighty and Majestic, will say: ‘No, but I am capable of that. Ask.’ The man will say: ‘Let me join the people.’","He will say: ‘Go and join the people.’ The man will run through Paradise until, when he approaches the people, a palace made of a single pearl will be raised before him, and he will fall in prostration. It will be said to him: ‘Raise your head. What is wrong with you?’ He will say: ‘I saw my Lord—or my Lord appeared to me!’ It will be said: ‘That is only one of your dwellings.’ Then he will meet a man and prepare to prostrate to him. It will be said to him: ‘Stop! What are you doing?’","He will say: ‘I thought you were an angel.’ The man will reply: ‘I am only one of your treasurers, one of your servants. Under my authority are one thousand managers like me.’ He will go ahead of him and open the palace for him. The palace will be inside a hollow pearl; its roofs, doors, locks, and keys will all be made from it. A green jewel lined with red will face him, and each jewel will lead into another jewel of a different color. In every jewel will be couches, wives, and maidservants.","The least of them will be a wide-eyed ḥūrī wearing seventy garments, yet the marrow of her shin will be visible through her garments. Her inner beauty will reflect him like a mirror, and his will reflect her. Whenever he turns away from her and then looks back, she will have increased seventyfold in beauty in his eyes compared with before. And whenever she turns away from him and then looks back, he will have increased seventyfold in beauty in her eyes.","He will say to her: ‘By Allah, you have increased seventyfold in beauty in my eyes!’ She will say: ‘And by Allah, you too have increased seventyfold in beauty in my eyes!’ Then it will be said to him: ‘Look out over your kingdom.’ He will look out, and it will be said: ‘Your kingdom extends a journey of one hundred years, all of which your sight can encompass.’” The narrator continued: ʿUmar said: “O Kaʿb, do you not hear what Ibn Umm ʿAbd is telling us concerning the lowest-ranking person in Paradise? Then what about the highest-ranking among them?”","Kaʿb replied: “O Commander of the Believers, it is what no eye has seen and no ear has heard. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, created a dwelling and placed in it whatever He willed of spouses, fruits, and drinks. Then He sealed it, and no one from His creation has ever seen it—not Jibrīl nor any other angel.” Then Kaʿb recited: “No soul knows what comfort of the eyes has been hidden for them as a reward for what they used to do.” [al-Sajdah 32:17] He continued: “Below that, Allah created two Gardens and adorned them with whatever He willed, and He showed them to whomever He willed among His creation.","Whoever has his record in ʿIlliyyīn will enter that dwelling which no one has seen. A man from the people of ʿIlliyyīn will go out walking through his kingdom, and no tent among the tents of Paradise will remain except that light from his face enters it. Its inhabitants will rejoice at his fragrance and say: ‘How wonderful this fragrance is! A man from the people of ʿIlliyyīn has gone out walking through his kingdom.’” Then someone said: “Woe to you, O Kaʿb! These hearts have become carried away, so restrain them.”","Kaʿb replied: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, Hell will have such a sigh on the Day of Resurrection that no angel brought near and no Messenger sent will remain except that he will fall to his knees. Even Ibrāhīm, the intimate friend of Allah, will say: ‘My Lord, myself! Myself!’ Even if you possessed deeds equal to the deeds of seventy Prophets in addition to your own deeds, you would still think that you might not be saved.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"محمد_بن_نصر_المروزی/تعظیم_قدر_الصلاہ","label":"محمد بن نصر المروزي في تعظيم قدر الصلاة","number":278},{"key":"عبد_اللہ_بن_احمد/السنہ","label":"عبد اللّٰه بن أحمد في السنة","number":1203},{"key":"الطبرانی/الکبیر","label":"الطبراني في الكبير","number":416},{"key":"الدارقطنی/الرویہ","label":"الدارقطني في الرؤية","number":161},{"key":"ابن_مندہ/التوحید","label":"ابن منده في التوحيد","number":531},{"key":"صححہ_الحاکم","label":"صححه الحاكم","number":589}]},{"num":16255,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي بن كعب قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((من خاف أدلج، ومن أدلج فقد بلغ المنزل، ألا إن سلعة اللّٰه غالية! ألا إن سلعة اللّٰه الجنة، جاءت الراجفة، تتبعها الرادفة، جاء الموت بما فيه))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الحاكم (٣٠٨/٤)، وأبو نعيم في الحلية (٣٧٧/٨).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب أن الجنة سلعة الله الغالية","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Ḥākim (4/308) and Abū Nuʿaym in al-Ḥilyah (8/377).","chapter_en":"Paradise Is the Precious Commodity of Allah","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ubayy ibn Kaʿb narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever fears sets out at the beginning of the night, and whoever sets out early reaches the destination. Indeed, the commodity of Allah is precious! Indeed, the commodity of Allah is Paradise. The first blast has come, followed by the second; death has come with all that it contains.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ابو_نعیم/الحلیہ","label":"أبو نعيم في الحلية","number":377},{"key":"hakim","label":"المستدرك على الصحيحين","number":7852,"n":7857}]},{"num":16256,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((من خاف أدلج، ومن أدلج بلغ المنزل، ألا إن سلعة اللّٰه غالية، ألا إن سلعة اللّٰه الجنة))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (٢٤٥٠) وعبد بن حميد (١٤٦٠) والحاكم (٣٠٧/٤).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب أن الجنة سلعة الله الغالية","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (2450), ʿAbd ibn Ḥumayd (1460), and al-Ḥākim (4/307).","chapter_en":"Paradise Is the Precious Commodity of Allah","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever fears sets out early in the night, and whoever sets out early reaches the destination. Indeed, the commodity of Allah is precious. Indeed, the commodity of Allah is Paradise.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"tirmidhi","label":"الترمذي","number":2450},{"key":"عبد_بن_حمید","label":"عبد بن حميد","number":1460},{"key":"hakim","label":"المستدرك على الصحيحين","number":7852,"n":7857}]},{"num":16257,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أنس بن مالك في قصة غزوة بدر قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((قوموا إلى جنة عرضها السماوات والأرض)).","قال: يقول عمير بن الحمام الأنصاري: يا رسول الله! جنة عرضها السماوات والأرض؟ قال:","((نعم)).","قال: بخ بخ. فقال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((ما يحملك على قول بخ بخ؟)).","قال: لا، والله يا رسول الله! إلا رجاءة أن أكون من أهلها، قال:","((فإنك من أهلها)).","فأخرج تمرات من قرنه فجعل يأكل منهن، ثم قال: لئن أنا حييت حتى آكل تمراتي هذه إنها لحياة طويلة، قال: فرمى بما كان معه من التمر، ثم قاتلهم حتى قتل."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (١٤٥ :١٩٠١).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في سعة الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (145 :1901).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Vastness of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik narrated concerning the Battle of Badr that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Rise toward a Paradise whose breadth is the heavens and the earth.” ʿUmayr ibn al-Ḥumām al-Anṣārī asked: “O Messenger of Allah, a Paradise whose breadth is the heavens and the earth?” He replied: “Yes.” ʿUmayr said: “Excellent! Excellent!” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked: “What made you say, ‘Excellent! Excellent!’?” He replied: “Nothing, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah, except the hope that I might be among its people.”","He said: “You are among its people.” ʿUmayr then took some dates from his quiver and began eating them. Then he said: “If I live long enough to finish eating these dates, that would indeed be a long life.” So he threw away the dates he had with him and fought them until he was killed."]},"intro":{"ar":["قال اللّٰه تعالى:","﴿وَسَارِعُوا إِلَىٰ مَغْفِرَةٍ مِنْ رَبِّكُمْ وَجَنَّةٍ عَرْضُهَا السَّمَاوَاتُ وَالْأَرْضُ أُعِدَّتْ لِلْمُتَّقِينَ﴾ [آل عمران: ١٣٣].","وقال تعالى:","﴿سَابِقُوا إِلَىٰ مَغْفِرَةٍ مِنْ رَبِّكُمْ وَجَنَّةٍ عَرْضُهَا كَعَرْضِ السَّمَاءِ وَالْأَرْضِ أُعِدَّتْ لِلَّذِينَ آمَنُوا بِاللَّهِ وَرُسُلِهِ ذَٰلِكَ فَضْلُ اللَّهِ يُؤْتِيهِ مَنْ يَشَاءُ وَاللَّهُ ذُو الْفَضْلِ الْعَظِيمِ﴾ [الحديد: ٢١]."],"en":["Allah, the Exalted, says:","“Hasten toward forgiveness from your Lord and a Paradise as vast as the heavens and the earth, prepared for the righteous.”","[Āl ʿImrān 3:133]","And He, the Exalted, says:","“Race toward forgiveness from your Lord and a Paradise whose breadth is like the breadth of the heaven and the earth, prepared for those who believe in Allah and His Messengers. That is the bounty of Allah, which He grants to whomever He wills. And Allah is the Possessor of tremendous bounty.”","[al-Ḥadīd 57:21]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":145}]},{"num":16258,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة قال: جاء رجل إلى النبي ﷺ فقال: يا محمد، أرأيت جنة عرضها السماوات والأرض، فأين النار؟ قال:","((أرأيت الليل الذي قد ألبس كل شيء، فأين جعل النهار؟)).","قال: اللّٰه أعلم، قال:","((كذلك يفعل اللّٰه ما يشاء))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه إسحاق بن راهويه (٤٣٧)، والبزار (٩٣٨٠)، وصححه ابن حبان (١٠٣)، والحاكم (٣٦/١).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في سعة الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Isḥāq ibn Rāhawayh (437), al-Bazzār (9380), authenticated by Ibn Ḥibbān (103), and al-Ḥākim (1/36).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Vastness of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated: A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Muḥammad, if Paradise is as vast as the heavens and the earth, then where is the Fire?” He replied: “Consider the night when it covers everything—where does the day go?” The man said: “Allah knows best.” He said: “Likewise, Allah does whatever He wills.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"اسحاق_بن_راہویہ","label":"إسحاق بن راهويه","number":437},{"key":"البزار","label":"البزار","number":9380},{"key":"صححہ_ابن_حبان","label":"صححه ابن حبان","number":103},{"key":"sh13159","label":"مسند إسحاق بن راهويه","number":437,"n":419},{"key":"hakim","label":"المستدرك على الصحيحين","number":103,"n":103}]},{"num":16259,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن سهل بن سعد، عن النبي ﷺ قال:","((في الجنة ثمانية أبواب، فيها باب يسمى الريان، لا يدخله إلا الصائمون))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (٣٢٥٧).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في عدد أبواب الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3257).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Number of the Gates of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Sahl ibn Saʿd narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Paradise has eight gates. Among them is a gate called al-Rayyān, through which none will enter except those who fasted.”"]},"intro":{"ar":["قال اللّٰه تعالى:","﴿وَسِيقَ الَّذِينَ اتَّقَوْا رَبَّهُمْ إِلَى الْجَنَّةِ زُمَرًا حَتَّىٰ إِذَا جَاءُوهَا وَفُتِحَتْ أَبْوَابُهَا وَقَالَ لَهُمْ خَزَنَتُهَا سَلَامٌ عَلَيْكُمْ طِبْتُمْ فَادْخُلُوهَا خَالِدِينَ﴾ [سورة الزمر: ٧٣]."],"en":["Allah, the Exalted, says:","“Those who feared their Lord will be driven to Paradise in groups, until when they reach it and its gates are opened, its keepers will say to them: ‘Peace be upon you. You have done well, so enter it to remain forever.’”","[al-Zumar 39:73]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":3257}]},{"num":16260,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبادة بن الصامت قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((من قال: أشهد أن لا إله إلا اللّه وحده لا شريك له، وأن محمدًا عبده ورسوله، وأن عيسى عبد الله، وابن أمته، وكلمته ألقاها إلى مريم وروح منه، وأن الجنة حق، وأن النار حق، أدخله اللّٰه من أي أبواب الجنة الثمانية شاء))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٢٨).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في عدد أبواب الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (28).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Number of the Gates of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever testifies that there is no deity except Allah alone, without partner; that Muḥammad is His servant and Messenger; that ʿĪsā is the servant of Allah, the son of His female servant, His Word which He cast to Maryam, and a spirit from Him; and that Paradise is true and the Fire is true—Allah will admit him through whichever of the eight gates of Paradise he wishes.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":28}]},{"num":16261,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عقبة بن عامر قال: كانت علينا رعاية الإبل، فجاءت نوبتي، فروحتها بعشي، فأدركت رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قائمًا يحدث الناس، فأدركت من قوله:","((ما من مسلم يتوضأ فيحسن وضوءه، ثم يقوم فيصلي ركعتين، مقبل عليهما بقلبه ووجهه، إلا وجبت له الجنة)).","قال فقلت: ما أجود هذه! فإذا قائل بين يدي يقول: التي قبلها أجود. فنظرت فإذا عمر، قال: إني قد رأيتك جئت آنفًا، قال:","((ما منكم من أحد يتوضأ فيبلغ - أو فيسبغ - الوضوء ثم يقول: أشهد أن لا إله إلا الله، وأن محمدًا عبد اللّٰه ورسوله إلا فتحت له أبواب الجنة الثمانية، يدخل من أيها شاء))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٢٣٤).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في عدد أبواب الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (234).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Number of the Gates of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir narrated: We used to take turns tending the camels. When my turn came, I brought them back in the evening and found the Messenger of Allah ﷺ standing and speaking to the people. I heard him say: “No Muslim performs wuḍūʾ and performs it well, then stands and prays two rakʿahs, turning toward them with both his heart and face, except that Paradise becomes obligatory for him.” I said: “How excellent this is!” Then someone in front of me said: “What came before it was even better.”","I looked and saw that it was ʿUmar. He said: “I saw that you had just arrived.” Then he related that the Prophet ﷺ said: “There is none among you who performs wuḍūʾ and completes—or perfects—his wuḍūʾ, then says: ‘I testify that there is no deity except Allah, and that Muḥammad is the servant of Allah and His Messenger,’ except that the eight gates of Paradise are opened for him, and he may enter through whichever of them he wishes.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":234}]},{"num":16262,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عقبة بن عامر قال: قال عمر بن الخطاب: إن نبي اللّٰه ﷺ قال:","((من مات لا يشرك بالله تعالى شيئًا، فتحت له أبواب الجنة، يدخل من أيها شاء، ولها ثمانية أبواب…)).","الحديث."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الطبراني في الأوسط (٧٩٤٣) - وعنه أبو نعيم في الحلية (٣٠٧/٩).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في عدد أبواب الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Awsaṭ (7943), and from him Abū Nuʿaym in al-Ḥilyah (9/307).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Number of the Gates of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir narrated that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb said: The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever dies without associating anything with Allah, the Exalted, the gates of Paradise will be opened for him and he may enter through whichever of them he wishes. Paradise has eight gates…” The hadith continues."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"الطبرانی/الاوسط","label":"الطبراني في الأوسط","number":7943},{"key":"وعنہ_ابو_نعیم/الحلیہ","label":"- وعنه أبو نعيم في الحلية","number":307},{"key":"sh28171","label":"المعجم الأوسط للطبراني","number":7947,"n":7932}]},{"num":16263,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عتبة بن عبد السلمي قال: سمعت رسول اللّٰه ﷺ يقول:","((ما من مسلم يموت له ثلاثة من الولد لم يبلغوا الحنث، إلا تلقوه من أبواب الجنة الثمانية، من أيها شاء دخل))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه ابن ماجه (١٦٠٤).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في عدد أبواب الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Ibn Mājah (1604).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Number of the Gates of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿUtbah ibn ʿAbd al-Sulamī narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “No Muslim has three children die before reaching the age of accountability except that they will meet him at the eight gates of Paradise, and he may enter through whichever gate he wishes.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ibnmajah","label":"ابن ماجه","number":1604}]},{"num":16264,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة قال: سمعت رسول اللّٰه ﷺ يقول:","((من أنفق زوجين من شيء من الأشياء في سبيل الله، دعي من أبواب - يعني الجنة -: يا عبد اللّٰه هذا خير، فمن كان من أهل الصلاة دعي من باب الصلاة، ومن كان من أهل الجهاد دعي من باب الجهاد، ومن كان من أهل الصدقة دعي من باب الصدقة، ومن كان من أهل الصيام دعي من باب الصيام، وباب الريان)).","فقال أبو بكر: ما على هذا الذي يدعى من تلك الأبواب من ضرورة، وقال: هل يدعى منها كلها أحد يا رسول الله؟ قال:","((نعم، وأرجو أن تكون منهم يا أبا بكر))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٣٦٦٦)، ومسلم (٨٥ - ١٠٢٧).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في أسماء أبواب الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3666) and Muslim (85 - 1027).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Names of the Gates of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever spends two of anything in the path of Allah will be called from the gates of Paradise: ‘O servant of Allah, this is good!’ Whoever was among the people of prayer will be called from the Gate of Prayer. Whoever was among the people of jihād will be called from the Gate of Jihād. Whoever was among the people of charity will be called from the Gate of Charity. And whoever was among the people of fasting will be called from the Gate of Fasting, the Gate of al-Rayyān.”","Abū Bakr said: “There is no hardship upon someone who is called from one of those gates, but will anyone be called from all of them, O Messenger of Allah?” He replied: “Yes, and I hope that you will be among them, O Abū Bakr.”"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["وفي لفظ لهما:","((من أنفق زوجين في سبيل الله، دعاه خزنة الجنة، كل خزنة باب: أي فل، هلم)).","فقال أبو بكر: يا رسول الله، ذلك الذي لا توى عليه، قال رسول الله ﷺ:","((إني لأرجو أن تكون منهم)).","وقوله: ((لا توى)) أي: لا هلاك."],"en":["In another wording narrated by both:","“Whoever spends two of anything in the path of Allah will be called by the keepers of Paradise, each keeper from his gate: ‘O so-and-so, come!’”","Abū Bakr said:","“O Messenger of Allah, such a person will have no loss upon him.”","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said:","“I certainly hope that you will be among them.”","The expression “lā tawā” means: there will be no destruction or loss."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":3666},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":85}]},{"num":16265,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة، أن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال:","((تفتح أبواب الجنة يوم الاثنين، ويوم الخميس، فيغفر لكل عبد لا يشرك بالله شيئًا، إلا رجلًا كانت بينه وبين أخيه شحناء، فيقال: أنظروا هذين حتى يصطلحا، أنظروا هذين حتى يصطلحا، أنظروا هذين حتى يصطلحا))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مالك في حسن الخلق (١٧) ومسلم (٢٥٦٥).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب فتح أبواب الجنة في يومي الاثنين والخميس","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Mālik in Ḥusn al-Khuluq (17) and Muslim (2565).","chapter_en":"The Gates of Paradise Are Opened on Mondays and Thursdays","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The gates of Paradise are opened on Monday and Thursday, and every servant who does not associate anything with Allah is forgiven, except a man between whom and his brother there is hostility. It will be said: ‘Delay these two until they reconcile. Delay these two until they reconcile. Delay these two until they reconcile.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"malik/حسن_الخلق","label":"مالك في حسن الخلق","number":17},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2565}]},{"num":16266,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة قال: أُتي رسول الله ﷺ يومًا بلحم، فرفع إليه الذراع، وكانت تعجبه، فذكر حديث الشفاعة الطويل، وجاء فيه:","((فأقول: يا رب، أمتي أمتي، فيقال: يا محمد، أدخل الجنة من أمتك من لا حساب عليه من الباب الأيمن من أبواب الجنة، وهم شركاء الناس فيما سوى ذلك من الأبواب، والذي نفس محمد بيده، إن ما بين المصراعين من مصاريع الجنة لكما بين مكة وهجر، أو كما بين مكة وبصرى))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٤٧١٢)، ومسلم (١٩٤).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في عرض أبواب الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4712) and Muslim (194).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Width of the Gates of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated: One day meat was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the foreleg was presented to him, which he liked. He then mentioned the lengthy hadith of intercession, in which he said: “I will say: ‘My Lord, my Ummah! My Ummah!’ It will be said: ʿO Muḥammad, admit into Paradise from your Ummah those who will have no reckoning through the right-hand gate of the gates of Paradise. They will share with the other people in the remaining gates.","By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muḥammad, the distance between the two leaves of one of the gates of Paradise is like the distance between Makkah and Hajar, or like the distance between Makkah and Buṣrā.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":4712},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":194}]},{"num":16267,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن خالد بن عمير العدوي قال: خطبنا عتبة بن غزوان، فحمد الله وأثنى عليه، ثم قال:","((أما بعد، فإن الدنيا قد آذنت بصرم، وولت حذاء، ولم يبق منها إلا صبابة كصبابة الإناء، يتصابها صاحبها، وإنكم منتقلون منها إلى دار لا زوال لها، فانتقلوا بخير ما بحضرتكم، فإنه قد ذكر لنا أن الحجر يلقى من شفة جهنم، فيهوي فيها سبعين عامًا، لا يدرك لها قعرًا، ووالله لتملأن، أفعجبتم؟ ولقد ذكر لنا أن ما بين مصراعين من مصاريع الجنة مسيرة أربعين سنة، وليأتين عليها يوم وهو كظيظ من الزحام، ولقد رأيتني سابع سبعة مع رسول اللّٰه ﷺ، ما لنا طعام إلا ورق الشجر، حتى قرحت أشداقنا…)).","الحديث بطوله."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٢٩٦٧).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في عرض أبواب الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2967).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Width of the Gates of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Khālid ibn ʿUmayr al-ʿAdawī narrated: ʿUtbah ibn Ghazwān delivered a sermon to us. He praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: “To proceed: This world has announced that it is coming to an end and has turned away swiftly. Nothing remains of it except a small amount like the dregs left in a vessel, which its owner tries to drink. You are moving from it to an abode that will never pass away, so move there with the best deeds you are able to take with you.","We have been told that a stone will be thrown from the edge of Hell and will fall through it for seventy years without reaching its bottom. By Allah, it will certainly be filled. Are you surprised? And we have been told that the distance between two leaves of one of the gates of Paradise is a journey of forty years, yet a day will certainly come when it will be crowded with people. I remember myself as one of seven people with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we had nothing to eat except the leaves of trees, until the corners of our mouths became ulcerated…”","The hadith continues at length."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2967}]},{"num":16268,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن معاوية بن حيدة القشيري أن رسول اللّه ﷺ قال:","((أنتم توفون سبعين أمة، أنتم آخرها، وأكرمها على الله، وما بين مصراعين من مصاريع الجنة مسيرة أربعين عامًا، وليأتين عليه يوم وإنه لكظيظ))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (٢٠٠٢٥) وعبد بن حميد (٤١١).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في عرض أبواب الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (20025) and ʿAbd ibn Ḥumayd (411).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Width of the Gates of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Muʿāwiyah ibn Ḥaydah al-Qushayrī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “You complete seventy nations. You are the last of them and the most honored of them before Allah. The distance between two leaves of one of the gates of Paradise is a journey of forty years, and a day will certainly come when it will be packed with people.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"عبد_بن_حمید","label":"عبد بن حميد","number":411},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":20025,"n":20025}]},{"num":16269,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبد اللّٰه بن سلام قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((إن ما بين مصراعي الجنة مقدار أربعين عامًا، وليأتين عليه يوم يزاحم عليه كازدحام الإبل وردت لخمس ظماء))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الطبراني في الكبير (٣٣٨/١٤ رقم ١٤٩٧٠).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في عرض أبواب الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Kabīr (14/338, no. 14970).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Width of the Gates of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn Salām narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The distance between the two leaves of the gate of Paradise is a journey of forty years, and a day will certainly come when people will crowd at it like thirsty camels crowding when they come to water after five days.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"الطبرانی/الکبیر","label":"الطبراني في الكبير","number":338}]},{"num":16270,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة، عن النبي ﷺ قال:","((من أنفق زوجين في سبيل اللّٰه دعاه خزنة الجنة - كل خزنة باب -: أي فل، هلم)).","قال أبو بكر: يا رسول اللّٰه، ذاك الذي لا توى عليه، فقال النبي ﷺ:","((إني لأرجو أن تكون منهم))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٢٨٤١)، ومسلم (٨٦ :١٠٢٧).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في خزنة الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (2841) and Muslim (86 :1027).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Keepers of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever spends two of anything in the path of Allah will be called by the keepers of Paradise—each keeper from his own gate—saying: ‘O so-and-so, come!’” Abū Bakr said: “O Messenger of Allah, such a person has nothing to fear from loss.” The Prophet ﷺ replied: “I certainly hope that you will be among them.”"]},"intro":{"ar":["قال اللّٰه تعالى:","﴿وَسِيقَ الَّذِينَ اتَّقَوْا رَبَّهُمْ إِلَى الْجَنَّةِ زُمَرًا حَتَّىٰ إِذَا جَاءُوهَا وَفُتِحَتْ أَبْوَابُهَا وَقَالَ لَهُمْ خَزَنَتُهَا سَلَامٌ عَلَيْكُمْ طِبْتُمْ فَادْخُلُوهَا خَالِدِينَ﴾ [سورة الزمر: ٧٣]."],"en":["Allah, the Exalted, says:","“Those who feared their Lord will be driven to Paradise in groups, until when they reach it and its gates are opened, its keepers will say to them: ‘Peace be upon you. You have done well, so enter it to remain forever.’”","[al-Zumar 39:73]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":2841},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":86}]},{"num":16271,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن سهل بن سعد، عن النبي ﷺ قال:","((إن أهل الجنة ليتراءون الغرف في الجنة، كما تتراءون الكوكب في السماء))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٦٥٥٥)، ومسلم (٢٨٣٠).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في غرف الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6555) and Muslim (2830).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Chambers of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Sahl ibn Saʿd narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The people of Paradise will see the lofty chambers in Paradise just as you see a star in the sky.”"]},"intro":{"ar":["قال اللّٰه تعالى:","﴿لَكِنِ الَّذِينَ اتَّقَوْا رَبَّهُمْ لَهُمْ غُرَفٌ مِنْ فَوْقِهَا غُرَفٌ مَبْنِيَّةٌ تَجْرِي مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْأَنْهَارُ وَعْدَ اللَّهِ لَا يُخْلِفُ اللَّهُ الْمِيعَادَ﴾ [الزمر: ٢٠].","وقال تعالى:","﴿وَالَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَعَمِلُوا الصَّالِحَاتِ لَنُبَوِّئَنَّهُمْ مِنَ الْجَنَّةِ غُرَفًا تَجْرِي مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْأَنْهَارُ خَالِدِينَ فِيهَا نِعْمَ أَجْرُ الْعَامِلِينَ﴾ [العنكبوت: ٥٨]."],"en":["Allah, the Exalted, says:","“But those who feared their Lord will have lofty chambers, with other chambers built above them, beneath which rivers flow. This is the promise of Allah, and Allah never fails in His promise.”","[al-Zumar 39:20]","And He, the Exalted, says:","“Those who believe and perform righteous deeds, We will surely settle them in lofty chambers of Paradise beneath which rivers flow, remaining therein forever. Excellent indeed is the reward of those who work righteousness.”","[al-ʿAnkabūt 29:58]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6555},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2830}]},{"num":16272,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي سعيد الخدري، عن النبي ﷺ قال:","((إن أهل الجنة يتراءون الغرف في الجنة، كما تراءون الكوكب الغارب في الأفق الشرقي والغربي))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٦٥٥٦)، ومسلم (٢٨٣١).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في غرف الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6556) and Muslim (2831).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Chambers of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The people of Paradise will see the lofty chambers in Paradise just as you see a distant star setting on the eastern or western horizon.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6556},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2831}]},{"num":16273,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي سعيد الخدري، أن رسول الله ﷺ قال:","((إن أهل الجنة ليتراءون أهل الغرف من فوقهم، كما تتراءون الكوكب الدري الغابر من الأفق من المشرق أو المغرب، لتفاضل ما بينهم)).","قالوا: يا رسول الله، تلك منازل الأنبياء لا يبلغها غيرهم، قال:","((بلى، والذي نفسي بيده، رجال آمنوا بالله وصدقوا المرسلين))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٣٢٥٦)، ومسلم (٦٣٣).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في غرف الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3256) and Muslim (633).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Chambers of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The people of Paradise will see those who dwell in the lofty chambers above them just as you see a brilliant star far away on the eastern or western horizon, because of the difference in rank between them.” They asked: “O Messenger of Allah, are those the dwellings of the Prophets, which no one else can reach?” He replied: “Yes. By the One in whose hand is my soul, they are for men who believed in Allah and affirmed the truthfulness of the Messengers.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":3256},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":633}]},{"num":16274,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة، عن النبي ﷺ، قال:","((إن أهل الجنة ليتراءون في الغرفة كما يتراءون الكوكب الشرقي أو الكوكب الغربي الغارب في الأفق أو الطالع، في تفاضل الدرجات)).","فقالوا: يا رسول الله، أولئك النبيون؟ قال:","((بلى، والذي نفسي بيده، وأقوام آمنوا بالله ورسوله وصدقوا المرسلين))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (٢٥٥٦)، وأحمد (٨٤٢٣)، ونعيم بن حماد في زوائده على الزهد لابن المبارك (٤١٨).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في غرف الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (2556), Aḥmad (8423), and Nuʿaym ibn Ḥammād in his additions to Ibn al-Mubārak’s al-Zuhd (418).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Chambers of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The people of Paradise will see those in the lofty chamber just as they see a star in the east or a star in the west, setting or rising upon the horizon, because of the differing ranks among them.” They asked: “O Messenger of Allah, are those the Prophets?” He replied: “Yes, and by the One in whose hand is my soul, also people who believed in Allah and His Messenger and affirmed the truthfulness of the Messengers.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"tirmidhi","label":"الترمذي","number":2556},{"key":"نعیم_بن_حماد/زوایدہ_علی_الزہد_لابن_المبارک","label":"نعيم بن حماد في زوائده على الزهد لابن المبارك","number":418},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":8423,"n":8423}]},{"num":16275,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبد اللّٰه بن عمرو، أن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال:","((إن في الجنة غرفة يرى ظاهرها من باطنها، وباطنها من ظاهرها)).","فقال أبو موسى الأشعري: لمن هي يا رسول الله؟ قال:","((لمن ألان الكلام، وأطعم الطعام، وبات لله قائمًا والناس نيام))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (٦٦١٥).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في غرف الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Imām Aḥmad (6615).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Chambers of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “In Paradise there is a chamber whose exterior can be seen from its interior and whose interior can be seen from its exterior.” Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī asked: “For whom is it, O Messenger of Allah?” He replied: “For the one who speaks gently, feeds others, and spends the night standing in prayer for Allah while the people are asleep.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"الامام_احمد","label":"الإمام أحمد","number":6615},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":6615,"n":6615}]},{"num":16276,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي مالك الأشعري قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((إن في الجنة غرفة يرى ظاهرها من باطنها، وباطنها من ظاهرها، أعدها اللّٰه لمن أطعم الطعام، وألان الكلام، وتابع الصيام، وصلى والناس نيام))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (٢٢٩٠٥)، والطبراني في الكبير (٣٤٦٦)، وصححه ابن خزيمة (٢١٣٧)، وابن حبان (٥٠٩).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في غرف الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Imām Aḥmad (22905) and al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Kabīr (3466), and authenticated by Ibn Khuzaymah (2137) and Ibn Ḥibbān (509).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Chambers of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Mālik al-Ashʿarī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “In Paradise there is a chamber whose exterior can be seen from its interior and whose interior can be seen from its exterior. Allah has prepared it for the one who feeds others, speaks gently, regularly fasts, and prays while the people are asleep.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"الامام_احمد","label":"الإمام أحمد","number":22905},{"key":"الطبرانی/الکبیر","label":"الطبراني في الكبير","number":3466},{"key":"صححہ_ابن_خزیمہ","label":"صححه ابن خزيمة","number":2137},{"key":"ibnhibban","label":"ابن حبان","number":509},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":22905,"n":22905}]},{"num":16277,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبد اللّٰه بن قيس، أن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال:","((إن في الجنة خيمة من لؤلؤة مجوفة، عرضها ستون ميلًا، في كل زاوية منها أهل ما يرون الآخرين، يطوف عليهم المؤمنون، وجنتان من فضة، آنيتهما وما فيهما، وجنتان من كذا، آنيتهما وما فيهما، وما بين القوم وبين أن ينظروا إلى ربهم إلا رداء الكبر على وجهه في جنة عدن))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٤٨٨٠-٤٨٧٩)، ومسلم (٢٤:٢٨٣٨) وفي الإيمان (١٨٠).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في خيمة الجنة وأوانيها","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4879-4880), Muslim (24 :2838), and in al-Īmān (180).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Tent of Paradise and Its Vessels","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":9,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn Qays narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “In Paradise there is a tent made of a hollow pearl, sixty miles wide. In each corner of it are inhabitants who do not see those in the other corners, and the believers will go around visiting them. There are two Gardens of silver—their vessels and everything within them are of silver—and two Gardens of another kind, with their vessels and everything within them. Nothing stands between the people and their looking at their Lord except the Veil of Majesty over His Face in the Garden of ʿAdn.”"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["واللفظ للبخاري، ولفظ مسلم نحوه، وفيه: ((جنتان من ذهب)) بدل ((وجنتان من كذا))، إلا أنه فرّق الحديث في موضعين؛ في أولهما إلى قوله: ((يطوف عليهم المؤمنون))، وفي الموضع الثاني: ((وجنتان من فضة))."],"en":["The wording is al-Bukhārī’s. Muslim narrated a similar wording, with “two Gardens of gold” in place of “two Gardens of another kind.” Muslim divided the report between two places: the first through “the believers will go around visiting them,” and the second beginning with “two Gardens of silver.”"]},"intro":{"ar":["قال اللّٰه تعالى:","﴿حُورٌ مَقْصُورَاتٌ فِي الْخِيَامِ﴾ [الرحمن: ٧٢].","وقال تعالى:","﴿وَيُطَافُ عَلَيْهِمْ بِآنِيَةٍ مِنْ فِضَّةٍ وَأَكْوَابٍ كَانَتْ قَوَارِيرَا ۝ قَوَارِيرَ مِنْ فِضَّةٍ قَدَّرُوهَا تَقْدِيرًا ۝ وَيُسْقَوْنَ فِيهَا كَأْسًا كَانَ مِزَاجُهَا زَنْجَبِيلًا ۝ عَيْنًا فِيهَا تُسَمَّىٰ سَلْسَبِيلًا﴾ [الإنسان: ١٥-١٨].","وقال تعالى:","﴿يُطَافُ عَلَيْهِمْ بِصِحَافٍ مِنْ ذَهَبٍ وَأَكْوَابٍ وَفِيهَا مَا تَشْتَهِيهِ الْأَنْفُسُ وَتَلَذُّ الْأَعْيُنُ وَأَنْتُمْ فِيهَا خَالِدُونَ﴾ [الزخرف: ٧١].","وقال تعالى:","﴿يَطُوفُ عَلَيْهِمْ وِلْدَانٌ مُخَلَّدُونَ ۝ بِأَكْوَابٍ وَأَبَارِيقَ وَكَأْسٍ مِنْ مَعِينٍ﴾ [سورة الواقعة: ١٧-١٨]."],"en":["Allah, the Exalted, says:","“Fair maidens secluded in pavilions.”","[al-Raḥmān 55:72]","And He, the Exalted, says:","“They will be served with vessels of silver and cups that are crystal—crystal of silver, measured precisely. And they will be given to drink therein from a cup whose mixture is ginger, from a spring therein called Salsabīl.”","[al-Insān 76:15-18]","And He, the Exalted, says:","“They will be served with dishes and cups of gold, and therein will be whatever the souls desire and the eyes delight in, and you will remain therein forever.”","[al-Zukhruf 43:71]","And He, the Exalted, says:","“Immortal youths will circulate among them with cups, pitchers, and a goblet from a flowing spring.”","[al-Wāqiʿah 56:17-18]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":4880},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":24},{"key":"وفی_الایمان","label":"وفي الإيمان","number":180}]},{"num":16278,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبد اللّٰه بن قيس، أن النبي ﷺ قال:","((جنان الفردوس أربع: ثنتان من ذهب حليتهما وآنيتهما وما فيهما، وثنتان من فضة آنيتهما وحليتهما وما فيهما، وليس بين القوم وبين أن ينظروا إلى ربهم عز وجل إلا رداء الكبرياء على وجهه في جنة عدن، وهذه الأنهار تشخب من جنة عدن، ثم صدع بعد ذلك أنهارًا))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (١٩٧٣١)، وأبو داود الطيالسي (٥٣١)، وعبد بن حميد (٥٤٥)، وأبو نعيم في صفة الجنة (١٤١).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في خيمة الجنة وأوانيها","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (19731), Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī (531), ʿAbd ibn Ḥumayd (545), and Abū Nuʿaym in Ṣifat al-Jannah (141).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Tent of Paradise and Its Vessels","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":9,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn Qays narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The Gardens of al-Firdaws are four: two of gold—their ornaments, vessels, and everything within them are of gold—and two of silver—their vessels, ornaments, and everything within them are of silver. Nothing stands between the people and their looking at their Lord, Mighty and Majestic, except the Veil of Majesty over His Face in the Garden of ʿAdn. These rivers gush forth from the Garden of ʿAdn, and from there they branch out into further rivers.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ابو_داود_الطیالسی","label":"أبو داود الطيالسي","number":531},{"key":"عبد_بن_حمید","label":"عبد بن حميد","number":545},{"key":"ابو_نعیم/صفہ_الجنہ","label":"أبو نعيم في صفة الجنة","number":141},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":19731,"n":19731}]},{"num":16279,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي ذر كان يحدث أن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال، فذكر قصة الإسراء والمعراج، وجاء فيه:","((ثم أدخلت الجنة فإذا فيها جنابذ اللؤلؤ، وإذا ترابها المسك))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٣٤٩)، ومسلم (١٦٣).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في وصف تربة الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (349) and Muslim (163).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Soil of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Dharr used to narrate that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, while mentioning the story of al-Isrāʾ and al-Miʿrāj: “Then I was admitted into Paradise, and there I saw domes of pearl, and its soil was musk.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":349},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":163}]},{"num":16280,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي سعيد، أن ابن صياد سأل النبي ﷺ عن تربة الجنة؟ فقال:","((درمكة بيضاء مسك خالص))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٩٣:٢٩٢٨).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في وصف تربة الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (93:2928).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Soil of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd narrated that Ibn Ṣayyād asked the Prophet ﷺ about the soil of Paradise. He replied: “Fine white flour, pure musk.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":93}]},{"num":16281,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر بن عبد اللّٰه قال: قال ناس من اليهود لأناس من أصحاب النبي ﷺ: هل يعلم نبيكم كم عدد خزنة جهنم؟ قالوا: لا ندري حتى نسأله، فجاء رجل إلى النبي ﷺ فقال: يا محمد، غلب أصحابك اليوم. قال:","((وبم غلبوا؟)).","قال: سألهم يهود: هل يعلم نبيكم كم عدد خزنة جهنم؟ قال:","((فما قالوا؟)).","قال: قالوا: لا ندري حتى نسأل نبينا. قال:","((أفغلب قوم سئلوا عما لا يعلمون؟ قالوا: لا نعلم حتى نسأل نبينا، لكنهم قد سألوا نبيهم، فقالوا: ﴿أَرِنَا اللَّهَ جَهْرَةً﴾ [النساء: ١٥٣]، علي بأعداء الله، إني سائلهم عن تربة الجنة، وهي الدرمك)).","فلما جاؤوا قالوا: يا أبا القاسم، كم عدد خزنة جهنم؟ قال:","((هكذا وهكذا، في مرة عشرة، وفي مرة تسعة)).","قالوا: نعم، قال لهم النبي ﷺ:","((ما تربة الجنة؟)).","قال: فسكتوا هنيهة، ثم قالوا: خبزة يا أبا القاسم، فقال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((الخبز من الدرمك))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (٣٣٢٧) - واللفظ له -، وأحمد (١٤٨٨٣).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في وصف تربة الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (3327), whose wording this is, and Aḥmad (14883).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Soil of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: Some Jews asked some of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ: “Does your Prophet know how many keepers Hell has?” They replied: “We do not know until we ask him.” A man then came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Muḥammad, your Companions were defeated today.” He asked: “How were they defeated?” The man replied: “The Jews asked them: ‘Does your Prophet know how many keepers Hell has?’” He asked: “What did they say?” He replied: “They said: ‘We do not know until we ask our Prophet.’”","The Prophet ﷺ said: “Are people defeated merely because they were asked about something they did not know and replied, ‘We do not know until we ask our Prophet’? Yet those people asked their own Prophet and said: ‘Show us Allah openly.’ [al-Nisāʾ 4:153] Bring these enemies of Allah to me. I will ask them about the soil of Paradise, which is fine flour.” When they came, they asked: “O Abū al-Qāsim, how many keepers does Hell have?” He gestured like this and like this—once with ten and once with nine.","They said: “Yes.” The Prophet ﷺ then asked them: “What is the soil of Paradise?” They remained silent for a short while, then said: “Bread, O Abū al-Qāsim.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Bread is made from fine flour.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"tirmidhi","label":"الترمذي","number":3327},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":14883,"n":14883}]},{"num":16282,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((صنفان من أهل النار لم أرهما: قوم معهم سياط كأذناب البقر، يضربون بها الناس، ونساء كاسيات عاريات مميلات مائلات، رؤوسهن كأسنمة البخت المائلة، لا يدخلن الجنة، ولا يجدن ريحها، وإن ريحها ليوجد من مسيرة كذا وكذا))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (١٢٥:٢١٢٨).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في ريح الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (125:2128).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Fragrance of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":11,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There are two groups among the people of the Fire whom I have not yet seen: people carrying whips like the tails of cattle, with which they strike the people; and women who are clothed yet naked, inclining others and themselves inclining, their heads like the leaning humps of Bactrian camels. They will not enter Paradise nor smell its fragrance, even though its fragrance can be detected from such-and-such a distance.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":125}]},{"num":16283,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبد اللّٰه بن عمرو، عن النبي ﷺ قال:","((من قتل نفسًا معاهدًا لم يرح رائحة الجنة، وإن ريحها ليوجد من مسيرة أربعين عامًا))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (٦٩١٤).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في ريح الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6914).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Fragrance of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":11,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever kills a person under a covenant of protection will not smell the fragrance of Paradise, even though its fragrance can be detected from a journey of forty years.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6914}]},{"num":16284,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن رجل، عن النبي ﷺ أنه قال:","((سيكون قوم لهم عهد، فمن قتل رجلًا منهم لم يرح رائحة الجنة، وإن ريحها ليوجد من مسيرة سبعين عامًا))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (١٦٥٩٠).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في ريح الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (16590).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Fragrance of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":11,"content":{"translation":{"en":["A man narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “There will be people who have a covenant of protection. Whoever kills one of them will not smell the fragrance of Paradise, even though its fragrance can be detected from a journey of seventy years.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":16590,"n":16590}]},{"num":16285,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة، عن النبي ﷺ قال:","((ألا من قتل نفسًا معاهدًا له ذمة اللّٰه وذمة رسوله، فقد أخفر بذمة الله، فلا يرح رائحة الجنة، وإن ريحها ليوجد من مسيرة سبعين خريفًا))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (١٤٠٣)، وابن ماجه (٢٦٨٧).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في ريح الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (1403) and Ibn Mājah (2687).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Fragrance of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":11,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Indeed, whoever kills a person under covenant who possesses the protection of Allah and the protection of His Messenger has violated the covenant of Allah. He will not smell the fragrance of Paradise, even though its fragrance can be detected from a journey of seventy years.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"tirmidhi","label":"الترمذي","number":1403},{"key":"ibnmajah","label":"ابن ماجه","number":2687}]},{"num":16286,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((من قتل نفسًا معاهدة بغير حقها لم يرح رائحة الجنة، وإن ريح الجنة توجد من مسيرة مائة عام))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الطبراني في الأوسط - مجمع البحرين (٢٤٩٢-٢٤٩١).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في ريح الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Awsaṭ — Majmaʿ al-Baḥrayn (2491-2492).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Fragrance of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":11,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever unlawfully kills a person under covenant will not smell the fragrance of Paradise, even though the fragrance of Paradise can be detected from a journey of one hundred years.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"الطبرانی/الاوسط_مجمع_البحرین","label":"الطبراني في الأوسط - مجمع البحرين","number":2492}]},{"num":16287,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي بكرة قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((من قتل نفسًا معاهدة بغير حلها حرم الله عليه الجنة أن يجد ريحها))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (٢٠٣٨٣).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في ريح الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (20383).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Fragrance of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":11,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Bakrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever unlawfully kills a person under covenant, Allah will forbid him even from smelling the fragrance of Paradise.”"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["ورواه عبد الرزاق (١٠٢/١٠) عن سفيان الثوري به، وزاد:","((وإن ريحها ليوجد من مسيرة مائة عام))."],"en":["ʿAbd al-Razzāq (10/102) also narrated it from Sufyān al-Thawrī and added:","“Its fragrance can be detected from a journey of one hundred years.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":20383,"n":20383}]},{"num":16288,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن الحسن قال: مرض معقل بن يسار مرضًا ثقل فيه، فأتاه ابن زياد يعوده فقال: إني محدثك حديثًا سمعته من رسول اللّٰه ﷺ يقول:","((من استرعي رعية، فلم يحطهم بنصيحة، لم يجد ريح الجنة، وريحها يوجد من مسيرة مائة عام)).","قال ابن زياد: ألا كنت حدثتني بهذا قبل الآن؟ قال: والآن لولا الذي أنت عليه لم أحدثك به."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (٢٠٣١٥).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في ريح الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (20315).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Fragrance of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":11,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Ḥasan narrated: Maʿqil ibn Yasār became seriously ill, and Ibn Ziyād came to visit him. Maʿqil said: “I will narrate to you a hadith that I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: ‘Whoever is entrusted with subjects but does not sincerely look after them will not smell the fragrance of Paradise, though its fragrance can be detected from a journey of one hundred years.’” Ibn Ziyād said: “Why did you not narrate this to me before now?”","He replied: “Even now, were it not for the condition you are in, I would not have narrated it to you.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":20315,"n":20315}]},{"num":16289,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبد اللّٰه بن عمرو، عن النبي ﷺ قال:","((من ادعى إلى غير أبيه لم يرح رائحة الجنة، وإن ريحها ليوجد من مسيرة سبعين عامًا))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (٦٥٩٢) والطيالسي (٢٣٨٨).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في ريح الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (6592) and al-Ṭayālisī (2388).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Fragrance of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":11,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever attributes himself to someone other than his father will not smell the fragrance of Paradise, even though its fragrance can be detected from a journey of seventy years.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"الطیالسی","label":"الطيالسي","number":2388},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":6592,"n":6592},{"key":"tayalisi","label":"مسند أبي داود الطيالسي","number":2388,"n":2388}]},{"num":16290,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبد اللّٰه بن عمرو بن العاص، أن النبي ﷺ قال:","((سيد ريحان أهل الجنة الحناء))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الطبراني في الكبير (٦٠٩/١٣ رقم ١٤٥٢٧).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في ريح الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Kabīr (13/609, no. 14527).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Fragrance of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":11,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The chief fragrant plant of the people of Paradise is henna.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"الطبرانی/الکبیر","label":"الطبراني في الكبير","number":609}]},{"num":16291,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة قال: قلنا: يا رسول الله، حدثنا عن الجنة، ما بناؤها؟ قال:","((لبنة ذهب ولبنة فضة، وملاطها المسك الأذفر، وحصباؤها اللؤلؤ والياقوت، وترابها الزعفران، من يدخلها ينعم ولا يبأس، ويخلد ولا يموت، لا تبلى ثيابه ولا يفنى شبابه))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (٨٠٤٣)، وعبد بن حميد (١٤٢٠)، وصححه ابن حبان (٧٣٨٧).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في لبنة الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (8043) and ʿAbd ibn Ḥumayd (1420), and authenticated by Ibn Ḥibbān (7387).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Bricks of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":12,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated: We said: “O Messenger of Allah, tell us about Paradise. What is its construction like?” He replied: “A brick of gold and a brick of silver. Its mortar is fragrant musk, its pebbles are pearls and rubies, and its soil is saffron. Whoever enters it will live in bliss and never suffer misery, will remain forever and never die, his clothes will never wear out, and his youth will never fade.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"عبد_بن_حمید","label":"عبد بن حميد","number":1420},{"key":"صححہ_ابن_حبان","label":"صححه ابن حبان","number":7387},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":8043,"n":8043},{"key":"ibnhibban","label":"صحيح ابن حبان (التقاسيم والأنواع)","number":5179,"n":5175}]},{"num":16292,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة، عن النبي ﷺ قال:","((بناء الجنة لبنة من ذهب، ولبنة من فضة))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (٨٧٤٧)، والبزار - كشف الأستار - (٣٥٠٩)، والطبراني في الأوسط (٢٥٣٢)، وأبو نعيم في صفة الجنة (١٣٧).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في لبنة الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (8747), al-Bazzār in Kashf al-Astār (3509), al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Awsaṭ (2532), and Abū Nuʿaym in Ṣifat al-Jannah (137).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Bricks of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":12,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The construction of Paradise consists of a brick of gold and a brick of silver.”"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["واللفظ لأحمد، وزاد البزار: ((وملاطها المسك))."],"en":["The wording is Aḥmad’s. Al-Bazzār added: “Its mortar is musk.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"البزار_کشف_الاستار","label":"البزار - كشف الأستار -","number":3509},{"key":"الطبرانی/الاوسط","label":"الطبراني في الأوسط","number":2532},{"key":"ابو_نعیم/صفہ_الجنہ","label":"أبو نعيم في صفة الجنة","number":137},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":8747,"n":8747},{"key":"sh28171","label":"المعجم الأوسط للطبراني","number":2532,"n":2522}]},{"num":16293,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر بن عبد الله قال: قال النبي ﷺ:","((رأيتني دخلت الجنة، فإذا أنا بالرميصاء - امرأة أبي طلحة - وسمعت خشفة، فقلت: من هذا؟ فقال: هذا بلال، ورأيت قصرًا بفنائه جارية، فقلت: لمن هذا؟ فقال: لعمر، فأردت أن أدخله فأنظر إليه، فذكرت غيرتك)).","فقال عمر: بأبي وأمي يا رسول الله! أعليك أغار؟"],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٣٦٧٩)، ومسلم (٦٣٣). وهذا لفظ البخاري، ولفظ مسلم نحوه، وفيه:","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في قصور الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3679) and Muslim (633). This is al-Bukhārī’s wording. Muslim narrated a similar version containing:","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Palaces of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":13,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “I saw myself entering Paradise, and there was al-Rumayṣāʾ—the wife of Abū Ṭalḥah. I heard the sound of footsteps and asked: ‘Who is this?’ It was said: ‘This is Bilāl.’ Then I saw a palace with a young woman in its courtyard. I asked: ‘Whose is this?’ It was said: ‘It belongs to ʿUmar.’ I wanted to enter it and look inside, but I remembered your jealousy.” ʿUmar said: “May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of Allah! Would I be jealous regarding you?”"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["((دخلت الجنة فرأيت فيها دارًا أو قصرًا…)).","وفي آخره: “فبكى عمر وقال: أي رسول اللّٰه، أو عليك يغار؟”.","وفي لفظ للبخاري (٥٢٢٦):","((دخلت الجنة، أو أتيت الجنة، فأبصرت قصرًا، فقلت: لمن هذا؟ قالوا: لعمر بن الخطاب، فأردت أن أدخله، فلم يمنعني إلا علمي بغيرتك)).","وفي لفظ للبخاري (٧٠٢٤):","((دخلت الجنة، فإذا أنا بقصر من ذهب، فقلت: لمن هذا؟ فقالوا: لرجل من قريش، فما منعني أن أدخله…))."],"en":["“I entered Paradise and saw in it a house or a palace…”","At its end, it states:","“ʿUmar wept and said: ‘O Messenger of Allah, would anyone be jealous regarding you?’”","In another wording of al-Bukhārī (5226):","“I entered Paradise—or I came to Paradise—and saw a palace. I asked: ‘Whose is this?’ They said: ‘It belongs to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb.’ I wanted to enter it, and nothing prevented me except my knowledge of your jealousy.”","And in another wording of al-Bukhārī (7024):","“I entered Paradise and saw a palace of gold. I asked: ‘Whose is this?’ They said: ‘It belongs to a man from Quraysh.’ Nothing prevented me from entering it…”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":3679},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":633}]},{"num":16294,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أنس قال: قال رسول الله ﷺ:","((دخلت الجنة، فإذا أنا بقصر من ذهب فقلت: لمن هذا القصر؟ قالوا: لشاب من قريش، فظننت أني أنا هو، فقلت: لمن هو؟ فقالوا: لعمر بن الخطاب)).","قال:","((فلولا ما علمت من غيرتك لدخلته)).","فقال عمر: عليك يا رسول اللّٰه أغار؟"],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الترمذي (٣٦٨٨)، والنسائي في فضائل الصحابة (٢٦)، وأحمد (١٢٠٤٦) - واللفظ له -.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في قصور الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (3688), al-Nasā’ī in Faḍāʾil al-Ṣaḥābah (26), and Aḥmad (12046), whose wording this is.","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Palaces of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":13,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I entered Paradise and saw a palace of gold. I asked: ‘Whose palace is this?’ They said: ‘It belongs to a young man from Quraysh.’ I thought that I was that man, so I asked: ‘Whose is it?’ They replied: ‘It belongs to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb.’” He then said: “Had I not known of your jealousy, I would have entered it.” ʿUmar replied: “Would I be jealous regarding you, O Messenger of Allah?”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"tirmidhi","label":"الترمذي","number":3688},{"key":"nasai/فضایل_الصحابہ","label":"النسائي في فضائل الصحابة","number":26},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":12046,"n":12046}]},{"num":16295,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن سهل بن سعد، عن رسول الله ﷺ قال:","((إن في الجنة لشجرة، يسير الراكب في ظلها مائة عام، لا يقطعها))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه مسلم (٢٨٢٧) والبخاري (٦٥٥٢).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في سعة شجر الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by Muslim (2827) and al-Bukhārī (6552).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Vastness of the Trees of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":14,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Sahl ibn Saʿd narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, in Paradise there is a tree under whose shade a rider could travel for one hundred years without reaching its end.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2827},{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6552}]},{"num":16296,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي سعيد الخدري، عن النبي ﷺ قال:","((إن في الجنة شجرة يسير الراكب الجواد المضمر السريع مائة عام ما يقطعها))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه مسلم (٢٨٢٨) والبخاري (٦٥٥٣).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في سعة شجر الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by Muslim (2828) and al-Bukhārī (6553).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Vastness of the Trees of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":14,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Indeed, in Paradise there is a tree beneath whose shade a rider on a swift, well-trained racing horse could travel for one hundred years without reaching its end.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2828},{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6553}]},{"num":16297,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أنس بن مالك، عن النبي ﷺ قال:","((إن في الجنة لشجرة، يسير الراكب في ظلها مائة عام، لا يقطعها))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (٣٢٥١).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في سعة شجر الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3251).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Vastness of the Trees of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":14,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Indeed, in Paradise there is a tree under whose shade a rider could travel for one hundred years without reaching its end.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":3251}]},{"num":16298,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة، عن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ أنه قال:","((إن في الجنة لشجرة يسير الراكب في ظلها مائة سنة))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٢٨٢٦).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في سعة شجر الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2826).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Vastness of the Trees of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":14,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, in Paradise there is a tree beneath whose shade a rider could travel for one hundred years.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2826}]},{"num":16299,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة، يبلغ به النبي ﷺ قال:","((إن في الجنة شجرة يسير الراكب في ظلها مائة عام، لا يقطعها، واقرؤوا إن شئتم: ﴿وَظِلٍّ مَمْدُودٍ﴾ [سورة الواقعة: ٣٠]))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٤٨٨١)، ومسلم (٧:٢٨٢٦).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في سعة شجر الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4881) and Muslim (7:2826).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Vastness of the Trees of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":14,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated, attributing it to the Prophet ﷺ: “Indeed, in Paradise there is a tree beneath whose shade a rider could travel for one hundred years without reaching its end. Recite, if you wish: ‘And extended shade.’ [al-Wāqiʿah 56:30]”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":4881},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":7}]},{"num":16300,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة، عن النبي ﷺ قال:","((من آمن بالله ورسوله، وأقام الصلاة، وصام رمضان، كان حقًا على اللّٰه أن يدخله الجنة، هاجر في سبيل الله، أو جلس في أرضه التي ولد فيها)).","قالوا: يا رسول الله، أفلا ننبئ الناس بذلك؟ قال:","((إن في الجنة مائة درجة، أعدها اللّٰه للمجاهدين في سبيله، كل درجتين ما بينهما كما بين السماء والأرض، فإذا سألتم اللّٰه فسلوه الفردوس، فإنه أوسط الجنة، وأعلى الجنة، وفوقه عرش الرحمن، ومنه تفجر أنهار الجنة))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (٧٤٢٣).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أن الجنة درجات","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (7423).","chapter_en":"Paradise Has Ranks and Degrees","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":15,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever believes in Allah and His Messenger, establishes the prayer, and fasts Ramaḍān, then it is a right upon Allah to admit him into Paradise, whether he emigrates in the path of Allah or remains in the land in which he was born.” They asked: “O Messenger of Allah, should we not give the people this good news?” He replied: “Indeed, in Paradise there are one hundred ranks which Allah has prepared for those who strive in His path. The distance between every two ranks is like the distance between the heaven and the earth.","So when you ask Allah, ask Him for al-Firdaws, for it is the central and highest part of Paradise. Above it is the Throne of the Most Merciful, and from it the rivers of Paradise spring forth.”"]},"intro":{"ar":["قال الله تعالى:","﴿أُولَٰئِكَ هُمُ الْمُؤْمِنُونَ حَقًّا لَهُمْ دَرَجَاتٌ عِنْدَ رَبِّهِمْ وَمَغْفِرَةٌ وَرِزْقٌ كَرِيمٌ﴾ [الأنفال: ٤].","وقال تعالى:","﴿الَّذِينَ يَرِثُونَ الْفِرْدَوْسَ هُمْ فِيهَا خَالِدُونَ﴾ [سورة المؤمنون: ١١]."],"en":["Allah, the Exalted, says:","“Those are the true believers. For them are ranks with their Lord, forgiveness, and a noble provision.”","[al-Anfāl 8:4]","And He, the Exalted, says:","“Those who will inherit al-Firdaws; they will remain therein forever.”","[al-Muʾminūn 23:11]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":7423}]},{"num":16301,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبادة بن الصامت، أن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال:","((في الجنة مائة درجة، ما بين كل درجتين كما بين السماء والأرض، والفردوس أعلاها درجة، ومنها تفجر أنهار الجنة الأربعة، ومن فوقها يكون العرش، فإذا سألتم الله، فسلوه الفردوس))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الترمذي (٢٥٣١).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أن الجنة درجات","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (2531).","chapter_en":"Paradise Has Ranks and Degrees","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":15,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “In Paradise there are one hundred ranks. The distance between every two ranks is like the distance between the heaven and the earth. Al-Firdaws is the highest of them, and from it the four rivers of Paradise spring forth. Above it is the Throne. So when you ask Allah, ask Him for al-Firdaws.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"tirmidhi","label":"الترمذي","number":2531}]},{"num":16302,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبد اللّٰه بن عمرو بن العاص، أنه سمع النبي ﷺ يقول:","((إذا سمعتم المؤذن، فقولوا مثل ما يقول، ثم صلوا علي، فإنه من صلى علي صلاة صلى اللّٰه عليه بها عشرًا، ثم سلوا اللّٰه لي الوسيلة، فإنها منزلة في الجنة، لا تنبغي إلا لعبد من عباد الله، وأرجو أن أكون أنا هو، فمن سأل لي الوسيلة حلت له الشفاعة))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٣٨٤).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أن الجنة درجات","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (384).","chapter_en":"Paradise Has Ranks and Degrees","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":15,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ narrated that he heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “When you hear the mu’adhdhin, repeat what he says, then invoke blessings upon me, for whoever invokes one blessing upon me, Allah will bless him ten times because of it. Then ask Allah to grant me al-Wasīlah, for it is a rank in Paradise that is fitting for only one servant among the servants of Allah, and I hope that I am that servant. Whoever asks Allah to grant me al-Wasīlah will become entitled to my intercession.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":384}]},{"num":16303,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي نجيح السلمي قال: حاصرنا مع نبي اللّٰه ﷺ حصن الطائف، فسمعت رسول الله ﷺ يقول:","((من بلغ بسهم فله درجة في الجنة)).","قال: فبلغت يومئذ ستة عشر سهمًا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (١٧٠٢٢)، وأبو داود (٣٩٦٥)، والترمذي (١٦٣٨)، والنسائي (٢٦/٦).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أن الجنة درجات","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (17022), Abū Dāwūd (3965), al-Tirmidhī (1638), and al-Nasā’ī (6/26).","chapter_en":"Paradise Has Ranks and Degrees","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":15,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Najīḥ al-Sulamī narrated: We besieged the fortress of al-Ṭā’if together with the Prophet of Allah ﷺ, and I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever shoots an arrow that reaches the enemy will have a rank in Paradise.” He said: “That day I shot sixteen arrows that reached their targets.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"abudawud","label":"أبو داود","number":3965},{"key":"tirmidhi","label":"الترمذي","number":1638},{"key":"nasai","label":"النسائي","number":26},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":17022,"n":17022}]},{"num":16304,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي سعيد الخدري، أن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال:","((يا أبا سعيد، من رضي بالله ربًا، وبالإسلام دينًا، وبمحمد نبيًا، وجبت له الجنة)).","فعجب لها أبو سعيد، فقال: أعدها علي يا رسول اللّٰه، ففعل، ثم قال:","((وأخرى يرفع بها العبد مائة درجة في الجنة، ما بين كل درجتين كما بين السماء والأرض)).","قال: وما هي يا رسول اللّه؟ قال:","((الجهاد في سبيل الله، الجهاد في سبيل الله))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (١٨٨٤).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أن الجنة درجات","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1884).","chapter_en":"Paradise Has Ranks and Degrees","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":15,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Abū Saʿīd, whoever is pleased with Allah as his Lord, Islam as his religion, and Muḥammad as his Prophet, Paradise becomes obligatory for him.” Abū Saʿīd was amazed by this and said: “Repeat it to me, O Messenger of Allah.” So he repeated it, then said: “There is another deed by which a servant is raised one hundred ranks in Paradise, the distance between every two ranks being like the distance between the heaven and the earth.”","He asked: “What is it, O Messenger of Allah?” He replied: “Jihād in the path of Allah. Jihād in the path of Allah.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":1884}]},{"num":16305,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أنس قال: أصيب حارثة يوم بدر وهو غلام، فجاءت أمه إلى النبي ﷺ فقالت: يا رسول الله، قد عرفت منزلة حارثة مني، فإن يك في الجنة أصبر وأحتسب، وإن تكن الأخرى ترى ما أصنع؟ فقال:","((ويحك، أو هبلت؟ أوجنة واحدة هي؟ إنها جنان كثيرة، وإنه لفي جنة الفردوس))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (٦٥٥٠).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أن الجنة درجات","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6550).","chapter_en":"Paradise Has Ranks and Degrees","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":15,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas narrated: Ḥārithah was killed at Badr while still a young boy. His mother came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, you know what place Ḥārithah held in my heart. If he is in Paradise, I will remain patient and seek reward from Allah; but if it is otherwise, you will see what I do.” He replied: “Woe to you! Have you lost your senses? Is there only one Paradise? There are many Gardens, and indeed he is in the Garden of al-Firdaws.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6550}]},{"num":16306,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أنس قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((غدوة في سبيل اللّٰه أو روحة خير من الدنيا وما فيها، ولقاب قوس أحدكم، أو موضع قدم من الجنة خير من الدنيا وما فيها، ولو أن امرأة من نساء أهل الجنة اطلعت إلى الأرض لأضاءت ما بينهما، ولملأت ما بينهما ريحًا، ولنصيفها - يعني الخمار - خير من الدنيا وما فيها))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (٦٥٦٨). ورواه أيضًا (٢٧٩٦) من وجه آخر بلفظ:","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب موضع قدم أو سوط من الجنة خير من الدنيا وما فيها","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6568). He also narrated it through another route (2796) with the wording:","chapter_en":"The Space of a Footstep or Whip in Paradise Is Better Than the World and Everything in It","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":16,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A morning journey in the path of Allah or an evening journey is better than the world and everything in it. The space occupied by the bow of one of you—or the space of a single foot—in Paradise is better than the world and everything in it. And if a woman from among the women of Paradise were to look toward the earth, she would illuminate everything between them and fill everything between them with fragrance. Even her head-covering is better than the world and everything in it.”"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["((ولقاب قوس أحدكم من الجنة، أو موضع قيد - يعني: سوطه - خير من الدنيا وما فيها…)).","الحديث."],"en":["“The space occupied by the bow of one of you in Paradise, or the space occupied by his whip, is better than the world and everything in it…”","The hadith continues."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6568},{"key":"ورواہ_ایضا","label":". ورواه أيضًا","number":2796}]},{"num":16307,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن سهل بن سعد قال: سمعت النبي ﷺ يقول:","((موضع سوط في الجنة خير من الدنيا وما فيها، ولغدوة في سبيل اللّٰه أو روحة خير من الدنيا وما فيها))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٦٤١٥)، ومسلم (١٨٨١).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب موضع قدم أو سوط من الجنة خير من الدنيا وما فيها","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6415) and Muslim (1881).","chapter_en":"The Space of a Footstep or Whip in Paradise Is Better Than the World and Everything in It","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":16,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Sahl ibn Saʿd narrated: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “The space occupied by a whip in Paradise is better than the world and everything in it, and a morning journey in the path of Allah or an evening journey is better than the world and everything in it.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6415},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":1881}]},{"num":16308,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة، عن النبي ﷺ قال:","((لقاب قوس في الجنة خير مما تطلع عليه الشمس وتغرب)).","وقال:","((لغدوة أو روحة في سبيل اللّٰه خير مما تطلع عليه الشمس وتغرب))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (٢٧٩٣).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب موضع قدم أو سوط من الجنة خير من الدنيا وما فيها","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (2793).","chapter_en":"The Space of a Footstep or Whip in Paradise Is Better Than the World and Everything in It","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":16,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The space occupied by a bow in Paradise is better than everything upon which the sun rises and sets.” And he said: “A morning journey or an evening journey in the path of Allah is better than everything upon which the sun rises and sets.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":2793}]},{"num":16309,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((قيد سوط أحدكم من الجنة خير من الدنيا ومثلها معها، ولقاب قوس أحدكم من الجنة خير من الدنيا ومثلها معها، ولنصيف امرأة من الجنة خير من الدنيا ومثلها معها)).","قال: قلت: يا أبا هريرة: ما النصيف؟ قال: “الخمار”."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (١٠٢٧٠) - واللفظ له -، وأبو نعيم في صفة الجنة (٥٩).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب موضع قدم أو سوط من الجنة خير من الدنيا وما فيها","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (10270), whose wording this is, and Abū Nuʿaym in Ṣifat al-Jannah (59).","chapter_en":"The Space of a Footstep or Whip in Paradise Is Better Than the World and Everything in It","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":16,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The space occupied by the whip of one of you in Paradise is better than this world and another world equal to it. The space occupied by the bow of one of you in Paradise is better than this world and another world equal to it. And the head-covering of a woman from Paradise is better than this world and another world equal to it.” The narrator said: I asked Abū Hurayrah: “What is the naṣīf?”","He replied: “The head-covering.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ابو_نعیم/صفہ_الجنہ","label":"أبو نعيم في صفة الجنة","number":59},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":10270,"n":10270}]},{"num":16310,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أنس قال: أهدي للنبي ﷺ جبة سندس، وكان ينهى عن الحرير، فعجب الناس منها، فقال:","((والذي نفس محمد بيده، لمناديل سعد بن معاذ في الجنة أحسن من هذا))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٢٦١٥)، ومسلم (٢٤٦٩).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في مناديل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (2615) and Muslim (2469).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Handkerchiefs of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":17,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas narrated: A garment of fine silk was gifted to the Prophet ﷺ, although he used to prohibit silk. The people were amazed by it. He said: “By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muḥammad, the handkerchiefs of Saʿd ibn Muʿādh in Paradise are finer than this.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":2615},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2469}]},{"num":16311,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أسماء بنت أبي بكر قالت: سمعت رسول اللّٰه ﷺ، وذكر سدرة المنتهى، قال:","((يسير الراكب في ظل الفنن منها مائة سنة، أو يستظل بظلها مائة راكب - شك يحيى - فيها فراش الذهب كأن ثمرها القلال))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (٢٥٤١)، وهناد بن السري في الزهد (١١٥)، وابن جرير في تفسيره (٣٩-٣٨٢٢).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في ثمار الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (2541), Hannād ibn al-Sarī in al-Zuhd (115), and Ibn Jarīr in his Tafsīr (39-3822).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Fruits of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":18,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Asmāʾ bint Abī Bakr narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mention Sidrat al-Muntahā and say: “A rider could travel beneath the shade of one of its branches for one hundred years—or one hundred riders could take shade beneath it,” Yaḥyā was uncertain which wording was used, “and upon it are golden moths, while its fruits are like large jars.”"]},"intro":{"ar":["قال تعالى:","﴿وَبَشِّرِ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَعَمِلُوا الصَّالِحَاتِ أَنَّ لَهُمْ جَنَّاتٍ تَجْرِي مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْأَنْهَارُ كُلَّمَا رُزِقُوا مِنْهَا مِنْ ثَمَرَةٍ رِزْقًا قَالُوا هَٰذَا الَّذِي رُزِقْنَا مِنْ قَبْلُ وَأُتُوا بِهِ مُتَشَابِهًا وَلَهُمْ فِيهَا أَزْوَاجٌ مُطَهَّرَةٌ وَهُمْ فِيهَا خَالِدُونَ﴾ [سورة البقرة: ٢٥].","وقال تعالى:","﴿فِيهِمَا فَاكِهَةٌ وَنَخْلٌ وَرُمَّانٌ﴾ [سورة الرحمن: ٦٨]."],"en":["Allah, the Exalted, says:","“Give glad tidings to those who believe and perform righteous deeds that they will have Gardens beneath which rivers flow. Whenever they are provided with fruit from them, they will say: ‘This is what we were provided with before,’ and they will be given things resembling one another. They will have purified spouses therein, and they will remain therein forever.”","[al-Baqarah 2:25]","And He, the Exalted, says:","“In both of them are fruits, date-palms, and pomegranates.”","[al-Raḥmān 55:68]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"tirmidhi","label":"الترمذي","number":2541},{"key":"ہناد_بن_السری/الزہد","label":"هناد بن السري في الزهد","number":115},{"key":"ابن_جریر/تفسیرہ","label":"ابن جرير في تفسيره","number":39}]},{"num":16312,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي أمامة قال: كان أصحاب رسول اللّٰه ﷺ يقولون: إن اللّٰه ينفعنا بالأعراب ومسائلهم، أقبل أعرابي يومًا، فقال: يا رسول الله، لقد ذكر اللّٰه في القرآن شجرة مؤذية، وما كنت أرى أن في الجنة شجرة تؤذي صاحبها. فقال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((وما هي؟)).","قال: السدر، فإن لها شوكًا. فقال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","﴿فِي سِدْرٍ مَخْضُودٍ﴾ [الواقعة: ٢٨]","((يخضد اللّٰه شوكه فيجعل مكان كل شوكة ثمرة، فإنها تنبت ثمرًا تفتق الثمرة منها عن اثنين وسبعين لونًا، ما منها لون يشبه الآخر))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الحاكم (٤٧٦/٢)، وعنه البيهقي في البعث والنشور (٢٦٤).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في ثمار الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Ḥākim (2/476), and from him by al-Bayhaqī in al-Baʿth wa-l-Nushūr (264).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Fruits of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":18,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Umāmah narrated: The Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: “Allah benefits us through the Bedouins and the questions they ask.” One day a Bedouin came and said: “O Messenger of Allah, Allah has mentioned in the Qurʾān a tree that causes harm, and I never thought there would be a tree in Paradise that could harm its owner.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked: “Which tree is that?” He replied: “The lote-tree, because it has thorns.”","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “‘Among thornless lote-trees.’ [al-Wāqiʿah 56:28] Allah will remove its thorns and place a fruit in the place of every thorn. It will bear fruits, each of which will open into seventy-two varieties, no variety resembling another.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"عنہ_البیہقی/البعث_والنشور","label":"عنه البيهقي في البعث والنشور","number":264},{"key":"hakim","label":"المستدرك على الصحيحين","number":3778,"n":3765}]},{"num":16313,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عتبة بن عبد السلمي قال: كنت جالسًا مع رسول اللّٰه ﷺ فجاء أعرابي، فقال: يا رسول الله، أسمعك تذكر شجرة في الجنة لا أعلم في الدنيا أكثر شوكًا منها - يعني الطلح -، فقال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((يجعل مكان كل شوكة مثل خصوة التيس الملبود - يعني الخصي -، فيها سبعون لونًا من الطعام لا يشبه لون الآخر))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الطبراني في الكبير (١٣٠/١٧)، ومسند الشاميين (٤٩٢).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في ثمار الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Kabīr (17/130) and Musnad al-Shāmiyyīn (492).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Fruits of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":18,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿUtbah ibn ʿAbd al-Sulamī narrated: I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a Bedouin came and said: “O Messenger of Allah, I hear you mentioning a tree in Paradise, yet I know of no tree in this world with more thorns than it”—meaning the ṭalḥ tree. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “In place of every thorn there will be something like the testicle of a thick-haired he-goat—meaning a castrated one—containing seventy varieties of food, no one variety resembling another.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"الطبرانی/الکبیر","label":"الطبراني في الكبير","number":130},{"key":"مسند_الشامیین","label":"مسند الشاميين","number":492}]},{"num":16314,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عتبة بن عبد السلمي قال: جاء أعرابي إلى رسول اللّه ﷺ، فقال: ما حوضك تحدث عنه؟ قال:","((كما بين البيضاء إلى بصرى، يمدني اللّٰه فيه بكراع لا يدري إنسان ممن خلق أين طرفاه)).","فكبر عمر بن الخطاب، فقال:","((أما الحوض فيرد عليه فقراء المهاجرين الذين يقاتلون في سبيل الله، ويموتون في سبيل الله. فأرجو أن يورثني الكراع فأشرب منه)).","وقال رسول اللّه ﷺ:","((إن ربي وعدني أن يدخل الجنة من أمتي سبعين ألفًا بغير حساب، ثم يشفع كل ألف بسبعين ألفًا، ثم يحثي ربي تبارك وتعالى بكفيه ثلاث حثيات)).","فكبر عمر وقال: إن السبعين الأولى ليشفعهم اللّٰه في آبائهم، وأبنائهم، وعشائرهم. وأرجو أن يجعلني اللّٰه في إحدى الحثيات الأواخر.","فقال الأعرابي: يا رسول الله، فيها فاكهة؟ قال:","((نعم، وفيها شجرة تدعى طوبى هي تطابق الفردوس)).","فقال: أي شجر أرضنا تشبه؟ قال:","((ليس تشبه من شجر أرضك، ولكن أتيت الشام؟)).","قال: لا يا رسول اللّه، قال:","((فإنها تشبه شجرة في الشام تدعى الجوزة تنبت على ساق واحد، ثم ينتشر أعلاها)).","قال: فما عظم أصلها؟ قال:","((لو ارتحلت جذعة من إبل أهلك لما قطعتها حتى تنكسر ترقوتها هرمًا)).","قال: فيها عنب؟ قال:","((نعم)).","قال: ما عظم العنقود منها؟ قال:","((مسيرة شهر للغراب الأبقع لا ينثني ولا يفتر)).","قال: فما عظم الحبة منه؟ قال: هل ذبح أبوك من غنمه تيسًا عظيمًا؟ قال: نعم. قال:","((فسلخ إهابه فأعطاه أمك، فقال: ادبغي هذا، ثم افري لنا منه ذنوبًا نروي به ماشيتنا)).","قال: نعم. قال: فإن تلك الحبة تشبعني وأهل بيتي؟ فقال النبي ﷺ:","((وعامة عشيرتك))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الطبراني في الأوسط (٤٠٤) - واللفظ له -، وفي الكبير (١٢٧-١٢٦/١٧)، وأحمد (١٧٦٤٢).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في ثمار الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Awsaṭ (404), whose wording this is, in al-Muʿjam al-Kabīr (17/126-127), and by Aḥmad (17642).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Fruits of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":18,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿUtbah ibn ʿAbd al-Sulamī narrated: A Bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked: “What is this Ḥawḍ that you speak about?” He replied: “It is like the distance between al-Bayḍāʾ and Buṣrā. Allah supplies it for me through an inlet whose two ends no created person knows.” ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb proclaimed Allah’s greatness. The Prophet ﷺ said: “As for the Ḥawḍ, the poor among the Muhājirūn who fight in the path of Allah and die in His path will come to it. I hope that the inlet will be granted to me so that I may drink from it.”","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ also said: “My Lord has promised me that seventy thousand from my Ummah will enter Paradise without reckoning. Then every thousand of them will intercede for seventy thousand, and then my Lord, Blessed and Exalted, will take three handfuls with His two Hands.” ʿUmar proclaimed Allah’s greatness and said: “The first seventy thousand will surely be enabled by Allah to intercede for their fathers, children, and clans. I hope that Allah will place me among one of the last three handfuls.”","The Bedouin asked: “O Messenger of Allah, does Paradise contain fruit?” He replied: “Yes. In it is a tree called Ṭūbā, which extends throughout al-Firdaws.” The Bedouin asked: “Which tree from our land does it resemble?” He replied: “It does not resemble any tree from your land. But have you been to al-Shām?” He replied: “No, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “It resembles a tree in al-Shām called the walnut tree. It grows from a single trunk, then spreads out above.”","He asked: “How large is its trunk?” He replied: “If a young she-camel from the camels of your family were to set out traveling around it, she would not complete the circuit before her collarbone broke from old age.” He asked: “Does it have grapes?” He replied: “Yes.” He asked: “How large is a cluster?” He replied: “A piebald crow could fly for a month without turning aside or tiring before traversing it.” He asked: “How large is a single grape?” The Prophet ﷺ asked: “Has your father ever slaughtered a large he-goat from his sheep?”","He replied: “Yes.” He said: “Did he skin it and give its hide to your mother, saying: ‘Tan this, then make from it a large bucket with which we can give our livestock enough water’?” He replied: “Yes.” The Bedouin asked: “Would one such grape satisfy me and my household?” The Prophet ﷺ replied: “And most of your clan as well.”"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["وقوله: ((بكراع)) أي بطرف من ماء الجنة. قال في النهاية: وفي حديث الحوض: ((فيمده اللّٰه بكراع)) أي طرف من ماء الجنة، فشبه بالكراع لقلته، وأنه كالكراع من الدابة."],"en":["Regarding the phrase “through an inlet” (بكراع), the author explains that it means an extremity or channel of water from Paradise. In al-Nihāyah, regarding the hadith of the Ḥawḍ, the phrase means that Allah supplies it through an extremity of the water of Paradise. It is compared to the lower leg of an animal because of its relative narrowness."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"الطبرانی/الاوسط","label":"الطبراني في الأوسط","number":404},{"key":"وفی_الکبیر","label":"وفي الكبير","number":127},{"key":"sh28171","label":"المعجم الأوسط للطبراني","number":402,"n":400},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":17642,"n":17642}]},{"num":16315,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر بن عبد اللّٰه قال: كسفت الشمس على عهد رسول اللّٰه ﷺ في يوم شديد الحر، فذكر الحديث وجاء فيه: ثم قال:","((إنه عرض علي كل شيء تولجونه، فعرضت علي الجنة، حتى لو تناولت منها قطفًا أخذته - أو قال: تناولت منها قطفًا - فقصرت يدي عنه…))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٩٠٤).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في ثمار الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (904).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Fruits of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":18,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: The sun was eclipsed during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on an intensely hot day. In the hadith, the Prophet ﷺ said: “Everything that you will enter was shown to me. Paradise was shown to me, to the point that if I had reached for a cluster from it, I would have taken it”—or he said: “I reached for a cluster from it, but my hand fell short of it…”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":904}]},{"num":16316,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبد اللّٰه بن عباس قال: انخسفت الشمس على عهد رسول اللّٰه ﷺ، فذكر الحديث في صلاة الخسوف، وجاء فيه: قالوا: يا رسول الله، رأيناك تناولت شيئًا في مقامك، ثم رأيناك تكعكعت؟ قال النبي ﷺ:","((إني رأيت الجنة، فتناولت عنقودًا، ولو أصبته لأكلتم منه ما بقيت الدنيا…)).","الحديث."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (١٠٥٢)، ومسلم (٩٠٧).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في ثمار الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (1052) and Muslim (907).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Fruits of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":18,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās narrated: The sun was eclipsed during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. In the hadith concerning the eclipse prayer, they said: “O Messenger of Allah, we saw you reaching for something while standing, then we saw you draw back.” The Prophet ﷺ replied: “I saw Paradise and reached for a cluster of grapes. Had I obtained it, you would have eaten from it for as long as this world remained.” The hadith continues."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":1052},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":907}]},{"num":16317,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أنس بن مالك قال: صلينا مع رسول اللّٰه ﷺ صلاة الصبح، قال: فبينما هو في الصلاة مد يده، ثم أخرها، فلما فرغ من الصلاة قلنا: يا رسول الله، صنعت في صلاتك هذه ما لم تكن تصنع؟ قال:","((إني رأيت الجنة، فرأيت دالية منها تدلت عناقيدها، كالدباء، فأردت أن أتناول منها، فأوحي إليها أن استأخري فاستأخرت، ثم عرضت علي النار بيني وبينكم حتى رأيت ظلي وظلكم، فأومأت إليكم أن استأخروا، فأوحي إلي أن أقرهم، فإنك أسلمت وأسلموا، وهاجرت وهاجروا، وجاهدت وجاهدوا، فلم أر لي عليكم فضلًا إلا بالنبوة))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه ابن خزيمة (٨٩٢)، والطحاوي في شرح المشكل (٥٧٦٢)، والحاكم (٤٥٦/٤).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في ثمار الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Ibn Khuzaymah (892), al-Ṭaḥāwī in Sharḥ al-Mushkil (5762), and al-Ḥākim (4/456).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Fruits of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":18,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik narrated: We prayed the dawn prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. While he was praying, he extended his hand and then drew it back. When he finished the prayer, we asked: “O Messenger of Allah, during this prayer you did something we had not seen you do before.” He replied: “I saw Paradise and saw within it a grapevine whose clusters were hanging down like gourds. I wanted to take from it, but it was revealed to it: ‘Move back,’ so it moved back.","Then the Fire was shown to me between myself and you, until I could see my shadow and your shadows. I gestured to you to move back. Then it was revealed to me: ‘Keep them in their places. You submitted and they submitted; you emigrated and they emigrated; you struggled and they struggled.’ So I saw no superiority that I had over you except Prophethood.”"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["وأما قوله تعالى:","﴿كُلَّمَا رُزِقُوا مِنْهَا مِنْ ثَمَرَةٍ رِزْقًا قَالُوا هَٰذَا الَّذِي رُزِقْنَا مِنْ قَبْلُ وَأُتُوا بِهِ مُتَشَابِهًا﴾ [البقرة: ٢٥]","فمعناها متشابهًا في اللون والمنظر، ومختلفًا في الطعم والذوق، ولو كانت ثمار الدنيا نزلت من الجنة مع آدم كما جاء في بعض الآثار لما اختلف طعمها وذوقها. لأن قوله تعالى: ﴿هَٰذَا الَّذِي رُزِقْنَا مِنْ قَبْلُ﴾ أي في الدنيا كما قال ابن مسعود وابن عباس وجماعة من الصحابة والتابعين، وهو الذي رجحه ابن جرير في تفسيره."],"en":["As for the statement of Allah, the Exalted:","“Whenever they are provided with fruit from it, they will say: ‘This is what we were provided with before,’ and they will be given things resembling one another.”","[al-Baqarah 2:25]","the author explains that they will resemble one another in color and appearance while differing in taste and flavor.","If the fruits of this world had descended from Paradise together with Ādam, as is mentioned in some reports, then their tastes and flavors would not differ.","The statement:","“This is what we were provided with before”","means: in the worldly life, as stated by Ibn Masʿūd, Ibn ʿAbbās, and a group of the Companions and Followers. This is also the interpretation preferred by Ibn Jarīr in his Tafsīr."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ابن_خزیمہ","label":"ابن خزيمة","number":892},{"key":"الطحاوی/شرح_المشکل","label":"الطحاوي في شرح المشكل","number":5762},{"key":"hakim","label":"الحاكم","number":456}]},{"num":16318,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أنس قال: سمع عبد الله بن سلام بقدوم رسول اللّٰه ﷺ وهو في أرض يخترف، فأتى النبي ﷺ، فقال: إني سائلك عن ثلاث لا يعلمهن إلا نبي: فما أول أشراط الساعة؟ وما أول طعام أهل الجنة؟ وما ينزع الولد إلى أبيه أو إلى أمه؟ قال:","((أخبرني بهن جبريل آنفًا)).","قال: جبريل؟! قال:","((نعم)).","قال: ذاك عدو اليهود من الملائكة، فقرأ هذه الآية:","﴿مَنْ كَانَ عَدُوًّا لِجِبْرِيلَ فَإِنَّهُ نَزَّلَهُ عَلَىٰ قَلْبِكَ﴾ [سورة البقرة: ٩٧].","((أما أول أشراط الساعة فنار تحشر الناس من المشرق إلى المغرب. وأما أول طعام أهل الجنة فزيادة كبد حوت. وإذا سبق ماء الرجل ماء المرأة نزع الولد، وإذا سبق ماء المرأة نزعت)).","قال: أشهد أن لا إله إلا اللّٰه، وأشهد أنك رسول الله…. الحديث."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (٤٤٨٠).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ذكر أول طعام يأكله أهل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4480).","chapter_en":"The First Food Eaten by the People of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":19,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas narrated: ʿAbdullāh ibn Salām heard that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had arrived while he was in a field gathering fruit. So he came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “I will ask you about three things that none knows except a Prophet: What is the first sign of the Hour? What is the first food the people of Paradise will eat? And what causes a child to resemble his father or his mother?” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Jibrīl informed me of them just now.”","He said: “Jibrīl?!” The Prophet ﷺ replied: “Yes.” He said: “He is the enemy of the Jews among the angels.” So the Prophet ﷺ recited: “Whoever is an enemy to Jibrīl—indeed, he has brought it down upon your heart.” [al-Baqarah 2:97] Then he said: “As for the first sign of the Hour, it is a fire that will gather the people from the east to the west. As for the first food of the people of Paradise, it will be the extra portion of a fish’s liver. And if the man’s fluid precedes the woman’s fluid, the child will resemble him; and if the woman’s fluid precedes, the child will resemble her.”","ʿAbdullāh ibn Salām said: “I testify that there is no deity except Allah, and I testify that you are the Messenger of Allah…” The hadith continues."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":4480}]},{"num":16319,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي سعيد الخدري، عن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال:","((تكون الأرض يوم القيامة خبزة واحدة، يكفؤها الجبار بيده، كما يكفأ أحدكم خبزته في السفر، نزلًا لأهل الجنة)).","قال: فأتى رجل من اليهود، فقال: بارك الرحمن عليك، أبا القاسم، ألا أخبرك بنزل أهل الجنة يوم القيامة؟ قال:","((بلى)).","قال: تكون الأرض خبزة واحدة - كما قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ - قال: فنظر إلينا رسول اللّٰه ﷺ، ثم ضحك حتى بدت نواجذه، قال: ألا أخبرك بإدامهم؟ قال:","((بلى)).","قال: إدامهم بالام ونون، قالوا: وما هذا؟ قال:","((ثور ونون، يأكل من زائدة كبدهما سبعون ألفًا))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٦٥٢٠)، ومسلم (٢٧٩٢).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ذكر أول طعام يأكله أهل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6520) and Muslim (2792).","chapter_en":"The First Food Eaten by the People of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":19,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “On the Day of Resurrection, the earth will become a single loaf of bread. The Almighty will turn it over with His Hand just as one of you turns over his bread while traveling, as hospitality for the people of Paradise.” Then a Jewish man came and said: “May the Most Merciful bless you, O Abū al-Qāsim. Shall I tell you about the hospitality of the people of Paradise on the Day of Resurrection?”","He replied: “Yes.” The man said: “The earth will become a single loaf of bread,” just as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had said. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at us and laughed until his molar teeth became visible. The man then said: “Shall I tell you what their accompanying dish will be?” He replied: “Yes.” He said: “Their accompanying dish will be bālām and nūn.” They asked: “What are those?” He replied: “An ox and a fish. Seventy thousand people will eat from the extra portions of their livers.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6520},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2792}]},{"num":16320,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن ثوبان مولى رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال: كنت قائمًا عند رسول اللّٰه ﷺ، فجاء حبر من أحبار اليهود، فقال: السلام عليك يا محمد! فدفعته دفعة كاد يصرع منها. فقال: لم تدفعني؟ فقلت: ألا تقول: يا رسول الله؟ فقال اليهودي: إنما ندعوه باسمه الذي سماه به أهله. فقال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((إن اسمي محمد الذي سماني به أهلي)).","فقال اليهودي: جئت أسألك. فقال له رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((أينفعك شيء إن حدثتك؟)).","قال: أسمع بأذني، فنكت رسول اللّٰه ﷺ بعود معه فقال:","((سل)).","فقال اليهودي: أين يكون الناس يوم تبدل الأرض غير الأرض والسماوات؟ فقال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((هم في الظلمة دون الجسر)).","قال: فمن أول الناس إجازة؟ قال:","((فقراء المهاجرين)).","قال اليهودي: فما تحفتهم حين يدخلون الجنة؟ قال:","((زيادة كبد النون)).","قال: فما غذاؤهم على إثرها؟ قال:","((ينحر لهم ثور الجنة الذي كان يأكل من أطرافها)).","قال: فما شرابهم عليه؟ قال:","((من عين فيها تسمى سلسبيلًا)).","قال: صدقت… الحديث."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٣١٥).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ذكر أول طعام يأكله أهل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (315).","chapter_en":"The First Food Eaten by the People of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":19,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Thawbān, the freedman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, narrated: I was standing with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a Jewish scholar came and said: “Peace be upon you, O Muḥammad.” I pushed him so forcefully that he nearly fell. He asked: “Why did you push me?” I said: “Why do you not say, ‘O Messenger of Allah’?” The Jewish man replied: “We only call him by the name his family gave him.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “My name is Muḥammad, the name by which my family named me.”","The Jewish man said: “I have come to ask you questions.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked: “Will it benefit you if I answer you?” He replied: “I will listen with my ears.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ began drawing with a stick he had and said: “Ask.” The Jewish man asked: “Where will the people be on the Day when the earth is changed into another earth and the heavens as well?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “They will be in darkness before the bridge.”","He asked: “Who will be the first people to cross?” He replied: “The poor among the Muhājirūn.” The Jewish man asked: “What will be their welcoming food when they enter Paradise?” He replied: “The extra portion of the fish’s liver.” He asked: “What will their food be after that?” He replied: “The ox of Paradise that used to graze along its edges will be slaughtered for them.” He asked: “What will they drink with it?” He replied: “From a spring therein called Salsabīl.”","The Jewish man said: “You have spoken the truth…” The hadith continues."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":315}]},{"num":16321,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أنس بن مالك قال: سئل رسول اللّٰه ﷺ: ما الكوثر؟ قال:","((ذاك نهر أعطانيه اللّه - يعني في الجنة - أشد بياضًا من اللبن، وأحلى من العسل، فيها طير أعناقها كأعناق الجزر)).","قال عمر: إن هذه لناعمة! قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((أكلتها أحسن منها))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (٢٥٤٢).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في طير الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (2542).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Birds of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":20,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked: “What is al-Kawthar?” He replied: “It is a river Allah has given me—meaning in Paradise—whiter than milk and sweeter than honey. In it are birds whose necks are like the necks of camels.” ʿUmar said: “Those must indeed be delightful!” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “Those who eat them are even better than they are.”"]},"intro":{"ar":["قال تعالى:","﴿وَلَحْمِ طَيْرٍ مِمَّا يَشْتَهُونَ﴾ [الواقعة: ٢١]."],"en":["Allah, the Exalted, says:","“And the meat of birds from whatever they desire.”","[al-Wāqiʿah 56:21]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"tirmidhi","label":"الترمذي","number":2542}]},{"num":16322,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن معاوية بن حيدة القشيري قال: سمعت رسول اللّٰه ﷺ يقول:","((إن في الجنة بحر الماء، وبحر العسل، وبحر اللبن، وبحر الخمر، ثم تشقق الأنهار بعد))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (٢٥٧١)، وأحمد (٢٠٠٥٢).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في أنهار الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (2571) and Aḥmad (20052).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Rivers of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":21,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Muʿāwiyah ibn Ḥaydah al-Qushayrī narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “In Paradise there is a sea of water, a sea of honey, a sea of milk, and a sea of wine. Then the rivers branch out from them afterward.”"]},"intro":{"ar":["قال تعالى:","﴿مَثَلُ الْجَنَّةِ الَّتِي وُعِدَ الْمُتَّقُونَ فِيهَا أَنْهَارٌ مِنْ مَاءٍ غَيْرِ آسِنٍ وَأَنْهَارٌ مِنْ لَبَنٍ لَمْ يَتَغَيَّرْ طَعْمُهُ وَأَنْهَارٌ مِنْ خَمْرٍ لَذَّةٍ لِلشَّارِبِينَ وَأَنْهَارٌ مِنْ عَسَلٍ مُصَفًّى وَلَهُمْ فِيهَا مِنْ كُلِّ الثَّمَرَاتِ وَمَغْفِرَةٌ مِنْ رَبِّهِمْ﴾ [محمد: ١٥]."],"en":["Allah, the Exalted, says:","“The description of the Paradise promised to the righteous is that in it are rivers of water whose taste and smell do not change, rivers of milk whose taste does not change, rivers of wine delightful to those who drink it, and rivers of purified honey. They will have therein every kind of fruit and forgiveness from their Lord.”","[Muḥammad 47:15]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"tirmidhi","label":"الترمذي","number":2571},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":20052,"n":20052}]},{"num":16323,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة، عن النبي ﷺ، قال:","((إن في الجنة مائة درجة، أعدها اللّٰه للمجاهدين في سبيله، كل درجتين ما بينهما كما بين السماء والأرض، فإذا سألتم اللّٰه فسلوه الفردوس، فإنه أوسط الجنة، وأعلى الجنة، وفوقه عرش الرحمن، ومنه تفجر أنهار الجنة))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (٧٤٢٣).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في أنهار الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (7423).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Rivers of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":21,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “In Paradise there are one hundred ranks which Allah has prepared for those who strive in His path. The distance between every two ranks is like the distance between the heaven and the earth. So when you ask Allah, ask Him for al-Firdaws, for it is the central and highest part of Paradise. Above it is the Throne of the Most Merciful, and from it the rivers of Paradise spring forth.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":7423}]},{"num":16324,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبادة بن الصامت، أن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال:","((في الجنة مائة درجة، ما بين كل درجتين كما بين السماء والأرض، والفردوس أعلاها درجة، ومنها تفجر أنهار الجنة الأربعة، ومن فوقها يكون العرش، فإذا سألتم الله، فسلوه الفردوس))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الترمذي (٢٥٣١)، وابن خزيمة في “التوحيد” (١٨٤)، والحاكم (٨٠/١).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في أنهار الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (2531), Ibn Khuzaymah in al-Tawḥīd (184), and al-Ḥākim (1/80).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Rivers of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":21,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “In Paradise there are one hundred ranks, the distance between every two ranks being like the distance between the heaven and the earth. Al-Firdaws is the highest of them, and from it the four rivers of Paradise spring forth. Above it is the Throne. So when you ask Allah, ask Him for al-Firdaws.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"tirmidhi","label":"الترمذي","number":2531},{"key":"ابن_خزیمہ/التوحید","label":"ابن خزيمة في “التوحيد”","number":184},{"key":"hakim","label":"الحاكم","number":80}]},{"num":16325,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((أنهار الجنة تخرج من تلال - أو من تحت جبال - مسك))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه ابن أبي حاتم كما في تفسير ابن كثير (٣٨٦/٨) وابن حبان (٧٤٠٨)، وأبو نعيم في صفة الجنة (٣١٣).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في أنهار الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Ibn Abī Ḥātim, as cited in Ibn Kathīr’s Tafsīr (8/386), Ibn Ḥibbān (7408), and Abū Nuʿaym in Ṣifat al-Jannah (313).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Rivers of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":21,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The rivers of Paradise emerge from hills—or from beneath mountains—of musk.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ابن_ابی_حاتم_کما/تفسیر_ابن_کثیر","label":"ابن أبي حاتم كما في تفسير ابن كثير","number":386},{"key":"ابو_نعیم/صفہ_الجنہ","label":"أبو نعيم في صفة الجنة","number":313},{"key":"ibnhibban","label":"صحيح ابن حبان (التقاسيم والأنواع)","number":5201,"n":5197}]},{"num":16326,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي أمامة الباهلي قال: سمعت رسول اللّٰه ﷺ يقول:","((بينا أنا نائم إذ أتاني رجلان، فأخذا بضبعي، فأتيا بي جبلًا وعرًا)).","فذكر حديثًا طويلًا وجاء فيه:","((فإذا أنا بالغلمان يلعبون بين نهرين، فقلت: من هؤلاء؟ قال: هؤلاء ذراري المؤمنين، ثم شرف بي شرفًا، فإذا أنا بثلاثة يشربون من خمر لهم، فقلت: من هؤلاء؟ قالوا: هذا إبراهيم، وموسى، وعيسى، وهم ينتظرونك))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه ابن خزيمة (١٩٨٦)، وعنه ابن حبان (٧٤٩١)، والحاكم (٤٣٠/١).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في أنهار الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Ibn Khuzaymah (1986), from him by Ibn Ḥibbān (7491), and by al-Ḥākim (1/430).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Rivers of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":21,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Umāmah al-Bāhilī narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “While I was sleeping, two men came to me, took me by my upper arms, and brought me to a rugged mountain.” He then mentioned a lengthy hadith, in which he said: “Then I saw young boys playing between two rivers. I asked: ‘Who are these?’ He said: ‘These are the children of the believers.’ Then I was taken up to a high place, and I saw three men drinking wine of their own. I asked: ‘Who are these?’","They said: ‘This is Ibrāhīm, Mūsā, and ʿĪsā, and they are waiting for you.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ابن_خزیمہ","label":"ابن خزيمة","number":1986},{"key":"عنہ_ابن_حبان","label":"عنه ابن حبان","number":7491},{"key":"hakim","label":"الحاكم","number":430},{"key":"ibnhibban","label":"صحيح ابن حبان (التقاسيم والأنواع)","number":3019,"n":3016}]},{"num":16327,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((سيحان وجيحان، والفرات والنيل، كل من أنهار الجنة))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٢٨٣٩).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما في الدنيا من أنهار الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2839).","chapter_en":"Rivers in This World That Are from the Rivers of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":22,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Sayḥān, Jayḥān, the Euphrates, and the Nile are all among the rivers of Paradise.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2839}]},{"num":16328,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((فجرت أربعة أنهار من الجنة: الفرات، والنيل، وسيحان، وجيحان))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (٧٥٤٤)، وأبو يعلى (٥٩٢١).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما في الدنيا من أنهار الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (7544) and Abū Yaʿlā (5921).","chapter_en":"Rivers in This World That Are from the Rivers of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":22,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Four rivers have been caused to flow from Paradise: the Euphrates, the Nile, Sayḥān, and Jayḥān.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ابو_یعلی","label":"أبو يعلى","number":5921},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":7544,"n":7544},{"key":"sh12520","label":"مسند أبي يعلى","number":5921,"n":5927}]},{"num":16329,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن مالك بن صعصعة قال: فذكر حديث الإسراء والمعراج، وجاء فيه:","((ورفعت لي سدرة المنتهى، فإذا نبقها كأنه قلال هجر، وورقها كأنه آذان الفيلة، في أصلها أربعة أنهار: نهران باطنان، ونهران ظاهران، فسألت جبريل، فقال: أما الباطنان: ففي الجنة، وأما الظاهران: النيل والفرات)).","الحديث."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٣٢٠٧)، ومسلم (١٦٤). واللفظ للبخاري.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما في الدنيا من أنهار الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3207) and Muslim (164). The wording above is al-Bukhārī’s.","chapter_en":"Rivers in This World That Are from the Rivers of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":22,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Mālik ibn Ṣaʿṣaʿah narrated, while mentioning the hadith of al-Isrāʾ and al-Miʿrāj: “Sidrat al-Muntahā was raised before me. Its fruits were like the large jars of Hajar, and its leaves were like the ears of elephants. At its base were four rivers: two hidden rivers and two visible rivers. I asked Jibrīl about them. He said: ʿAs for the two hidden rivers, they are in Paradise. As for the two visible rivers, they are the Nile and the Euphrates.’”","The hadith continues."]},"buhuth":{"ar":["وفي مسلم بلفظ:","((وحدث نبي الله ﷺ أنه رأى أربعة أنهار يخرج من أصلها نهران ظاهران، ونهران باطنان، فقلت: يا جبريل، ما هذه الأنهار؟ قال: أما النهران الباطنان فنهران في الجنة، وأما الظاهران: فالنيل والفرات…)).","الحديث."],"en":["Muslim narrates it with the wording:","“The Prophet of Allah ﷺ related that he saw four rivers emerging from its base, two visible and two hidden. I asked: ‘O Jibrīl, what are these rivers?’ He replied: ‘The two hidden rivers are two rivers in Paradise, while the two visible rivers are the Nile and the Euphrates…’”","The hadith continues."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":3207},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":164}]},{"num":16330,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن ابن عمر قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((إن أزواج أهل الجنة ليغنين أزواجهن أحسن أصوات سمعها أحد قط. إن مما يغنين به: نحن الخيرات الحسان، أزواج قوم كرام، ينظرن بقرة أعيان. وإن مما يغنين به: نحن الخالدات فلا يمتنه، نحن الآمنات فلا يخفنه، نحن المقيمات فلا يظعنه))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الطبراني في الأوسط (٤٩١٧)، والصغير (٢٦٠-٢٥٩/١) - وعنه أبو نعيم في صفة الجنة (٣٢٢).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب سماع الصوت الحسن في الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Awsaṭ (4917) and al-Muʿjam al-Ṣaghīr (1/259-260), and from him by Abū Nuʿaym in Ṣifat al-Jannah (322).","chapter_en":"Hearing Beautiful Voices in Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":23,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The wives of the people of Paradise will sing to their husbands with the most beautiful voices anyone has ever heard. Among what they will sing is: ‘We are the good and beautiful ones, wives of noble men, looking with eyes full of delight.’ And among what they will sing is: ‘We are the everlasting ones and will never die. We are the secure ones and will never fear. We are the abiding ones and will never depart.’”"]},"intro":{"ar":["قال تعالى:","﴿ادْخُلُوا الْجَنَّةَ أَنْتُمْ وَأَزْوَاجُكُمْ تُحْبَرُونَ﴾ [الزخرف: ٧٠].","وقال تعالى:","﴿فَأَمَّا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَعَمِلُوا الصَّالِحَاتِ فَهُمْ فِي رَوْضَةٍ يُحْبَرُونَ﴾ [سورة الروم: ١٥].","قوله: ﴿يُحْبَرُونَ﴾ من الحبور، وهو السرور الشديد، يقال: حبره إذا سره سرورًا تهلل به وجهه، وظهر فيه أثره. ومن نعم الجنة أن أهلها يسمعون الصوت الحسن، يتهلل منه وجوههم، ولذا فسر بعض أهل العلم الحبور بسماع الصوت الحسن.","قال يحيى بن أبي كثير، في قوله عز وجل: ﴿فَهُمْ فِي رَوْضَةٍ يُحْبَرُونَ﴾ قال: السماع. ومعنى السماع مثل ما ورد في الحديث أن الحور العين يرفعن بأصواتهن. رواه الترمذي (٢٥٦٥)."],"en":["Allah, the Exalted, says:","“Enter Paradise, you and your spouses, rejoicing.”","[al-Zukhruf 43:70]","And He, the Exalted, says:","“As for those who believed and performed righteous deeds, they will be rejoicing in a garden.”","[al-Rūm 30:15]","The word “yuḥbarūn” comes from ḥubūr, meaning intense joy. It is said, “He delighted him,” when he brought him such joy that his face became radiant and the effect of that joy became visible upon him.","Among the blessings of Paradise is that its people will hear beautiful voices that cause their faces to brighten with delight. For this reason, some scholars interpreted ḥubūr as hearing beautiful voices.","Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr said concerning the statement of Allah, Mighty and Majestic:","“They will be rejoicing in a garden,”","that it means hearing.","The meaning of this hearing is like what is mentioned in the hadith that the ḥūr al-ʿīn will raise their voices in song. Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (2565)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"الطبرانی/الاوسط","label":"الطبراني في الأوسط","number":4917},{"key":"الصغیر","label":"الصغير","number":260},{"key":"وعنہ_ابو_نعیم/صفہ_الجنہ","label":"- وعنه أبو نعيم في صفة الجنة","number":322},{"key":"sh28171","label":"المعجم الأوسط للطبراني","number":4917,"n":4905}]},{"num":16331,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أنس بن مالك أن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال:","((إن في الجنة لسوقًا، يأتونها كل جمعة، فتهب ريح الشمال فتحثو في وجوههم وثيابهم، فيزدادون حسنًا وجمالًا، فيرجعون إلى أهليهم وقد ازدادوا حسنًا وجمالًا، فيقول لهم أهلوهم: والله لقد ازددتم بعدنا حسنًا وجمالًا، فيقولون: وأنتم، والله لقد ازددتم بعدنا حسنًا وجمالًا))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٢٨٣٣).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب سوق الجنة وما ينالون فيها من النعيم والجمال","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2833).","chapter_en":"The Market of Paradise and the Bliss and Beauty Its People Will Attain There","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":24,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, in Paradise there is a market which they will visit every Friday. Then a northern wind will blow over their faces and clothes, and they will increase in beauty and splendor. They will return to their families having increased in beauty and splendor, and their families will say to them: ‘By Allah, you have increased in beauty and splendor since you left us.’ They will reply: ‘And you, by Allah, have also increased in beauty and splendor since we left you.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2833}]},{"num":16332,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن سعد بن أبي وقاص، عن النبي ﷺ قال:","((لو أن ما يقل ظفر مما في الجنة بدا لتزخرفت له ما بين خوافق السماوات والأرض، ولو أن رجلًا من أهل الجنة اطلع فبدا أساوره لطمس ضوء الشمس كما تطمس الشمس ضوء النجوم))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (٢٥٣٨)، وأحمد (١٤٦٧)، والبغوي في شرح السنة (٤٣٧٧).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في حلية أهل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (2538), Aḥmad (1467), and al-Baghawī in Sharḥ al-Sunnah (4377).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Adornment of the People of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":25,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “If even an amount from Paradise as small as what a fingernail could carry were to appear, everything between the horizons of the heavens and the earth would be adorned because of it. And if a man from the people of Paradise were to look out and his bracelets became visible, their light would overwhelm the light of the sun just as the sun overwhelms the light of the stars.”"]},"intro":{"ar":["قال تعالى:","﴿إِنَّ اللَّهَ يُدْخِلُ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَعَمِلُوا الصَّالِحَاتِ جَنَّاتٍ تَجْرِي مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْأَنْهَارُ يُحَلَّوْنَ فِيهَا مِنْ أَسَاوِرَ مِنْ ذَهَبٍ وَلُؤْلُؤًا وَلِبَاسُهُمْ فِيهَا حَرِيرٌ﴾ [الحج: ٢٣].","وقال تعالى:","﴿أُولَٰئِكَ لَهُمْ جَنَّاتُ عَدْنٍ تَجْرِي مِنْ تَحْتِهِمُ الْأَنْهَارُ يُحَلَّوْنَ فِيهَا مِنْ أَسَاوِرَ مِنْ ذَهَبٍ وَيَلْبَسُونَ ثِيَابًا خُضْرًا مِنْ سُنْدُسٍ وَإِسْتَبْرَقٍ مُتَّكِئِينَ فِيهَا عَلَى الْأَرَائِكِ نِعْمَ الثَّوَابُ وَحَسُنَتْ مُرْتَفَقًا﴾ [الكهف: ٣١]."],"en":["Allah, the Exalted, says:","“Indeed, Allah will admit those who believe and perform righteous deeds into Gardens beneath which rivers flow. They will be adorned therein with bracelets of gold and pearls, and their clothing therein will be silk.”","[al-Ḥajj 22:23]","And He, the Exalted, says:","“Those will have Gardens of perpetual residence beneath which rivers flow. They will be adorned therein with bracelets of gold and will wear green garments of fine silk and brocade, reclining therein upon couches. Excellent is the reward, and beautiful is the resting place.”","[al-Kahf 18:31]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"tirmidhi","label":"الترمذي","number":2538},{"key":"البغوی/شرح_السنہ","label":"البغوي في شرح السنة","number":4377},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":1467,"n":1467},{"key":"sharhsunna","label":"شرح السنة للبغوي","number":4377,"n":4286}]},{"num":16333,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي حازم قال: كنت خلف أبي هريرة، وهو يتوضأ للصلاة، فكان يمد يده حتى تبلغ إبطه، فقلت له: يا أبا هريرة، ما هذا الوضوء؟ فقال: يا بني فروخ، أنتم ها هنا؟ لو علمت أنكم ها هنا ما توضأت هذا الوضوء، سمعت النبي ﷺ، خليلي، يقول:","((تبلغ الحلية من المؤمن حيث يبلغ الوضوء))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٢٥٠).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في حلية أهل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (250).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Adornment of the People of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":25,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Ḥāzim narrated: I was behind Abū Hurayrah while he was performing wuḍūʾ for prayer. He washed his arm until the water reached his armpit. I asked: “O Abū Hurayrah, what kind of wuḍūʾ is this?” He replied: “O sons of Farrūkh, are you here? Had I known that you were here, I would not have performed wuḍūʾ like this before you. I heard the Prophet ﷺ, my close friend, say: ‘The adornment of the believer will reach as far as the water of his wuḍūʾ reaches.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":250}]},{"num":16334,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((من سره أن يسقيه اللّٰه عز وجل الخمر في الآخرة، فليتركها في الدنيا، ومن سره أن يكسوه اللّٰه الحرير في الآخرة، فليتركه في الدنيا، أنهار الجنة تفجر من تحت تلال - أو من تحت جبال - المسك، ولو كان أدنى أهل الجنة حلية عدلت بحلية أهل الدنيا جميعًا، لكان ما يحليه اللّٰه عز وجل به في الآخرة أفضل من حلية أهل الدنيا جميعًا))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه البيهقي في البعث والنشور (٢٦٦).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في حلية أهل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Bayhaqī in al-Baʿth wa-l-Nushūr (266).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Adornment of the People of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":25,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever would be pleased for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, to give him wine to drink in the Hereafter should leave it in this world. And whoever would be pleased for Allah to clothe him in silk in the Hereafter should leave it in this world. The rivers of Paradise gush forth from beneath hills—or from beneath mountains—of musk. If even the adornment of the lowest-ranking person in Paradise were weighed against the adornment of all the people of this world, what Allah, Mighty and Majestic, adorns him with in the Hereafter would be better than all the adornment of the people of this world.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"البیہقی/البعث_والنشور","label":"البيهقي في البعث والنشور","number":266}]},{"num":16335,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن سهل بن سعد الساعدي يقول: شهدت من رسول اللّٰه ﷺ مجلسًا وصف فيه الجنة حتى انتهى، ثم قال النبي ﷺ في آخر حديثه:","((فيها ما لا عين رأت، ولا أذن سمعت، ولا خطر على قلب بشر)).","ثم اقترأ هذه الآية:","﴿تَتَجَافَىٰ جُنُوبُهُمْ عَنِ الْمَضَاجِعِ يَدْعُونَ رَبَّهُمْ خَوْفًا وَطَمَعًا وَمِمَّا رَزَقْنَاهُمْ يُنْفِقُونَ ۝ فَلَا تَعْلَمُ نَفْسٌ مَا أُخْفِيَ لَهُمْ مِنْ قُرَّةِ أَعْيُنٍ جَزَاءً بِمَا كَانُوا يَعْمَلُونَ﴾ [السجدة: ١٦-١٧]."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٢٨٢٥).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب في الجنة ما لا عين رأت، ولا أذن سمعت، ولا خطر على قلب بشر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2825).","chapter_en":"In Paradise Is What No Eye Has Seen, No Ear Has Heard, and What Has Never Occurred to a Human Heart","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":26,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Sahl ibn Saʿd al-Sāʿidī said: I attended a gathering with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in which he described Paradise until he finished. At the end of his speech, he said: “In it is what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and what has never occurred to a human heart.” Then he recited: “Their sides forsake their beds as they call upon their Lord in fear and hope, and they spend from what We have provided them. No soul knows what comfort of the eyes has been hidden for them as a reward for what they used to do.”","[al-Sajdah 32:16-17]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2825}]},{"num":16336,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة، عن النبي ﷺ:","((يقول اللّٰه تعالى: أعددت لعبادي الصالحين ما لا عين رأت، ولا أذن سمعت، ولا خطر على قلب بشر، ذخرًا بله ما أطلعتم عليه، ثم قرأ: ﴿فَلَا تَعْلَمُ نَفْسٌ مَا أُخْفِيَ لَهُمْ مِنْ قُرَّةِ أَعْيُنٍ جَزَاءً بِمَا كَانُوا يَعْمَلُونَ﴾ [السجدة: ١٧]))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٤٧٨٠)، ومسلم (٤:٢٨٢٤).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب في الجنة ما لا عين رأت، ولا أذن سمعت، ولا خطر على قلب بشر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4780) and Muslim (4:2824).","chapter_en":"In Paradise Is What No Eye Has Seen, No Ear Has Heard, and What Has Never Occurred to a Human Heart","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":26,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Allah, the Exalted, says: ‘I have prepared for My righteous servants what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and what has never occurred to a human heart—as a treasure beyond what you have been shown.’” Then he recited: “No soul knows what comfort of the eyes has been hidden for them as a reward for what they used to do.” [al-Sajdah 32:17]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":4780},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":4}]},{"num":16337,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن المغيرة بن شعبة يرفعه قال:","((سأل موسى ربه، ما أدنى أهل الجنة منزلة؟ قال: هو رجل يجيء بعد ما أدخل أهل الجنة الجنة، فيقال له: ادخل الجنة، فيقول: أي رب كيف؟ وقد نزل الناس منازلهم، وأخذوا أخذاتهم؟ فيقال له: أترضى أن يكون لك مثل ملك ملك من ملوك الدنيا؟ فيقول: رضيت رب، فيقول: لك ذلك، ومثله ومثله ومثله ومثله، فقال في الخامسة: رضيت رب، فيقول: هذا لك، وعشرة أمثاله، ولك ما اشتهت نفسك، ولذت عينك، فيقول: رضيت رب. قال: رب، فأعلاهم منزلة؟ قال: أولئك الذين أردت، غرست كرامتهم بيدي، وختمت عليها، فلم تر عين، ولم تسمع أذن، ولم يخطر على قلب بشر)).","قال: ومصداقه في كتاب اللّٰه عز وجل:","﴿فَلَا تَعْلَمُ نَفْسٌ مَا أُخْفِيَ لَهُمْ مِنْ قُرَّةِ أَعْيُنٍ﴾ [سورة السجدة: ١٧]."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (١٨٩).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب في الجنة ما لا عين رأت، ولا أذن سمعت، ولا خطر على قلب بشر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (189).","chapter_en":"In Paradise Is What No Eye Has Seen, No Ear Has Heard, and What Has Never Occurred to a Human Heart","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":26,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah narrated, attributing it to the Prophet ﷺ: “Mūsā asked his Lord: ‘What is the lowest rank of the people of Paradise?’ He said: ʿIt is a man who will come after the people of Paradise have already been admitted into Paradise. It will be said to him: “Enter Paradise.” He will say: “My Lord, how can I, when the people have already settled in their dwellings and received what was allotted to them?” It will be said to him: “Would you be pleased to have the equivalent of the kingdom of one of the kings of the world?”","He will say: “I am pleased, my Lord.” He will say: “You shall have that, and the like of it, and the like of it, and the like of it, and the like of it.” At the fifth, he will say: “I am pleased, my Lord.” He will say: “All of that is yours, and ten times as much. And you shall have whatever your soul desires and whatever delights your eyes.” He will say: “I am pleased, my Lord.” Mūsā then asked: “My Lord, what about those of the highest rank?” He said: “Those are the ones whom I chose. I planted their honor with My Hand and sealed it. No eye has seen it, no ear has heard it, and it has never occurred to a human heart.””","He said: Its confirmation is in the Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: “No soul knows what comfort of the eyes has been hidden for them.” [al-Sajdah 32:17]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":189}]},{"num":16338,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة قال: سمعت رسول اللّٰه ﷺ يقول:","((لن يدخل أحدًا عمله الجنة)).","قالوا: ولا أنت يا رسول الله؟ قال:","((لا، ولا أنا، إلا أن يتغمدني اللّٰه بفضل ورحمة، فسددوا وقاربوا، ولا يتمنين أحدكم الموت: إما محسنًا فلعله أن يزداد خيرًا، وإما مسيئًا فلعله أن يستعتب))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٥٦٧٣)، ومسلم (٧٥ :٢٨١٦).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب لا يدخل الجنة أحد إلا بفضل من الله ورحمته سبحانه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (5673) and Muslim (75 :2816).","chapter_en":"No One Enters Paradise Except by the Grace and Mercy of Allah, Glorified Is He","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “No one will be admitted into Paradise by his deeds alone.” They asked: “Not even you, O Messenger of Allah?” He replied: “Not even me, unless Allah envelops me in His grace and mercy. So strive to remain upon the right course and come as close to perfection as you can. And none of you should wish for death. If he is a doer of good, perhaps he will increase in goodness; and if he is a sinner, perhaps he will seek Allah’s pardon and correction.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":5673},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":75}]},{"num":16339,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عائشة زوج النبي ﷺ أنها كانت تقول: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((سددوا، وقاربوا، وأبشروا، فإنه لن يدخل الجنة أحدًا عمله)).","قالوا: ولا أنت يا رسول الله؟ قال:","((ولا أنا، إلا أن يتغمدني اللّٰه منه برحمة، واعلموا أن أحب العمل إلى اللّٰه أدومه وإن قل))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٦٤٦٤)، ومسلم (٢٨١٨).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب لا يدخل الجنة أحد إلا بفضل من الله ورحمته سبحانه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6464) and Muslim (2818).","chapter_en":"No One Enters Paradise Except by the Grace and Mercy of Allah, Glorified Is He","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀ’ishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, used to narrate that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Remain upon the right course, come as close to perfection as you can, and receive glad tidings, for no one will be admitted into Paradise by his deeds alone.” They asked: “Not even you, O Messenger of Allah?” He replied: “Not even me, unless Allah envelops me in mercy from Him. And know that the deed most beloved to Allah is the one performed most consistently, even if it is small.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6464},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2818}]},{"num":16340,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((قاربوا، وسددوا، فإنه ليس أحد منكم ينجيه عمله)).","قالوا: ولا إياك يا رسول الله؟ قال:","((ولا إياي، إلا أن يتغمدني اللّٰه برحمته))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٢٨١٧)، وأحمد (١٤٦٢٨).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب لا يدخل الجنة أحد إلا بفضل من الله ورحمته سبحانه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2817) and Aḥmad (14628).","chapter_en":"No One Enters Paradise Except by the Grace and Mercy of Allah, Glorified Is He","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Come as close as you can to what is right and remain steadfast, for none of you will be saved by his deeds alone.” They asked: “Not even you, O Messenger of Allah?” He replied: “Not even me, unless Allah envelops me in His mercy.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2817},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":14628,"n":14628}]},{"num":16341,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر قال: سمعت النبي ﷺ يقول:","((لا يدخل أحدًا منكم عمله الجنة، ولا يجيره من النار، ولا أنا، إلا برحمة من اللّٰه))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٧٧:٢٨١٧).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب لا يدخل الجنة أحد إلا بفضل من الله ورحمته سبحانه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (77:2817).","chapter_en":"No One Enters Paradise Except by the Grace and Mercy of Allah, Glorified Is He","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir narrated: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “The deeds of none of you will admit him into Paradise, nor protect him from the Fire—not even me—except through mercy from Allah.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":77}]},{"num":16342,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أسد بن كرز، قال: قال لي رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((يا أسد بن كرز، لا تدخلك الجنة عمل، ولكن برحمة اللّه)).","قلت: ولا أنت يا رسول اللّه؟ قال:","((ولا أنا، إلا أن يتلافاني اللّٰه أو تغمدني اللّه منه برحمة))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه البخاري في التاريخ الكبير (٤٩/٢)، والطبراني في الكبير (٣١٦/١).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب لا يدخل الجنة أحد إلا بفضل من الله ورحمته سبحانه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Tārīkh al-Kabīr (2/49) and al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Kabīr (1/316).","chapter_en":"No One Enters Paradise Except by the Grace and Mercy of Allah, Glorified Is He","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Asad ibn Kurz narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “O Asad ibn Kurz, no deed will admit you into Paradise; rather, it will be by the mercy of Allah.” I asked: “Not even you, O Messenger of Allah?” He replied: “Not even me, unless Allah comes to my aid or envelops me in mercy from Him.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari/التاریخ_الکبیر","label":"البخاري في التاريخ الكبير","number":49},{"key":"الطبرانی/الکبیر","label":"الطبراني في الكبير","number":316}]},{"num":16343,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أنس قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((أنا أكثر الأنبياء تبعًا يوم القيامة، وأنا أول من يقرع باب الجنة))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٣٣١:١٩٦).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب النبي ﷺ أول من يقرع باب الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (331:196).","chapter_en":"The Prophet ﷺ Will Be the First to Knock at the Gate of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I will have the greatest number of followers among the Prophets on the Day of Resurrection, and I will be the first to knock at the gate of Paradise.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":331}]},{"num":16344,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أنس بن مالك قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((آتي باب الجنة يوم القيامة فأستفتح، فيقول الخازن: من أنت؟ فأقول: محمد، فيقول: بك أمرت، لا أفتح لأحد قبلك))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (١٩٧).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب النبي ﷺ أول من يقرع باب الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (197).","chapter_en":"The Prophet ﷺ Will Be the First to Knock at the Gate of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I will come to the gate of Paradise on the Day of Resurrection and ask for it to be opened. The gatekeeper will ask: ‘Who are you?’ I will reply: ‘Muḥammad.’ He will say: ‘I was commanded concerning you not to open it for anyone before you.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":197}]},{"num":16345,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((نحن الآخرون الأولون يوم القيامة، ونحن أول من يدخل الجنة، بيد أنهم أوتوا الكتاب من قبلنا وأوتيناه من بعدهم، فاختلفوا، فهدانا اللّه لما اختلفوا فيه من الحق، فهذا يومهم الذي اختلفوا فيه هدانا اللّٰه له)).","قال: يوم الجمعة.","((فاليوم لنا، وغدًا لليهود، وبعد غد للنصارى))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه مسلم (٢٠ :٨٥٥) والبخاري (٦٦٢٤).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب أن الأمة المحمدية أول من يدخل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by Muslim (20 :855) and al-Bukhārī (6624).","chapter_en":"The Ummah of Muḥammad ﷺ Will Be the First Nation to Enter Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “We are the last nation in this world, yet the first on the Day of Resurrection, and we will be the first to enter Paradise. They were given the Scripture before us, while we were given it after them. They differed concerning the truth, and Allah guided us to that concerning which they differed. This is their day concerning which they differed, and Allah guided us to it.” He meant Friday.","“So today belongs to us, tomorrow to the Jews, and the day after tomorrow to the Christians.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":20},{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6624}]},{"num":16346,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبد اللّه بن مسعود قال: كنا مع رسول اللّٰه ﷺ في قبة، فذكر حديثًا طويلًا، جاء فيه:","((إن الجنة لا يدخلها إلا نفس مسلمة…)).","الحديث."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٦٥٢٨)، ومسلم (٣٧٧:٢٢١).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب الجنة لا يدخلها إلا نفس مسلمة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6528) and Muslim (377:221).","chapter_en":"None Will Enter Paradise Except a Muslim Soul","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated: We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a tent. He mentioned a lengthy hadith, in which he said: “Indeed, none will enter Paradise except a Muslim soul…” The hadith continues."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6528},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":377}]},{"num":16347,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن كعب بن مالك، أن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ بعثه وأوس بن الحدثان أيام التشريق، فناديا:","((أنه لا يدخل الجنة إلا مؤمن، وأيام منى أيام أكل وشرب))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (١١٤٢).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب الجنة لا يدخلها إلا نفس مسلمة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1142).","chapter_en":"None Will Enter Paradise Except a Muslim Soul","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Kaʿb ibn Mālik narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent him and Aws ibn al-Ḥadathān during the Days of Tashrīq to proclaim: “None will enter Paradise except a believer, and the days of Minā are days of eating and drinking.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":1142}]},{"num":16348,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عمر بن الخطاب قال: لما كان يوم خيبر أقبل نفر من صحابة النبي ﷺ، فقالوا: فلان شهيد، فلان شهيد، حتى مروا على رجل، فقالوا: فلان شهيد، فقال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((كلا، إني رأيته في النار في بردة غلها - أو عباءة -)).","ثم قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((يا ابن الخطاب، اذهب فناد في الناس، أنه لا يدخل الجنة إلا المؤمنون)).","قال: فخرجت فناديت:","((ألا إنه لا يدخل الجنة إلا المؤمنون))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (١١٤).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب الجنة لا يدخلها إلا نفس مسلمة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (114).","chapter_en":"None Will Enter Paradise Except a Muslim Soul","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb narrated: On the day of Khaybar, a group of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ came saying: “So-and-so is a martyr, so-and-so is a martyr.” Then they passed by a man and said: “So-and-so is a martyr.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No. I saw him in the Fire because of a cloak—or an outer garment—that he had unlawfully taken from the spoils.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, go and proclaim among the people that none will enter Paradise except the believers.”","ʿUmar said: So I went out and proclaimed: “Indeed, none will enter Paradise except the believers.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":114}]},{"num":16349,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أم سلمة قالت: قلت للنبي ﷺ: إن هشام بن المغيرة كان يصل الرحم، ويقري الضيف، ويفك العناة، ويطعم الطعام، ولو أدرك أسلم، هل ذلك نافعه؟ قال:","((لا، إنه كان يعطي للدنيا وذكرها وحمدها، ولم يقل يومًا قط: رب اغفر لي يوم الدين))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أبو يعلى (٦٩٦٥) - واللفظ له -، وابن أبي شيبة في مسنده - كما في المطالب العالية - (٢٨٧١)، والطبراني في الكبير (٦٠٦/٢٣).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب الجنة لا يدخلها إلا نفس مسلمة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Abū Yaʿlā (6965), whose wording this is, Ibn Abī Shaybah in his Musnad, as cited in al-Maṭālib al-ʿĀliyah (2871), and al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Kabīr (23/606).","chapter_en":"None Will Enter Paradise Except a Muslim Soul","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Umm Salamah narrated: I said to the Prophet ﷺ: “Hishām ibn al-Mughīrah used to maintain ties of kinship, honor guests, free captives, and feed people. Had he lived until Islam and accepted it, would those deeds have benefited him?” He replied: “No. He used to give for the sake of this world, its reputation, and its praise, and he never once said: ‘My Lord, forgive me on the Day of Judgment.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ابو_یعلی","label":"أبو يعلى","number":6965},{"key":"ابن_ابی_شیبہ/مسندہ_کما_فی_المطالب_العالیہ","label":"ابن أبي شيبة في مسنده - كما في المطالب العالية -","number":2871},{"key":"الطبرانی/الکبیر","label":"الطبراني في الكبير","number":606},{"key":"sh12520","label":"مسند أبي يعلى","number":6965,"n":6971}]},{"num":16350,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة، عن النبي ﷺ، قال:","((يلقى إبراهيم أباه آزر يوم القيامة، وعلى وجه آزر قترة وغبرة، فيقول له إبراهيم: ألم أقل لك لا تعصني، فيقول أبوه: فاليوم لا أعصيك، فيقول إبراهيم: يا رب إنك وعدتني أن لا تخزيني يوم يبعثون، فأي خزي أخزى من أبي الأبعد؟ فيقول اللّٰه تعالى: إني حرمت الجنة على الكافرين، ثم يقال: يا إبراهيم، ما تحت رجليك؟ فينظر، فإذا هو بذيخ ملتطخ، فيؤخذ بقوائمه فيلقى في النار))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (٣٣٥٠).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أن الله حرم الجنة على الكافرين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3350).","chapter_en":"Allah Has Forbidden Paradise to the Disbelievers","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Ibrāhīm will meet his father Āzar on the Day of Resurrection, and Āzar’s face will be covered with darkness and dust. Ibrāhīm will say to him: ‘Did I not tell you not to disobey me?’ His father will reply: ‘Today I will not disobey you.’ Ibrāhīm will say: ‘My Lord, You promised me that You would not disgrace me on the Day they are resurrected. What disgrace could be greater than my distant father?’","Allah, the Exalted, will say: ‘I have forbidden Paradise to the disbelievers.’ Then it will be said: ‘O Ibrāhīm, what is beneath your feet?’ He will look and see a male hyena smeared with filth. It will be seized by its legs and thrown into the Fire.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":3350}]},{"num":16351,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي سعيد الخدري، أن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال:","((ليأخذن رجل بيد أبيه يوم القيامة، يريد أن يدخله الجنة، فينادى: إن الجنة لا يدخلها مشرك، إن اللّٰه حرم الجنة على كل مشرك، فيقول: أي رب، أي رب، أبي! قال: فيتحول في صورة قبيحة، وريح منتنة، فيتركه)).","قال أبو سعيد: “كان أصحاب محمد ﷺ يرون أنه إبراهيم، ولم يزدهم رسول اللّٰه ﷺ على ذلك”."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه ابن حبان في صحيحه (٢٥٢) - واللفظ له -، والبزار - كشف الأستار - (٩٤).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أن الله حرم الجنة على الكافرين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Ibn Ḥibbān in his Ṣaḥīḥ (252), whose wording this is, and al-Bazzār in Kashf al-Astār (94).","chapter_en":"Allah Has Forbidden Paradise to the Disbelievers","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A man will take his father by the hand on the Day of Resurrection, wanting to bring him into Paradise. Then it will be proclaimed: ‘No polytheist will enter Paradise. Allah has forbidden Paradise to every polytheist.’ The man will say: ‘My Lord! My Lord! My father!’ Then his father will be transformed into an ugly form with a foul smell, so he will leave him.” Abū Saʿīd said: “The Companions of Muḥammad ﷺ understood this man to be Ibrāhīm, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not add anything beyond that.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ibnhibban/صحیحہ","label":"ابن حبان في صحيحه","number":252},{"key":"البزار_کشف_الاستار","label":"البزار - كشف الأستار -","number":94},{"key":"ibnhibban","label":"صحيح ابن حبان (التقاسيم والأنواع)","number":5158,"n":5154}]},{"num":16352,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أنس بن مالك، أن أعرابيًا قال لرسول اللّٰه ﷺ: متى الساعة؟ فقال له رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((ما أعددت لها؟)).","قال: حب اللّٰه ورسوله. قال:","((أنت مع من أحببت))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه مسلم (٢٦٣٩)، والبخاري (٧١٥٣).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب من أحب الله ورسوله يكون معه في الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by Muslim (2639) and al-Bukhārī (7153).","chapter_en":"Whoever Loves Allah and His Messenger Will Be with Him in Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik narrated that a Bedouin asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “When is the Hour?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked him: “What have you prepared for it?” He replied: “Love for Allah and His Messenger.” He said: “You will be with those whom you love.”"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["ورواه من طريق آخر عن أنس بن مالك، قال: بينما أنا والنبي ﷺ خارجان من المسجد، فلقينا رجلًا عند سدة المسجد، فقال: يا رسول الله، متى الساعة؟ قال النبي ﷺ:","((ما أعددت لها؟)).","فكأن الرجل استكان، ثم قال: يا رسول الله: ما أعددت لها كبير صيام ولا صلاة ولا صدقة، ولكني أحب اللّه ورسوله. قال:","((أنت مع من أحببت))."],"en":["It is also narrated through another route from Anas ibn Mālik:","While the Prophet ﷺ and I were leaving the mosque, we met a man at the entrance of the mosque.","He asked:","“O Messenger of Allah, when is the Hour?”","The Prophet ﷺ asked:","“What have you prepared for it?”","The man appeared humbled and replied:","“O Messenger of Allah, I have not prepared for it a great amount of fasting, prayer, or charity, but I love Allah and His Messenger.”","He said:","“You will be with those whom you love.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2639},{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":7153}]},{"num":16353,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبادة بن الصامت، عن النبي ﷺ قال:","((من شهد أن لا إله إلا اللّٰه وحده لا شريك له، وأن محمدًا عبده ورسوله، وأن عيسى عبدالله ورسوله، وكلمته ألقاها إلى مريم، وروح منه، والجنة حق، والنار حق، أدخله اللّٰه الجنة على ما كان من العمل))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٣٤٣٥) ورواه مسلم (٢٨) من وجه آخر، وزاد:","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب من شهد بالتوحيد ومات عليه دخل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3435). Muslim (28) narrated it through another route and added:","chapter_en":"Whoever Testifies to Tawḥīd and Dies upon It Will Enter Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever testifies that there is no deity except Allah alone, without partner; that Muḥammad is His servant and Messenger; that ʿĪsā is the servant of Allah and His Messenger, His Word which He cast to Maryam, and a spirit from Him; and that Paradise is true and the Fire is true—Allah will admit him into Paradise regardless of what his deeds had been.”"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["((وأدخله اللّٰه من أي أبواب الجنة الثمانية شاء))."],"en":["“Allah will admit him through whichever of the eight gates of Paradise he wishes.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":3435},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":28}]},{"num":16354,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي ذر قال: خرجت ليلة من الليالي، فإذا رسول اللّٰه ﷺ يمشي وحده، وليس معه إنسان، قال: فظننت أنه يكره أن يمشي معه أحد، قال: فجعلت أمشي في ظل القمر، فالتفت فرآني، فقال:","((من هذا؟)).","قلت: أبو ذر، جعلني اللّٰه فداءك، قال:","((يا أبا ذر تعاله)).","قال: فمشيت معه ساعة، فقال:","((إن المكثرين هم المقلون يوم القيامة، إلا من أعطاه اللّٰه خيرًا، فنفح فيه يمينه وشماله وبين يديه ووراءه، وعمل فيه خيرًا)).","قال: فمشيت معه ساعة، فقال لي:","((اجلس ها هنا)).","قال: فأجلسني في قاع حوله حجارة، فقال لي:","((اجلس ها هنا حتى أرجع إليك)).","قال: فانطلق في الحرة حتى لا أراه، فلبث عني فأطال اللبث، ثم إني سمعته وهو مقبل، وهو يقول:","((وإن سرق، وإن زنى)).","قال: فلما جاء لم أصبر حتى قلت: يا نبي اللّٰه جعلني اللّٰه فداءك، من تكلم في جانب الحرة؟ ما سمعت أحدًا يرجع إليك شيئًا؟ قال:","((ذلك جبريل، عرض لي في جانب الحرة، قال: بشر أمتك أنه من مات لا يشرك بالله شيئًا دخل الجنة، قلت: يا جبريل، وإن سرق، وإن زنى؟ قال: نعم. قال: قلت: وإن سرق، وإن زنى؟ قال: نعم، وإن شرب الخمر))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٦٤٤٣)، ومسلم (٣٣:٩٤).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب من شهد بالتوحيد ومات عليه دخل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6443) and Muslim (33:94).","chapter_en":"Whoever Testifies to Tawḥīd and Dies upon It Will Enter Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Dharr narrated: One night I went out and saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ walking alone with no one accompanying him. I thought that perhaps he disliked having anyone walk with him, so I began walking in the shadow of the moon. He turned and saw me and asked: “Who is this?” I replied: “Abū Dharr, may Allah make me your ransom.” He said: “O Abū Dharr, come here.” I walked with him for a while, and he said: “Those who possess much wealth will be the ones with little reward on the Day of Resurrection, except the one to whom Allah gives wealth and he distributes it to his right, to his left, in front of him, and behind him, and uses it in good.”","I continued walking with him for a while, then he said: “Sit here.” He seated me in a low area surrounded by stones and said: “Remain here until I return to you.” Then he went into the rocky plain until I could no longer see him. He remained away for a long time. Then I heard him returning while saying: “Even if he steals, and even if he commits fornication.” When he came back, I could not restrain myself and said: “O Prophet of Allah, may Allah make me your ransom, who was speaking to you on the side of the rocky plain? I did not hear anyone responding to you.”","He replied: “That was Jibrīl. He appeared to me at the side of the rocky plain and said: ‘Give your Ummah the glad tidings that whoever dies without associating anything with Allah will enter Paradise.’ I said: ‘O Jibrīl, even if he steals and commits fornication?’ He said: ‘Yes.’ I said: ‘Even if he steals and commits fornication?’ He said: ‘Yes, even if he drinks wine.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6443},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":33}]},{"num":16355,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن ابن مسعود قال: قال رسول الله ﷺ:","((من مات يشرك بالله شيئًا دخل النار)).","وقلت أنا: “من مات لا يشرك بالله شيئًا دخل الجنة”."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (١٢٣٨)، ومسلم (٩٢).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب من شهد بالتوحيد ومات عليه دخل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (1238) and Muslim (92).","chapter_en":"Whoever Testifies to Tawḥīd and Dies upon It Will Enter Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn Masʿūd narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever dies while associating anything with Allah will enter the Fire.” Ibn Masʿūd said: “And I say: Whoever dies without associating anything with Allah will enter Paradise.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":1238},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":92}]},{"num":16356,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن معاذ قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((من مات وهو يشهد أن لا إله إلا الله، وأن محمدًا رسول اللّٰه صادقًا من قلبه، دخل الجنة))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (٢٢٠٠٣)، والنسائي في عمل اليوم والليلة (١١٣٤)، وابن خزيمة في التوحيد (٥١٤).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب من شهد بالتوحيد ومات عليه دخل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (22003), al-Nasā’ī in ʿAmal al-Yawm wa-l-Laylah (1134), and Ibn Khuzaymah in al-Tawḥīd (514).","chapter_en":"Whoever Testifies to Tawḥīd and Dies upon It Will Enter Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Muʿādh narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever dies testifying sincerely from his heart that there is no deity except Allah and that Muḥammad is the Messenger of Allah will enter Paradise.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"nasai/عمل_الیوم_واللیلہ","label":"النسائي في عمل اليوم والليلة","number":1134},{"key":"ابن_خزیمہ/التوحید","label":"ابن خزيمة في التوحيد","number":514},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":22003,"n":22003},{"key":"amalyawm","label":"عمل اليوم والليلة للنسائي","number":1134,"n":1140}]},{"num":16357,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن معاذ بن جبل قال حين حضرته الوفاة: اكشفوا عني سجف القبة أحدثكم حديثًا سمعته من رسول اللّٰه ﷺ يقول:","((من شهد أن لا إله إلا الله، مخلصًا من قلبه، أو يقينًا من قلبه، دخل الجنة، ولم تمسه النار))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (٢٢٠٦٠)، والحميدي (٣٦٩)، والطبراني في الكبير (٤١/٢٠).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب من شهد بالتوحيد ومات عليه دخل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (22060), al-Ḥumaydī (369), and al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Kabīr (20/41).","chapter_en":"Whoever Testifies to Tawḥīd and Dies upon It Will Enter Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Muʿādh ibn Jabal said when death approached him: “Raise the curtain of the tent from me so that I may narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” He said: “Whoever testifies that there is no deity except Allah sincerely from his heart—or with certainty in his heart—will enter Paradise, and the Fire will not touch him.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"الحمیدی","label":"الحميدي","number":369},{"key":"الطبرانی/الکبیر","label":"الطبراني في الكبير","number":41},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":22060,"n":22060},{"key":"humaydi","label":"مسند الحميدي","number":373,"n":384}]},{"num":16358,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة، أن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال:","((كل أمتي يدخلون الجنة إلا من أبى)).","قالوا: يا رسول الله، ومن يأبى؟ قال:","((من أطاعني دخل الجنة، ومن عصاني فقد أبى))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (٧٢٨٠).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب من استجاب للنبي ﷺ وأطاعه دخل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (7280).","chapter_en":"Whoever Responds to the Prophet ﷺ and Obeys Him Will Enter Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “All of my Ummah will enter Paradise except those who refuse.” They asked: “O Messenger of Allah, who would refuse?” He replied: “Whoever obeys me will enter Paradise, and whoever disobeys me has refused.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":7280}]},{"num":16359,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن سهل بن سعد، عن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال:","((من يضمن لي ما بين لحييه وما بين رجليه أضمن له الجنة))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (٦٤٧٤).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب من ضمن ما بين لحييه ورجليه فله الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6474).","chapter_en":"Whoever Guarantees What Is Between His Jaws and His Legs Is Guaranteed Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":9,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Sahl ibn Saʿd narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever guarantees for me what is between his two jaws and what is between his two legs, I guarantee Paradise for him.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6474}]},{"num":16360,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن صعصعة بن معاوية قال: انتهيت إلى الربذة، فإذا أنا بأبي ذر، قد تلقاني برواحل قد أوردها، ثم أصدرها، وقد أعلق قربة في عنق بعير منها ليشرب ويسقي أصحابه، وكان خلقًا من أخلاق العرب، قلت: يا أبا ذر مالك؟ قال: لي عملي. قلت: إيه يا أبا ذر، ما سمعت رسول الله ﷺ يقول؟ قال: سمعت رسول اللّٰه ﷺ يقول:","((من أنفق زوجين من ماله ابتدرته حجبة الجنة)).","قلنا: ما هذان الزوجان؟ قال: إن كانت رجالًا فرجلان، وإن كانت خيلًا ففرسان، وإن كانت إبلًا فبعيران، حتى عد أصناف المال كله."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (٢١٤١٣) وابن حبان (٤٦٤٣)، والحاكم (٨٦/٢).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب من أنفق زوجين ابتدرته حجبة الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (21413), Ibn Ḥibbān (4643), and al-Ḥākim (2/86).","chapter_en":"Whoever Spends Two of His Possessions Will Be Rushed to by the Gatekeepers of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ṣaʿṣaʿah ibn Muʿāwiyah narrated: I arrived at al-Rabadhah and found Abū Dharr. He met me with some riding animals that he had brought to water and then led away. He had hung a waterskin around the neck of one of the camels so that he could drink from it and give drink to his companions. This was among the customs of the Arabs. I asked: “O Abū Dharr, what do you possess?” He replied: “I have my deeds.” I said: “Tell me, O Abū Dharr, what did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say?”","He replied: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever spends two of his possessions, the gatekeepers of Paradise will rush to receive him.” We asked: “What are these two?” He explained: “If they are men, then two men; if horses, then two horses; if camels, then two camels,” and he continued enumerating all categories of wealth."]},"buhuth":{"ar":["قوله ((زوجين من ماله)) قال ابن حبان: “العرب في لغتها تسمي الفردين المتلازمين زوجين، قال اللّٰه تعالى:","﴿وَمِنْ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ خَلَقْنَا زَوْجَيْنِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَذَكَّرُونَ﴾ [الذاريات: ٤٩]."],"en":["Regarding the phrase “two of his possessions,” Ibn Ḥibbān said:","“In the Arabic language, two individual things joined together are called a pair.”","Allah, the Exalted, says:","“And of everything We created two mates, that perhaps you may remember.”","[al-Dhāriyāt 51:49]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ibnhibban","label":"ابن حبان","number":4643},{"key":"hakim","label":"الحاكم","number":86},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":21413,"n":21413}]},{"num":16361,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة: أن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال:","((يقول اللّٰه تعالى: ما لعبدي المؤمن عندي جزاء، إذا قبضت صفيه من أهل الدنيا ثم احتسبه، إلا الجنة))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (٦٤٢٤).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب من قبض الله صفيه فاحتسب فله الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6424).","chapter_en":"Whoever Loses a Beloved One Taken by Allah and Patiently Seeks Reward Will Have Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":11,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah, the Exalted, says: ‘There is no reward with Me for My believing servant, when I take away his beloved one from the people of this world and he patiently seeks My reward, except Paradise.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6424}]},{"num":16362,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة، عن النبي ﷺ، قال:","((عجب اللّه من قوم يدخلون الجنة في السلاسل))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (٣٠١٠).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب يدخل الجنة قوم في السلاسل","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3010).","chapter_en":"People Will Enter Paradise in Chains","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":12,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Allah marvels at people who enter Paradise in chains.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":3010}]},{"num":16363,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي أمامة قال: استضحك رسول اللّٰه ﷺ يومًا، فقيل له: يا رسول الله، ما أضحكك؟ قال:","((قوم يساقون إلى الجنة مقرنين في السلاسل))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (٢٢٢٠٣)، والطبراني في الكبير (٣٤٠/٨)، والبيهقي في الشعب (٣٦٠٥).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب يدخل الجنة قوم في السلاسل","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (22203), al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Kabīr (8/340), and al-Bayhaqī in al-Shuʿab (3605).","chapter_en":"People Will Enter Paradise in Chains","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":12,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Umāmah narrated: One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed. It was asked: “O Messenger of Allah, what made you laugh?” He replied: “People being driven toward Paradise bound together in chains.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"الطبرانی/الکبیر","label":"الطبراني في الكبير","number":340},{"key":"البیہقی/الشعب","label":"البيهقي في الشعب","number":3605},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":22203,"n":22203}]},{"num":16364,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي الطفيل قال: ضحك رسول اللّٰه ﷺ فقيل: يا رسول اللّٰه مم ضحكت؟ قال:","((رأيت أناسًا من أمتي يساقون إلى الجنة في السلاسل))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الدولابي في الكنى (١٢٦٤)، والبزار (٢٧٨٠).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب يدخل الجنة قوم في السلاسل","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Dūlābī in al-Kunā (1264) and al-Bazzār (2780).","chapter_en":"People Will Enter Paradise in Chains","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":12,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū al-Ṭufayl narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed. It was asked: “O Messenger of Allah, what made you laugh?” He replied: “I saw people from my Ummah being driven toward Paradise in chains.”"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["قوله: ((يدخلون الجنة في السلاسل)) له معنيان:","١- الكفار الذين أُسروا وقُيدوا بالسلاسل، ثم أسلموا، فيدخلون الجنة بسلاسلهم.","٢- المسلمون الذين قُيدوا بالسلاسل في سجون الكفار، وماتوا فيها، يدخلون الجنة بسلاسلهم."],"en":["Regarding the statement:","“They enter Paradise in chains,”","the author says it has two meanings:","1. Disbelievers who were captured and bound in chains, then later accepted Islam, and consequently enter Paradise.","2. Muslims who were bound in chains in the prisons of disbelievers and died there, then enter Paradise with their chains."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"الدولابی/الکنی","label":"الدولابي في الكنى","number":1264},{"key":"البزار","label":"البزار","number":2780}]},{"num":16365,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة، عن النبي ﷺ قال:","((يدخل الجنة أقوام أفئدتهم مثل أفئدة الطير))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٢٨٤٠).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب يدخل الجنة أقوام أفئدتهم مثل أفئدة الطير","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2840).","chapter_en":"People Whose Hearts Are Like the Hearts of Birds Will Enter Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":13,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “People whose hearts are like the hearts of birds will enter Paradise.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2840}]},{"num":16366,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبد الله بن عمرو قال: سمعت رسول اللّٰه ﷺ يقول:","((إن فقراء المهاجرين يسبقون الأغنياء يوم القيامة إلى الجنة بأربعين خريفًا))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٢٩٧٩). وهذا خاص بفقراء المهاجرين.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب يدخل الفقراء الجنة قبل الأغنياء","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2979).","chapter_en":"The Poor Will Enter Paradise Before the Rich","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":14,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The poor among the Muhājirūn will precede the wealthy into Paradise on the Day of Resurrection by forty years.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The author states that this specifically concerns the poor among the Muhājirūn."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2979}]},{"num":16367,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي سعيد الخدري قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((فقراء المهاجرين يدخلون الجنة قبل أغنيائهم بخمسمائة سنة))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (٢٣٥١)، وابن ماجه (٤١٢٣).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب يدخل الفقراء الجنة قبل الأغنياء","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (2351) and Ibn Mājah (4123).","chapter_en":"The Poor Will Enter Paradise Before the Rich","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":14,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The poor among the Muhājirūn will enter Paradise five hundred years before their wealthy ones.”"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["ولا منافاة بين أربعين خريفًا وبين خمس مائة سنة؛ فإن ذلك يعود إلى اختلاف مراتبهم في الفقر والغنى."],"en":["There is no contradiction between forty years and five hundred years, because the difference relates to the varying degrees of poverty and wealth among them."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"tirmidhi","label":"الترمذي","number":2351},{"key":"ibnmajah","label":"ابن ماجه","number":4123}]},{"num":16368,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((يدخل فقراء المؤمنين الجنة قبل أغنيائهم خمس مائة عام))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (٢٣٥٤، ٢٣٥٣)، وابن ماجه (٤١٢٢)، وابن حبان (٦٧٦).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب يدخل الفقراء الجنة قبل الأغنياء","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (2354, 2353), Ibn Mājah (4122), and Ibn Ḥibbān (676).","chapter_en":"The Poor Will Enter Paradise Before the Rich","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":14,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The poor believers will enter Paradise five hundred years before their wealthy ones.”"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["وهذا عام لجميع المسلمين، بما فيهم فقراء المهاجرين."],"en":["The author notes that this applies generally to all Muslims, including the poor among the Muhājirūn."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"tirmidhi","label":"الترمذي","number":2354},{"key":"ibnmajah","label":"ابن ماجه","number":4122},{"key":"ibnhibban","label":"ابن حبان","number":676}]},{"num":16369,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبدالله بن عمرو قال: كنت عند رسول اللّٰه ﷺ وطلعت الشمس، فقال:","((يأتي اللّٰه قوم يوم القيامة، نورهم كنور الشمس)).","فقال أبو بكر: أنحن هم يا رسول اللّه؟ قال:","((لا، ولكم خير كثير، ولكنهم الفقراء والمهاجرون الذين يحشرون من أقطار الأرض)).","وقال:","((طوبى للغرباء، طوبى للغرباء، طوبى للغرباء)).","فقيل: من الغرباء يا رسول الله؟ قال:","((ناس صالحون في ناس سوء كثير، من يعصيهم أكثر ممن يطيعهم))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (٧٠٧٢).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب يدخل الفقراء الجنة قبل الأغنياء","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (7072).","chapter_en":"The Poor Will Enter Paradise Before the Rich","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":14,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr narrated: I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when the sun rose. He said: “Allah will bring forth people on the Day of Resurrection whose light will be like the light of the sun.” Abū Bakr asked: “Are we among them, O Messenger of Allah?” He replied: “No, although you have abundant good. Rather, they are the poor Muhājirūn who will be gathered from the farthest regions of the earth.” He also said: “Glad tidings to the strangers! Glad tidings to the strangers! Glad tidings to the strangers!”","It was asked: “Who are the strangers, O Messenger of Allah?” He replied: “Righteous people among a great many evil people; those who disobey them are more numerous than those who obey them.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":7072,"n":7072}]},{"num":16370,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبد اللّٰه بن عمرو بن العاص، عن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ أنه قال:","((هل تدرون أول من يدخل الجنة من خلق اللّٰه؟)).","قالوا: الله ورسوله أعلم. قال:","((أول من يدخل الجنة من خلق اللّٰه فقراء المهاجرون، الذين تسد بهم الثغور، ويتقى بهم المكاره، ويموت أحدهم وحاجته في صدره، لا يستطيع لها قضاء، فيقول اللّٰه عز وجل لمن يشاء من ملائكته: ائتوهم فحيوهم، فتقول الملائكة: نحن سكان سمائك، وخيرتك من خلقك، أفتأمرنا أن نأتي هؤلاء فنسلم عليهم؟ قال: إنهم كانوا عبادًا يعبدوني، لا يشركون بي شيئًا، وتسد بهم الثغور، ويتقى بهم المكاره، ويموت أحدهم وحاجته في صدره، لا يستطيع لها قضاء. قال: فتأتيهم الملائكة عند ذلك، فيدخلون عليهم من كل باب:","﴿سَلَامٌ عَلَيْكُمْ بِمَا صَبَرْتُمْ فَنِعْمَ عُقْبَى الدَّارِ﴾ [الرعد: ٢٤]))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (٦٥٧٠، ٦٥٧١)، والبزار (٢٤٥٧)، وصححه ابن حبان (٧٤٢١)، والحاكم (٧١/٢).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب يدخل الفقراء الجنة قبل الأغنياء","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (6570, 6571), al-Bazzār (2457), authenticated by Ibn Ḥibbān (7421), and al-Ḥākim (2/71).","chapter_en":"The Poor Will Enter Paradise Before the Rich","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":14,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do you know who among Allah’s creation will be the first to enter Paradise?” They replied: “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said: “The first of Allah’s creation to enter Paradise will be the poor Muhājirūn—those through whom the frontier posts are defended and hardships are warded off. One of them dies while a need remains in his heart that he was unable to fulfill.","Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will say to whichever angels He wills: ‘Go to them and greet them.’ The angels will say: ‘We are the inhabitants of Your heaven and the chosen among Your creation. Do You command us to go to these people and greet them?’ He will say: ‘They were servants who worshipped Me and associated nothing with Me. Through them the frontier posts were defended and hardships were warded off. One of them would die while a need remained in his heart that he was unable to fulfill.’","Then the angels will come to them and enter upon them through every gate, saying: ‘Peace be upon you for what you patiently endured. Excellent indeed is the final home.’ [al-Raʿd 13:24]”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"البزار","label":"البزار","number":2457},{"key":"صححہ_ابن_حبان","label":"صححه ابن حبان","number":7421},{"key":"hakim","label":"الحاكم","number":71},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":6570,"n":6570},{"key":"sh12862","label":"كشف الأستار عن زوائد البزار","number":3665,"n":3666},{"key":"ibnhibban","label":"صحيح ابن حبان (التقاسيم والأنواع)","number":5174,"n":5170}]},{"num":16371,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبد اللّٰه بن عمرو، عن النبي ﷺ قال:","((تجتمعون يوم القيامة فيقال: أين فقراء هذه الأمة ومساكينها؟ قال: فيقومون، فيقال لهم: ماذا عملتم؟ فيقولون: ربنا ابتليتنا فصبرنا، وآتيت الأموال والسلطان غيرنا، فيقول الله: صدقتم، قال: فيدخلون الجنة قبل الناس، ويبقى شدة الحساب على ذوي الأموال والسلطان)).","قالوا: فأين المؤمنون يومئذ؟ قال:","((يوضع لهم كراسي من نور وتظلل عليهم الغمام، يكون ذلك اليوم أقصر على المؤمنين من ساعة من نهار))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه ابن حبان (٧٤١٩)، والطبراني (٥٥٣/١٣).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب يدخل الفقراء الجنة قبل الأغنياء","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Ibn Ḥibbān (7419) and al-Ṭabarānī (13/553).","chapter_en":"The Poor Will Enter Paradise Before the Rich","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":14,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “You will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be said: ‘Where are the poor and needy of this Ummah?’ They will stand, and it will be asked: ‘What did you do?’ They will say: ‘Our Lord, You tested us and we were patient, while You gave wealth and authority to others besides us.’ Allah will say: ‘You have spoken the truth.’ Then they will enter Paradise before the other people, while the severity of the reckoning will remain upon those who possessed wealth and authority.”","They asked: “Where will the believers be at that time?” He replied: “Chairs of light will be placed for them, and clouds will shade them. That Day will be shorter for the believers than an hour of a daytime.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"الطبرانی","label":"الطبراني","number":553},{"key":"ibnhibban","label":"صحيح ابن حبان (التقاسيم والأنواع)","number":5113,"n":5109}]},{"num":16372,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن ثوبان مولى رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال: كنت قائمًا عند رسول اللّه ﷺ، فجاء حبر من أحبار اليهود، فقال: السلام عليك يا محمد! فدفعته دفعة كاد يصرع منها. فقال: لم تدفعني؟ فقلت: ألا تقول: يا رسول الله؟ فقال اليهودي: إنما ندعوه باسمه الذي سماه به أهله. فقال رسول اللٰه ﷺ:","((إن اسمي محمد الذي سماني به أهلي)).","فقال اليهودي: جئت أسألك. فقال له رسول اللٰه ﷺ:","((أينفعك شيء إن حدثتك؟)).","قال: أسمع بأذني، فنكت رسول اللّٰه ﷺ بعود معه، فقال:","((سل)).","فقال اليهودي: أين يكون الناس يوم تبدل الأرض غير الأرض والسماوات؟ فقال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((هم في الظلمة دون الجسر)).","قال: فمن أول الناس إجازة؟ قال:","((فقراء المهاجرين))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٣٤ :٣١٥).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب يدخل الفقراء الجنة قبل الأغنياء","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (34 :315).","chapter_en":"The Poor Will Enter Paradise Before the Rich","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":14,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Thawbān, the freedman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, narrated: I was standing with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a Jewish scholar came and said: “Peace be upon you, O Muḥammad.” I pushed him so forcefully that he nearly fell. He asked: “Why did you push me?” I said: “Why do you not say, ‘O Messenger of Allah’?” The Jewish man replied: “We only call him by the name his family gave him.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “My name is Muḥammad, the name by which my family named me.”","The Jewish man said: “I have come to ask you.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked: “Will it benefit you if I answer you?” He replied: “I will listen with my ears.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ began drawing with a stick he had and said: “Ask.” The Jewish man asked: “Where will the people be on the Day when the earth is changed into another earth and the heavens as well?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “They will be in darkness before the bridge.” He asked: “Who will be the first people to cross?”","He replied: “The poor among the Muhājirūn.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":34}]},{"num":16373,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي سعيد الخدري قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((يخلص المؤمنون من النار، فيحبسون على قنطرة بين الجنة والنار، فيقص لبعضهم من بعض مظالم كانت بينهم في الدنيا، حتى إذا هذبوا ونقوا أذن لهم في دخول الجنة، فوالذي نفس محمد بيده، لأحدهم أهدى بمنزله في الجنة منه بمنزله كان في الدنيا))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (٦٥٣٥).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب انتزاع الغل من صدور أهل الجنة قبل الدخول فيها","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6535).","chapter_en":"Resentment Will Be Removed from the Hearts of the People of Paradise Before They Enter It","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":15,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The believers will be delivered from the Fire, then detained upon a bridge between Paradise and the Fire. Retribution will be taken among them for wrongs they committed against one another in the worldly life. When they have been purified and cleansed, permission will be granted to them to enter Paradise. By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muḥammad, each of them will know his dwelling in Paradise more readily than he knew his dwelling in this world.”"]},"intro":{"ar":["قال الله تعالى:","﴿وَنَزَعْنَا مَا فِي صُدُورِهِمْ مِنْ غِلٍّ إِخْوَانًا عَلَىٰ سُرُرٍ مُتَقَابِلِينَ﴾ [الحجر: ٤٧]."],"en":["Allah, the Exalted, says:","“We will remove whatever resentment is in their hearts, so they will be brothers, facing one another upon couches.”","[al-Ḥijr 15:47]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6535}]},{"num":16374,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن حصين بن عبد الرحمن قال: كنت عند سعيد بن جبير، فقال: أيكم رأى الكوكب الذي انقض البارحة؟ قلت: أنا، ثم قلت: أما إني لم أكن في صلاة، ولكني لدغت، قال: فماذا صنعت؟ قلت: استرقيت، قال: فما حملك على ذلك؟ قلت: حديث حدثناه الشعبي، فقال: وما حدثكم الشعبي؟ قلت: حدثنا عن بريدة بن حصيب الأسلمي، أنه قال: لا رقية إلا من عين، أو حمة، فقال: قد أحسن من انتهى إلى ما سمع، ولكن حدثنا ابن عباس، عن النبي ﷺ قال:","((عرضت علي الأمم، فرأيت النبي ومعه الرهيط، والنبي ومعه الرجل والرجلان، والنبي ليس معه أحد، إذ رفع لي سواد عظيم، فظننت أنهم أمتي، فقيل لي: هذا موسى ﷺ وقومه، ولكن انظر إلى الأفق، فنظرت فإذا سواد عظيم، فقيل لي: انظر إلى الأفق الآخر، فإذا سواد عظيم، فقيل لي: هذه أمتك ومعهم سبعون ألفًا يدخلون الجنة بغير حساب ولا عذاب)).","ثم نهض فدخل منزله، فخاض الناس في أولئك الذين يدخلون الجنة بغير حساب ولا عذاب، فقال بعضهم: فلعلهم الذين صحبوا رسول اللّه ﷺ، وقال بعضهم: فلعلهم الذين ولدوا في الإسلام ولم يشركوا بالله، وذكروا أشياء. فخرج عليهم رسول الله ﷺ فقال:","((ما الذي تخوضون فيه؟)).","فأخبروه، فقال:","((هم الذين لا يرقون، ولا يسترقون، ولا يتطيرون، وعلى ربهم يتوكلون)).","فقام عكاشة بن محصن، فقال: ادع اللّٰه أن يجعلني منهم، فقال:","((أنت منهم)).","ثم قام رجل آخر، فقال: ادع اللّٰه أن يجعلني منهم، فقال:","((سبقك بها عكاشة))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه مسلم (٢٢٠) والبخاري (٦٥٤١). وذكر البخاري بعض هذه القصة في كتاب الطب (٥٧٠٥).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب سبعون ألفًا يدخلون الجنة بغير حساب","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by Muslim (220) and al-Bukhārī (6541). Al-Bukhārī also mentioned part of this account in Kitāb al-Ṭibb (5705).","chapter_en":"Seventy Thousand Will Enter Paradise Without Reckoning","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":16,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ḥuṣayn ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated: I was with Saʿīd ibn Jubayr when he asked: “Which of you saw the star that fell last night?” I said: “I did.” Then I added: “I was not praying at the time, however; I had been stung.” He asked: “What did you do?” I replied: “I sought ruqyah.” He asked: “What made you do that?” I replied: “A hadith al-Shaʿbī narrated to us.” He asked: “What did al-Shaʿbī narrate to you?” I said: “He narrated to us from Buraydah ibn al-Ḥuṣayb al-Aslamī that he said: ‘There is no ruqyah except for the evil eye or a venomous sting.’”","Saʿīd said: “The one who stops at what he has heard has done well. But Ibn ʿAbbās narrated to us from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: ʿThe nations were shown to me. I saw a Prophet accompanied by a small group, a Prophet accompanied by one or two men, and a Prophet with no one at all. Then a vast multitude was shown to me, and I thought they were my Ummah. But it was said to me: “This is Mūsā ﷺ and his people. Look toward the horizon.” I looked and saw a vast multitude. Then it was said to me: “Look toward the other horizon.” I looked and saw another vast multitude.","It was said to me: “This is your Ummah, and with them are seventy thousand who will enter Paradise without reckoning or punishment.”’” Then the Prophet ﷺ stood and entered his home. The people began discussing who those people might be who would enter Paradise without reckoning or punishment. Some said: “Perhaps they are those who accompanied the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” Others said: “Perhaps they are those who were born in Islam and never associated anything with Allah.”","They mentioned various possibilities. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to them and asked: “What are you discussing?” They told him, and he said: “They are those who do not perform ruqyah for others, do not ask others for ruqyah, do not believe in evil omens, and place their trust in their Lord.” ʿUkāshah ibn Miḥṣan stood and said: “Ask Allah to make me among them.” He replied: “You are among them.” Then another man stood and said: “Ask Allah to make me among them.”","He replied: “ʿUkāshah has preceded you to it.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":220},{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6541},{"key":"وذکر_البخاری_بعض_ہذہ_القصہ/کتاب_الطب","label":". وذكر البخاري بعض هذه القصة في كتاب الطب","number":5705}]},{"num":16375,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة، أن النبي ﷺ قال:","((يدخل من أمتي الجنة سبعون ألفًا بغير حساب)).","فقال رجل: يا رسول الله، ادع اللّٰه أن يجعلني منهم، قال:","((اللهم اجعله منهم)).","ثم قام آخر، فقال: يا رسول الله، ادع اللّٰه أن يجعلني منهم، قال:","((سبقك بها عكاشة))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٢١٦).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب سبعون ألفًا يدخلون الجنة بغير حساب","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (216).","chapter_en":"Seventy Thousand Will Enter Paradise Without Reckoning","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":16,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Seventy thousand from my Ummah will enter Paradise without reckoning.” A man said: “O Messenger of Allah, ask Allah to make me among them.” He said: “O Allah, make him among them.” Then another man stood and said: “O Messenger of Allah, ask Allah to make me among them.” He replied: “ʿUkāshah has preceded you to it.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":216}]},{"num":16376,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة قال: سمعت رسول اللّٰه ﷺ يقول:","((يدخل الجنة من أمتي زمرة هي سبعون ألفًا، تضيء وجوههم إضاءة القمر)).","فقام عكاشة بن محصن الأسدي، يرفع نمرة عليه، قال: ادع اللّٰه لي يا رسول اللّٰه أن يجعلني منهم، فقال:","((اللهم اجعله منهم)).","ثم قام رجل من الأنصار فقال: يا رسول الله، ادع اللّٰه أن يجعلني منهم، فقال رسول الله ﷺ:","((سبقك عكاشة))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في اللباس (٥٨١١) ومسلم (٣٦٩ :٢١٦).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب سبعون ألفًا يدخلون الجنة بغير حساب","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Libās (5811) and Muslim (369 :216).","chapter_en":"Seventy Thousand Will Enter Paradise Without Reckoning","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":16,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “A group of seventy thousand from my Ummah will enter Paradise, their faces shining like the moon.” ʿUkāshah ibn Miḥṣan al-Asadī stood, lifting the striped cloak he was wearing, and said: “O Messenger of Allah, ask Allah to make me among them.” He said: “O Allah, make him among them.” Then a man from the Anṣār stood and said: “O Messenger of Allah, ask Allah to make me among them.”","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “ʿUkāshah has preceded you.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari/اللباس","label":"البخاري في اللباس","number":5811},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":369}]},{"num":16377,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة أن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال:","((يدخل الجنة من أمتي سبعون ألفًا زمرة واحدة منهم على صورة القمر))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٢١٧).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب سبعون ألفًا يدخلون الجنة بغير حساب","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (217).","chapter_en":"Seventy Thousand Will Enter Paradise Without Reckoning","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":16,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Seventy thousand from my Ummah will enter Paradise as a single group, their appearance like the moon.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":217}]},{"num":16378,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر بن عبد اللّٰه قال في حديث طويل:","((فتنجو أول زمرة وجوههم كالقمر ليلة البدر سبعون ألفًا لا يحاسبون، ثم الذين يلونهم كأضوأ نجم في السماء، ثم كذلك، ثم تحل الشفاعة)).","الحديث."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (١٩١).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب سبعون ألفًا يدخلون الجنة بغير حساب","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (191).","chapter_en":"Seventy Thousand Will Enter Paradise Without Reckoning","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":16,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated in a lengthy hadith: “The first group to be saved will consist of seventy thousand whose faces will be like the full moon. They will not be brought to account. Those who follow them will be like the brightest star in the sky, then those after them likewise. Then intercession will be permitted.” The hadith continues."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":191}]},{"num":16379,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن سهل بن سعد، أن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال:","((ليدخلن الجنة من أمتي سبعون ألفًا، أو سبعمائة ألف - لا يدري أبو حازم أيهما قال - متماسكون، آخذ بعضهم بعضًا، لا يدخل أولهم حتى يدخل آخرهم، وجوههم على صورة القمر ليلة البدر))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٦٥٥٤)، ومسلم (٢١٩).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب سبعون ألفًا يدخلون الجنة بغير حساب","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6554) and Muslim (219).","chapter_en":"Seventy Thousand Will Enter Paradise Without Reckoning","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":16,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Sahl ibn Saʿd narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Seventy thousand from my Ummah—or seven hundred thousand; Abū Ḥāzim was uncertain which he said—will certainly enter Paradise holding closely to one another, each taking hold of the other. The first of them will not enter until the last of them has entered, and their faces will be like the full moon.”"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["قوله: ((أو سبعمائة ألف)) الأخذ باليقين وهو: ((سبعون ألف)) - أولى، وعليه تدل الأحاديث الأخرى.","وقوله: ((متماسكون، آخذ بعضهم بعضًا)) أي ممسك بعضهم بيد بعض. ويدخلون معترضين صفًا واحدًا بعضهم بجنب بعض. وهذا صريح في عظم باب الجنة."],"en":["Regarding the phrase:","“Or seven hundred thousand,”","the author states that it is preferable to adopt the certain wording, “seventy thousand,” as this is supported by the other hadiths.","Regarding the phrase:","“Holding closely to one another, each taking hold of the other,”","the author explains that each will be holding the hand of another. They will enter spread out in a single row, side by side.","This clearly demonstrates the immense width of the gate of Paradise."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6554},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":219}]},{"num":16380,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عمران بن حصين قال: قال نبي اللّٰه ﷺ:","((يدخل الجنة من أمتي سبعون ألفًا بغير حساب)).","قالوا: ومن هم يا رسول الله؟ قال:","((هم الذين لا يكتوون ولا يسترقون، وعلى ربهم يتوكلون)).","فقام عكاشة، فقال: ادع اللّٰه أن يجعلني منهم، قال:","((أنت منهم)).","قال: فقام رجل، فقال: يا نبي الله، ادع اللّٰه أن يجعلني منهم، قال:","((سبقك بها عكاشة))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٢١٨).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب سبعون ألفًا يدخلون الجنة بغير حساب","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (218).","chapter_en":"Seventy Thousand Will Enter Paradise Without Reckoning","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":16,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn narrated that the Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: “Seventy thousand from my Ummah will enter Paradise without reckoning.” They asked: “Who are they, O Messenger of Allah?” He replied: “They are those who do not cauterize themselves, do not ask others for ruqyah, and place their trust in their Lord.” ʿUkāshah stood and said: “Ask Allah to make me among them.” He replied: “You are among them.” Then another man stood and said: “O Prophet of Allah, ask Allah to make me among them.”","He replied: “ʿUkāshah has preceded you to it.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":218}]},{"num":16381,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن رفاعة بن عرابة الجهني قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((…وقد وعدني ربي عز وجل أن يدخل من أمتي سبعين ألفًا لا حساب عليهم، ولا عذاب، وإني لأرجو أن لا يدخلوها حتى تبوؤوا أنتم ومن صلح من آبائكم وأزواجكم وذرياتكم مساكن في الجنة))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (١٦٢١٥).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب سبعون ألفًا يدخلون الجنة بغير حساب","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (16215).","chapter_en":"Seventy Thousand Will Enter Paradise Without Reckoning","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":16,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Rifāʿah ibn ʿArābah al-Juhanī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “…My Lord, Mighty and Majestic, has promised me that seventy thousand from my Ummah will enter Paradise without reckoning and without punishment. And I hope that they will not enter it until you, together with the righteous among your fathers, spouses, and descendants, have taken up your dwellings in Paradise.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":16215,"n":16215}]},{"num":16382,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن ابن مسعود، أن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ أري الأمم بالموسم، فراثت عليه أمته، قال:","((فأريت أمتي، فأعجبني كثرتهم، قد ملؤوا السهل والجبل، فقيل لي: إن مع هؤلاء سبعين ألفًا يدخلون الجنة بغير حساب، هم الذين لا يكتوون، ولا يسترقون، ولا يتطيرون، وعلى ربهم يتوكلون)).","فقال عكاشة: يا رسول الله، ادع اللّٰه أن يجعلني منهم. فدعا له، ثم قام - يعني آخر - فقال: يا رسول الله، ادع اللّٰه أن يجعلني منهم. قال:","((سبقك بها عكاشة))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (٣٨١٩)، والبزار في مسنده - كشف الأستار - (٣٩٣٩)، وصححه ابن حبان (٦٠٨٤).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب سبعون ألفًا يدخلون الجنة بغير حساب","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (3819), al-Bazzār in his Musnad — Kashf al-Astār (3939), and authenticated by Ibn Ḥibbān (6084).","chapter_en":"Seventy Thousand Will Enter Paradise Without Reckoning","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":16,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn Masʿūd narrated that the nations were shown to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the season, and his Ummah was delayed in being shown to him. He said: “Then my Ummah was shown to me, and their great number amazed me. They filled the plain and the mountain. It was said to me: ‘Among these are seventy thousand who will enter Paradise without reckoning. They are those who do not cauterize themselves, do not ask others for ruqyah, do not believe in evil omens, and place their trust in their Lord.’”","ʿUkāshah said: “O Messenger of Allah, ask Allah to make me among them.” So he supplicated for him. Then another man stood and said: “O Messenger of Allah, ask Allah to make me among them.” He replied: “ʿUkāshah has preceded you to it.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"البزار/مسندہ_کشف_الاستار","label":"البزار في مسنده - كشف الأستار -","number":3939},{"key":"صححہ_ابن_حبان","label":"صححه ابن حبان","number":6084},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":3819,"n":3819}]},{"num":16383,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبد اللّٰه بن مسعود قال: تحدثنا عند رسول اللّٰه ﷺ ذات ليلة حتى أكرينا الحديث، ثم رجعنا إلى أهلنا، فلما أصبحنا، غدونا على رسول اللّٰه ﷺ فقال:","((عرضت علي الأنبياء الليلة، وأتباعها من أممها، فجعل النبي يمر ومعه الثلاثة من أمته، والنبي معه العصابة من أمته، والنبي معه النفر من أمته، والنبي معه الرجل من أمته، والنبي ما معه أحد من أمته، حتى مر علي موسى بن عمران ﷺ في كبكبة من بني إسرائيل، فلما رأيتهم أعجبوني، قلت: يا رب من هؤلاء؟ فقال: هذا أخوك موسى بن عمران ومن معه من بني إسرائيل، قلت: يا رب، فأين أمتي؟ قال: انظر عن يمينك، فإذا الظراب ظراب مكة، قد سد بوجوه الرجال، قلت: من هؤلاء يا رب؟ قال: أمتك، قلت: رضيت رب، قال: أرضيت؟ قلت: نعم، قال: انظر عن يسارك)).","قال:","((فنظرت، فإذا الأفق قد سد بوجوه الرجال، فقال: رضيت؟ قلت: رضيت، قيل: فإن مع هؤلاء سبعين ألفًا يدخلون الجنة، لا حساب لهم)).","فأنشأ عكاشة بن محصن، أحد بني أسد بن خزيمة، فقال: يا نبي الله، ادع اللّٰه أن يجعلني منهم، فقال:","((اللهم اجعله منهم)).","ثم أنشأ رجل آخر منهم، فقال: يا رسول الله، ادع اللّٰه أن يجعلني منهم، قال:","((سبقك بها عكاشة))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (٣٩٨٩).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب سبعون ألفًا يدخلون الجنة بغير حساب","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (3989).","chapter_en":"Seventy Thousand Will Enter Paradise Without Reckoning","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":16,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated: One night we remained with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ talking until the conversation became lengthy, then we returned to our families. The next morning we went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: “Last night the Prophets and the followers from their nations were shown to me. A Prophet would pass with three members of his nation, another Prophet with a group from his nation, another with a small number, another with one man, and another Prophet with no one from his nation.","Then Mūsā ibn ʿImrān ﷺ passed before me with a large gathering of the Children of Israel. When I saw them, I was impressed by them. I said: ‘My Lord, who are these?’ He said: ‘This is your brother Mūsā ibn ʿImrān and those with him from the Children of Israel.’ I asked: ‘My Lord, then where is my Ummah?’ He said: ‘Look to your right.’ I looked, and the hills of Makkah were covered with the faces of men. I asked: ‘Who are these, my Lord?’ He said: ‘Your Ummah.’","I said: ‘I am pleased, my Lord.’ He asked: ‘Are you pleased?’ I said: ‘Yes.’ He said: ‘Look to your left.’” The Prophet ﷺ continued: “I looked, and the entire horizon was filled with the faces of men. He asked: ‘Are you pleased?’ I said: ‘I am pleased.’ Then it was said: ‘Among these are seventy thousand who will enter Paradise without reckoning.’” ʿUkāshah ibn Miḥṣan, one of Banū Asad ibn Khuzaymah, stood and said: “O Prophet of Allah, ask Allah to make me among them.”","He said: “O Allah, make him among them.” Then another man stood and said: “O Messenger of Allah, ask Allah to make me among them.” He replied: “ʿUkāshah has preceded you to it.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":3987,"n":3987}]},{"num":16384,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي أمامة، أن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال:","((إن الله وعدني أن يدخل من أمتي الجنة سبعين ألفًا بغير حساب)).","فقال يزيد بن الأخنس السلمي: والله ما أولئك في أمتك إلا كالذباب الأصهب في الذبان! فقال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((فإن ربي قد وعدني سبعين ألفًا، مع كل ألف سبعون ألفًا، وزادني ثلاث حثيات))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (٢٢١٥٦)، وابن حبان (٧٢٤٦).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب يدخل من أمة محمد سبعون ألفًا، مع كل ألف سبعون ألفًا","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (22156) and Ibn Ḥibbān (7246).","chapter_en":"Seventy Thousand from the Ummah of Muḥammad ﷺ Will Enter Paradise, and with Every Thousand Another Seventy Thousand","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":17,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Umāmah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah has promised me that seventy thousand from my Ummah will enter Paradise without reckoning.” Yazīd ibn al-Akhnas al-Sulamī said: “By Allah, those among your Ummah are only like a reddish fly among all the flies!” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “My Lord has also promised me seventy thousand with every thousand, and He has additionally granted me three handfuls.”"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["وقوله: ((مع كل ألف سبعون ألفًا)) هذه زيادة من اللّه عز وجل بعد استزادة النبي ﷺ، كما في الحديث الآتي:"],"en":["Regarding the phrase:","“With every thousand, seventy thousand,”","the author states that this was an additional grant from Allah, Mighty and Majestic, after the Prophet ﷺ asked Him for an increase, as explained in the following hadith."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":22156,"n":22156},{"key":"ibnhibban","label":"صحيح ابن حبان (التقاسيم والأنواع)","number":5161,"n":5157}]},{"num":16385,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة، عن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ أنه قال:","((سألت ربي عز وجل فوعدني أن يدخل من أمتي سبعين ألفًا على صورة القمر ليلة البدر. فاستزدت، فزادني مع كل ألف سبعين ألفًا، فقلت: أي رب، إن لم يكن هؤلاء مهاجري أمتي؟ قال: إذن أكملهم لك من الأعراب))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (٨٧٠٧).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب يدخل من أمة محمد سبعون ألفًا، مع كل ألف سبعون ألفًا","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (8707).","chapter_en":"Seventy Thousand from the Ummah of Muḥammad ﷺ Will Enter Paradise, and with Every Thousand Another Seventy Thousand","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":17,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I asked my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, and He promised me that seventy thousand from my Ummah would enter Paradise with the appearance of the full moon. I asked Him for more, so He increased them by seventy thousand with every thousand. I said: ‘My Lord, what if those numbers are not completed by the Muhājirūn of my Ummah?’ He said: ‘Then I will complete their number for you from the Bedouins.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":8707,"n":8707}]},{"num":16386,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عتبة بن عبد السلمي قال: جاء أعرابي إلى رسول اللّٰه ﷺ فقال له: ما حوضك الذي تحدث عنه؟ قال:","((هو كما بين البيضاء إلى بصرى، ثم يمدني اللّٰه عز وجل فيه بكراع، فلا يدري بشر ممن خلق أين طرفاه)).","قال: فكبر عمر بن الخطاب. فقال: أما الحوض فيزدحم عليه فقراء المهاجرين الذين يقتلون في سبيل الله، ويموتون في سبيل اللّٰه عز وجل، وأرجو أن يوردني اللّٰه عز وجل الكراع فأشرب منه. فقال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((إن ربي عز وجل وعدني أن يدخل الجنة من أمتي سبعين ألفًا بغير حساب، ثم يشفع كل ألف بسبعين ألفًا، ثم يحثي لي بكفيه ثلاث حثيات)).","وكبر عمر فقال: إن السبعين الألف الأولين يشفعهم اللّٰه عز وجل في آبائهم وأبنائهم وعشائرهم، وأرجو أن يجعلني اللّٰه عز وجل في أحد الحثيات الأواخر."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الفسوي في تاريخه (٣٤٢-٣٤١/٢)، والطبراني في الكبير (١٢٧-١٢٦/١٧).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب يدخل من أمة محمد سبعون ألفًا، مع كل ألف سبعون ألفًا","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Fasawī in his Tārīkh (2/341-342) and al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Kabīr (17/126-127).","chapter_en":"Seventy Thousand from the Ummah of Muḥammad ﷺ Will Enter Paradise, and with Every Thousand Another Seventy Thousand","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":17,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿUtbah ibn ʿAbd al-Sulamī narrated: A Bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked: “What is this Ḥawḍ that you speak about?” He replied: “It is like the distance from al-Bayḍāʾ to Buṣrā. Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will supply it for me through an inlet whose two ends no human being among His creation knows.” ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb proclaimed Allah’s greatness. He said: “As for the Ḥawḍ, the poor among the Muhājirūn who are killed in the path of Allah and die in the path of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will crowd around it. I hope that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will bring me to that inlet so that I may drink from it.”","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “My Lord, Mighty and Majestic, has promised me that seventy thousand from my Ummah will enter Paradise without reckoning. Then every thousand will intercede for seventy thousand, and then He will take three handfuls for me with His two Hands.” ʿUmar proclaimed Allah’s greatness and said: “The first seventy thousand will be enabled by Allah, Mighty and Majestic, to intercede for their fathers, their children, and their clans. And I hope that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will place me in one of the final handfuls.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"الفسوی/تاریخہ","label":"الفسوي في تاريخه","number":342},{"key":"الطبرانی/الکبیر","label":"الطبراني في الكبير","number":127}]},{"num":16387,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن شريح بن عبيد قال: مرض ثوبان بحمص، وعليها عبدالله بن قرط الأزدي، فلم يعده، فدخل على ثوبان رجل من الكلاعيين عائدًا. فقال له ثوبان: أتكتب؟ فقال: نعم. فقال: اكتب. فكتب للأمير عبدالله بن قرط: من ثوبان مولى رسول اللّٰه ﷺ، أما بعد، فإنه لو كان لموسى وعيسى مولى بحضرتك لعدته، ثم طوى الكتاب وقال له: أتبلغه إياه؟ فقال: نعم. فانطلق الرجل بكتابه فدفعه إلى ابن قرط، فلما قرأه قام فزعًا، فقال الناس: ما شأنه أحدث أمر؟ فأتى ثوبان حتى دخل عليه، فعاده وجلس عنده ساعة، ثم قام فأخذ ثوبان بردائه، وقال: اجلس حتى أحدثك حديثًا سمعته من رسول اللّٰه ﷺ، سمعته يقول:","((ليدخلن الجنة من أمتي سبعون ألفًا لا حساب عليهم ولا عذاب، مع كل ألف سبعون ألفًا))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (٢٢٤١٨).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب يدخل من أمة محمد سبعون ألفًا، مع كل ألف سبعون ألفًا","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (22418).","chapter_en":"Seventy Thousand from the Ummah of Muḥammad ﷺ Will Enter Paradise, and with Every Thousand Another Seventy Thousand","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":17,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Shurayḥ ibn ʿUbayd narrated: Thawbān became ill in Ḥimṣ while ʿAbdullāh ibn Qurṭ al-Azdī was its governor, but he did not visit him. A man from the Kalāʿiyyīn entered upon Thawbān to visit him. Thawbān asked: “Can you write?” He replied: “Yes.” Thawbān said: “Write.” So he wrote to the governor ʿAbdullāh ibn Qurṭ: “From Thawbān, the freedman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. To proceed: Had there been a freedman of Mūsā or ʿĪsā present near you, you would have visited him.”","Then he folded the letter and asked: “Will you deliver this to him?” The man replied: “Yes.” He went and handed the letter to Ibn Qurṭ. When he read it, he stood up alarmed. The people asked: “What is the matter? Has something happened?” He went to Thawbān, entered upon him, visited him, and sat with him for a while. When he stood to leave, Thawbān took hold of his cloak and said: “Sit down until I narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”","He said: “Seventy thousand from my Ummah will certainly enter Paradise without reckoning or punishment, and with every thousand will be another seventy thousand.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":22418,"n":22418}]},{"num":16388,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي سعيد الأنماري، أن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال:","((إن ربي وعدني أن يدخل الجنة من أمتي سبعين ألفًا بغير حساب، ويشفع كل ألف لسبعين ألفًا، ثم يحثي ربي ثلاث حثيات بكفيه)).","قال قيس: فقلت لأبي سعيد: أنت سمعت هذا من رسول الله ﷺ؟ قال: نعم، بأذني ووعاه قلبي. قال أبو سعيد:","((وذلك إن شاء اللّه يستوعب مهاجري أمته، ويوفي اللّٰه عز وجل بقيته من أعرابنا))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الطبراني في الأوسط (٤٠٦)، وفي الكبير (٣٠٥-٣٠٤/٢٢).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب يدخل من أمة محمد سبعون ألفًا، مع كل ألف سبعون ألفًا","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Awsaṭ (406) and al-Muʿjam al-Kabīr (22/304-305).","chapter_en":"Seventy Thousand from the Ummah of Muḥammad ﷺ Will Enter Paradise, and with Every Thousand Another Seventy Thousand","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":17,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Anmārī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “My Lord has promised me that seventy thousand from my Ummah will enter Paradise without reckoning. Every thousand of them will intercede for seventy thousand, then my Lord will take three handfuls with His two Hands.” Qays said: I asked Abū Saʿīd: “Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” He replied: “Yes, with my own ears, and my heart retained it.” Abū Saʿīd said: “That, Allah willing, will encompass the Muhājirūn of his Ummah, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will complete the remainder from our Bedouins.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"الطبرانی/الاوسط","label":"الطبراني في الأوسط","number":406},{"key":"وفی_الکبیر","label":"وفي الكبير","number":305},{"key":"sh28171","label":"المعجم الأوسط للطبراني","number":404,"n":402}]},{"num":16389,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أنس، عن النبي ﷺ قال:","((يدخل الجنة من أمتي سبعون ألفًا)).","قالوا: زدنا يا رسول اللّه، قال:","((لكل رجل سبعون ألفًا)).","قالوا: زدنا يا رسول الله، وكان على كثيب، فحثا بيده. قالوا: زدنا يا رسول اللّٰه فقال:","((هذا)).","وحثا بيده، قالوا: يا نبي الله، أبعد اللّٰه من دخل النار بعد هذا."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو يعلى (٣٧٨٣).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب يدخل من أمة محمد سبعون ألفًا، مع كل ألف سبعون ألفًا","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abū Yaʿlā (3783).","chapter_en":"Seventy Thousand from the Ummah of Muḥammad ﷺ Will Enter Paradise, and with Every Thousand Another Seventy Thousand","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":17,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Seventy thousand from my Ummah will enter Paradise.” They said: “Give us more, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “For every one of them, seventy thousand.” They said: “Give us more, O Messenger of Allah.” He was upon a mound, so he scooped with his hand. They again said: “Give us more, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “And this.” Then he scooped with his hand again. They said: “O Prophet of Allah, may Allah cast far away whoever enters the Fire after all of this.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ابو_یعلی","label":"أبو يعلى","number":3783},{"key":"sh12520","label":"مسند أبي يعلى","number":3783,"n":3788}]},{"num":16390,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أنس، أن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال:","((يدخل الجنة من أمتي سبعون ألفًا بغير حساب)).","فقال أبو بكر: يا رسول اللّه، زدنا، قال:","((وهكذا)).","فقال عمر: يا أبا بكر، إن شاء اللّٰه أدخلهم الجنة حفنة واحدة."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه البزار - كشف الأستار - (٣٥٤٨).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب يدخل من أمة محمد سبعون ألفًا، مع كل ألف سبعون ألفًا","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Bazzār in Kashf al-Astār (3548).","chapter_en":"Seventy Thousand from the Ummah of Muḥammad ﷺ Will Enter Paradise, and with Every Thousand Another Seventy Thousand","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":17,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Seventy thousand from my Ummah will enter Paradise without reckoning.” Abū Bakr said: “O Messenger of Allah, give us more.” He said: “And like this,” gesturing with a handful. ʿUmar then said: “O Abū Bakr, if Allah wills, He can admit them all into Paradise in a single handful.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"البزار_کشف_الاستار","label":"البزار - كشف الأستار -","number":3548}]},{"num":16391,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبد الله بن مسعود قال: كنا مع النبي ﷺ في قبة، فقال:","((أترضون أن تكونوا ربع أهل الجنة؟)).","قلنا: نعم، قال:","((أترضون أن تكونوا ثلث أهل الجنة؟)).","قلنا: نعم، قال:","((أترضون أن تكونوا شطر أهل الجنة؟)).","قلنا: نعم، قال:","((والذي نفس محمد بيده، إني لأرجو أن تكونوا نصف أهل الجنة، وذلك أن الجنة لا يدخلها إلا نفس مسلمة، وما أنتم في أهل الشرك إلا كالشعرة البيضاء في جلد الثور الأسود، أو كالشعرة السوداء في جلد الثور الأحمر))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٦٥٢٨)، ومسلم (٣٧٧ :٢٢١).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب في عدد أهل الجنة من هذه الأمة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6528) and Muslim (377 :221).","chapter_en":"The Number of the People of Paradise from This Ummah","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":18,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated: We were with the Prophet ﷺ in a tent when he asked: “Would you be pleased to constitute one quarter of the people of Paradise?” We replied: “Yes.” He asked: “Would you be pleased to constitute one third of the people of Paradise?” We replied: “Yes.” He asked: “Would you be pleased to constitute half of the people of Paradise?” We replied: “Yes.” He said: “By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muḥammad, I hope that you will constitute half of the people of Paradise.","That is because none will enter Paradise except a Muslim soul, and compared with the people of shirk, you are only like a white hair on the hide of a black bull, or a black hair on the hide of a red bull.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6528},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":377}]},{"num":16392,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي سعيد قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((يقول الله: يا آدم، فيقول: لبيك وسعديك، والخير في يديك، قال: يقول: أخرج بعث النار، قال: وما بعث النار؟ قال: من كل ألف تسع مائة وتسعة وتسعين، فذاك حين يشيب الصغير، ﴿وَتَضَعُ كُلُّ ذَاتِ حَمْلٍ حَمْلَهَا وَتَرَى النَّاسَ سُكَارَىٰ وَمَا هُمْ بِسُكَارَىٰ وَلَكِنَّ عَذَابَ اللَّهِ شَدِيدٌ﴾ [الحج: ٢])).","فاشتد ذلك عليهم فقالوا: يا رسول الله، أينا ذلك الرجل؟ قال:","((أبشروا، فإن من يأجوج ومأجوج ألفًا ومنكم رجل)).","ثم قال:","((والذي نفسي بيده، إني لأطمع أن تكونوا ثلث أهل الجنة)).","قال: فحمدنا اللّٰه وكبرنا، ثم قال:","((والذي نفسي بيده، إني لأطمع أن تكونوا شطر أهل الجنة، إن مثلكم في الأمم كمثل الشعرة البيضاء في جلد الثور الأسود، أو الرقمة في ذراع الحمار))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٦٥٣٠)، ومسلم (٣٧٩ :٢٢٢).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب في عدد أهل الجنة من هذه الأمة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6530) and Muslim (379 :222).","chapter_en":"The Number of the People of Paradise from This Ummah","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":18,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah will say: ‘O Ādam.’ He will reply: ‘Here I am at Your service and ready to obey You, and all good is in Your Hands.’ Allah will say: ‘Bring forth the contingent of the Fire.’ He will ask: ‘What is the contingent of the Fire?’ Allah will say: ‘From every thousand, nine hundred and ninety-nine.’ That will be the time when the young child turns gray, when every pregnant woman will miscarry, and you will see the people as though intoxicated, though they are not intoxicated; rather, the punishment of Allah is severe.”","[al-Ḥajj 22:2] This weighed heavily upon them, so they asked: “O Messenger of Allah, which one of us will be that one?” He replied: “Receive glad tidings. From Yaʾjūj and Maʾjūj there will be one thousand, and from you one.” Then he said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, I hope that you will constitute one third of the people of Paradise.” We praised Allah and proclaimed His greatness. Then he said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, I hope that you will constitute half of the people of Paradise.","Your likeness among all the nations is like a white hair on the hide of a black bull, or like a mark upon the foreleg of a donkey.”"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["وقوله: ((فذاك حين يشيب الصغير)) معناه موافق لقوله تعالى:","﴿فَكَيْفَ تَتَّقُونَ إِنْ كَفَرْتُمْ يَوْمًا يَجْعَلُ الْوِلْدَانَ شِيبًا﴾ [المزمل: ١٧]."],"en":["Regarding the statement:","“That will be the time when the young child turns gray,”","its meaning corresponds to the statement of Allah, the Exalted:","“Then how will you protect yourselves, if you disbelieve, from a Day that will turn children gray-haired?”","[al-Muzzammil 73:17]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6530},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":379}]},{"num":16393,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر بن عبد اللّٰه قال: سمعت رسول اللّٰه ﷺ يقول:","((أرجو أن يكون من يتبعني من أمتي يوم القيامة، ربع أهل الجنة)).","قال: فكبرنا. قال:","((أرجو أن يكونوا ثلث أهل الجنة)).","قال: فكبرنا. قال:","((أرجو أن يكونوا الشطر))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (١٥١١٤)، والبزار - كشف الأستار - (٣٥٣٣).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب في عدد أهل الجنة من هذه الأمة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (15114) and al-Bazzār in Kashf al-Astār (3533).","chapter_en":"The Number of the People of Paradise from This Ummah","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":18,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “I hope that those from my Ummah who follow me on the Day of Resurrection will constitute one quarter of the people of Paradise.” We proclaimed Allah’s greatness. Then he said: “I hope that they will constitute one third of the people of Paradise.” We again proclaimed Allah’s greatness. Then he said: “I hope that they will constitute half.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"البزار_کشف_الاستار","label":"البزار - كشف الأستار -","number":3533},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":15114,"n":15114}]},{"num":16394,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة، أن النبي ﷺ قال:","((أول من يدعى يوم القيامة آدم، فتراءى ذريته، فيقال: هذا أبوكم آدم، فيقول: لبيك وسعديك، فيقول: أخرج بعث جهنم من ذريتك، فيقول: يا رب كم أخرج؟ فيقول: أخرج من كل مائة تسعة وتسعين)).","فقالوا: يا رسول الله، إذا أخذ منا من كل مائة تسعة وتسعون، فماذا يبقى منا؟ قال:","((إن أمتي في الأمم كالشعرة البيضاء في الثور الأسود))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (٦٥٢٩).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب في عدد أهل الجنة من هذه الأمة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6529).","chapter_en":"The Number of the People of Paradise from This Ummah","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":18,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The first to be called on the Day of Resurrection will be Ādam. His descendants will be shown to him, and it will be said: ‘This is your father Ādam.’ He will say: ‘Here I am at Your service and ready to obey You.’ It will be said: ‘Bring forth from your descendants the contingent for Hell.’ He will ask: ‘My Lord, how many should I bring forth?’ He will say: ‘From every hundred, ninety-nine.’”","They asked: “O Messenger of Allah, if ninety-nine out of every hundred of us are taken, then what will remain of us?” He replied: “My Ummah among the other nations is like a white hair on a black bull.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6529}]},{"num":16395,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أنس بن مالك قال: أنزلت:","﴿يَا أَيُّهَا النَّاسُ اتَّقُوا رَبَّكُمْ إِنَّ زَلْزَلَةَ السَّاعَةِ شَيْءٌ عَظِيمٌ﴾ إلى قوله تعالى: ﴿وَلَكِنَّ عَذَابَ اللَّهِ شَدِيدٌ﴾ [الحج: ١-٢].","قال: نزلت على النبي ﷺ وهو في مسير له، فرفع بها صوته حتى ثاب إليه أصحابه، فقال:","((أتدرون أي يوم هذا؟ يوم يقول اللّٰه لآدم: يا آدم، قم فابعث بعث النار: من كل ألف تسعمائة وتسعة وتسعين إلى النار، وواحدًا إلى الجنة)).","قال: فكبر ذلك على المسلمين، فقال النبي ﷺ:","((سددوا وقاربوا وأبشروا، فوالذي نفسي بيده، ما أنتم في الناس إلا كالشامة في جنب البعير، أو الرقمة في ذراع الدابة، فإن معكم خليقتين ما كانتا مع شيء قط إلا كثرتاه: يأجوج ومأجوج ومن هلك من كفرة الإنس والجن))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه عبد الرزاق في تفسيره (٣١/٢) - واللفظ له -، وعبد بن حميد (١١٨٥)، وصححه ابن حبان (٧٣٥٤).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب في عدد أهل الجنة من هذه الأمة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq in his Tafsīr (2/31), whose wording this is, ʿAbd ibn Ḥumayd (1185), and authenticated by Ibn Ḥibbān (7354).","chapter_en":"The Number of the People of Paradise from This Ummah","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":18,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik narrated: The verses were revealed: “O mankind, fear your Lord. Indeed, the convulsion of the Hour is a tremendous thing…” up to the statement: “…but the punishment of Allah is severe.” [al-Ḥajj 22:1-2] They were revealed to the Prophet ﷺ while he was traveling. He raised his voice reciting them until his Companions gathered around him. He asked: “Do you know what Day this is? It is the Day when Allah will say to Ādam: ‘O Ādam, rise and send forth the contingent of the Fire: from every thousand, nine hundred and ninety-nine to the Fire and one to Paradise.’”","This greatly distressed the Muslims. The Prophet ﷺ then said: “Remain upon the right course, come as close as you can, and receive glad tidings. By the One in whose hand is my soul, compared with mankind you are only like a small mark on the side of a camel, or a mark on the foreleg of an animal. For with you are two creations which have never been together with anything except that they greatly increased its number: Yaʾjūj and Maʾjūj, and those who perished among the disbelievers of mankind and the jinn.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"عبد_الرزاق/تفسیرہ","label":"عبد الرزاق في تفسيره","number":31},{"key":"عبد_بن_حمید","label":"عبد بن حميد","number":1185},{"key":"صححہ_ابن_حبان","label":"صححه ابن حبان","number":7354},{"key":"ibnhibban","label":"صحيح ابن حبان (التقاسيم والأنواع)","number":5076,"n":5072}]},{"num":16396,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي الدرداء، عن النبي ﷺ قال:","((إن اللّٰه تعالى يقول يوم القيامة لآدم: قم فجهز من ذريتك تسع مائة وتسعة وتسعين إلى النار، وواحدًا إلى الجنة)).","فبكى أصحابه وبكوا، ثم قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((ارفعوا رؤوسكم، والذي نفسي بيده، ما أمتي في الأمم إلا كالشعرة البيضاء في جلد الثور الأسود)).","فخفف ذلك عنهم."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (٢٧٤٨٩).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب في عدد أهل الجنة من هذه الأمة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (27489).","chapter_en":"The Number of the People of Paradise from This Ummah","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":18,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū al-Dardāʾ narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Allah, the Exalted, will say to Ādam on the Day of Resurrection: ‘Rise and prepare from your descendants nine hundred and ninety-nine for the Fire and one for Paradise.’” His Companions began to weep. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Raise your heads. By the One in whose hand is my soul, my Ummah among the other nations is only like a white hair on the hide of a black bull.” This eased their distress."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":27489,"n":27489}]},{"num":16397,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن بريدة قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((أهل الجنة عشرون ومائة صف، ثمانون منها من هذه الأمة، وأربعون من سائر الأمم))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الترمذي (٢٥٤٦)، وأحمد (٢٢٩٤٠)، وابن حبان (٧٤٥٩)، والحاكم (٨٢-٨١/١).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب في عدد أهل الجنة من هذه الأمة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (2546), Aḥmad (22940), Ibn Ḥibbān (7459), and al-Ḥākim (1/81-82).","chapter_en":"The Number of the People of Paradise from This Ummah","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":18,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Buraydah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The people of Paradise will form one hundred and twenty rows. Eighty of those rows will be from this Ummah, and forty will be from all the other nations.”"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["يحمل هذه الزيادة على فضل من اللّٰه بعد النصف."],"en":["The author explains that this increase beyond one half is to be understood as an additional bounty granted by Allah."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"tirmidhi","label":"الترمذي","number":2546},{"key":"hakim","label":"الحاكم","number":82},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":22940,"n":22940},{"key":"ibnhibban","label":"صحيح ابن حبان (التقاسيم والأنواع)","number":5160,"n":5156}]},{"num":16398,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي التياح قال: كان لمطرف بن عبد اللّٰه امرأتان، فجاء من عند إحداهما، فقالت الأخرى: جئت من عند فلانة؟ فقال: جئت من عند عمران بن حصين، فحدثنا أن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال:","((إن أقل ساكني الجنة النساء))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٢٧٣٨).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أقل ساكني الجنة النساء","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2738).","chapter_en":"Women Are the Least Numerous Inhabitants of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":19,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū al-Tayyāḥ narrated: Muṭarrif ibn ʿAbdullāh had two wives. He came from one of them, and the other asked: “Have you come from so-and-so?” He replied: “I came from ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn, who narrated to us that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘Women are the least numerous inhabitants of Paradise.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2738}]},{"num":16399,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عمارة بن خزيمة قال: بينما نحن مع عمرو بن العاص في حج أو عمرة، فقال: بينما نحن مع رسول اللّٰه ﷺ في هذا الشعب إذ قال:","((انظروا، هل ترون شيئًا؟)).","فقلنا: نرى غرابًا فيها غراب أعصم أحمر المنقار والرجلين. فقال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((لا يدخل الجنة من النساء إلا من كان منهن مثل هذا الغراب في الغربان))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (١٧٧٧٠) - واللفظ له -، وأبو يعلى (٧٣٤٣)، والحاكم (٦٠٢/٤).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أقل ساكني الجنة النساء","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (17770), whose wording this is, Abū Yaʿlā (7343), and al-Ḥākim (4/602).","chapter_en":"Women Are the Least Numerous Inhabitants of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":19,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿUmārah ibn Khuzaymah narrated: While we were with ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ during Ḥajj or ʿUmrah, he said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in this mountain pass, he said: “Look. Do you see anything?” We replied: “We see a flock of crows among which there is a white-marked crow with a red beak and red legs.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No women will enter Paradise except in a proportion like that crow among the other crows.”"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["قوله: ((مثل هذا الغراب في الغربان))، أي: قلة دخول النساء الجنة، كقلة هذا النوع من الغراب."],"en":["Regarding the statement:","“Like this crow among the other crows,”","the author explains that it refers to the small number of women entering Paradise, comparable to the rarity of that particular type of crow among other crows."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ابو_یعلی","label":"أبو يعلى","number":7343},{"key":"hakim","label":"الحاكم","number":602},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":17770,"n":17770}]},{"num":16400,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أنس بن مالك، عن النبي ﷺ قال:","((يخرج قوم من النار بعد ما مسهم منها سفع، فيدخلون الجنة، فيسميهم أهل الجنة: الجهنميين)).","وفي لفظ:","((ليصيبن أقوامًا سفع من النار بذنوب أصابوها عقوبة، ثم يدخلهم اللّٰه الجنة بفضل رحمته، يقال لهم: الجهنميون))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (٦٥٥٩) و(٧٤٥٠) باللفظ الثاني.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أهل الجنة الذين يقال لهم: الجهنميون","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6559), and also (7450) with the second wording.","chapter_en":"The People of Paradise Who Will Be Called “al-Jahannamiyyūn”","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":20,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Some people will be brought out of the Fire after being scorched by it, then they will enter Paradise. The people of Paradise will call them ‘al-Jahannamiyyūn.’”","In another wording: “Some people will certainly be scorched by the Fire as punishment for sins they committed. Then Allah will admit them into Paradise by the bounty of His mercy, and they will be called ‘al-Jahannamiyyūn.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6559},{"key":"و","label":"و","number":7450}]},{"num":16401,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عمران بن حصين، عن النبي ﷺ قال:","((يخرج قوم من النار بشفاعة محمد ﷺ فيدخلون الجنة يسمون: الجهنميين))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (٦٥٦٦).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أهل الجنة الذين يقال لهم: الجهنميون","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6566).","chapter_en":"The People of Paradise Who Will Be Called “al-Jahannamiyyūn”","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":20,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “People will be brought out of the Fire through the intercession of Muḥammad ﷺ and will enter Paradise. They will be called al-Jahannamiyyūn.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6566}]},{"num":16402,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن ابن مسعود، أن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال:","((يكون في النار قوم ما شاء الله، ثم يرحمهم اللّه فيخرجهم، فيكونون في أدنى الجنة، فيغتسلون في نهر الحياة، ويسميهم أهل الجنة جهنميين، لو أضاف أحدهم أهل الدنيا لأطعمهم وسقاهم، ولحفهم وفرشهم)).","قال: - وأحسبه - قال:","((وزوجهم لا ينقص ذلك مما عنده شيئًا))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (٤٣٣٧)، وأبو يعلى (٤٩٧٩) - واللفظ له -، وابن حبان (٧٤٢٨)، وأبو نعيم في صفة الجنة (٤٤٨).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أهل الجنة الذين يقال لهم: الجهنميون","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (4337), Abū Yaʿlā (4979), whose wording this is, Ibn Ḥibbān (7428), and Abū Nuʿaym in Ṣifat al-Jannah (448).","chapter_en":"The People of Paradise Who Will Be Called “al-Jahannamiyyūn”","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":20,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn Masʿūd narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Some people will remain in the Fire for as long as Allah wills. Then Allah will have mercy upon them and bring them out. They will be placed in the lowest part of Paradise and will bathe in the River of Life. The people of Paradise will call them al-Jahannamiyyūn. If one of them were to host all the people of the world, he would be able to feed them, give them drink, provide them with coverings, and furnish them.”","The narrator said: I think he also said: “And provide them with spouses, without any of what he possesses being diminished.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ابو_یعلی","label":"أبو يعلى","number":4979},{"key":"ibnhibban","label":"ابن حبان","number":7428},{"key":"ابو_نعیم/صفہ_الجنہ","label":"أبو نعيم في صفة الجنة","number":448},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":4337,"n":4337},{"key":"sh12520","label":"مسند أبي يعلى","number":4979,"n":4984}]},{"num":16403,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن حماد بن زيد، عن عمرو بن دينار، عن جابر، أن النبي ﷺ قال:","((يخرج من النار بالشفاعة كأنهم الثعارير)).","قلت: ما الثعارير؟ قال:","((الضغابيس، وكان قد سقط فمه)).","فقلت لعمرو بن دينار: أبا محمد، سمعت جابر بن عبدالله يقول: سمعت النبي ﷺ يقول:","((يخرج بالشفاعة من النار))؟","قال: نعم.","وفي لفظ عن حماد بن زيد قال: قلت لعمرو بن دينار: أسمعت جابر بن عبد اللّٰه يقول: سمعت النبي ﷺ يقول:","((إن اللّٰه يخرج قومًا من النار بالشفاعة))؟","قال: نعم."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٦٥٥٨)، ومسلم (٣١٨ :١٩١).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب أهل الجنة الذين يقال لهم: الجهنميون","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6558) and Muslim (318 :191).","chapter_en":"The People of Paradise Who Will Be Called “al-Jahannamiyyūn”","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":20,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from Jābir, that the Prophet ﷺ said: “People will be brought out of the Fire through intercession, looking like small shoots.” The narrator asked: “What are al-thaʿārīr?” He replied: “Tender plant shoots.” His teeth had fallen out, affecting his pronunciation. I asked ʿAmr ibn Dīnār: “O Abū Muḥammad, did you hear Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh say that he heard the Prophet ﷺ say: ‘People will be brought out of the Fire through intercession’?”","He replied: “Yes.”","In another wording, Ḥammād ibn Zayd said: I asked ʿAmr ibn Dīnār: “Did you hear Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh say that he heard the Prophet ﷺ say: ‘Allah will bring people out of the Fire through intercession’?” He replied: “Yes.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6558},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":318}]},{"num":16404,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي سعيد الخدري، أن النبي ﷺ قال:","((إذا دخل أهل الجنة الجنة، وأهل النار النار، يقول الله: من كان في قلبه مثقال حبة من خردل من إيمان فأخرجوه، فيخرجون قد امتحشوا وعادوا حممًا، فيلقون في نهر الحياة، فينبتون كما تنبت الحبة في حميل السيل - أو قال: حمية السيل -)).","وقال النبي ﷺ:","((ألم تروا أنها تنبت صفراء ملتوية))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٦٥٦٠)، ومسلم (١٨٤).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب أهل الجنة الذين يقال لهم: الجهنميون","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6560) and Muslim (184).","chapter_en":"The People of Paradise Who Will Be Called “al-Jahannamiyyūn”","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":20,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “When the people of Paradise have entered Paradise and the people of the Fire have entered the Fire, Allah will say: ‘Bring out whoever has in his heart faith equal to the weight of a mustard seed.’ They will be brought out after having been completely charred and turned to coal. Then they will be cast into the River of Life and will grow just as a seed grows in the sediment carried by a flood.”","The Prophet ﷺ said: “Have you not seen how it emerges yellow and twisted?”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6560},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":184}]},{"num":16405,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ في حديث الرؤية الطويل:","((إذا فرغ الله من القضاء بين العباد، وأراد أن يخرج برحمته من أراد من أهل النار، أمر الملائكة أن يخرجوا من النار من كان لا يشرك بالله شيئًا ممن أراد اللّٰه تعالى أن يرحمه ممن يقول: لا إله إلا الله، فيعرفونهم في النار، يعرفونهم بأثر السجود، تأكل النار من ابن آدم إلا أثر السجود، حرم الله على النار أن تأكل أثر السجود، فيخرجون من النار وقد امتحشوا، فيصب عليهم ماء الحياة، فينبتون منه كما تنبت الحبة في حميل السيل…)).","الحديث."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٧٤٣٧)، ومسلم (١٨٢).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب أهل الجنة الذين يقال لهم: الجهنميون","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (7437) and Muslim (182).","chapter_en":"The People of Paradise Who Will Be Called “al-Jahannamiyyūn”","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":20,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said in the lengthy hadith of the Vision: “When Allah has finished judging between the servants and wishes by His mercy to bring out whomever He wills from the people of the Fire, He will command the angels to bring out from the Fire those whom Allah, the Exalted, wishes to have mercy upon from among those who did not associate anything with Allah and who used to say: ‘There is no deity except Allah.’","The angels will recognize them in the Fire by the marks of prostration. The Fire consumes the son of Ādam except for the marks of prostration; Allah has forbidden the Fire from consuming the marks of prostration. They will be brought out of the Fire completely charred. Then the Water of Life will be poured over them, and they will grow from it just as a seed grows in the sediment carried by a flood…” The hadith continues."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":7437},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":182}]},{"num":16406,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن حذيفة، أن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال:","((يخرج الله قومًا منتنين قد محشتهم النار بشفاعة الشافعين، فيدخلهم الجنة، فيسمون: الجهنميون))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (٢٣٤٢٣)، وأبو داود الطيالسي في “مسنده” (٤٢٠).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب أهل الجنة الذين يقال لهم: الجهنميون","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (23423) and Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī in his Musnad (420).","chapter_en":"The People of Paradise Who Will Be Called “al-Jahannamiyyūn”","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":20,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ḥudhayfah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah will bring out people who have become foul-smelling and whom the Fire has charred, through the intercession of the intercessors. He will admit them into Paradise, and they will be called al-Jahannamiyyūn.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ابو_داود_الطیالسی/مسندہ","label":"أبو داود الطيالسي في “مسنده”","number":420},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":23423,"n":23423}]},{"num":16407,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبيد بن عمير قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((يخرج اللّٰه تعالى قومًا من النار بعدما امتحشوا فيها، وصاروا فحمًا، فيلقون في نهر على باب الجنة، يسمى نهر الحياة، فينبتون فيها كما تنبت الحبة في حميل السيل، أو كما تنبت الثعارير، فيدخلون الجنة، فيقال: هؤلاء عتقاء اللّٰه عز وجل من النار)).","وقال رجل متهم برأي الخوارج، يقال له هارون أبو موسى أو أبو موسى بن هارون: ما هذا الذي تحدث به أبا عاصم؟ فقال: إليك عني يا علج! فلو لم أسمعه من أكثر من ثلاثين من أصحاب رسول اللّٰه ﷺ لم أحدث به."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه ابن أبي عمر - المطالب العالية (٤٥٦٠) واللفظ له -، والبيهقي في شعب الإيمان (٣١٩).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أهل الجنة الذين يقال لهم: الجهنميون","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Ibn Abī ʿUmar, as cited in al-Maṭālib al-ʿĀliyah (4560), whose wording this is, and al-Bayhaqī in Shuʿab al-Īmān (319).","chapter_en":"The People of Paradise Who Will Be Called “al-Jahannamiyyūn”","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":20,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿUbayd ibn ʿUmayr narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah, the Exalted, will bring people out of the Fire after they have been completely charred in it and become like coal. They will be cast into a river at the gate of Paradise called the River of Life. There they will grow as a seed grows in the sediment carried by a flood, or as tender shoots grow. Then they will enter Paradise, and it will be said: ‘These are those whom Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has freed from the Fire.’”","A man suspected of holding the views of the Khawārij, named Hārūn Abū Mūsā—or Abū Mūsā ibn Hārūn—said: “What is this that you are narrating, O Abū ʿĀṣim?” He replied: “Away from me, you uncouth man! Had I not heard it from more than thirty of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I would not have narrated it.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ابن_ابی_عمر_المطالب_العالیہ","label":"ابن أبي عمر - المطالب العالية","number":4560},{"key":"البیہقی/شعب_الایمان","label":"البيهقي في شعب الإيمان","number":319}]},{"num":16408,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن مسروق، قال: سألنا عبد اللّٰه عن هذه الآية:","﴿وَلَا تَحْسَبَنَّ الَّذِينَ قُتِلُوا فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ أَمْوَاتًا بَلْ أَحْيَاءٌ عِنْدَ رَبِّهِمْ يُرْزَقُونَ﴾ [آل عمران: ١٦٩].","قال: أما إنا قد سألنا عن ذلك، فقال:","((أرواحهم في جوف طير خضر، لها قناديل معلقة بالعرش، تسرح من الجنة حيث شاءت، ثم تأوي إلى تلك القناديل…))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (١٨٨٧).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء أن أرواح المؤمنين من الشهداء وغيرهم كالطير تعلق في شجر الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1887).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated That the Souls of the Believers, Including the Martyrs and Others, Are Like Birds That Feed Among the Trees of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":21,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Masrūq narrated: We asked ʿAbdullāh about this verse: “Do not think of those who have been killed in the path of Allah as dead. Rather, they are alive with their Lord, receiving provision.” [Āl ʿImrān 3:169] He said: “We ourselves asked about that, and he said: ‘Their souls are inside green birds. They have lamps suspended from the Throne. They roam freely throughout Paradise wherever they wish, then return to those lamps…’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":1887}]},{"num":16409,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبد الرحمن بن كعب بن مالك الأنصاري أنه أخبره أن أباه كعب بن مالك كان يحدث أن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال:","((إنما نسمة المؤمن طير يعلق في شجر الجنة، حتى يرجعه اللّٰه إلى جسده يوم القيامة))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مالك في الجنائز (٤٩) والنسائي (٢٠٧٣)، وابن ماجه (٤٢٧١).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء أن أرواح المؤمنين من الشهداء وغيرهم كالطير تعلق في شجر الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Mālik in al-Janāʾiz (49), al-Nasā’ī (2073), and Ibn Mājah (4271).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated That the Souls of the Believers, Including the Martyrs and Others, Are Like Birds That Feed Among the Trees of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":21,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Kaʿb ibn Mālik al-Anṣārī reported that his father, Kaʿb ibn Mālik, used to narrate that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The soul of the believer is a bird that feeds among the trees of Paradise until Allah returns it to his body on the Day of Resurrection.”"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["وقوله: ((نسمة المؤمن)) بفتحتين، الروح."],"en":["Regarding the phrase “nasamat al-muʾmin,” with both vowels pronounced as fatḥah, it means: the soul."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"malik/الجنایز","label":"مالك في الجنائز","number":49},{"key":"nasai","label":"النسائي","number":2073},{"key":"ibnmajah","label":"ابن ماجه","number":4271}]},{"num":16410,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي سعيد الخدري قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((يخلص المؤمنون من النار، فيحبسون على قنطرة بين الجنة والنار، فيقص لبعضهم من بعض مظالم كانت بينهم في الدنيا، حتى إذا هذبوا ونقوا أذن لهم في دخول الجنة، فوالذي نفس محمد بيده، لأحدهم أهدى بمنزله في الجنة منه بمنزله كان في الدنيا))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (٦٥٣٥).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أهل الجنة أهدى بمنازلهم في الجنة من منازلهم كانت لهم في الدنيا","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6535).","chapter_en":"The People of Paradise Will Know Their Homes in Paradise Better Than They Knew Their Homes in This World","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":22,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The believers will be delivered from the Fire, then detained upon a bridge between Paradise and the Fire. Retribution will be taken among them for wrongs they committed against one another in the worldly life. When they have been refined and purified, they will be given permission to enter Paradise. By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muḥammad, each of them will know his dwelling in Paradise better than he knew his dwelling in this world.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6535}]},{"num":16411,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن ابن مسعود أن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال:","((آخر من يدخل الجنة رجل، فهو يمشي مرة ويكبو مرة، وتسفعه النار مرة، فإذا ما جاوزها التفت إليها، فقال: تبارك الذي نجاني منك، لقد أعطاني اللّٰه شيئًا ما أعطاه أحدًا من الأولين والآخرين. فترفع له شجرة، فيقول: أي رب، أدنني من هذه الشجرة فلأستظل بظلها، وأشرب من مائها. فيقول اللّٰه عز وجل: يا ابن آدم لعلي إن أعطيتكها سألتني غيرها؟ فيقول: لا يا رب. ويعاهده أن لا يسأله غيرها، وربه يعذره لأنه يرى ما لا صبر له عليه، فيدنيه منها فيستظل بظلها ويشرب من مائها، ثم ترفع له شجرة هي أحسن من الأولى، فيقول: أي رب، أدنني من هذه لأشرب من مائها وأستظل بظلها لا أسألك غيرها. فيقول: يا ابن آدم ألم تعاهدني أن لا تسألني غيرها؟ فيقول: لعلي إن أدنيتك منها تسألني غيرها؟ فيعاهده أن لا يسأله غيرها، وربه يعذره لأنه يرى ما لا صبر له عليه، فيدنيه منها، فيستظل بظلها، ويشرب من مائها، ثم ترفع له شجرة هي عند باب الجنة هي أحسن من الأوليين. فيقول: أي رب، أدنني من هذه لأستظل بظلها وأشرب من مائها، لا أسألك غيرها. فيقول: يا ابن آدم ألم تعاهدني أن لا تسألني غيرها؟ قال: بلى يا رب، هذه لا أسألك غيرها، وربه يعذره لأنه يرى ما لا صبر له عليه. فيدنيه منها، فإذا أدناه منها يسمع أصوات أهل الجنة، فيقول: أي رب، أدخلنيها. فيقول: يا ابن آدم ما يصريني منك؟ أيرضيك أن أعطيك الدنيا ومثلها معها؟ قال: يا رب، أتستهزئ مني وأنت رب العالمين؟)).","ضحك ابن مسعود، فقال: ألا تسألوني مم أضحك؟ فقالوا: مم تضحك؟ قال: هكذا ضحك رسول اللّٰه ﷺ، فقالوا: مم تضحك يا رسول الله؟ قال:","((من ضحك رب العالمين حين قال: أتستهزئ مني وأنت رب العالمين؟ فيقول: إني لا أستهزئ منك، ولكني على ما أشاء قدير، فيدخله الجنة))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (١٨٧).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أدنى أهل الجنة منزلة فيها","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (187).","chapter_en":"The Lowest-Ranking Person in Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":23,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn Masʿūd narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The last person to enter Paradise will be a man who walks at one time, stumbles at another, and at another time is scorched by the Fire. When he has finally passed beyond it, he will turn toward it and say: ‘Blessed is the One who saved me from you. Allah has given me something He has given to no one among the first or the last.’ Then a tree will be raised before him. He will say: ‘My Lord, bring me near this tree so that I may shelter in its shade and drink from its water.’","Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will say: ‘O son of Ādam, perhaps if I give you that, you will ask Me for something else.’ He will say: ‘No, my Lord,’ and he will promise Him that he will ask for nothing else. His Lord will excuse him because he sees something for which he has no patience. So He will bring him near it, and he will take shade beneath it and drink from its water. Then another tree, more beautiful than the first, will be raised before him. He will say: ‘My Lord, bring me near this one so that I may drink from its water and shelter in its shade. I will ask You for nothing else.’","He will say: ‘O son of Ādam, did you not promise Me that you would ask for nothing else? Perhaps if I bring you near it, you will ask Me for something more.’ Again he will promise not to ask for anything else, and his Lord will excuse him because he sees something for which he has no patience. So He will bring him near it, and he will shelter in its shade and drink from its water. Then another tree will be raised before him at the gate of Paradise, more beautiful than the first two.","He will say: ‘My Lord, bring me near this one so that I may shelter in its shade and drink from its water. I will ask You for nothing else.’ He will say: ‘O son of Ādam, did you not promise Me that you would ask for nothing else?’ He will say: ‘Yes, my Lord. This one, and I will ask You for nothing beyond it.’ His Lord will excuse him because he sees something for which he has no patience. So He will bring him near it. When he is brought near it, he will hear the voices of the people of Paradise and say: ‘My Lord, admit me into it.’","Allah will say: ‘O son of Ādam, what will finally bring your asking of Me to an end? Would it please you if I gave you the whole world and another like it with it?’ He will say: ‘My Lord, are You mocking me while You are the Lord of all the worlds?’” Ibn Masʿūd laughed and said: “Will you not ask me why I am laughing?” They asked: “Why are you laughing?” He replied: “This is how the Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed.” They asked: “Why are you laughing, O Messenger of Allah?”","He said: “Because of the laughter of the Lord of the worlds when the man says: ‘Are You mocking me while You are the Lord of all the worlds?’ Allah will say: ‘I am not mocking you, but I am capable of whatever I will.’ Then He will admit him into Paradise.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":187}]},{"num":16412,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي سعيد الخدري، أن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال:","((إن أدنى أهل الجنة منزلة رجل صرف اللّه وجهه عن النار قبل الجنة ومثل له شجرة ذات ظل، فقال: أي رب، قدمني إلى هذه الشجرة أكون في ظلها)).","وساق الحديث بنحو حديث ابن مسعود، ولم يذكر: فيقول: ((يا ابن آدم، ما يصريني منك؟)) إلى آخر الحديث، وزاد فيه:","((ويذكره الله، سل كذا وكذا، فإذا انقطعت به الأماني، قال الله: هو لك وعشرة أمثاله)).","قال:","((ثم يدخل بيته، فتدخل عليه زوجتاه من الحور العين، تقولان: الحمد لله الذي أحياك لنا، وأحيانا لك)).","قال:","((فيقول: ما أعطي أحد مثل ما أعطيت))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (١٨٨).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أدنى أهل الجنة منزلة فيها","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (188).","chapter_en":"The Lowest-Ranking Person in Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":23,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The lowest-ranking person in Paradise will be a man whose face Allah turns away from the Fire toward Paradise. A tree with shade will be made to appear before him, and he will say: ‘My Lord, bring me near this tree so that I may remain in its shade.’” He then related the hadith in a manner similar to the narration of Ibn Masʿūd, but without the wording: “O son of Ādam, what will finally bring your asking of Me to an end?”","up to the end of that narration. He added: “Allah will remind him: ‘Ask for such-and-such, and such-and-such.’ When all his wishes have been exhausted, Allah will say: ‘All of that is yours, and ten times as much.’” He said: “Then he will enter his house, and his two wives from the ḥūr al-ʿīn will enter upon him and say: ‘All praise is for Allah who brought you to life for us and brought us to life for you.’” He will say: “No one has been given anything like what I have been given.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":188}]},{"num":16413,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن المغيرة بن شعبة يرفعه إلى رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال:","((سأل موسى ربه: ما أدنى أهل الجنة منزلة؟ قال: هو رجل يجيء بعد ما أدخل أهل الجنة الجنة، فيقال له: ادخل الجنة، فيقول: أي رب، كيف وقد نزل الناس منازلهم، وأخذوا أخذاتهم؟ فيقال له: أترضى أن يكون لك مثل ملك ملك من ملوك الدنيا؟ فيقول: رضيت رب، فيقول: لك ذلك، ومثله ومثله ومثله ومثله، فقال في الخامسة: رضيت رب، فيقول: هذا لك وعشرة أمثاله، ولك ما اشتهت نفسك، ولذت عينك، فيقول: رضيت رب، قال: رب، فأعلاهم منزلة؟ قال: أولئك الذين أردت، غرست كرامتهم بيدي، وختمت عليها، فلم تر عين، ولم تسمع أذن، ولم يخطر على قلب بشر)).","قال: ومصداقه في كتاب اللّٰه عز وجل:","﴿فَلَا تَعْلَمُ نَفْسٌ مَا أُخْفِيَ لَهُمْ مِنْ قُرَّةِ أَعْيُنٍ﴾ [السجدة: ١٧]."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (١٨٩).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أدنى أهل الجنة منزلة فيها","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (189).","chapter_en":"The Lowest-Ranking Person in Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":23,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah narrated, attributing it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “Mūsā asked his Lord: ‘What is the lowest rank among the people of Paradise?’ He said: ʿIt is a man who will come after the people of Paradise have already entered Paradise. It will be said to him: “Enter Paradise.” He will say: “My Lord, how can I, when the people have already settled in their dwellings and received what was allotted to them?” It will be said to him: “Would you be pleased to have the equivalent of the kingdom of one of the kings of this world?”","He will say: “I am pleased, my Lord.” He will say: “You will have that, and another like it, and another like it, and another like it, and another like it.” At the fifth, he will say: “I am pleased, my Lord.” He will say: “All of that is yours, and ten times as much, and you will have whatever your soul desires and whatever delights your eyes.” He will say: “I am pleased, my Lord.” Mūsā asked: “My Lord, what about those of the highest rank?” He said: “Those are the ones whom I chose. I planted their honor with My Hand and sealed it. No eye has seen it, no ear has heard it, and it has never occurred to a human heart.””","He said: Its confirmation is in the Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: “No soul knows what comfort of the eyes has been hidden for them.” [al-Sajdah 32:17]"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["قوله: ((أردت)) معناه اخترت واصطفيت.","وقوله: ((غرست كرامتهم)) معناه اصطفيتهم وتوليتهم، فلا يتطرق إلى كرامتهم تغيير."],"en":["Regarding the phrase “whom I chose,” the author explains that it means: whom I selected and specially chose.","Regarding the phrase “I planted their honor,” the author explains that it means: I specially selected them and took charge of them, so no alteration can reach the honor prepared for them."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":189}]},{"num":16414,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي ذر قال: قال رسول الله ﷺ:","((إني لأعلم آخر أهل الجنة دخولًا الجنة، وآخر أهل النار خروجًا منها، رجل يؤتى به يوم القيامة، فيقال: اعرضوا عليه صغار ذنوبه، وارفعوا عنه كبارها، فتعرض عليه صغار ذنوبه، فيقال: عملت يوم كذا وكذا كذا وكذا، وعملت يوم كذا وكذا كذا وكذا، فيقول: نعم، لا يستطيع أن ينكر، وهو مشفق من كبار ذنوبه أن تعرض عليه، فيقال له: فإن لك مكان كل سيئة حسنة، فيقول: رب، قد عملت أشياء لا أراها ها هنا)).","فلقد رأيت رسول اللّٰه ﷺ ضحك حتى بدت نواجذه."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (١٩٠).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أدنى أهل الجنة منزلة فيها","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (190).","chapter_en":"The Lowest-Ranking Person in Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":23,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Dharr narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I certainly know the last person to enter Paradise and the last person to come out of the Fire. A man will be brought on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be said: ‘Present his minor sins to him, but withhold his major sins from him.’ His minor sins will be presented to him, and it will be said: ‘On such-and-such a day you did this and this, and on such-and-such a day you did this and this.’","He will say: ‘Yes,’ unable to deny them, while fearing that his major sins will also be shown to him. Then it will be said to him: ‘For every evil deed, you will have a good deed in its place.’ He will say: ‘My Lord, I committed other things that I do not see here!’” Abū Dharr said: “I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ laugh until his molar teeth became visible.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":190}]},{"num":16415,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبد اللّٰه بن مسعود قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((إني لأعلم آخر أهل النار خروجًا منها، وآخر أهل الجنة دخولًا، رجل يخرج من النار كبوًا، فيقول الله: اذهب فادخل الجنة، فيأتيها، فيخيل إليه أنها ملأى، فيرجع فيقول: يا رب، وجدتها ملأى، فيقول: اذهب فادخل الجنة، فيأتيها فيخيل إليه أنها ملأى، فيرجع فيقول: يا رب وجدتها ملأى، فيقول: اذهب فادخل الجنة، فإن لك مثل الدنيا وعشرة أمثالها - أو: إن لك مثل عشرة أمثال الدنيا - فيقول: تسخر مني - أو: تضحك مني - وأنت الملك)).","فلقد رأيت رسول اللّٰه ﷺ ضحك حتى بدت نواجذه، وكان يقول:","((ذاك أدنى أهل الجنة منزلة))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٦٥٧١)، ومسلم (٣٠٨ :١٨٦).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب أدنى أهل الجنة منزلة فيها","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6571) and Muslim (308 :186).","chapter_en":"The Lowest-Ranking Person in Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":23,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I certainly know the last person to come out of the Fire and the last person to enter Paradise. A man will emerge from the Fire crawling. Allah will say to him: ‘Go and enter Paradise.’ He will go to it, but it will appear to him to be full. So he will return and say: ‘My Lord, I found it full.’ Allah will say: ‘Go and enter Paradise.’ He will go to it, but again it will appear to him to be full. So he will return and say: ‘My Lord, I found it full.’","Allah will say: ‘Go and enter Paradise, for you shall have the equivalent of the world and ten times as much’—or: ‘You shall have the equivalent of ten worlds.’ He will say: ‘Are You mocking me—or laughing at me—while You are the King?’” Ibn Masʿūd said: “I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ laugh until his molar teeth became visible.” And he used to say: “That is the lowest-ranking person in Paradise.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6571},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":308}]},{"num":16416,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((إن أدنى مقعد أحدكم من الجنة أن يقول له: تمن، فيتمنى ويتمنى، فيقول له: هل تمنيت؟ فيقول: نعم، فيقول له: فإن لك ما تمنيت ومثله معه))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٣٠١ :١٨٢).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أدنى أهل الجنة منزلة فيها","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (301 :182).","chapter_en":"The Lowest-Ranking Person in Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":23,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The lowest dwelling of one of you in Paradise will be that it is said to him: ‘Wish.’ So he will wish and continue wishing. Then it will be said to him: ‘Have you finished wishing?’ He will say: ‘Yes.’ Then it will be said to him: ‘You shall have everything you wished for, and another like it with it.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":301}]},{"num":16417,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة، أن ناسًا قالوا لرسول اللّٰه ﷺ: يا رسول الله، هل نرى ربنا يوم القيامة؟ فقال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ… فذكر حديثًا طويلًا، وفيه:","((ثم يفرغ الله تعالى من القضاء بين العباد، ويبقى رجل مقبل بوجهه على النار - وهو آخر أهل الجنة دخولًا الجنة - فيقول: أي رب، اصرف وجهي عن النار، فإنه قد قشبني ريحها وأحرقني ذكاؤها. فيدعو الله ما شاء الله أن يدعوه، ثم يقول اللّٰه تبارك وتعالى: هل عسيت إن فعلت ذلك بك أن تسأل غيره؟ فيقول: لا أسألك غيره، ويعطي ربه من عهود ومواثيق ما شاء الله، فيصرف الله وجهه عن النار، فإذا أقبل على الجنة ورآها سكت ما شاء الله أن يسكت. ثم يقول: أي رب، قدمني إلى باب الجنة. فيقول اللّٰه له: أليس قد أعطيت عهودك ومواثيقك لا تسألني غير الذي أعطيتك، ويلك يا ابن آدم ما أغدرك! فيقول: أي رب، ويدعو الله حتى يقول له: فهل عسيت إن أعطيتك ذلك أن تسأل غيره؟ فيقول: لا وعزتك، فيعطي ربه ما شاء الله من عهود ومواثيق، فيقدمه إلى باب الجنة، فإذا قام على باب الجنة انفهقت له الجنة، فرأى ما فيها من الخير والسرور. فيسكت ما شاء الله أن يسكت، ثم يقول: أي رب، أدخلني الجنة. فيقول اللّٰه تبارك وتعالى له: أليس قد أعطيت عهودك ومواثيقك أن لا تسأل غير ما أعطيت؟! ويلك يا ابن آدم ما أغدرك! فيقول: أي رب، لا أكون أشقى خلقك، فلا يزال يدعو اللّٰه حتى يضحك الله تبارك وتعالى منه، فإذا ضحك اللّٰه منه قال: ادخل الجنة، فإذا دخلها قال اللّٰه له: تمن، فيسأل ربه ويتمنى، حتى إن الله ليذكره من كذا وكذا، حتى إذا انقطعت به الأماني. قال اللّٰه تعالى: ذلك لك ومثله معه))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٧٤٣٧)، ومسلم (١٨٢).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب أدنى أهل الجنة منزلة فيها","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (7437) and Muslim (182).","chapter_en":"The Lowest-Ranking Person in Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":23,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that some people asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “O Messenger of Allah, will we see our Lord on the Day of Resurrection?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then mentioned a lengthy hadith, in which he said: “Then Allah, the Exalted, will finish judging between the servants, and one man will remain facing the Fire. He will be the last person from the people of Paradise to enter Paradise. He will say: ‘My Lord, turn my face away from the Fire, for its wind has poisoned me and its flame has burned me.’","He will supplicate to Allah for as long as Allah wills that he supplicate. Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will say: ‘If I do that for you, perhaps you will ask for something else.’ He will say: ‘I will ask You for nothing else,’ and he will give his Lord whatever covenants and pledges Allah wills. So Allah will turn his face away from the Fire. When he faces Paradise and sees it, he will remain silent for as long as Allah wills. Then he will say: ‘My Lord, bring me to the gate of Paradise.’","Allah will say to him: ‘Did you not give your covenants and pledges that you would ask Me for nothing beyond what I had already given you? Woe to you, O son of Ādam! How treacherous you are!’ He will say: ‘My Lord…’ and continue supplicating to Allah until He says to him: ‘If I give you that, perhaps you will ask for something else.’ He will say: ‘No, by Your Might,’ and he will give his Lord whatever covenants and pledges Allah wills. So He will bring him to the gate of Paradise.","When he stands at the gate of Paradise, Paradise will open wide before him, and he will see all the goodness and joy within it. He will remain silent for as long as Allah wills, then say: ‘My Lord, admit me into Paradise.’ Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will say to him: ‘Did you not give your covenants and pledges that you would ask for nothing beyond what I had given you? Woe to you, O son of Ādam! How treacherous you are!’ He will say: ‘My Lord, do not make me the most wretched of Your creation.’","He will continue supplicating to Allah until Allah, Blessed and Exalted, laughs at him. When Allah laughs at him, He will say: ‘Enter Paradise.’ When he enters it, Allah will say to him: ‘Wish.’ So he will ask his Lord and make wishes, until Allah Himself reminds him of such-and-such things. When all his wishes are exhausted, Allah, the Exalted, will say: ‘All of that is yours, and another like it with it.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":7437},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":182}]},{"num":16418,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن سهل بن سعد قال: قال رسول اللّه ﷺ:","((إن أدنى أهل الجنة منزلة - وليس فيها دني - الذي يتمنى، فيقول بلسان طلق ذلق، وعقل مجتمع: أعطني أعطني كذا، حتى إذا لم يجد شيئًا لقن، فقيل له: قل كذا، قل كذا، فيقال له: هو لك ومثله معه))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الطبراني في الكبير (٢٠٨/٦)، وأبو نعيم في صفة الجنة (٤٤٥).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أدنى أهل الجنة منزلة فيها","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Kabīr (6/208) and Abū Nuʿaym in Ṣifat al-Jannah (445).","chapter_en":"The Lowest-Ranking Person in Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":23,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Sahl ibn Saʿd narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The lowest-ranking person in Paradise—and there is nothing lowly in Paradise—is the one who will make wishes. With a fluent tongue and a fully composed mind he will say: ‘Give me this, give me that,’ until he can think of nothing more. Then he will be prompted and it will be said to him: ‘Ask for such-and-such, ask for such-and-such.’ Then it will be said to him: ‘It is yours, and another like it with it.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"الطبرانی/الکبیر","label":"الطبراني في الكبير","number":208},{"key":"ابو_نعیم/صفہ_الجنہ","label":"أبو نعيم في صفة الجنة","number":445}]},{"num":16419,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((بينا هو، يعني آخر من يدخل الجنة، يمضي فيها، إذ رأى ضوءًا، فيخر ساجدًا، فيقال له: ما لك؟ فيقول: أليس هذا ربي تجلى لي؟ فإذا هو برجل قائم، فيقول: لا، هذا منزل من منازلك، وأنا قهرمان من قهارمتك، ولك مثلي ألف قهرمان، ثم يمشي أمامه، فيدخل أدنى قصوره، لا يشرف على شيء منها إلا أنفذ بصره أقصى مملكته مسيرة مائة سنة))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو نعيم (٤٤١).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في قهرمان أهل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abū Nuʿaym (441).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Stewards of the People of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":24,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “While he—that is, the last person to enter Paradise—is walking through it, he will see a light and fall down in prostration. It will be asked: ‘What is the matter with you?’ He will say: ‘Is this not my Lord manifesting Himself to me?’ But it will only be a man standing there, who will say: ‘No. This is merely one of your dwellings, and I am one steward among your stewards. You have one thousand stewards like me.’","Then he will walk ahead of him until he enters the lowest of his palaces. Whenever he looks out from any part of it, his sight will reach the farthest limit of his kingdom—a journey of one hundred years.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ابو_نعیم","label":"أبو نعيم","number":441}]},{"num":16420,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة قال: قال رسول الله ﷺ:","((خلق اللّه عز وجل آدم على صورته، طوله ستون ذراعًا، فلما خلقه قال: اذهب فسلم على أولئك النفر، وهم نفر من الملائكة جلوس، فاستمع ما يحيونك، فإنها تحيتك وتحية ذريتك، قال: فذهب فقال: السلام عليكم، فقالوا: السلام عليك ورحمة الله، قال فزادوه: ورحمة اللّه، قال: فكل من يدخل الجنة على صورة آدم وطوله ستون ذراعًا، فلم يزل الخلق ينقص بعده حتى الآن))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٣٣٢٦)، ومسلم (٢٨٤١).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب دخول أهل الجنة الجنة على صورة آدم عليه السلام، وطوله ستون ذراعًا","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3326) and Muslim (2841).","chapter_en":"The People of Paradise Will Enter Paradise in the Form of Ādam عليه السلام, Whose Height Was Sixty Cubits","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":25,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah, Mighty and Majestic, created Ādam upon his form, his height being sixty cubits. When He created him, He said: ‘Go and greet that group,’ and they were a group of angels sitting together, ‘and listen to how they greet you, for that will be your greeting and the greeting of your descendants.’ So he went and said: ‘Peace be upon you.’ They replied: ‘Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah,’ adding: ‘and the mercy of Allah.’","Everyone who enters Paradise will enter upon the form of Ādam and at a height of sixty cubits. Creation has continued to decrease in stature after him until now.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":3326},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2841}]},{"num":16421,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة، أن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال:","((إن أهل الجنة يدخلون الجنة على قدر آدم ستون ذراعًا، وعلى ذلك قطعت سررهم))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الطبراني في مسند الشاميين (٢٠٧٤)، وأبو نعيم في صفة الجنة (٢٤٨).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب دخول أهل الجنة الجنة على صورة آدم عليه السلام، وطوله ستون ذراعًا","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in Musnad al-Shāmiyyīn (2074) and Abū Nuʿaym in Ṣifat al-Jannah (248).","chapter_en":"The People of Paradise Will Enter Paradise in the Form of Ādam عليه السلام, Whose Height Was Sixty Cubits","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":25,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The people of Paradise will enter Paradise at the stature of Ādam—sixty cubits—and their couches have been made according to that measure.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"الطبرانی/مسند_الشامیین","label":"الطبراني في مسند الشاميين","number":2074},{"key":"ابو_نعیم/صفہ_الجنہ","label":"أبو نعيم في صفة الجنة","number":248},{"key":"sh13162","label":"مسند الشاميين للطبراني","number":2075,"n":2068}]},{"num":16422,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((أهل الجنة جرد مرد كحل، لا يفنى شبابهم، ولا تبلى ثيابهم))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (٢٥٣٩)، والدارمي (٢٨٦٨)، وأبو نعيم في صفة الجنة (٢٥٦).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب أن أهل الجنة جرد مرد كحل","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (2539), al-Dārimī (2868), and Abū Nuʿaym in Ṣifat al-Jannah (256).","chapter_en":"The People of Paradise Will Be Hairless, Beardless, and Kohl-Eyed","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":26,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The people of Paradise will be hairless, beardless, and kohl-eyed. Their youth will never fade, and their clothes will never wear out.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"tirmidhi","label":"الترمذي","number":2539},{"key":"darimi","label":"الدارمي","number":2868},{"key":"ابو_نعیم/صفہ_الجنہ","label":"أبو نعيم في صفة الجنة","number":256}]},{"num":16423,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن المقدام بن معدي كرب حدثهم أن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال:","((ما من أحد يموت سقطًا ولا هرمًا، وإنما الناس فيما بين ذلك، إلا بعث ابن ثلاثين سنة، فمن كان من أهل الجنة كان على مسحة آدم، وصورة يوسف، وقلب أيوب، ومن كان من أهل النار عظموا وفخموا كالجبال))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الطبراني في الكبير (٢٨٠/٢٠) من طريقين أحدهما حسن.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب أطفال المؤمنين يكمل خلقهم عند دخولهم الجنة أبناء ثلاث وثلاثين سنة على خلق آدم ستون ذراعًا","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Kabīr (20/280) through two routes, one of which is good.","chapter_en":"The Children of the Believers Will Have Their Creation Completed upon Entering Paradise at the Age of Thirty-Three, upon the Form of Ādam, Sixty Cubits Tall","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":27,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Miqdām ibn Maʿdī Karib narrated to them that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No one dies as a miscarried child or in extreme old age—and people die at all ages between those two—except that he will be resurrected at the age of thirty. Whoever is among the people of Paradise will be upon the appearance of Ādam, the beauty of Yūsuf, and the heart of Ayyūb. As for those who are among the people of the Fire, they will be enlarged and made huge like mountains.”"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["وقد سئل شيخ الإسلام ابن تيمية عن أطفال المؤمنين هل يدومون على حالتهم التي ماتوا عليها، أم يكبرون ويتزوجون؟ وكذلك البنات هل يتزوجن.","فأجاب: “الحمد لله، إذا دخلوا الجنة دخلوها كما يدخلها الكبار على صورة أبيهم آدم طوله ستون ذراعًا في عرض سبعة أذرع، ويتزوجون كما يتزوج الكبار، ومن مات من النساء ولم يتزوجن فإنها تزوج في الآخرة، وكذلك من مات من الرجال فإنه يتزوج في الآخرة. والله تعالى أعلم”. مجموع الفتاوى (٣١٠/٤).","وأما قوله تعالى:","﴿يَطُوفُ عَلَيْهِمْ وِلْدَانٌ مُخَلَّدُونَ﴾ [الواقعة: ١٧].","وقوله تعالى:","﴿وَيَطُوفُ عَلَيْهِمْ وِلْدَانٌ مُخَلَّدُونَ إِذَا رَأَيْتَهُمْ حَسِبْتَهُمْ لُؤْلُؤًا مَنْثُورًا﴾ [سورة الإنسان: ١٩].","فهم من خلق اللّٰه تعالى في الجنة لخدمة أهل الجنة، وقضاء حوائجهم، صغار الأسنان في غاية الحسن والبهاء، وهم ليسوا من أطفال المؤمنين كما هو شائع بين الناس، لأن أطفال المؤمنين يكونون مع آبائهم وأمهاتهم كما قال تعالى:","﴿وَالَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَاتَّبَعَتْهُمْ ذُرِّيَّتُهُمْ بِإِيمَانٍ أَلْحَقْنَا بِهِمْ ذُرِّيَّتَهُمْ﴾ [الطور: ٢١].","بالوصف الذي جاء ذكره في حديث معدي كرب، أي: أبناء ثلاثين سنة."],"en":["Shaykh al-Islām Ibn Taymiyyah was asked whether the children of the believers will remain in the same state in which they died, or whether they will grow up and marry, and likewise whether girls will marry.","He replied:","“Praise be to Allah. When they enter Paradise, they will enter it just as adults enter it, upon the form of their father Ādam, whose height was sixty cubits and whose width was seven cubits. They will marry just as adults marry. A woman who died without having married will be married in the Hereafter, and likewise a man who died will marry in the Hereafter. And Allah, the Exalted, knows best.”","Majmūʿ al-Fatāwā (4/310).","As for the statement of Allah, the Exalted:","“Immortal youths will circulate among them.”","[al-Wāqiʿah 56:17]","And His statement:","“Immortal youths will circulate among them; when you see them, you would think them scattered pearls.”","[al-Insān 76:19]","the author explains that these are beings created by Allah, the Exalted, in Paradise to serve the people of Paradise and attend to their needs. They will be young in age and at the utmost degree of beauty and splendor.","They are not the children of the believers, as is commonly assumed among people, because the children of the believers will be with their fathers and mothers, as Allah, the Exalted, says:","“Those who believed and whose descendants followed them in faith—We will join their descendants with them.”","[al-Ṭūr 52:21]","They will be in the condition mentioned in the hadith of Maʿdī Karib, namely, at the age of thirty."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"الطبرانی/الکبیر","label":"الطبراني في الكبير","number":280}]},{"num":16424,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة، عن النبي ﷺ، قال:","((من يدخل الجنة ينعم لا يبأس، لا تبلى ثيابه، ولا يفنى شبابه))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٢٨٣٦).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أهل الجنة لا يمرضون ولا يهرمون ولا يموتون","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2836).","chapter_en":"The People of Paradise Will Not Become Ill, Grow Old, or Die","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":28,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever enters Paradise will live in bliss and never suffer misery. His clothes will never wear out, and his youth will never fade.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2836}]},{"num":16425,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي سعيد الخدري، وأبي هريرة، عن النبي ﷺ قال:","((ينادي مناد: إن لكم أن تصحوا فلا تسقموا أبدًا، وإن لكم أن تحيوا فلا تموتوا أبدًا، وإن لكم أن تشبوا فلا تهرموا أبدًا، وإن لكم أن تنعموا فلا تبأسوا أبدًا)).","فذلك قوله عز وجل:","﴿وَنُودُوا أَنْ تِلْكُمُ الْجَنَّةُ أُورِثْتُمُوهَا بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُونَ﴾ [الأعراف: ٤٣]."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٢٨٣٧).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أهل الجنة لا يمرضون ولا يهرمون ولا يموتون","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2837).","chapter_en":"The People of Paradise Will Not Become Ill, Grow Old, or Die","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":28,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī and Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “A caller will proclaim: ‘You shall remain healthy and never become ill. You shall live and never die. You shall remain young and never grow old. And you shall live in bliss and never suffer misery.’” That is the meaning of the statement of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: “They will be called: ‘This is the Paradise which you have inherited for what you used to do.’” [al-Aʿrāf 7:43]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2837}]},{"num":16426,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة قال: قلنا: يا رسول الله، حدثنا عن الجنة، ما بناؤها؟ قال:","((لبنة ذهب ولبنة فضة، وملاطها المسك الأذفر، وحصباؤها اللؤلؤ والياقوت، وترابها الزعفران، من يدخلها ينعم ولا يبأس، ويخلد ولا يموت، لا تبلى ثيابه، ولا يفنى شبابه))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (٨٠٤٣)، وعبد بن حميد (١٤٢٠)، وصححه ابن حبان (٧٣٨٧).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب أهل الجنة لا يمرضون ولا يهرمون ولا يموتون","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (8043), ʿAbd ibn Ḥumayd (1420), and authenticated by Ibn Ḥibbān (7387).","chapter_en":"The People of Paradise Will Not Become Ill, Grow Old, or Die","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":28,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated: We said: “O Messenger of Allah, tell us about Paradise. What is its construction?” He replied: “A brick of gold and a brick of silver. Its mortar is fragrant musk, its pebbles are pearls and rubies, and its soil is saffron. Whoever enters it will live in bliss and never suffer misery, will remain forever and never die, his clothes will never wear out, and his youth will never fade.”"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["وقوله: ((ملاطها)) بكسر الميم، هو الطين الذي يجعله البناء بين كل طبقتين من لبنات الحائط."],"en":["Regarding the word “mulāṭuhā,” with a kasrah on the letter mīm, it means the mortar that a builder places between each layer of bricks in a wall."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"عبد_بن_حمید","label":"عبد بن حميد","number":1420},{"key":"صححہ_ابن_حبان","label":"صححه ابن حبان","number":7387},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":8043,"n":8043},{"key":"ibnhibban","label":"صحيح ابن حبان (التقاسيم والأنواع)","number":5179,"n":5175}]},{"num":16427,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((إن أول زمرة يدخلون الجنة على صورة القمر ليلة البدر، ثم الذين يلونهم على أشد كوكب دري في السماء إضاءة، لا يبولون ولا يتغوطون، ولا يتفلون ولا يمتخطون، أمشاطهم الذهب، ورشحهم المسك، ومجامرهم الألوة، وأزواجهم الحور العين، على خلق رجل واحد، على صورة أبيهم آدم، ستون ذراعًا في السماء))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٣٣٢٧)، ومسلم (١٥ :٢٨٣٤).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب أهل الجنة يأكلون ويشربون، ولكن لا يبولون ولا يتغوطون","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3327) and Muslim (15 :2834).","chapter_en":"The People of Paradise Will Eat and Drink, but They Will Neither Urinate nor Defecate","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":29,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The first group to enter Paradise will have the appearance of the full moon. Those who follow them will be like the brightest shining star in the sky. They will neither urinate nor defecate, spit nor blow their noses. Their combs will be of gold, their perspiration will be musk, and their incense burners will contain aloeswood. Their spouses will be the ḥūr al-ʿīn. They will all be of one physical form, upon the form of their father Ādam, sixty cubits tall.”"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["قوله: ((الألوة)) هي العود الذي يتبخر به، وهو العود الهندي.","وقوله: ((أخلاقهم على خلق رجل واحد)). قال النووي: “قد ذكر مسلم في الكتاب اختلاف ابن أبي شيبة وأبي كريب في ضبطه، فابن أبي شيبة يرويه بضم الخاء واللام، وأبو كريب بفتح الخاء وإسكان اللام، وكلاهما صحيح، وقد اختلف فيه رواة صحيح البخاري أيضًا. ويرجح الضم بقوله في الحديث الآخر: ((لا اختلاف بينهم ولا تباغض، قلوبهم قلب واحد)) وقد يرجح الفتح بقوله ﷺ في تمام الحديث: ((على صورة أبيهم آدم)) أو ((على طوله))”."],"en":["The word “al-alūwah” refers to the wood burned as incense, namely Indian aloeswood.","Regarding the phrase “akhlaqahum ʿalā khalqi rajulin wāḥid,” al-Nawawī said:","“Muslim mentioned in his book the difference between Ibn Abī Shaybah and Abū Kurayb in how this word is vocalized. Ibn Abī Shaybah narrated it with a ḍammah on the khāʾ and lām, while Abū Kurayb narrated it with a fatḥah on the khāʾ and a sukūn on the lām. Both readings are correct. The narrators of Ṣaḥīḥ al-Bukhārī also differed concerning it.","The reading with the ḍammah may be supported by the other hadith: ‘There will be no disagreement or hatred among them; their hearts will be one heart.’","The reading with the fatḥah may be supported by the end of the hadith: ‘upon the form of their father Ādam,’ or ‘upon his height.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":3327},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":15}]},{"num":16428,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة قال: قال رسول الله ﷺ:","((أول زمرة تلج الجنة صورتهم على صورة القمر ليلة البدر، لا يبصقون فيها، ولا يمتخطون، ولا يتغوطون، آنيتهم فيها الذهب، أمشاطهم من الذهب والفضة، ومجامرهم الألوة، ورشحهم المسك، ولكل واحد منهم زوجتان، يرى مخ سوقهما من وراء اللحم من الحسن، لا اختلاف بينهم ولا تباغض، قلوبهم قلب واحد، يسبحون اللّٰه بكرة وعشيًا))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٣٢٤٥)، ومسلم (١٧:٢٨٣٤).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب أهل الجنة يأكلون ويشربون، ولكن لا يبولون ولا يتغوطون","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3245) and Muslim (17:2834).","chapter_en":"The People of Paradise Will Eat and Drink, but They Will Neither Urinate nor Defecate","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":29,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The first group to enter Paradise will have the appearance of the full moon. They will neither spit, blow their noses, nor defecate therein. Their vessels will be of gold, their combs of gold and silver, their incense burners will contain aloeswood, and their perspiration will be musk. Each one of them will have two wives, and because of their beauty the marrow of their shins will be visible through the flesh.","There will be no disagreement or hatred among them. Their hearts will be as one heart, glorifying Allah morning and evening.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":3245},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":17}]},{"num":16429,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر بن عبد اللّٰه قال: سمعت النبي ﷺ يقول:","((إن أهل الجنة يأكلون فيها ويشربون، ولا يتفلون ولا يبولون ولا يتغوطون ولا يمتخطون)).","قالوا: فما بال الطعام؟ قال:","((جشاء ورشح كرشح المسك، يلهمون التسبيح والتحميد، كما تلهمون النفس))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٢٨٣٥).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أهل الجنة يأكلون ويشربون، ولكن لا يبولون ولا يتغوطون","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2835).","chapter_en":"The People of Paradise Will Eat and Drink, but They Will Neither Urinate nor Defecate","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":29,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “The people of Paradise will eat and drink therein, but they will neither spit, urinate, defecate, nor blow their noses.” They asked: “Then what becomes of the food?” He replied: “It will be discharged as belching and perspiration like the fragrance of musk. They will be inspired to glorify and praise Allah just as you are inspired to breathe.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2835}]},{"num":16430,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة، أن يهوديًا سأل رسول الله ﷺ، فقال: إلام يصير طعام أهل الجنة؟ قال:","((يصير رشحًا مثل حباب المسك))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه البزار (٧٦٧٥)، والطبراني في مسند الشاميين (١٧١٤).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب أهل الجنة يأكلون ويشربون، ولكن لا يبولون ولا يتغوطون","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Bazzār (7675) and al-Ṭabarānī in Musnad al-Shāmiyyīn (1714).","chapter_en":"The People of Paradise Will Eat and Drink, but They Will Neither Urinate nor Defecate","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":29,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that a Jewish man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “What does the food of the people of Paradise become?” He replied: “It becomes perspiration like droplets of musk.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"البزار","label":"البزار","number":7675},{"key":"الطبرانی/مسند_الشامیین","label":"الطبراني في مسند الشاميين","number":1714},{"key":"sh13162","label":"مسند الشاميين للطبراني","number":1714,"n":1714}]},{"num":16431,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر بن عبد اللّٰه قال: قيل: يا رسول الله، هل ينام أهل الجنة؟ قال:","((لا، النوم أخو الموت))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه البزار - كشف الأستار - (٣٥١٧).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب أهل الجنة لا ينامون","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Bazzār in Kashf al-Astār (3517).","chapter_en":"The People of Paradise Will Not Sleep","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":30,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: It was asked: “O Messenger of Allah, will the people of Paradise sleep?” He replied: “No. Sleep is the brother of death.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"البزار_کشف_الاستار","label":"البزار - كشف الأستار -","number":3517}]},{"num":16432,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن محمد بن سيرين قال: إما تفاخروا وإما تذاكروا: الرجال في الجنة أكثر أم النساء؟ فقال أبو هريرة: أو لم يقل أبو القاسم ﷺ:","((إن أول زمرة تدخل الجنة على صورة القمر ليلة البدر، والتي تليها على أضوأ كوكب دري في السماء، لكل امرئ منهم زوجتان اثنتان، يرى مخ سوقهما من وراء اللحم، وما في الجنة أعزب))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٢٨٣٤).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في صفة نساء أهل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2834).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Women of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":31,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn narrated: The people were either boasting or discussing whether men or women would be more numerous in Paradise. Abū Hurayrah said: “Did Abū al-Qāsim ﷺ not say: ‘The first group to enter Paradise will have the appearance of the full moon, and the group after them will be like the brightest shining star in the sky. Every man among them will have two wives, and the marrow of their shins will be visible through the flesh. There will be no unmarried person in Paradise.’”"]},"intro":{"ar":["قال اللّٰه تعالى:","﴿وَحُورٌ عِينٌ ۝ كَأَمْثَالِ اللُّؤْلُؤِ الْمَكْنُونِ﴾ [سورة الواقعة: ٢٢-٢٣].","وقال تعالى:","﴿وَعِنْدَهُمْ قَاصِرَاتُ الطَّرْفِ أَتْرَابٌ﴾ [سورة ص: ٥٢].","وقال تعالى:","﴿فِيهِنَّ خَيْرَاتٌ حِسَانٌ ۝ فَبِأَيِّ آلَاءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبَانِ ۝ حُورٌ مَقْصُورَاتٌ فِي الْخِيَامِ ۝ فَبِأَيِّ آلَاءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبَانِ ۝ لَمْ يَطْمِثْهُنَّ إِنْسٌ قَبْلَهُمْ وَلَا جَانٌّ﴾ [سورة الرحمن: ٧٠-٧٤].","وقال تعالى:","﴿وَالَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَعَمِلُوا الصَّالِحَاتِ سَنُدْخِلُهُمْ جَنَّاتٍ تَجْرِي مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْأَنْهَارُ خَالِدِينَ فِيهَا أَبَدًا لَهُمْ فِيهَا أَزْوَاجٌ مُطَهَّرَةٌ وَنُدْخِلُهُمْ ظِلًّا ظَلِيلًا﴾ [سورة النساء: ٥٧]."],"en":["Allah, the Exalted, says:","“And fair women with wide, beautiful eyes, like well-protected pearls.”","[al-Wāqiʿah 56:22-23]","And He, the Exalted, says:","“And with them will be women who restrain their glances, equal in age.”","[Ṣād 38:52]","And He, the Exalted, says:","“In them are good and beautiful women. So which of the favors of your Lord will you both deny? Fair women secluded in pavilions. So which of the favors of your Lord will you both deny? No human or jinn has touched them before.”","[al-Raḥmān 55:70-74]","And He, the Exalted, says:","“Those who believe and perform righteous deeds, We will admit them into Gardens beneath which rivers flow, remaining therein forever. They will have purified spouses therein, and We will admit them into deep shade.”","[al-Nisāʾ 4:57]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2834}]},{"num":16433,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة، عن النبي ﷺ قال:","((للرجل من أهل الجنة زوجتان من حور العين، على كل واحدة سبعون حلة، يرى مخ ساقها من وراء الثياب))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (٨٥٤٢).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في صفة نساء أهل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (8542).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Women of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":31,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “A man from the people of Paradise will have two wives from the ḥūr al-ʿīn. Each one will wear seventy garments, yet the marrow of her shin will be visible through the garments.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":8542,"n":8542}]},{"num":16434,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أنس قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((غدوة في سبيل اللّه أو روحة خير من الدنيا وما فيها، ولقاب قوس أحدكم أو موضع قدم من الجنة خير من الدنيا وما فيها، ولو أن امرأة من نساء أهل الجنة اطلعت إلى الأرض لأضاءت ما بينهما، ولملأت ما بينهما ريحًا، ولنصيفها - يعني الخمار - خير من الدنيا وما فيها))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (٦٥٦٨).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في صفة نساء أهل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6568).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Women of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":31,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A morning journey in the path of Allah or an evening journey is better than the world and everything in it. The space occupied by the bow of one of you, or a single footstep in Paradise, is better than the world and everything in it. And if a woman from among the women of Paradise were to look toward the earth, she would illuminate everything between them and fill everything between them with fragrance. Even her head-covering is better than the world and everything in it.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6568}]},{"num":16435,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبد اللّٰه بن مسعود، عن النبي ﷺ قال:","((أول زمرة يدخل الجنة من أمتي وجوههم كالقمر ليلة البدر، والزمرة الثانية كأحسن كوكب دري في السماء، لكل امرئ منهم زوجتان، على كل زوجة سبعون حلة، يرى مخ سوقهن من وراء الحلل، كما ترى الشراب الأحمر في الزجاجة البيضاء))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه البزار (١٨٥٥)، والطبراني في الكبير (١٩٩-١٩٨/١٠)، وأبو نعيم في صفة الجنة (٢٥٤).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في صفة نساء أهل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Bazzār (1855), al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Kabīr (10/198-199), and Abū Nuʿaym in Ṣifat al-Jannah (254).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Women of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":31,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The first group from my Ummah to enter Paradise will have faces like the full moon, and the second group will be like the most beautiful shining star in the sky. Each man among them will have two wives. Each wife will wear seventy garments, yet the marrow of their shins will be visible through those garments, just as red drink can be seen through a clear white glass vessel.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"البزار","label":"البزار","number":1855},{"key":"الطبرانی/الکبیر","label":"الطبراني في الكبير","number":199},{"key":"ابو_نعیم/صفہ_الجنہ","label":"أبو نعيم في صفة الجنة","number":254},{"key":"sh12862","label":"كشف الأستار عن زوائد البزار","number":3536,"n":3537}]},{"num":16436,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن سعيد بن عامر بن حذيم قال: بلغ عمر أنه لا يدخر في بيته من الحاجة، فبعث إليه بعشرة آلاف، فأخذها، فجعل يفرقها صررًا، فقالت له امرأته: أين تذهب بهذه؟ قال: أذهب بها إلى من يرجح لنا فيها، فما أبقى منها إلا شيئًا يسيرًا، فلما نفد الذي كان عندهم قالت له امرأته: اذهب إلى بعض أصحابك الذين أعطيتهم يرجحون لك، فخذ من أرباحهم، وجعل يدافعها ويماطلها حتى طال ذلك، فقال: سمعت رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((لو أن حوراء أطلعت إصبعًا من أصابعها لوجد ريحها كل ذي روح)).","فأنا أدعهن، لكن والله لأنتن أحق أن أدعكن لهن منهن لكن."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو يعلى كما في المطالب العالية (٤٦٠٨)، والطبراني في الكبير (٧٢-٧١/٦) - واللفظ له -، وأبو نعيم في الحلية (٢٤٧-٢٤٦/١).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في صفة نساء أهل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abū Yaʿlā, as cited in al-Maṭālib al-ʿĀliyah (4608), al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Kabīr (6/71-72), whose wording this is, and Abū Nuʿaym in al-Ḥilyah (1/246-247).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Women of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":31,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Saʿīd ibn ʿĀmir ibn Ḥudhaym narrated: ʿUmar learned that Saʿīd kept nothing in his home beyond what was needed, so he sent him ten thousand. Saʿīd took it and began dividing it into small bundles. His wife asked: “Where are you taking this?” He replied: “I am giving it to those who will make it yield greater profit for us.” He kept only a very small amount. When what they had was exhausted, his wife said: “Go to some of your companions to whom you gave the money so that they can make a profit for you, and take from its returns.”","He kept delaying her and putting her off for a long time, then said: “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘If a ḥūrī were merely to reveal one of her fingers, every living creature would smell its fragrance.’ So I am abandoning them? By Allah, you women are even more deserving that I abandon you for them than they are.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ابو_یعلی_کما/المطالب_العالیہ","label":"أبو يعلى كما في المطالب العالية","number":4608},{"key":"الطبرانی/الکبیر","label":"الطبراني في الكبير","number":72},{"key":"ابو_نعیم/الحلیہ","label":"أبو نعيم في الحلية","number":247}]},{"num":16437,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن سعيد بن عامر بن حذيم قال: سمعت رسول اللّٰه ﷺ يقول:","((لو أن امرأة من أهل الجنة أشرفت إلى أهل الأرض لملأت الأرض ريح مسك، ولأذهبت ضوء الشمس والقمر)).","وإني والله ما كنت لأختارك عليهن، ودفع في صدرها - يعني امرأته -."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه البزار - كشف الأستار - (٣٥٢٨)، والطبراني في الكبير (٧٢/٦).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في صفة نساء أهل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Bazzār in Kashf al-Astār (3528) and al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Kabīr (6/72).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Women of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":31,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Saʿīd ibn ʿĀmir ibn Ḥudhaym narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “If a woman from among the people of Paradise were to look down upon the people of the earth, she would fill the earth with the fragrance of musk and would overwhelm the light of the sun and the moon.” Saʿīd then said to his wife: “By Allah, I would never choose you over them,” and he pushed her in the chest."]},"buhuth":{"ar":["قوله: ((امرأته)) يعني امرأة سعيد بن عامر، دفع في صدرها زوجها سعيد."],"en":["Regarding the phrase “his wife,” the author clarifies that it refers to the wife of Saʿīd ibn ʿĀmir, and that it was her husband Saʿīd who pushed her in the chest."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"البزار_کشف_الاستار","label":"البزار - كشف الأستار -","number":3528},{"key":"الطبرانی/الکبیر","label":"الطبراني في الكبير","number":72}]},{"num":16438,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن زيد بن أرقم قال: أتى النبي ﷺ رجل من اليهود، فقال: يا أبا القاسم، ألست تزعم أن أهل الجنة يأكلون فيها ويشربون؟ وقال لأصحابه: إن أقر لي بهذه خصمته. فقال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((بلى والذي نفسي بيده، إن أحدهم ليعطى قوة مائة رجل في المطعم والمشرب والشهوة والجماع)).","قال: فقال له اليهودي: فإن الذي يأكل ويشرب تكون له الحاجة. قال: فقال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((حاجة أحدهم عرق يفيض من جلودهم مثل ريح المسك، فإذا البطن قد ضمر))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (١٩٢٦٩)، وابن حبان (٧٤٢٤)، وأبو نعيم في صفة الجنة (٣٢٩).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في جماع أهل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (19269), Ibn Ḥibbān (7424), and Abū Nuʿaym in Ṣifat al-Jannah (329).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning Sexual Intercourse of the People of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":32,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Zayd ibn Arqam narrated: A Jewish man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Abū al-Qāsim, do you not claim that the people of Paradise will eat and drink there?” He said to his companions: “If he admits this to me, I will defeat him in argument.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “Yes, by the One in whose hand is my soul, each one of them will be given the strength of one hundred men in eating, drinking, desire, and sexual intercourse.” The Jewish man said: “But one who eats and drinks must relieve himself.”","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “The relief of one of them will be perspiration flowing from his skin with the fragrance of musk, and then his abdomen will become flat.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ابو_نعیم/صفہ_الجنہ","label":"أبو نعيم في صفة الجنة","number":329},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":19269,"n":19269},{"key":"ibnhibban","label":"صحيح ابن حبان (التقاسيم والأنواع)","number":5202,"n":5198}]},{"num":16439,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أنس، عن النبي ﷺ، قال:","((يعطى المؤمن في الجنة قوة كذا وكذا من الجماع)).","قيل: يا رسول الله، أو يطيق ذلك؟ قال:","((يعطى قوة مائة))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (٢٥٣٦)، وأبو داود الطيالسي (٢١٢٤) وابن حبان (٧٤٠٠).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في جماع أهل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (2536), Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī (2124), and Ibn Ḥibbān (7400).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning Sexual Intercourse of the People of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":32,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The believer in Paradise will be given such-and-such strength for sexual intercourse.” It was asked: “O Messenger of Allah, will he really be capable of that?” He replied: “He will be given the strength of one hundred.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"tirmidhi","label":"الترمذي","number":2536},{"key":"ابو_داود_الطیالسی","label":"أبو داود الطيالسي","number":2124},{"key":"ibnhibban","label":"ابن حبان","number":7400},{"key":"tayalisi","label":"مسند أبي داود الطيالسي","number":2124,"n":2124}]},{"num":16440,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة، عن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ أنه قيل له: أنطأ في الجنة؟ قال:","((نعم، والذي نفسي بيده دحمًا دحمًا، فإذا قام عنها رجعت مطهرة بكرًا))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه ابن حبان (٧٤٠٢)، وأبو نعيم في صفة الجنة (٣٩٣).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في جماع أهل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Ibn Ḥibbān (7402) and Abū Nuʿaym in Ṣifat al-Jannah (393).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning Sexual Intercourse of the People of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":32,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked: “Will there be sexual intercourse in Paradise?” He replied: “Yes, by the One in whose hand is my soul, vigorously and repeatedly. When he rises from her, she will return purified and a virgin.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ابو_نعیم/صفہ_الجنہ","label":"أبو نعيم في صفة الجنة","number":393},{"key":"ibnhibban","label":"صحيح ابن حبان (التقاسيم والأنواع)","number":5187,"n":5183}]},{"num":16441,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة قال: قيل: يا رسول الله، أنفضي إلى نسائنا في الجنة؟ فقال:","((إي والذي نفسي بيده، إن الرجل ليفضي في اليوم الواحد إلى مئة عذراء))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البزار (١٠٠٧٢)، والطبراني في الصغير (٧٩٥)، وفي الأوسط (٧٢٢).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في جماع أهل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bazzār (10072), al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Ṣaghīr (795), and al-Muʿjam al-Awsaṭ (722).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning Sexual Intercourse of the People of Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":32,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated: It was asked: “O Messenger of Allah, will we have intimate relations with our wives in Paradise?” He replied: “Yes, by the One in whose hand is my soul, a man will have intimate relations with one hundred virgins in a single day.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"البزار","label":"البزار","number":10072},{"key":"الطبرانی/الصغیر","label":"الطبراني في الصغير","number":795},{"key":"وفی_الاوسط","label":"وفي الأوسط","number":722},{"key":"sh12862","label":"كشف الأستار عن زوائد البزار","number":3525,"n":3526}]},{"num":16442,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي سعيد الخدري قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((المؤمن إذا اشتهى الولد في الجنة كان حمله ووضعه وسنه في ساعة كما يشتهي))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (٢٥٦٣)، وابن ماجه (٤٣٣٨)، وأحمد (١١٠٦٣)، وابن حبان (٧٤٠٤).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في الحمل والولادة في الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (2563), Ibn Mājah (4338), Aḥmad (11063), and Ibn Ḥibbān (7404).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning Pregnancy and Childbirth in Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":33,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If a believer desires a child in Paradise, its pregnancy, birth, and reaching the age he desires will all take place within a single hour, exactly as he wishes.”"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["هذا الحديث يدل على الحمل والوضع في الجنة، لمن شاء ذلك من أهل الجنة، وعموم نصوص القرآن تدل على ذلك."],"en":["The author states that this hadith indicates the occurrence of pregnancy and childbirth in Paradise for whoever among its people desires that, and that the general purport of the Qurʾānic texts also indicates this."]},"intro":{"ar":["قال تعالى:","﴿لَهُمْ مَا يَشَاءُونَ فِيهَا وَلَدَيْنَا مَزِيدٌ﴾ [سورة ق: ٣٥].","قوله: ﴿لَهُمْ مَا يَشَاءُونَ فِيهَا﴾ أي: أنهم يجدون فيها جميع أصناف الملاذ، وكلما طلبوا أحضر لهم، قال تعالى:","﴿وَلَكُمْ فِيهَا مَا تَشْتَهِي أَنْفُسُكُمْ وَلَكُمْ فِيهَا مَا تَدَّعُونَ﴾ [فصلت: ٣١]."],"en":["Allah, the Exalted, says:","“They will have whatever they wish therein, and with Us is even more.”","[Qāf 50:35]","Regarding His statement:","“They will have whatever they wish therein,”","the author explains that they will find therein every kind of pleasure, and whatever they request will be brought to them.","Allah, the Exalted, says:","“You will have therein whatever your souls desire, and you will have therein whatever you ask for.”","[Fuṣṣilat 41:31]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"tirmidhi","label":"الترمذي","number":2563},{"key":"ibnmajah","label":"ابن ماجه","number":4338},{"key":"ibnhibban","label":"ابن حبان","number":7404},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":11063,"n":11063}]},{"num":16443,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة، أن النبي ﷺ كان يومًا يحدث، وعنده رجل من أهل البادية:","((أن رجلًا من أهل الجنة استأذن ربه في الزرع، فقال له: أو لست فيما شئت؟ قال: بلى، ولكني أحب أن أزرع، فأسرع وبذر، فتبادر الطرف نباته واستواؤه واستحصاده وتكويره أمثال الجبال، فيقول اللّٰه تعالى: دونك يا ابن آدم، فإنه لا يشبعك شيء)).","فقال الأعرابي: يا رسول الله، لا تجد هذا إلا قرشيًا أو أنصاريًا، فإنهم أصحاب زرع، فأما نحن فلسنا بأصحاب زرع، فضحك رسول اللّٰه ﷺ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (٢٣٤٨) و(٧٥١٩).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب من أهل الجنة من يرغب في الزراعة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (2348) and (7519).","chapter_en":"Some of the People of Paradise Will Desire Farming","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":34,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated: One day the Prophet ﷺ was speaking while a Bedouin man was present. He said: “A man from the people of Paradise will ask his Lord for permission to farm. Allah will say to him: ‘Are you not already enjoying whatever you desire?’ He will reply: ‘Yes, but I love farming.’ So he will quickly sow the seed, and in the blink of an eye it will sprout, mature, be harvested, and gathered into heaps like mountains. Allah, the Exalted, will say: ‘Take it, O son of Ādam, for nothing ever satisfies you.’”","The Bedouin said: “O Messenger of Allah, you will only find such a man to be from Quraysh or the Anṣār, because they are farmers. As for us, we are not farmers.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":2348},{"key":"و","label":"و","number":7519}]},{"num":16444,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر بن عبد اللّٰه قال: سمعت النبي ﷺ يقول:","((إن أهل الجنة يأكلون فيها ويشربون، ولا يتفلون ولا يبولون ولا يتغوطون ولا يمتخطون)).","قالوا: فما بال الطعام؟ قال:","((جشاء ورشح كرشح المسك، يلهمون التسبيح والتحميد، كما تلهمون النفس)).","وفي لفظ:","((ويلهمون التسبيح والتكبير، كما يلهمون النفس))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٢٠، ١٨ :٢٨٣٥).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أهل الجنة يلهمون التسبيح والتحميد كما تلهمون النفس","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (20, 18 :2835).","chapter_en":"The People of Paradise Will Be Inspired to Glorify and Praise Allah Just as You Are Inspired to Breathe","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":35,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “The people of Paradise will eat and drink therein, but they will neither spit, urinate, defecate, nor blow their noses.” They asked: “Then what becomes of the food?” He replied: “It will be discharged as belching and perspiration like the fragrance of musk. They will be inspired to glorify and praise Allah just as you are inspired to breathe.”","In another wording: “They will be inspired to glorify Allah and proclaim His greatness just as they are inspired to breathe.”"]},"intro":{"ar":["قال اللّٰه تعالى:","﴿إِنَّ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَعَمِلُوا الصَّالِحَاتِ يَهْدِيهِمْ رَبُّهُمْ بِإِيمَانِهِمْ تَجْرِي مِنْ تَحْتِهِمُ الْأَنْهَارُ فِي جَنَّاتِ النَّعِيمِ ۝ دَعْوَاهُمْ فِيهَا سُبْحَانَكَ اللَّهُمَّ وَتَحِيَّتُهُمْ فِيهَا سَلَامٌ وَآخِرُ دَعْوَاهُمْ أَنِ الْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ رَبِّ الْعَالَمِينَ﴾ [سورة يونس: ٩-١٠]."],"en":["Allah, the Exalted, says:","“Indeed, those who believe and perform righteous deeds—their Lord will guide them by their faith. Rivers will flow beneath them in Gardens of Bliss. Their prayer therein will be: ‘Glory be to You, O Allah,’ and their greeting therein will be: ‘Peace,’ and the conclusion of their prayer will be: ‘All praise belongs to Allah, Lord of the worlds.’”","[Yūnus 10:9-10]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":20}]},{"num":16445,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي سعيد الخدري قال: قال النبي ﷺ:","((إن اللّه يقول لأهل الجنة: يا أهل الجنة، فيقولون: لبيك ربنا، وسعديك، والخير في يديك، فيقول: هل رضيتم؟ فيقولون: وما لنا لا نرضى يا رب وقد أعطيتنا ما لم تعط أحدًا من خلقك، فيقول: ألا أعطيكم أفضل من ذلك؟ فيقولون: رب وأي شيء أفضل من ذلك؟ فيقول: أحل عليكم رضواني، فلا أسخط عليكم بعده أبدًا))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٧٥١٨)، ومسلم (٢٨٢٩).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب لا يسخط الله على أهل الجنة أبدًا","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (7518) and Muslim (2829).","chapter_en":"Allah Will Never Be Angry with the People of Paradise Again","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":36,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Allah will say to the people of Paradise: ‘O people of Paradise!’ They will reply: ‘Here we are at Your service, our Lord, ready to obey You, and all good is in Your Hands.’ He will ask: ‘Are you pleased?’ They will say: ‘Why should we not be pleased, our Lord, when You have given us what You have not given to anyone else among Your creation?’ He will say: ‘Shall I not give you something better than that?’","They will ask: ‘Our Lord, what could be better than that?’ He will say: ‘I bestow My pleasure upon you, and I will never be angry with you after this.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":7518},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2829}]},{"num":16446,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر بن عبد الله قال: قال رسول الله ﷺ:","((إذا دخل أهل الجنة الجنة، قال الله تعالى: هل تشتهون شيئًا فأزيدكموه؟ قالوا: يا ربنا، وهل بقي شيء إلا وقد نلناه؟ فيقول: نعم، رضائي، فلا أسخط عليكم أبدًا))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه ابن حبان (٧٤٣٩)، والحاكم (٨٢/١)، وأبو نعيم في صفة الجنة (٢٨٣).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب لا يسخط الله على أهل الجنة أبدًا","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Ibn Ḥibbān (7439), al-Ḥākim (1/82), and Abū Nuʿaym in Ṣifat al-Jannah (283).","chapter_en":"Allah Will Never Be Angry with the People of Paradise Again","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise","part_no":66,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":36,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When the people of Paradise enter Paradise, Allah, the Exalted, will say: ‘Do you desire anything so that I may increase you?’ They will say: ‘Our Lord, is there anything left that we have not already received?’ He will say: ‘Yes—My pleasure. I will never be angry with you again.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ibnhibban","label":"ابن حبان","number":7439},{"key":"hakim","label":"الحاكم","number":82},{"key":"ابو_نعیم/صفہ_الجنہ","label":"أبو نعيم في صفة الجنة","number":283}]},{"num":16447,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عدي بن حاتم قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((ما منكم من أحد إلا سيكلمه الله، ليس بينه وبينه ترجمان، فينظر أيمن منه، فلا يرى إلا ما قدم، وينظر أشأم منه فلا يرى إلا ما قدم، وينظر بين يديه فلا يرى إلا النار تلقاء وجهه، فاتقوا النار ولو بشق تمرة))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٦٥٣٩)، ومسلم (٦٧ :١٠١٦).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب الوقاية من النار","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6539) and Muslim (67 :1016).","chapter_en":"Protecting Oneself from the Fire","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":4,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAdī ibn Ḥātim narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is none among you except that Allah will speak to him directly, with no interpreter between him and Allah. He will look to his right and see nothing except what he sent forward. He will look to his left and see nothing except what he sent forward. Then he will look ahead and see nothing except the Fire directly before his face. So protect yourselves from the Fire, even with half a date.”"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["وزاد في رواية:","((فمن لم يجد فبكلمة طيبة))."],"en":["Another narration adds:","“And whoever cannot find even that, then with a good word.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6539},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":67}]},{"num":16448,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبدالله بن مسعود قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((يؤتى بجهنم يومئذ لها سبعون ألف زمام، مع كل زمام سبعون ألف ملك يجرونها))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٢٨٤٢).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أن جهنم لها سبعون ألف زمام","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2842).","chapter_en":"Hell Will Have Seventy Thousand Reins","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":4,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Hell will be brought forth on that Day with seventy thousand reins, and with every rein will be seventy thousand angels dragging it.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2842}]},{"num":16449,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أنس بن مالك قال: قال النبي ﷺ:","((لا تزال جهنم تقول: هل من مزيد؟ حتى يضع فيها رب العزة تبارك وتعالى قدمه، فتقول: قط قط وعزتك. ويزوى بعضها إلى بعض))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٦٦٦١)، ومسلم (٣٧ :٢٨٤٨).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في سعة جهنم","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6661) and Muslim (37 :2848).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Vastness of Hell","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":4,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Hell will continue saying: ‘Is there any more?’ until the Lord of Might, Blessed and Exalted, places His Foot in it. Then it will say: ‘Enough! Enough! By Your Might!’ and its parts will contract together.”"]},"intro":{"ar":["قال الله تعالى:","﴿يَوْمَ نَقُولُ لِجَهَنَّمَ هَلِ امْتَلَأْتِ وَتَقُولُ هَلْ مِنْ مَزِيدٍ﴾ [سورة ق: ٣٠]."],"en":["Allah, the Exalted, says:","“On the Day We will say to Hell, ‘Are you filled?’ and it will say, ‘Is there any more?’”","[Qāf 50:30]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6661},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":37}]},{"num":16450,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن سمرة قال: قال النبي ﷺ:","((رأيت الليلة رجلين أتياني، قالا: الذي يوقد النار مالك خازن النار، وأنا جبريل، وهذا ميكائيل))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٣٢٣٦)، ومسلم (٢٢٧٥).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب خازن النار يوقد النار","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3236) and Muslim (2275).","chapter_en":"The Keeper of the Fire Tends the Fire","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":4,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Samurah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Last night I saw two men who came to me. They said: ‘The one tending the Fire is Mālik, the keeper of the Fire. I am Jibrīl, and this is Mīkāʾīl.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":3236},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2275}]},{"num":16451,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن ابن عباس قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((مررت ليلة أسري بي على موسى بن عمران عليه السلام، رجل آدم طوال جعد كأنه من رجال شنوءة، ورأيت عيسى ابن مريم مربوع الخلق إلى الحمرة والبياض سبط الرأس، وأري مالكًا خازن النار…)).","الحديث."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٣٢٣٩)، ومسلم (٢٦٧ :١٦٥).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب خازن النار يوقد النار","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3239) and Muslim (267 :165).","chapter_en":"The Keeper of the Fire Tends the Fire","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":4,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿAbbās narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “On the night I was taken on the Night Journey, I passed by Mūsā ibn ʿImrān, peace be upon him, a tall, dark-complexioned man with curly hair, as though he were one of the men of Shanūʾah. I saw ʿĪsā ibn Maryam, of medium stature, with a complexion inclining toward red and white, and with straight hair. And Mālik, the keeper of the Fire, was shown to me…” The hadith continues."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":3239},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":267}]},{"num":16452,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة قال: كنا مع رسول اللّٰه ﷺ إذ سمع وجبة، فقال النبي ﷺ:","((تدرون ما هذا؟)).","قال: قلنا: اللّٰه ورسوله أعلم. قال:","((هذا حجر رمي به في النار منذ سبعين خريفًا، فهو يهوي في النار الآن، حتى انتهى إلى قعرها))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٢٨٤٤).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في بعد قعر جهنم","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2844).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Great Depth of Hell","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":4,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated: We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he heard a loud crash. The Prophet ﷺ asked: “Do you know what that was?” We replied: “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said: “That was a stone which was thrown into the Fire seventy years ago. It has been falling through the Fire until just now it reached its bottom.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2844}]},{"num":16453,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة أن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال:","((إن العبد ليتكلم بالكلمة ما يتبين فيها، يهوي بها في النار أبعد ما بين المشرق والمغرب))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٦٤٧٧)، ومسلم (٥٠ :٢٩٨٨).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في بعد قعر جهنم","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6477) and Muslim (50 :2988).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Great Depth of Hell","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":4,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A servant may utter a word without considering its consequences, and because of it he will fall into the Fire farther than the distance between the east and the west.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6477},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":50}]},{"num":16454,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة، عن النبي ﷺ قال:","((إن العبد ليتكلم بالكلمة من رضوان اللّٰه لا يلقي لها بالًا يرفعه اللّٰه بها درجات، وإن العبد ليتكلم بالكلمة من سخط اللّٰه لا يلقي لها بالًا يهوي بها في جهنم))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (٦٤٧٨).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في بعد قعر جهنم","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6478).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Great Depth of Hell","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":4,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “A servant may utter a word pleasing to Allah without giving it much thought, and Allah will raise him by it many ranks. And a servant may utter a word displeasing to Allah without giving it much thought, and because of it he will fall into Hell.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6478}]},{"num":16455,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن خالد بن عمير العدوي قال: خطبنا عتبة بن غزوان، فحمد اللّٰه وأثنى عليه، ثم قال: أما بعد فإن الدنيا قد آذنت بصرم وولت حذاء، ولم يبق منها إلا صبابة كصبابة الإناء، يتصابها صاحبها، وإنكم منتقلون منها إلى دار لا زوال لها، فانتقلوا بخير ما بحضرتكم، فإنه قد ذكر لنا أن الحجر يلقى من شفة جهنم فيهوي فيها سبعين عامًا لا يدرك لها قعر، ووالله لتملأن، أفعجبتم؟…","الحديث بطوله."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٢٩٦٧).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في بعد قعر جهنم","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2967).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Great Depth of Hell","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":4,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Khālid ibn ʿUmayr al-ʿAdawī narrated: ʿUtbah ibn Ghazwān delivered a sermon to us. He praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: “To proceed: This world has announced that it is coming to an end and has turned away swiftly. Nothing remains of it except a small amount like the dregs remaining in a vessel, which its owner tries to drink. You are moving from it to an abode that will never pass away, so move there with the best deeds you are able to take with you.","We have been told that a stone will be thrown from the edge of Hell and will fall through it for seventy years without reaching its bottom. By Allah, it will certainly be filled. Are you surprised?…” The hadith continues at length."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2967}]},{"num":16456,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي سعيد الخدري يقول: إنا يومًا عند رسول اللّٰه ﷺ فرأيناه كئيبًا، فقال بعضهم: يا رسول اللّٰه! بأبي وأمي ومالي أراك هكذا؟ فقال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((سمعت هدة لم أسمع مثلها، فأتاني جبريل، فسألته عنها، فقال: هذا صخر قذف به في النار منذ سبعين خريفًا فاليوم استقر قراره)).","فقال أبو سعيد: والذي ذهب بنفس نبينا ﷺ! ما رأيته ضاحكًا بعد ذلك اليوم حتى واراه التراب."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه ابن أبي شيبة (٣٥٢٨٦).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في بعد قعر جهنم","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah (35286).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Great Depth of Hell","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":4,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated: One day we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and noticed that he appeared deeply distressed. Someone said: “O Messenger of Allah, may my father, mother, and wealth be sacrificed for you; why do I see you in this state?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “I heard a tremendous crash unlike anything I had ever heard. Then Jibrīl came to me, so I asked him about it. He said: ‘This is a rock that was thrown into the Fire seventy years ago, and today it finally reached its resting place.’”","Abū Saʿīd said: “By the One who took the soul of our Prophet ﷺ, I never saw him laugh after that day until the earth covered him.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ابن_ابی_شیبہ","label":"ابن أبي شيبة","number":35286},{"key":"sh9944","label":"المصنف لابن أبي شيبة","number":34149,"n":34129}]},{"num":16457,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبد اللّه بن عمرو قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((لو أن رصاصة مثل هذه - وأشار إلى مثل جمجمة - أرسلت من السماء إلى الأرض وهي مسيرة خمس مائة سنة لبلغت الأرض قبل الليل، ولو أنها أرسلت من رأس السلسلة لسارت أربعين خريفًا، الليل والنهار، قبل أن تبلغ أصلها أو قعرها))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (٢٥٨٨)، وأحمد (٦٨٥٦)، والحاكم (٤٣٩-٤٣٨/٢).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في بعد قعر جهنم","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (2588), Aḥmad (6856), and al-Ḥākim (2/438-439).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Great Depth of Hell","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":4,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If a lead ball like this”—and he gestured to something the size of a skull—“were released from the sky toward the earth, though the distance is a journey of five hundred years, it would reach the earth before nightfall. But if it were released from the top of the chain in Hell, it would travel for forty years, by night and day, before reaching its end or its bottom.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"tirmidhi","label":"الترمذي","number":2588},{"key":"hakim","label":"الحاكم","number":439},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":6856,"n":6856}]},{"num":16458,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((تخرج عنق من النار يوم القيامة، لها عينان تبصران، وأذنان تسمعان، ولسان ينطق، يقول: إني وكلت بثلاثة: بكل جبار عنيد، وبكل من دعا مع اللّٰه إلهًا آخر، وبالمصورين))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الترمذي (٢٥٧٤)، وأحمد (٨٤٣٠)، والبيهقي في “الشعب” (٥٩٠٤).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب تخرج عنق من النار يوم القيامة تتكلم","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (2574), Aḥmad (8430), and al-Bayhaqī in al-Shuʿab (5904).","chapter_en":"A Neck Will Emerge from the Fire on the Day of Resurrection and Speak","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":4,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A neck will emerge from the Fire on the Day of Resurrection. It will have two eyes with which it sees, two ears with which it hears, and a tongue with which it speaks. It will say: ‘I have been entrusted with three: every obstinate tyrant, everyone who called upon another deity alongside Allah, and the image-makers.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"tirmidhi","label":"الترمذي","number":2574},{"key":"البیہقی/الشعب","label":"البيهقي في “الشعب”","number":5904},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":8430,"n":8430}]},{"num":16459,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي سعيد، عن نبي اللّٰه ﷺ أنه قال:","((يخرج عنق من النار يتكلم يقول: وكلت اليوم بثلاثة: بكل جبار، وبمن جعل مع اللّٰه إلهًا آخر، وبمن قتل نفسًا بغير نفس، فينطوي عليهم، فيقذفهم في غمرات جهنم))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (١١٣٥٤)، وابن أبي شيبة (٣٥٢٧٨)، وأبو يعلى (١١٤٦)، والبزار - كشف الأستار - (٣٥٠٠).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب تخرج عنق من النار يوم القيامة تتكلم","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (11354), Ibn Abī Shaybah (35278), Abū Yaʿlā (1146), and al-Bazzār in Kashf al-Astār (3500).","chapter_en":"A Neck Will Emerge from the Fire on the Day of Resurrection and Speak","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":4,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd narrated that the Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: “A neck will emerge from the Fire and speak, saying: ‘Today I have been entrusted with three: every tyrant, whoever set up another deity alongside Allah, and whoever killed a soul without just cause.’ It will wrap itself around them and cast them into the depths of Hell.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ابن_ابی_شیبہ","label":"ابن أبي شيبة","number":35278},{"key":"ابو_یعلی","label":"أبو يعلى","number":1146},{"key":"البزار_کشف_الاستار","label":"البزار - كشف الأستار -","number":3500},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":11354,"n":11354}]},{"num":16460,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة أن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال:","((نار بني آدم التي يوقدون جزء من سبعين جزءًا من نار جهنم)).","فقالوا: يا رسول اللّٰه إن كانت لكافية، قال:","((إنها فضلت عليها بتسعة وستين جزءًا))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك في كتاب جهنم (١) ومسلم (٢٨٤٣) والبخاري (٣٢٦٥).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في شدة نار جهنم","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by Mālik in Kitāb Jahannam (1), Muslim (2843), and al-Bukhārī (3265).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Intensity of the Fire of Hell","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":4,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The fire which the children of Ādam kindle is one part out of seventy parts of the Fire of Hell.” They said: “O Messenger of Allah, this fire would have been sufficient!” He replied: “The Fire of Hell has been made sixty-nine parts more intense than it.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"malik/کتاب_جہنم","label":"مالك في كتاب جهنم","number":1},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2843},{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":3265}]},{"num":16461,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة أن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال:","((هذه النار جزء من مئة جزء من جهنم))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (٨٩٢١).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في شدة نار جهنم","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (8921).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Intensity of the Fire of Hell","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":4,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “This fire is one part out of one hundred parts of Hell.”"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["قلت: يحمل قوله: “سبعين جزء” وقوله: “مئة جزء” في أوقات مختلفة شدة وخفة، ويحمل أيضًا حسب أشخاص داخلين فيها."],"en":["The author says that the wording “seventy parts” and the wording “one hundred parts” may be understood as referring to different times of greater or lesser intensity, and may also vary according to those who enter it."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":8921,"n":8921}]},{"num":16462,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن سمرة بن جندب أن النبي ﷺ قال:","((منهم من تأخذه النار إلى كعبيه، ومنهم من تأخذه النار إلى ركبتيه، ومنهم من تأخذه النار إلى حجزته، ومنهم من تأخذه النار إلى ترقوته))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٣٣ :٢٨٤٥).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أن الداخلين في جهنم تصيبهم النار حسب ذنوبهم","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (33 :2845).","chapter_en":"Those Who Enter Hell Will Be Reached by the Fire According to Their Sins","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":4,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Samurah ibn Jundub narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Among them are those whom the Fire will reach up to their ankles; among them are those whom it will reach up to their knees; among them are those whom it will reach up to their waist; and among them are those whom it will reach up to their collarbones.”"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["قوله: “حجزته” هي معقد الإزار والسراويل. قوله: “ترقوته” هي العظم الذي بين ثغرة النحر والعنق."],"en":["The word “ḥujzatihi” refers to the place where the waist-wrapper or trousers are tied.","The word “tarquwatihi” refers to the collarbone between the hollow at the base of the throat and the neck."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":33}]},{"num":16463,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((اشتكت النار إلى ربها، فقالت: رب أكل بعضي بعضًا، فأذن لها بنفسين: نفس في الشتاء، ونفس في الصيف، فأشد ما تجدون من الحر وأشد ما تجدون من الزمهرير))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٣٢٦٠)، ومسلم (٦١٧).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في شكوى النار إلى ربها من شدة حرها وبردها","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3260) and Muslim (617).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Fire Complaining to Its Lord About the Severity of Its Heat and Cold","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":4,"chapter_no":9,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The Fire complained to its Lord, saying: ‘My Lord, one part of me is consuming another.’ So He permitted it two breaths: one in winter and one in summer. Thus the most severe heat you experience and the most severe bitter cold you experience are from it.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":3260},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":617}]},{"num":16464,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن مجاهد أن الناس كانوا يطوفون بالبيت وابن عباس جالس معه محجن، فقال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","﴿يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا اتَّقُوا اللَّهَ حَقَّ تُقَاتِهِ وَلَا تَمُوتُنَّ إِلَّا وَأَنْتُمْ مُسْلِمُونَ﴾","((ولو أن قطرة من الزقوم قطرت لأمرت على أهل الأرض عيشهم، فكيف بمن ليس لهم طعام إلا الزقوم))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الترمذي (٢٥٨٥)، وابن ماجه (٤٣٢٥)، وأحمد (٢٧٣٥)، وابن أبي حاتم (٧٢٣/٣)، وصححه ابن حبان (٧٤٧٠)، والحاكم (٢٩٤/٢).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في طعام أهل النار وشرابهم","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (2585), Ibn Mājah (4325), Aḥmad (2735), Ibn Abī Ḥātim (3/723), and authenticated by Ibn Ḥibbān (7470) and al-Ḥākim (2/294).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Food and Drink of the People of the Fire","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":4,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Mujāhid narrated: The people were circumambulating the House while Ibn ʿAbbās was sitting with a hooked staff. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “‘O you who believe, fear Allah as He should be feared and do not die except in a state of submission.’ If a single drop of Zaqqūm were to fall upon the earth, it would ruin the livelihood of the people of the earth. So what of those whose only food will be Zaqqūm?”"]},"intro":{"ar":["قال اللّٰه تعالى:","﴿إِنَّ شَجَرَتَ الزَّقُّومِ ۝ طَعَامُ الْأَثِيمِ ۝ كَالْمُهْلِ يَغْلِي فِي الْبُطُونِ ۝ كَغَلْيِ الْحَمِيمِ ۝ خُذُوهُ فَاعْتِلُوهُ إِلَىٰ سَوَاءِ الْجَحِيمِ ۝ ثُمَّ صُبُّوا فَوْقَ رَأْسِهِ مِنْ عَذَابِ الْحَمِيمِ﴾ [الدخان: ٤٣-٤٨].","وقال تعالى:","﴿فَلَيْسَ لَهُ الْيَوْمَ هَاهُنَا حَمِيمٌ ۝ وَلَا طَعَامٌ إِلَّا مِنْ غِسْلِينٍ ۝ لَا يَأْكُلُهُ إِلَّا الْخَاطِئُونَ﴾ [الحاقة: ٣٥-٣٧].","وقال تعالى:","﴿تَصْلَىٰ نَارًا حَامِيَةً ۝ تُسْقَىٰ مِنْ عَيْنٍ آنِيَةٍ ۝ لَيْسَ لَهُمْ طَعَامٌ إِلَّا مِنْ ضَرِيعٍ ۝ لَا يُسْمِنُ وَلَا يُغْنِي مِنْ جُوعٍ﴾ [الغاشية: ٤-٧]."],"en":["Allah, the Exalted, says:","“Indeed, the tree of Zaqqūm is the food of the sinful. Like molten metal, it will boil in the bellies like the boiling of scalding water. ‘Seize him and drag him into the midst of the blazing Fire. Then pour over his head the torment of scalding water.’”","[al-Dukhān 44:43-48]","And He, the Exalted, says:","“So today he has no devoted friend here, nor any food except foul discharge, which none will eat except the sinners.”","[al-Ḥāqqah 69:35-37]","And He, the Exalted, says:","“They will enter a blazing Fire, given drink from a boiling spring. They will have no food except from a bitter thorny plant, which neither nourishes nor satisfies hunger.”","[al-Ghāshiyah 88:4-7]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"tirmidhi","label":"الترمذي","number":2585},{"key":"ibnmajah","label":"ابن ماجه","number":4325},{"key":"ابن_ابی_حاتم","label":"ابن أبي حاتم","number":723},{"key":"صححہ_ابن_حبان","label":"صححه ابن حبان","number":7470},{"key":"hakim","label":"الحاكم","number":294},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":2735,"n":2735}]},{"num":16465,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة، عن النبي ﷺ قال:","((إن الحميم ليصب على رؤوسهم، فينفذ الحميم حتى يخلص إلى جوفه، فيسلت ما في جوفه، حتى يمرق من قدميه - وهو الصهر -، ثم يعاد كما كان))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (٢٥٨٢)، وأحمد (٨٨٦٤)، والحاكم (٣٨٧/٢).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في طعام أهل النار وشرابهم","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (2582), Aḥmad (8864), and al-Ḥākim (2/387).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Food and Drink of the People of the Fire","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":4,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Scalding water will be poured over their heads. It will penetrate until it reaches their insides, dissolving whatever is within them, until it exits through their feet. This is the melting. Then they will be restored as they were.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"tirmidhi","label":"الترمذي","number":2582},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":8864,"n":8864},{"key":"hakim","label":"المستدرك على الصحيحين","number":3458,"n":3445}]},{"num":16466,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر: أن رجلًا قدم من جيشان - وجيشان من اليمن -، فسأل النبي ﷺ عن شراب يشربونه بأرضهم من الذرة يقال له: المزر، فقال النبي ﷺ:","((أو مسكر هو؟)).","قال: نعم. قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((كل مسكر حرام، إن على اللّٰه عز وجل عهدًا لمن يشرب المسكر أن يسقيه من طينة خبال)).","قالوا: يا رسول الله! وما طينة الخبال؟ قال:","((عرق أهل النار، أو عصارة أهل النار))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٢٠٠٢).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في طعام أهل النار وشرابهم","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2002).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Food and Drink of the People of the Fire","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":4,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir narrated: A man came from Jayshān—and Jayshān is in Yemen—and asked the Prophet ﷺ about a drink they made in their land from millet called al-mizr. The Prophet ﷺ asked: “Is it intoxicating?” He replied: “Yes.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Every intoxicant is forbidden. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has made a covenant that whoever drinks intoxicants will be given to drink from Ṭīnat al-Khabāl.” They asked: “O Messenger of Allah, what is Ṭīnat al-Khabāl?”","He replied: “The sweat of the people of the Fire, or the discharge of the people of the Fire.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2002}]},{"num":16467,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبد اللّٰه بن عمرو بن العاص عن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ أنه قال:","((من ترك الصلاة سكرًا مرة واحدة، فكأنما كانت له الدنيا وما عليها فسلبها، ومن ترك الصلاة سكرًا أربع مرات، كان حقًا على اللّٰه عز وجل أن يسقيه من طينة الخبال)).","قيل: وما طينة الخبال يا رسول الله؟ قال:","((عصارة أهل جهنم))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (٦٦٥٩).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في طعام أهل النار وشرابهم","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (6659).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Food and Drink of the People of the Fire","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":4,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever abandons the prayer because of intoxication one time, it is as though he possessed the whole world and everything upon it and then had it taken away from him. And whoever abandons the prayer because of intoxication four times, it becomes a right upon Allah, Mighty and Majestic, to give him drink from Ṭīnat al-Khabāl.” It was asked: “What is Ṭīnat al-Khabāl, O Messenger of Allah?”","He replied: “The discharge of the people of Hell.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":6659,"n":6659}]},{"num":16468,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبدالله بن الحارث بن جزء الزبيدي قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((إن في النار حيات كأمثال أعناق البخت، تلسع إحداهن اللسعة، فيجد حموتها أربعين خريفًا، وإن في النار عقارب كأمثال البغال الموكفة، تلسع إحداهن اللسعة، فيجد حموتها أربعين سنة))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (١٧٧١٢).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في حيات النار وعقاربها","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Imām Aḥmad (17712).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Snakes and Scorpions of the Fire","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":4,"chapter_no":11,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Ḥārith ibn Jazʾ al-Zubaydī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, in the Fire are snakes like the necks of Bactrian camels. One of them will bite a person, and he will feel the burning pain of its venom for forty years. And in the Fire are scorpions like saddled mules. One of them will sting a person, and he will feel the burning pain of its venom for forty years.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"الامام_احمد","label":"الإمام أحمد","number":17712},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":17712,"n":17712}]},{"num":16469,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عتبان بن مالك الأنصاري قال: غدا علي رسول اللّٰه ﷺ فقال:","((لن يوافي عبد يوم القيامة، يقول: لا إله إلا اللّٰه يبتغي به وجه اللّٰه إلا حرّم اللّٰه عليه النار))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٦٤٢٣-٦٤٢٢)، ومسلم (٢٦٤ :٣٣). واللفظ للبخاري.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب تحريم الله النار على من قال: لا إله إلا الله يبتغي به وجه الله","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6422-6423) and Muslim (264 :33). The wording is al-Bukhārī’s.","chapter_en":"Allah Has Forbidden the Fire to Whoever Says “Lā Ilāha Illā Allah,” Seeking Thereby the Face of Allah","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿItbān ibn Mālik al-Anṣārī narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to me one morning and said: “No servant will come on the Day of Resurrection saying, ‘There is no deity except Allah,’ seeking thereby the Face of Allah, except that Allah will forbid the Fire to him.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6423},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":264}]},{"num":16470,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي بكرة، عن النبي ﷺ قال في حديث طويل:","((ثم يؤذن للملائكة والنبيين والشهداء أن يشفعوا، فيشفعون ويخرجون، ويشفعون ويخرجون، ويشفعون ويخرجون)).","وزاد عفان مرة فقال أيضًا:","((ويشفعون ويخرجون من كان في قلبه ما يزن ذرة من إيمان))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (٢٠٤٤٠)، والبزار (٣٦٧١)، والطبراني في الصغير (٩٢٩)، وابن أبي عاصم في السنة (٨٣٨).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب يخرج من النار من كان في قلبه ما يزن ذرة من إيمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (20440), al-Bazzār (3671), al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Ṣaghīr (929), and Ibn Abī ʿĀṣim in al-Sunnah (838).","chapter_en":"Whoever Has in His Heart Faith Weighing as Much as an Atom Will Be Brought Out of the Fire","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Bakrah narrated from the Prophet ﷺ in a lengthy hadith: “Then permission will be given to the angels, the Prophets, and the martyrs to intercede. So they will intercede and bring people out; they will intercede and bring people out; they will intercede and bring people out.” On one occasion, ʿAffān added: “They will intercede and bring out whoever has in his heart faith weighing as much as an atom.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"البزار","label":"البزار","number":3671},{"key":"الطبرانی/الصغیر","label":"الطبراني في الصغير","number":929},{"key":"ابن_ابی_عاصم/السنہ","label":"ابن أبي عاصم في السنة","number":838},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":20440,"n":20440},{"key":"sh12862","label":"كشف الأستار عن زوائد البزار","number":3467,"n":3468}]},{"num":16471,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي سعيد الخدري قال: سمعت رسول اللّٰه ﷺ يقول:","((يوضع الصراط بين ظهري جهنم، عليه حسك كحسك السعدان، ثم يستجيز الناس، فناج مسلم، ومجروح به، ثم ناج ومحتبس به منكوس فيها، فإذا فرغ اللّٰه عز وجل من القضاء بين العباد يفقد المؤمنون رجالًا كانوا معهم في الدنيا يصلون بصلاتهم، ويزكون بزكاتهم، ويصومون صيامهم، ويحجون حجهم، ويغزون غزوهم، فيقولون: أي ربنا، عباد من عبادك كانوا معنا في الدنيا يصلون صلاتنا، ويزكون زكاتنا، ويصومون صيامنا، ويحجون حجنا، ويغزون غزونا، لا نراهم، فيقول: اذهبوا إلى النار فمن وجدتم فيها منهم فأخرجوه. قال: فيجدونهم قد أخذتهم النار على قدر أعمالهم، فمنهم من أخذته إلى قدميه، ومنهم من أخذته إلى نصف ساقيه، ومنهم من أخذته إلى ركبتيه، ومنهم من أزرته، ومنهم من أخذته إلى ثدييه، ومنهم من أخذته إلى عنقه، ولم تغش الوجوه، فيستخرجونهم منها، فيطرحون في ماء الحياة)).","قيل: يا رسول الله، وما الحياة؟ قال:","((غسل أهل الجنة، فينبتون نبات الزرعة)).","وقال مرة فيه:","((كما تنبت الزرعة في غثاء السيل، ثم يشفع الأنبياء في كل من كان يشهد أن لا إله إلا اللّٰه مخلصًا، فيخرجونهم منها، قال: ثم يتحنن اللّٰه برحمته على من فيها، فما يترك فيها عبدًا في قلبه مثقال حبة من إيمان إلا أخرجه منها))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (١١٠٨١) واللفظ له، وابن خزيمة في التوحيد (٦٤٨)، وابن ماجه (٤٢٨٠) مختصرًا، والحاكم (٥٨٥-٥٨٦/٤) - وصححه -.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب يخرج من النار من كان في قلبه ما يزن ذرة من إيمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (11081), whose wording this is, Ibn Khuzaymah in al-Tawḥīd (648), Ibn Mājah (4280) in abbreviated form, and al-Ḥākim (4/585-586), who authenticated it.","chapter_en":"Whoever Has in His Heart Faith Weighing as Much as an Atom Will Be Brought Out of the Fire","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The Ṣirāṭ will be placed across Hell. Upon it will be hooks like the thorns of al-Saʿdān. Then the people will attempt to cross. Some will be saved unharmed, some will be wounded by it yet escape, while others will be held back and thrown headfirst into it. When Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has finished judging between the servants, the believers will notice that certain men who had been with them in the worldly life are missing—men who used to pray as they prayed, pay zakāh as they paid zakāh, fast as they fasted, perform Ḥajj as they performed Ḥajj, and fight as they fought.","They will say: ‘Our Lord, there were servants among Your servants who were with us in the world. They prayed as we prayed, paid zakāh as we did, fasted as we fasted, performed Ḥajj as we did, and fought as we fought, yet we do not see them.’ He will say: ‘Go to the Fire, and whoever among them you find there, bring him out.’ They will find that the Fire has reached them according to their deeds. Some will have been reached up to their feet, some halfway up their shins, some up to their knees, some up to their waists, some up to their chests, and some up to their necks, while their faces will not have been covered.","They will bring them out and cast them into the Water of Life.” It was asked: “O Messenger of Allah, what is the Water of Life?” He replied: “It is the washing-water of the people of Paradise, and they will grow as a plant grows.” On another occasion he said: “Just as a plant grows in the debris carried by a flood. Then the Prophets will intercede for everyone who sincerely testified that there is no deity except Allah, and they will bring them out of it.","Then Allah, through His mercy, will show compassion to those remaining therein, and He will not leave in it any servant who has in his heart the weight of a grain of faith except that He will bring him out.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ابن_خزیمہ/التوحید","label":"ابن خزيمة في التوحيد","number":648},{"key":"ibnmajah","label":"ابن ماجه","number":4280},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":11081,"n":11081},{"key":"hakim","label":"المستدرك على الصحيحين","number":8738,"n":8749}]},{"num":16472,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أنس بن مالك: أن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال:","((يخرج من النار أربعة، فيعرضون على الله، فيلتفت أحدهم، فيقول: أي رب إذ أخرجتني منها فلا تعدني فيها، فينجيه اللّٰه منها))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٣٢١ :١٩٢).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب من يخرج من النار يحسن الظن بالله أن لا يعيده فيها","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (321 :192).","chapter_en":"One Who Is Brought Out of the Fire Thinks Well of Allah That He Will Not Return Him to It","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Four people will be brought out of the Fire and presented before Allah. One of them will turn back and say: ‘My Lord, now that You have brought me out of it, do not return me to it.’ So Allah will save him from it.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":321}]},{"num":16473,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن النعمان بن بشير قال: سمعت النبي ﷺ يقول:","((إن أهون أهل النار عذابًا يوم القيامة لرجل توضع في أخمص قدميه جمرة يغلي منها دماغه))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٦٥٦١)، ومسلم (٢١٣).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب أهون أهل النار عذابًا","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6561) and Muslim (213).","chapter_en":"The Person Receiving the Lightest Punishment among the People of the Fire","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Nuʿmān ibn Bashīr narrated: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “The person receiving the lightest punishment among the people of the Fire on the Day of Resurrection will be a man beneath the arches of whose feet a burning coal will be placed, causing his brain to boil.”"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["ورواه مسلم أيضًا وفيه:","((توضع في أخمص قدميه جمرتان يغلي منهما دماغه)).","وهي عند البخاري (٦٥٦٢) وزاد في آخره:","((كما يغلي المرجل والقمقم)).","ورواه مسلم أيضًا من وجه آخر:","((إن أهون أهل النار عذابًا من له نعلان وشراكان من نار يغلي منها دماغه كما يغلي المرجل، ما يرى أن أحدًا أشد منه عذابًا، وإنه لأهونهم عذابًا)).","قوله: “أخمص” هو المتجافي من الرجل عن الأرض. قوله: “شراكان” الشراك أحد سير النعل، وهو الذي يكون على وجهها وعلى ظهر القدم. قوله: “المرجل” هو قدر معروف سواء كان من حديد، أو نحاس، أو حجارة، أو خزف."],"en":["Muslim also narrates:","“Two burning coals will be placed beneath the arches of his feet, causing his brain to boil.”","Al-Bukhārī (6562) adds at the end:","“Just as a cooking pot or a narrow-necked vessel boils.”","Muslim also narrates through another route:","“The person receiving the lightest punishment among the people of the Fire will be one who has two sandals and two straps of fire, because of which his brain will boil just as a cooking pot boils. He will think that no one is suffering a punishment more severe than his, yet he will in fact be the one receiving the lightest punishment among them.”","The author explains that “akhmaṣ” is the hollow part of the foot that does not touch the ground.","“Shirākān” is the dual of shirāk, one of the straps of a sandal which lies across its surface and over the top of the foot.","“Al-mirjal” is a well-known cooking pot, whether made of iron, copper, stone, or earthenware."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6561},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":213}]},{"num":16474,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي سعيد الخدري أن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال:","((إن أدنى أهل النار عذابًا ينتعل نعلين من نار يغلي دماغه من حرارة نعليه))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٢١١).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أهون أهل النار عذابًا","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (211).","chapter_en":"The Person Receiving the Lightest Punishment among the People of the Fire","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The person receiving the lightest punishment among the people of the Fire will wear two sandals of fire, from whose heat his brain will boil.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":211}]},{"num":16475,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن ابن عباس أن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال:","((أهون أهل النار عذابًا أبو طالب، وهو منتعل بنعلين يغلي منهما دماغه))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٢١٢).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أهون أهل النار عذابًا","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (212).","chapter_en":"The Person Receiving the Lightest Punishment among the People of the Fire","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿAbbās narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The person receiving the lightest punishment among the people of the Fire is Abū Ṭālib. He will wear two sandals because of which his brain will boil.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":212}]},{"num":16476,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة عن النبي ﷺ قال:","((أهون أهل النار عذابًا عليه نعلان يغلي منها دماغه))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (٩٥٧٦)، وابن حبان (٧٤٧٢)، والحاكم (٥٨٠/٤).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب أهون أهل النار عذابًا","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (9576), Ibn Ḥibbān (7472), and al-Ḥākim (4/580).","chapter_en":"The Person Receiving the Lightest Punishment among the People of the Fire","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The person receiving the lightest punishment among the people of the Fire will have two sandals upon him, because of which his brain will boil.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ibnhibban","label":"ابن حبان","number":7472},{"key":"hakim","label":"الحاكم","number":580},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":9576,"n":9576}]},{"num":16477,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي سعيد أن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ ذكر عنده عمه أبو طالب فقال:","((لعله تنفعه شفاعتي يوم القيامة، فيجعل في ضحضاح من نار يبلغ كعبيه يغلي منه دماغه))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٣٨٨٥)، ومسلم (٢١٠).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب تخفيف العذاب لأبي طالب بشفاعة النبي ﷺ","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3885) and Muslim (210).","chapter_en":"The Punishment of Abū Ṭālib Will Be Lightened through the Intercession of the Prophet ﷺ","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd narrated: Abū Ṭālib, the uncle of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, was mentioned in his presence, and he said: “Perhaps my intercession will benefit him on the Day of Resurrection, so that he will be placed in a shallow portion of the Fire reaching his ankles, from which his brain will boil.”"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["قوله: “ضحضاح” هو ما رق من الماء على وجه الأرض إلى نحو الكعبين، واستعير في النار."],"en":["The word “ḍaḥḍāḥ” refers literally to shallow water spread over the ground to about ankle level, and here it is used figuratively for the Fire."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":3885},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":210}]},{"num":16478,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عباس بن عبد المطلب قال: يا رسول اللّٰه هل نفعت أبا طالب بشيء؟ فإنه كان يحوطك ويغضب لك؟ قال:","((نعم، هو في ضحضاح من نار، لولا أنا لكان في الدرك الأسفل من النار)).","وفي لفظ:","((نعم، وجدته في غمرات من النار فأخرجته إلى ضحضاح))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٦٢٠٨)، ومسلم (٣٥٧ :٢٠٩).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب تخفيف العذاب لأبي طالب بشفاعة النبي ﷺ","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6208) and Muslim (357 :209).","chapter_en":"The Punishment of Abū Ṭālib Will Be Lightened through the Intercession of the Prophet ﷺ","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-ʿAbbās ibn ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib asked: “O Messenger of Allah, have you benefited Abū Ṭālib in any way? He used to protect you and become angry on your behalf.” He replied: “Yes. He is in a shallow portion of the Fire. Were it not for me, he would have been in the lowest depth of the Fire.”","In another wording: “Yes. I found him in the depths of the Fire and brought him out to a shallow portion of it.”"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["قوله: “غمرات” واحدتها غمرة، وهي المعظم من الشيء."],"en":["The word “ghamarāt”, singular ghamrah, means the deep or overwhelming part of something."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6208},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":357}]},{"num":16479,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أنس بن مالك، عن النبي ﷺ قال:","((يقول الله تعالى لأهون أهل النار عذابًا يوم القيامة: لو أن لك ما في الأرض من شيء أكنت تفتدي به؟ فيقول: نعم، فيقول: أردت منك أهون من هذا، وأنت في صلب آدم: أن لا تشرك بي شيئًا، فأبيت إلا أن تشرك بي))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٦٥٥٧)، ومسلم (٢٨٠٥).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب تمني أهل النار الفداء بكل ما في الأرض والخروج من النار","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6557) and Muslim (2805).","chapter_en":"The People of the Fire Will Wish to Ransom Themselves with Everything on Earth and Escape the Fire","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Allah, the Exalted, will say to the person receiving the lightest punishment among the people of the Fire on the Day of Resurrection: ‘If you possessed everything on earth, would you ransom yourself with it?’ He will say: ‘Yes.’ Allah will say: ‘I asked of you something easier than that while you were still in the loins of Ādam: that you should not associate anything with Me, but you refused except to associate partners with Me.’”"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["علق الحافظ ابن حجر على قوله: “وأنت في صلب آدم” فيه إشارة إلى قوله تعالى:","﴿وَإِذْ أَخَذَ رَبُّكَ مِنْ بَنِي آدَمَ مِنْ ظُهُورِهِمْ ذُرِّيَّتَهُمْ وَأَشْهَدَهُمْ عَلَى أَنْفُسِهِمْ أَلَسْتُ بِرَبِّكُمْ قَالُوا بَلَىٰ شَهِدْنَا أَنْ تَقُولُوا يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ إِنَّا كُنَّا عَنْ هَٰذَا غَافِلِينَ﴾ [الأعراف: ١٧٢].","انظر: فتح الباري (٣٦٩/٦)."],"en":["Al-Ḥāfiẓ Ibn Ḥajar commented that the words:","“while you were in the loins of Ādam”","allude to the statement of Allah, the Exalted:","“And when your Lord took from the children of Ādam, from their loins, their descendants and made them testify concerning themselves: ‘Am I not your Lord?’ They said: ‘Yes, we testify,’ lest you should say on the Day of Resurrection, ‘Indeed, we were unaware of this.’”","[al-Aʿrāf 7:172]","See: Fatḥ al-Bārī (6/369)."]},"intro":{"ar":["قال اللّٰه تعالى:","﴿إِنَّ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا لَوْ أَنَّ لَهُمْ مَا فِي الْأَرْضِ جَمِيعًا وَمِثْلَهُ مَعَهُ لِيَفْتَدُوا بِهِ مِنْ عَذَابِ يَوْمِ الْقِيَامَةِ مَا تُقُبِّلَ مِنْهُمْ وَلَهُمْ عَذَابٌ أَلِيمٌ﴾ [المائدة: ٣٦]."],"en":["Allah, the Exalted, says:","“Indeed, those who disbelieve—even if they possessed everything on earth and another equal amount with it to ransom themselves from the punishment of the Day of Resurrection, it would not be accepted from them, and they will have a painful punishment.”","[al-Māʾidah 5:36]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6557},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2805}]},{"num":16480,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أنس بن مالك أن نبي اللّٰه ﷺ كان يقول:","((يجاء بالكافر يوم القيامة، فيقال له: أرأيت لو كان لك ملء الأرض ذهبًا أكنت تفتدي به؟ فيقول: نعم، فيقال له: قد كنت سئلت ما هو أيسر من ذلك)).","وفي رواية:","((فيقال له: كذبت، قد سئلت ما هو أيسر من ذلك))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٦٥٣٨)، ومسلم (٥٣-٥٢ :٢٨٠٥).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب تمني أهل النار الفداء بكل ما في الأرض والخروج من النار","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6538) and Muslim (52-53 :2805).","chapter_en":"The People of the Fire Will Wish to Ransom Themselves with Everything on Earth and Escape the Fire","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Prophet of Allah ﷺ used to say: “A disbeliever will be brought on the Day of Resurrection and asked: ‘If you possessed enough gold to fill the earth, would you ransom yourself with it?’ He will reply: ‘Yes.’ It will be said to him: ‘You were asked for something far easier than that.’”","In another narration: “It will be said to him: ‘You have lied. You were asked for something far easier than that.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6538},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":53}]},{"num":16481,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي أمامة الباهلي قال: سمعت رسول اللّٰه ﷺ يقول: (( بينا أنا نائم إذ أتاني رجلان فأخذا بضبعي فأتيا بي جبلا وعرا فقالا لي: اصعد حتى إذا كنت في سواء الجبل فإذا أنا بصوت شديد فقلت: ما هذه الأصوات؟ قال: هذا عواء أهل النار، ثم انطلق بي فإذا أنا بقوم معلقين بعراقيبهم مشققة أشداقهم تسيل أشداقهم دما، فقلت: من هؤلاء؟ قال: هؤلاء الذين يفطرون قبل تحلة صومهم، ثم انطلق بي فإذا بقوم أشد شيء انتفاخا وأنتنه ريحا وأسوأه منظرا، فقلت: من هؤلاء؟ قيل: الزانون والزواني، ثم انطلق بي فإذا بنساء تنهشن ثديهن الحيات قلت: ما بال هؤلاء؟ قيل: هؤلاء يمنعن أولادهن ألبانهن… )) الحديث."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه ابن خزيمة (١٩٨٦)، وعنه ابن حبان (٧٤٩١)، والحاكم (١٥٦٨)، وعنه البيهقي (٤/٢١٦).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب تنوع العذاب في النار حسب الجرائم","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Ibn Khuzaymah (1986); through him by Ibn Ḥibbān (7491); al-Ḥākim (1568); and through him by al-Bayhaqī (4/216).","chapter_en":"The Different Forms of Punishment in the Fire According to the Crimes Committed","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Umāmah al-Bāhilī said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “While I was sleeping, two men came to me, took hold of me by my upper arms, and brought me to a rugged mountain. They said to me, ‘Climb.’ When I reached the middle of the mountain, I suddenly heard a terrible sound. I said, ‘What are these sounds?’ He said, ‘This is the howling of the people of the Fire.’ “Then I was taken onward, and suddenly I came upon people suspended by their Achilles tendons, with the corners of their mouths torn open and blood flowing from their mouths. I said, ‘Who are these?’ He said, ‘These are those who break their fast before the proper time for ending their fast.’","“Then I was taken onward, and suddenly I came upon people who were extremely swollen, with the foulest odor and the most horrible appearance. I said, ‘Who are these?’ It was said, ‘The male and female adulterers.’ “Then I was taken onward, and suddenly I came upon women whose breasts were being bitten by snakes. I said, ‘What is the matter with these women?’ It was said, ‘These are women who withheld their milk from their children…’” The ḥadīth continues."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ابن_خزیمہ","label":"ابن خزيمة","number":1986},{"key":"عنہ_ابن_حبان","label":"عنه ابن حبان","number":7491},{"key":"عنہ_البیہقی","label":"عنه البيهقي","number":4},{"key":"ibnhibban","label":"صحيح ابن حبان (التقاسيم والأنواع)","number":3019,"n":3016},{"key":"hakim","label":"المستدرك على الصحيحين","number":1568,"n":1557}]},{"num":16482,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((ضرس الكافر - أو ناب الكافر - مثل أحد، وغلظ جلده مسيرة ثلاث))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٢٨٥١).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب في عظم أهل النار وغلظ أجسامهم حسب أعمالهم وجرائمهم في الدنيا","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2851).","chapter_en":"The Enormous Size and Thickness of the Bodies of the People of the Fire According to Their Deeds and Crimes in This World","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The molar tooth—or canine tooth—of the disbeliever will be like Mount Uḥud, and the thickness of his skin will be a journey of three days.”"]},"intro":{"ar":["قال الله تعالى:","﴿إِنَّ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا بِآيَاتِنَا سَوْفَ نُصْلِيهِمْ نَارًا كُلَّمَا نَضِجَتْ جُلُودُهُمْ بَدَّلْنَاهُمْ جُلُودًا غَيْرَهَا لِيَذُوقُوا الْعَذَابَ إِنَّ اللَّهَ كَانَ عَزِيزًا حَكِيمًا﴾ [النساء: ٥٦].","أي تبدل جلودهم لأن الإحساس بالألم مرتبط بالجلود دون اللحوم.","وقد جاء وصف جلود الكفار في النار في الحديث:"],"en":["Allah, the Exalted, says:","“Indeed, those who disbelieve in Our signs, We will burn them in a Fire. Whenever their skins are completely burned, We will replace them with other skins so that they may taste the punishment. Indeed, Allah is Almighty, All-Wise.”","[al-Nisāʾ 4:56]","That is, their skins will be replaced because the sensation of pain is connected to the skin rather than the flesh.","The description of the skins of the disbelievers in the Fire has also been mentioned in the hadiths:"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2851}]},{"num":16483,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة عن النبي ﷺ قال:","((ما بين منكبي الكافر في النار مسيرة ثلاثة أيام للراكب المسرع))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٦٥٥١)، ومسلم (٢٨٥٢).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب في عظم أهل النار وغلظ أجسامهم حسب أعمالهم وجرائمهم في الدنيا","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6551) and Muslim (2852).","chapter_en":"The Enormous Size and Thickness of the Bodies of the People of the Fire According to Their Deeds and Crimes in This World","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The distance between the two shoulders of the disbeliever in the Fire will be a journey of three days for a swift rider.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6551},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2852}]},{"num":16484,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة، عن النبي ﷺ قال:","((إن غلظ جلد الكافر اثنان وأربعون ذراعًا، وإن ضرسه مثل أحد، وإن مجلسه من جهنم كما بين مكة والمدينة))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الترمذي (٢٥٧٧) واللفظ له، وابن أبي عاصم في السنة (٦١٠)، وابن حبان (٧٤٨٦)، والحاكم (٥٩٥/٤)، والبيهقي في الأسماء والصفات (٧٤٣).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب في عظم أهل النار وغلظ أجسامهم حسب أعمالهم وجرائمهم في الدنيا","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (2577), whose wording this is, Ibn Abī ʿĀṣim in al-Sunnah (610), Ibn Ḥibbān (7486), al-Ḥākim (4/595), and al-Bayhaqī in al-Asmāʾ wa-l-Ṣifāt (743).","chapter_en":"The Enormous Size and Thickness of the Bodies of the People of the Fire According to Their Deeds and Crimes in This World","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The thickness of the disbeliever’s skin will be forty-two cubits, his molar tooth will be like Mount Uḥud, and the space he occupies in Hell will be like the distance between Makkah and Madīnah.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"tirmidhi","label":"الترمذي","number":2577},{"key":"ابن_ابی_عاصم/السنہ","label":"ابن أبي عاصم في السنة","number":610},{"key":"ibnhibban","label":"ابن حبان","number":7486},{"key":"hakim","label":"الحاكم","number":595},{"key":"البیہقی/الاسما_والصفات","label":"البيهقي في الأسماء والصفات","number":743},{"key":"sh9270","label":"الأسماء والصفات للبيهقي","number":743,"n":742}]},{"num":16485,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((ضرس الكافر يوم القيامة مثل أحد، وفخذه مثل البيضاء، ومقعده من النار مسيرة ثلاث مثل الربذة))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (٢٥٧٨).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب في عظم أهل النار وغلظ أجسامهم حسب أعمالهم وجرائمهم في الدنيا","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (2578).","chapter_en":"The Enormous Size and Thickness of the Bodies of the People of the Fire According to Their Deeds and Crimes in This World","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The molar tooth of the disbeliever on the Day of Resurrection will be like Mount Uḥud, his thigh will be like al-Bayḍāʾ, and the space he occupies in the Fire will be a journey of three days, like the distance to al-Rabadhah.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"tirmidhi","label":"الترمذي","number":2578}]},{"num":16486,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((ضرس الكافر يوم القيامة مثل أحد، وعرض جلده سبعون ذراعًا، وفخذه مثل ورقان، ومقعده من النار مثل ما بيني وبين الربذة))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (٨٣٤٥).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب في عظم أهل النار وغلظ أجسامهم حسب أعمالهم وجرائمهم في الدنيا","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (8345).","chapter_en":"The Enormous Size and Thickness of the Bodies of the People of the Fire According to Their Deeds and Crimes in This World","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The molar tooth of the disbeliever on the Day of Resurrection will be like Mount Uḥud, the width of his skin will be seventy cubits, his thigh will be like Mount Warqān, and the space he occupies in the Fire will be like the distance between here and al-Rabadhah.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":8345,"n":8345}]},{"num":16487,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((ضرس الكافر مثل أحد، وفخذه مثل البيضاء، ومقعده من النار كما بين قديد ومكة، وكثافة جلده اثنان وأربعون ذراعًا بذراع الجبار))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (٨٤١٠)، وابن أبي عاصم في السنة (٦١١).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب في عظم أهل النار وغلظ أجسامهم حسب أعمالهم وجرائمهم في الدنيا","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (8410) and Ibn Abī ʿĀṣim in al-Sunnah (611).","chapter_en":"The Enormous Size and Thickness of the Bodies of the People of the Fire According to Their Deeds and Crimes in This World","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The molar tooth of the disbeliever will be like Mount Uḥud, his thigh will be like al-Bayḍāʾ, the space he occupies in the Fire will be like the distance between Qudayd and Makkah, and the thickness of his skin will be forty-two cubits measured by the cubit of the jabbār.”"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["قوله: “بذراع الجبار” المقصود به بذراع الرجل الطويل الذي لا تبلغه أيدي الناس من أجل إفراطه في الطول، وليس المقصود به الرب تبارك وتعالى، فإن الحديث ليس من أحاديث الصفات على الصحيح من أقوال أهل العلم، وفيما يلي ذكر جملة من أقوال العلماء المحققين في ذلك:","قال الحافظ أبو بكر بن إسحاق - شيخ الحاكم -: “معنى قوله: بذراع الجبار: أي جبار من جبايرة الآدميين ممن كان في القرون الأولى ممن كان أعظم خلقًا وأطول أعضاء وذراعًا من الناس”. ذكره الحاكم في المستدرك.","وقال ابن قتيبة في تأويل مختلف الحديث: “إن لهذا الحديث مخرجًا حسنًا إن كان النبي ﷺ أراده، وهو أن يكون الجبار ههنا الملك، قال اللّٰه تبارك وتعالى: ﴿وَمَا أَنْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ بِجَبَّارٍ﴾ [سورة ق: ٤٥] أي بملك مسلط، والجبابرة: الملوك، وهذا كما يقول الناس: هو كذا وكذا ذراعًا بذراع الملك، يريدون: بالذراع الأكبر، وأحسبه ملك من ملوك العجم، كان تام الذراع، فتنسب إليه”.","وقال الذهبي: “ليس ذا من الصفات في شيء”."],"en":["Regarding the phrase “by the cubit of the jabbār,” the author explains that what is intended is the cubit of an exceptionally tall man whose height is beyond the reach of ordinary people. It is not intended as a reference to the Lord, Blessed and Exalted.","According to what the author considers the sounder view among the scholars, this hadith is not among the hadiths concerning the Divine Attributes. He then cites a number of statements from verifying scholars concerning this matter:","Al-Ḥāfiẓ Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq, the teacher of al-Ḥākim, said:","“The meaning of his statement, ‘by the cubit of the jabbār,’ is: the cubit of one of the mighty men among human beings from the earlier generations, one who was greater in physical build and whose limbs and forearms were longer than those of ordinary people.”","Al-Ḥākim mentioned this in al-Mustadrak.","Ibn Qutaybah said in Taʾwīl Mukhtalif al-Ḥadīth:","“This hadith has a sound interpretation, if this is what the Prophet ﷺ intended: that al-jabbār here means a king. Allah, Blessed and Exalted, says:","‘And you are not over them a tyrannical controller.’","[Qāf 50:45]","meaning a ruler imposed over them. The jabābirah are kings. This resembles the way people say: ‘It is such-and-such cubits according to the king’s cubit,’ meaning the larger cubit. I think it referred to one of the kings of Persia who possessed an unusually long cubit, and the measure came to be attributed to him.”","Al-Dhahabī said:","“This has nothing to do with the Divine Attributes.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ابن_ابی_عاصم/السنہ","label":"ابن أبي عاصم في السنة","number":611},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":8410,"n":8410}]},{"num":16488,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن يزيد بن حيان التيمي قال: انطلقت أنا وحصين بن سبرة وعمر بن مسلم إلى زيد بن أرقم، وحدثنا زيد في مجلسه ذلك قال: إن الرجل من أهل النار ليعظم للنار حتى يكون الضرس من أضراسه كأحد."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (١٩٢٦٦، ١٩٢٦٥).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب في عظم أهل النار وغلظ أجسامهم حسب أعمالهم وجرائمهم في الدنيا","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (19266, 19265).","chapter_en":"The Enormous Size and Thickness of the Bodies of the People of the Fire According to Their Deeds and Crimes in This World","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Yazīd ibn Ḥayyān al-Taymī narrated: Ḥuṣayn ibn Sabrah, ʿUmar ibn Muslim, and I went to Zayd ibn Arqam. During that gathering, Zayd narrated to us: “A man from among the people of the Fire will be made so enormous for the Fire that one of his molar teeth will be like Mount Uḥud.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":19266,"n":19266}]},{"num":16489,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن مجاهد قال: قال ابن عباس: أتدري ما سعة جهنم؟ قلت: لا، قال: أجل، واللّٰه ما تدري، إن بين شحمة أذن أحدهم وبين عاتقه مسيرة سبعين خريفًا، تجري فيها أودية القيح والدم، قلت: أنهارًا؟ قال: لا، بل أودية، ثم قال: أتدرون ما سعة جهنم؟ قلت: لا، قال: أجل، والله ما ندري، حدثتني عائشة أنها سألت رسول الله ﷺ عن قوله:","﴿وَالْأَرْضُ جَمِيعًا قَبْضَتُهُ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ وَالسَّمَاوَاتُ مَطْوِيَّاتٌ بِيَمِينِهِ﴾ [الزمر: ٦٧]","فأين الناس يومئذ يا رسول الله؟ قال:","((هم على جسر جهنم))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (٢٤٨٥٦)، والحاكم (٤٣٦/٢)، والبغوي في شرح السنة (٤٤١٥).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب في عظم أهل النار وغلظ أجسامهم حسب أعمالهم وجرائمهم في الدنيا","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (24856), al-Ḥākim (2/436), and al-Baghawī in Sharḥ al-Sunnah (4415).","chapter_en":"The Enormous Size and Thickness of the Bodies of the People of the Fire According to Their Deeds and Crimes in This World","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Mujāhid narrated: Ibn ʿAbbās said: “Do you know how vast Hell is?” I replied: “No.” He said: “Indeed, by Allah, you do not know. The distance between the earlobe of one of its inhabitants and his shoulder will be a journey of seventy years, and through that space valleys of pus and blood will flow.” I asked: “Rivers?” He replied: “No, rather valleys.” Then he said: “Do you know how vast Hell is?” I replied: “No.” He said: “Indeed, by Allah, we do not know. ʿĀ’ishah narrated to me that she asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ concerning the statement of Allah: ‘The whole earth will be in His Grip on the Day of Resurrection, and the heavens will be folded in His Right Hand.’","[al-Zumar 39:67] ‘Where will the people be at that time, O Messenger of Allah?’” He replied: “They will be upon the bridge over Hell.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"البغوی/شرح_السنہ","label":"البغوي في شرح السنة","number":4415},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":24856,"n":24856},{"key":"hakim","label":"المستدرك على الصحيحين","number":3630,"n":3617},{"key":"sharhsunna","label":"شرح السنة للبغوي","number":4415,"n":4329}]},{"num":16490,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عائشة قالت: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((رأيت جهنم يحطم بعضها بعضًا، ورأيت عمرًا يجر قصبه، وهو أول من سيب السوائب))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٤٦٢٤)، ومسلم (٣:٩٠١).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب رؤية النبي ﷺ عمرو بن عامر الخزاعي في النار وهو أول من سيب السوائب","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4624) and Muslim (3:901).","chapter_en":"The Prophet ﷺ Saw ʿAmr ibn ʿĀmir al-Khuzāʿī in the Fire; He Was the First to Set Free the Sāʾibah Animals","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":9,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀ’ishah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I saw Hell crushing its parts against one another, and I saw ʿAmr dragging his intestines. He was the first to set free the sāʾibah animals.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":4624},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":3}]},{"num":16491,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((رأيت عمرو بن عامر الخزاعي يجر قصبه في النار، كان أول من سيب السوائب))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٤٦٢٣)، ومسلم (٥١ :٢٨٥٦).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب رؤية النبي ﷺ عمرو بن عامر الخزاعي في النار وهو أول من سيب السوائب","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4623) and Muslim (51 :2856).","chapter_en":"The Prophet ﷺ Saw ʿAmr ibn ʿĀmir al-Khuzāʿī in the Fire; He Was the First to Set Free the Sāʾibah Animals","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":9,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I saw ʿAmr ibn ʿĀmir al-Khuzāʿī dragging his intestines in the Fire. He was the first to set free the sāʾibah animals.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":4623},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":51}]},{"num":16492,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((رأيت عمرو بن لحي بن قمعة بن خندف أبا بني كعب هؤلاء، يجر قصبه في النار))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٢٨٥٦).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب رؤية النبي ﷺ عمرو بن عامر الخزاعي في النار وهو أول من سيب السوائب","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2856).","chapter_en":"The Prophet ﷺ Saw ʿAmr ibn ʿĀmir al-Khuzāʿī in the Fire; He Was the First to Set Free the Sāʾibah Animals","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":9,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I saw ʿAmr ibn Luḥayy ibn Qamaʿah ibn Khindif, the forefather of these Banū Kaʿb, dragging his intestines in the Fire.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2856}]},{"num":16493,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((عرضت علي النار، فرأيت فيها ابن قمعة بن خندف، وهو يجر قصبه في النار، وهو أول من سيب السائبة، وغير عهد إبراهيم، وأشبه من رأيت به أكثم بن الجون)).","قال: فقال أكثم: يا رسول اللّه أيضُرُّني شبهه؟ قال:","((لا، إنك مسلم وهو كافر))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو يعلى (٦١٢١).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب رؤية النبي ﷺ عمرو بن عامر الخزاعي في النار وهو أول من سيب السوائب","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abū Yaʿlā (6121).","chapter_en":"The Prophet ﷺ Saw ʿAmr ibn ʿĀmir al-Khuzāʿī in the Fire; He Was the First to Set Free the Sāʾibah Animals","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":9,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The Fire was shown to me, and in it I saw Ibn Qamaʿah ibn Khindif dragging his intestines in the Fire. He was the first to set free the sāʾibah animal and the one who altered the covenant and religion of Ibrāhīm. The person I have seen who most resembles him is Aktham ibn al-Jawn.” Aktham asked: “O Messenger of Allah, will my resemblance to him harm me?” He replied: “No. You are a Muslim, while he was a disbeliever.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ابو_یعلی","label":"أبو يعلى","number":6121},{"key":"sh12520","label":"مسند أبي يعلى","number":6121,"n":6127}]},{"num":16494,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن قيس بن عباد قال: قلنا لعمار: أرأيت قتالكم، أرأيًا رأيتموه؟ فإن الرأي يخطئ ويصيب، أو عهدًا عهده إليكم رسول اللّٰه ﷺ؟ فقال: ما عهد إلينا رسول اللّٰه ﷺ شيئًا لم يعهده إلى الناس كافة، وقال: إن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال:","((إن في أمتي اثني عشر منافقًا لا يدخلون الجنة، ولا يجدون ريحها، حتى يلج الجمل في سم الخياط، ثمانية منهم تكفيكهم الدبيلة، سراج من النار يظهر في أكتافهم، حتى ينجم من صدورهم))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٢٧٧٩).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أن المنافقين في النار","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2779).","chapter_en":"The Hypocrites Will Be in the Fire","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Qays ibn ʿUbād narrated: We asked ʿAmmār: “Regarding your fighting, was it based on an opinion you formed? For opinion may be right or wrong. Or was it based on a covenant that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ specifically entrusted to you?” He replied: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not entrust us with anything that he did not entrust to the people generally.” He then said that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Among my Ummah are twelve hypocrites who will neither enter Paradise nor smell its fragrance until a camel passes through the eye of a needle.","For eight of them, al-Dubaylah itself will be sufficient: a blazing fire that will appear in their shoulders and emerge through their chests.”"]},"intro":{"ar":["قال الله تعالى:","﴿بَشِّرِ الْمُنَافِقِينَ بِأَنَّ لَهُمْ عَذَابًا أَلِيمًا﴾ [النساء: ١٣٨].","وقال:","﴿إِنَّ اللَّهَ جَامِعُ الْمُنَافِقِينَ وَالْكَافِرِينَ فِي جَهَنَّمَ جَمِيعًا﴾ [النساء: ١٤٠].","وقال تعالى:","﴿إِنَّ الْمُنَافِقِينَ فِي الدَّرْكِ الْأَسْفَلِ مِنَ النَّارِ﴾ [النساء: ١٤٥].","وقال تعالى:","﴿وَعَدَ اللَّهُ الْمُنَافِقِينَ وَالْمُنَافِقَاتِ وَالْكُفَّارَ نَارَ جَهَنَّمَ﴾ [التوبة: ٦٨]."],"en":["Allah, the Exalted, says:","“Give the hypocrites tidings that for them is a painful punishment.”","[al-Nisāʾ 4:138]","And He says:","“Indeed, Allah will gather the hypocrites and the disbelievers all together in Hell.”","[al-Nisāʾ 4:140]","And He, the Exalted, says:","“Indeed, the hypocrites will be in the lowest depths of the Fire.”","[al-Nisāʾ 4:145]","And He, the Exalted, says:","“Allah has promised the hypocrite men and hypocrite women, and the disbelievers, the Fire of Hell.”","[al-Tawbah 9:68]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2779}]},{"num":16495,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة، عن النبي ﷺ قال:","((بينا أنا قائم إذا زمرة، حتى إذا عرفتهم خرج رجل من بيني وبينهم، فقال: هلم، فقلت: أين؟ قال: إلى النار والله، قلت: وما شأنهم؟ قال: إنهم ارتدوا بعدك على أدبارهم القهقرى. ثم إذا زمرة، حتى إذا عرفتهم خرج رجل من بيني وبينهم، فقال: هلم، قلت أين؟ قال: إلى النار والله، قلت: ما شأنهم؟ قال: إنهم ارتدوا بعدك على أدبارهم القهقرى، فلا أراه يخلص منهم إلا مثل همل النعم))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (٦٥٨٧).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ذهاب المرتدين إلى النار","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6587).","chapter_en":"The Apostates Will Be Taken to the Fire","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":11,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “While I am standing, a group will appear. When I recognize them, a man will come out from between me and them and say: ‘Come!’ I will ask: ‘Where?’ He will say: ‘To the Fire, by Allah.’ I will ask: ‘What is the matter with them?’ He will say: ‘They turned back on their heels after you.’ Then another group will appear. When I recognize them, a man will come out from between me and them and say: ‘Come!’","I will ask: ‘Where?’ He will say: ‘To the Fire, by Allah.’ I will ask: ‘What is the matter with them?’ He will say: ‘They turned back on their heels after you.’ I do not think that any of them will escape except as few as stray camels.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6587}]},{"num":16496,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبد اللّه بن عمر، أن رسول اللّه ﷺ قال:","((عذبت امرأة في هرة سجنتها حتى ماتت، فدخلت فيها النار، لا هي أطعمتها ولا سقتها إذ حبستها، ولا هي تركتها تأكل من خشاش الأرض))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٣٤٨٢)، ومسلم (٢٢٤٢).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب أن امرأة دخلت النار في هرة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3482) and Muslim (2242).","chapter_en":"A Woman Entered the Fire Because of a Cat","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":12,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A woman was punished because of a cat that she imprisoned until it died, and because of it she entered the Fire. She neither fed it nor gave it water while she kept it confined, nor did she release it to eat from the creatures of the earth.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":3482},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2242}]},{"num":16497,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة، عن رسول اللٰه ﷺ قال:","((دخلت امرأة النار في هرة ربطتها، فلا هي أطعمتها، ولا هي أرسلتها تأكل من خشاش الأرض، حتى ماتت هزلًا)).","قال الزهري: ذلك، لئلا يتكل رجل، ولا ييأس رجل."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٢٦١٩).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أن امرأة دخلت النار في هرة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2619).","chapter_en":"A Woman Entered the Fire Because of a Cat","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":12,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A woman entered the Fire because of a cat that she tied up. She neither fed it nor released it to eat from the creatures of the earth, until it died from emaciation.” Al-Zuhrī said: “This is so that no person becomes complacent, and no person falls into despair.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2619}]},{"num":16498,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر بن عبد الله، قال: كسفت الشمس على عهد رسول الله ﷺ في يوم شديد الحر، فصلى رسول اللّٰه ﷺ بأصحابه، وفيه: ثم قال:","((إنه عرض علي كل شيء تولجونه، فعرضت علي الجنة، حتى لو تناولت منها قطفًا أخذته - أو قال: تناولت منها قطفًا - فقصرت يدي عنه، وعرضت علي النار، فرأيت فيها امرأة من بني إسرائيل تعذب في هرة لها، ربطتها فلم تطعمها، ولم تدعها تأكل من خشاش الأرض، ورأيت أبا ثمامة عمرو بن مالك يجر قصبه في النار…)).","الحديث."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٩ :٩٠٤).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أن امرأة دخلت النار في هرة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (9 :904).","chapter_en":"A Woman Entered the Fire Because of a Cat","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":12,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: The sun was eclipsed during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on an intensely hot day, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ led his Companions in prayer. In the hadith, he later said: “Everything that you will enter was shown to me. Paradise was shown to me, to the point that if I had reached for one of its clusters, I would have taken it—or he said: I reached for one of its clusters, but my hand fell short of it.","The Fire was also shown to me, and I saw in it a woman from the Children of Israel being punished because of a cat she owned. She had tied it up, neither feeding it nor allowing it to eat from the creatures of the earth. And I saw Abū Thumāmah, ʿAmr ibn Mālik, dragging his intestines in the Fire…” The hadith continues."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":9}]},{"num":16499,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر بن عبد اللّه قال: انكسفت الشمس في عهد رسول اللّٰه ﷺ يوم مات إبراهيم ابن رسول اللّه ﷺ فذكر الحديث، وفيه:","((ما من شيء توعدونه إلا قد رأيته في صلاتي هذه، لقد جيء بالنار، وذلكم حين رأيتموني تأخرت، مخافة أن يصيبني من لفحها، وحتى رأيت فيها صاحب المحجن يجر قصبه في النار، كان يسرق الحاج بمحجنه، فإن فطن له قال: إنما تعلق بمحجني، وإن غفل عنه ذهب به، وحتى رأيت فيها صاحبة الهرة التي ربطتها فلم تطعمها، ولم تدعها تأكل من خشاش الأرض، حتى ماتت جوعًا، ثم جيء بالجنة، وذلكم حين رأيتموني تقدمت حتى قمت في مقامي، ولقد مددت يدي وأنا أريد أن أتناول من ثمرها لتنظروا إليه، ثم بدا لي أن لا أفعل، فما من شيء توعدونه إلا قد رأيته في صلاتي هذه))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (١٠ :٩٠٤).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أن امرأة دخلت النار في هرة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (10 :904).","chapter_en":"A Woman Entered the Fire Because of a Cat","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":12,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: The sun was eclipsed during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day his son Ibrāhīm died. In the hadith, he said: “There is nothing you have been promised except that I saw it during this prayer. The Fire was brought before me. That was when you saw me step backward, fearing that some of its scorching heat might reach me. I saw in it the man with the hooked staff dragging his intestines in the Fire. He used to steal from the pilgrims with his hooked staff. If he was noticed, he would say: ‘It merely became caught on my staff,’ but if the person did not notice, he would take it away.","I also saw in it the woman with the cat, who tied it up, neither feeding it nor allowing it to eat from the creatures of the earth, until it died of hunger. Then Paradise was brought before me. That was when you saw me move forward until I stood in my place. I stretched out my hand intending to take some of its fruit so that you could look at it, but then it occurred to me not to do so. There is nothing you have been promised except that I saw it during this prayer.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":10}]},{"num":16500,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبد اللّٰه بن عمرو قال: انكسفت الشمس على عهد رسول اللّٰه ﷺ - فذكر الحديث - ثم قال:","((لقد عرضت علي الجنة حتى لو شئت لتعاطيت قطفًا من قطوفها، وعرضت علي النار حتى جعلت أتقيها حتى خشيت أن تغشاكم، فجعلت أقول: ألم تعدني أن لا تعذبهم وأنا فيهم، رب ألم تعدني أن لا تعذبهم وهم يستغفرونك)).","قال:","((فرأيت فيها الحميرية السوداء صاحبة الهرة، كانت حبستها، فلم تطعمها ولم تسقها، ولم تتركها تأكل من خشاش الأرض، فرأيتها كلما أدبرت نهشت في النار. ورأيت فيها صاحب بدنتي رسول الله ﷺ أخا دعدع، يدفع في النار بقضيبين ذي شعبتين. ورأيت صاحب المحجن، فرأيته في النار على محجنه متوكئًا))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود (١١٩٤)، والنسائي (١٤٨٢)، وأحمد (٦٤٨٣، ٦٧٦٣)، وابن خزيمة (١٣٩٣)، والحاكم (٣٢٩/١)، وابن خزيمة (١٣٩٢)، وابن حبان (٢٨٣٨). واللفظ له.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أن امرأة دخلت النار في هرة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (1194), al-Nasā’ī (1482), Aḥmad (6483, 6763), Ibn Khuzaymah (1393), al-Ḥākim (1/329), Ibn Khuzaymah (1392), and Ibn Ḥibbān (2838), whose wording this is.","chapter_en":"A Woman Entered the Fire Because of a Cat","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":12,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr narrated: The sun was eclipsed during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He then mentioned the hadith and said: “Paradise was shown to me, to the point that, had I wished, I could have reached for one of its clusters. The Fire was also shown to me, and I kept trying to shield myself from it until I feared that it might engulf you. I began saying: ‘Did You not promise me that You would not punish them while I am among them? My Lord, did You not promise me that You would not punish them while they seek Your forgiveness?’”","He continued: “I saw in it the black Ḥimyarī woman who owned the cat. She had imprisoned it, neither feeding it nor giving it drink, nor allowing it to eat from the creatures of the earth. I saw that whenever she turned away, it would tear at her in the Fire. I saw in it the man responsible for the sacrificial camels of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, the brother of Daʿdaʿ, being driven in the Fire with two forked rods. And I saw the man with the hooked staff; I saw him in the Fire leaning upon his hooked staff.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"abudawud","label":"أبو داود","number":1194},{"key":"nasai","label":"النسائي","number":1482},{"key":"ابن_خزیمہ","label":"ابن خزيمة","number":1393},{"key":"hakim","label":"الحاكم","number":329},{"key":"ابن_خزیمہ","label":"ابن خزيمة","number":1392},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":6483,"n":6483},{"key":"ibnhibban","label":"صحيح ابن حبان (التقاسيم والأنواع)","number":7089,"n":7089}]},{"num":16501,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن ابن عباس قال: قال النبي ﷺ:","((أريت النار فإذا أكثر أهلها النساء، يكفرن)).","قيل: أيكفرن بالله؟ قال:","((يكفرن العشير، ويكفرن الإحسان، لو أحسنت إلى إحداهن الدهر، ثم رأت منك شيئًا، قالت: ما رأيت منك خيرًا قط))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك في الكسوف (٢) والبخاري (١٠٥٢)، ومسلم (٩٠٧).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب أكثر أهل النار النساء","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by Mālik in al-Kusūf (2), al-Bukhārī (1052), and Muslim (907).","chapter_en":"Most of the People of the Fire Are Women","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":13,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿAbbās narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “I was shown the Fire, and I saw that most of its inhabitants were women because they are ungrateful.” It was asked: “Do they disbelieve in Allah?” He replied: “They are ungrateful to their husbands and ungrateful for kindness. If you were good to one of them throughout an entire lifetime, then she saw something from you that displeased her, she might say: ‘I have never seen any good from you at all.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"malik/الکسوف","label":"مالك في الكسوف","number":2},{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":1052},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":907}]},{"num":16502,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن زينب امرأة عبد اللّٰه بن مسعود قالت: خطبنا رسول اللّٰه ﷺ فقال:","((يا معشر النساء تصدقن ولو من حليكن، فإنكن أكثر أهل جهنم يوم القيامة))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (١٤٦٦)، ومسلم (١٠٠٠)، ورواه الترمذي (٦٣٥)، وابن ماجه (١٨٣٤)، وأحمد (٢٧٠٤٨)، وصححه ابن حبان (٤٢٤٨).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب أكثر أهل النار النساء","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (1466) and Muslim (1000). It was also narrated by al-Tirmidhī (635), Ibn Mājah (1834), Aḥmad (27048), and authenticated by Ibn Ḥibbān (4248).","chapter_en":"Most of the People of the Fire Are Women","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":13,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Zaynab, the wife of ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd, narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us and said: “O women, give in charity, even from your jewelry, for you will be the majority of the people of Hell on the Day of Resurrection.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":1466},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":1000},{"key":"tirmidhi","label":"الترمذي","number":635},{"key":"ibnmajah","label":"ابن ماجه","number":1834},{"key":"صححہ_ابن_حبان","label":"صححه ابن حبان","number":4248},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":27048,"n":27048},{"key":"ibnhibban","label":"صحيح ابن حبان (التقاسيم والأنواع)","number":629,"n":629}]},{"num":16503,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي سعيد الخدري قال: خرج رسول اللّٰه ﷺ في أضحى أو في فطر إلى المصلى، فمر على النساء، فقال:","((يا معشر النساء تصدقن، فإني أريتكن أكثر أهل النار)).","فقلن: وبم يا رسول الله؟ قال:","((تكثرن اللعن، وتكفرن العشير…)).","الحديث."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٣٠٤)، ومسلم (٨٠).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب أكثر أهل النار النساء","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (304) and Muslim (80).","chapter_en":"Most of the People of the Fire Are Women","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":13,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to the prayer place on the day of al-Aḍḥā or al-Fiṭr. He passed by the women and said: “O women, give in charity, for I was shown that you are the majority of the people of the Fire.” They asked: “Why is that, O Messenger of Allah?” He replied: “You frequently curse and are ungrateful to your husbands…” The hadith continues."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":304},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":80}]},{"num":16504,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبد الله بن عمر، عن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ أنه قال:","((يا معشر النساء تصدقن، وأكثرن الاستغفار، فإني رأيتكن أكثر أهل النار)).","فقالت امرأة منهن جزلة: وما لنا يا رسول اللّٰه أكثر أهل النار؟ قال:","((تكثرن اللعن، وتكفرن العشير…)).","الحديث."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٧٩).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أكثر أهل النار النساء","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (79).","chapter_en":"Most of the People of the Fire Are Women","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":13,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O women, give in charity and frequently seek forgiveness, for I have seen that you are the majority of the people of the Fire.” An intelligent woman among them asked: “Why is it, O Messenger of Allah, that we are the majority of the people of the Fire?” He replied: “You frequently curse and are ungrateful to your husbands…” The hadith continues."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":79}]},{"num":16505,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر بن عبد اللّٰه قال: شهدت مع رسول اللّٰه ﷺ الصلاة يوم العيد، فبدأ بالصلاة قبل الخطبة بغير أذان ولا إقامة، ثم قام متوكئًا على بلال، فأمر بتقوى الله، وحث على طاعته، ووعظ الناس وذكرهم، ثم مضى حتى أتى النساء، فوعظهن وذكرهن فقال:","((تصدقن، فإن أكثركن حطب جهنم)).","فقامت امرأة من سطة النساء سفعاء الخدين، فقالت: لم يا رسول الله؟ قال:","((لأنكن تكثرن الشكاة، وتكفرن العشير))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٤ :٨٨٥).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أكثر أهل النار النساء","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (4 :885).","chapter_en":"Most of the People of the Fire Are Women","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":13,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: I attended the Eid prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He began with the prayer before the sermon, without adhān or iqāmah. Then he stood leaning upon Bilāl, commanded the people to fear Allah, encouraged them to obey Him, admonished them, and reminded them. Then he went to the women, admonished and reminded them, and said: “Give in charity, for most of you will be fuel for Hell.” A woman from among the ordinary women, whose cheeks were darkened, stood and asked: “Why, O Messenger of Allah?”","He replied: “Because you frequently complain and are ungrateful to your husbands.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":4}]},{"num":16506,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن ابن مسعود، أن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال:","((تصدقن يا معشر النساء، ولو من حليكن، فإنكن أكثر أهل النار)).","فقامت امرأة ليست من علية النساء، فقالت: لم يا رسول الله؟ قال:","((لأنكن تكثرن اللعن، وتكفرن العشير)).","وفي رواية:","((وما رأيت ناقصات عقل ودين أغلب للب الرجال منكن))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (٤١٥٢، ٣٥٦٩)، وأبو يعلى (٥١٤٤، ٥١١٢)، والحاكم (١٩٠/٢).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب أكثر أهل النار النساء","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (4152, 3569), Abū Yaʿlā (5144, 5112), and al-Ḥākim (2/190).","chapter_en":"Most of the People of the Fire Are Women","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":13,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn Masʿūd narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O women, give in charity, even from your jewelry, for you are the majority of the people of the Fire.” A woman who was not from among the prominent women stood and asked: “Why, O Messenger of Allah?” He replied: “Because you frequently curse and are ungrateful to your husbands.”","In another narration: “I have not seen anyone deficient in reason and religion more capable of overcoming the mind of a resolute man than you.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ابو_یعلی","label":"أبو يعلى","number":5144},{"key":"hakim","label":"الحاكم","number":190},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":4152,"n":4152}]},{"num":16507,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبد الرحمن بن شبل قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((إن الفساق هم أهل النار)).","قيل: يا رسول الله، ومن الفساق؟ قال:","((النساء)).","قال رجل: يا رسول الله، أو لسن أمهاتنا وأخواتنا وأزواجنا؟ قال:","((بلى، ولكنهن إذا أعطين لم يشكرن، وإذا ابتلين لم يصبرن))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (١٥٥٣١)، والحاكم (٦٠٤/٤).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب أكثر أهل النار النساء","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (15531) and al-Ḥākim (4/604).","chapter_en":"Most of the People of the Fire Are Women","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":13,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Shibl narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, the defiantly disobedient are the people of the Fire.” It was asked: “O Messenger of Allah, who are the defiantly disobedient?” He replied: “Women.” A man asked: “O Messenger of Allah, are they not our mothers, sisters, and wives?” He replied: “Yes. But when they are given something, they are not grateful, and when they are tested, they are not patient.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":15531,"n":15531},{"key":"hakim","label":"المستدرك على الصحيحين","number":8787,"n":8799}]},{"num":16508,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي موسى الأشعري قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((إذا كان يوم القيامة دفع اللّٰه عز وجل إلى كل مسلم يهوديًا أو نصرانيًا، فيقول: هذا فكاكك من النار))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٢٧٦٧).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فكاك المسلم من الكفار","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2767).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Muslim’s Ransom from among the Disbelievers","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":14,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “On the Day of Resurrection, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will assign to every Muslim a Jew or a Christian and will say: ‘This is your ransom from the Fire.’”"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["قوله: “فكاكك من النار” أي أنت كنت معرضًا لدخول النار، ولكن من أجل اختيارك الإسلام جعل اللّٰه فكاكك في النار يهوديًا أو نصرانيًا (ويلحق بهم عموم الكفار)، فكان ذلك فكاكه من النار."],"en":["Regarding the phrase “your ransom from the Fire,” the author explains:","You were exposed to the possibility of entering the Fire, but because you chose Islam, Allah placed in the Fire in your stead a Jew or a Christian—and the generality of disbelievers is included with them—so that became his ransom from the Fire."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2767}]},{"num":16509,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي موسى الأشعري، عن النبي ﷺ قال:","((لا يموت رجل مسلم إلا أدخل اللّٰه مكانه النار يهوديًا أو نصرانيًا))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٥٠ :٢٧٦٧).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فكاك المسلم من الكفار","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (50 :2767).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Muslim’s Ransom from among the Disbelievers","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":14,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “No Muslim man dies except that Allah admits into the Fire in his place a Jew or a Christian.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":50}]},{"num":16510,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي موسى، عن النبي ﷺ قال:","((يجيء يوم القيامة ناس من المسلمين بذنوب أمثال الجبال، فيغفرها اللّٰه لهم ويضعها على اليهود والنصارى))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٥١ :٢٧٦٧).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فكاك المسلم من الكفار","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (51 :2767).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Muslim’s Ransom from among the Disbelievers","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":14,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Mūsā narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “On the Day of Resurrection, some Muslims will come with sins like mountains. Allah will forgive them and place them upon the Jews and Christians.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":51}]},{"num":16511,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((ما منكم من أحد إلا له منزلان: منزل في الجنة ومنزل في النار. فإذا مات فدخل النار ورث أهل الجنة منزله. فذلك قوله تعالى: ﴿أُولَٰئِكَ هُمُ الْوَارِثُونَ﴾ [المؤمنون: ١٠]))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه ابن ماجه (٤٣٤١)، والبيهقي في الشعب (٣٧٣)، وابن أبي حاتم كما ذكر ابن كثير في تفسيره (٤٦٤/٥).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فكاك المسلم من الكفار","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Ibn Mājah (4341), al-Bayhaqī in al-Shuʿab (373), and Ibn Abī Ḥātim, as cited by Ibn Kathīr in his Tafsīr (5/464).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Muslim’s Ransom from among the Disbelievers","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل النار","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of the Fire","part_no":66,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":14,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is none among you except that he has two dwellings: a dwelling in Paradise and a dwelling in the Fire. If he dies and enters the Fire, the people of Paradise will inherit his dwelling. That is the meaning of the statement of Allah, the Exalted: ‘Those are the inheritors.’ [al-Muʾminūn 23:10]”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ibnmajah","label":"ابن ماجه","number":4341},{"key":"البیہقی/الشعب","label":"البيهقي في الشعب","number":373},{"key":"ابن_ابی_حاتم_کما_ذکر_ابن_کثیر/تفسیرہ","label":"ابن أبي حاتم كما ذكر ابن كثير في تفسيره","number":464}]},{"num":16512,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة، أن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال:","((لو يعلم المؤمن ما عند اللّٰه من العقوبة، ما طمع بجنته أحد، ولو يعلم الكافر ما عند اللّٰه من الرحمة، ما قنط من جنته أحد))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٢٧٥٥).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في شدة عقوبة الله وسعة رحمته","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2755).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Severity of Allah’s Punishment and the Vastness of His Mercy","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة والنار معًا","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise and the Fire Together","part_no":66,"group_no":6,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If the believer knew the full extent of the punishment with Allah, no one would hope for His Paradise. And if the disbeliever knew the full extent of the mercy with Allah, no one would despair of His Paradise.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2755}]},{"num":16513,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أنس بن مالك قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((حفت الجنة بالمكاره، وحفت النار بالشهوات))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٢٨٢٢).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب حفت الجنة بالمكاره وحفت النار بالشهوات","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2822).","chapter_en":"Paradise Is Surrounded by Hardships and the Fire Is Surrounded by Desires","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة والنار معًا","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise and the Fire Together","part_no":66,"group_no":6,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Paradise is surrounded by hardships, and the Fire is surrounded by desires.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2822}]},{"num":16514,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة أن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال:","((حجبت النار بالشهوات، وحجبت الجنة بالمكاره))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٦٤٨٧)، ومسلم (٢٨٢٣).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب حفت الجنة بالمكاره وحفت النار بالشهوات","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6487) and Muslim (2823).","chapter_en":"Paradise Is Surrounded by Hardships and the Fire Is Surrounded by Desires","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة والنار معًا","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise and the Fire Together","part_no":66,"group_no":6,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The Fire has been veiled by desires, and Paradise has been veiled by hardships.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6487},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2823}]},{"num":16515,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة عن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال:","((لما خلق اللّٰه الجنة والنار أرسل جبريل إلى الجنة، فقال: انظر إليها، وإلى ما أعددت لأهلها فيها، قال: فجاءها، ونظر إليها وإلى ما أعد اللّٰه لأهلها فيها، قال: فرجع إليه قال: فوعزتك لا يسمع بها أحد إلا دخلها، فأمر بها، فحفت بالمكاره، فقال: ارجع إليها فانظر إلى ما أعددت لأهلها فيها. قال: فرجع إليها فإذا هي قد حفت بالمكاره، فرجع إليه فقال: وعزتك لقد خفت أن لا يدخلها أحد. قال: اذهب إلى النار، فانظر إليها وإلى ما أعددت لأهلها فيها، فإذا هي يركب بعضها بعضًا، فرجع إليه فقال: وعزتك لا يسمع بها أحد فيدخلها، فأمر بها فحفت بالشهوات، فقال: ارجع إليها، فرجع إليها فقال: وعزتك لقد خشيت أن لا ينجو منها أحد إلا دخلها))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (٤٧٤٤)، والترمذي (٢٥٦٠)، والنسائي (٣٧٦٣)، وصححه ابن حبان (٧٣٩٤).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب حفت الجنة بالمكاره وحفت النار بالشهوات","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (4744), al-Tirmidhī (2560), al-Nasā’ī (3763), and authenticated by Ibn Ḥibbān (7394).","chapter_en":"Paradise Is Surrounded by Hardships and the Fire Is Surrounded by Desires","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة والنار معًا","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise and the Fire Together","part_no":66,"group_no":6,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When Allah created Paradise and the Fire, He sent Jibrīl to Paradise and said: ‘Look at it and at what I have prepared in it for its people.’ So he went to it and looked at it and at what Allah had prepared therein for its people. Then he returned and said: ‘By Your Might, no one will hear about it except that he will enter it.’ Then Allah commanded that it be surrounded by hardships and said: ‘Return to it and look at what I have prepared therein for its people.’","He returned and found that it had been surrounded by hardships. So he returned to Allah and said: ‘By Your Might, I fear that no one will enter it.’ Then He said: ‘Go to the Fire and look at it and at what I have prepared in it for its people.’ He went and saw its parts piled one upon another. He returned and said: ‘By Your Might, no one will hear about it and then enter it.’ Then Allah commanded that it be surrounded by desires and said: ‘Return to it.’","He returned and then said: ‘By Your Might, I fear that no one will escape it without entering it.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"abudawud","label":"أبو داود","number":4744},{"key":"tirmidhi","label":"الترمذي","number":2560},{"key":"nasai","label":"النسائي","number":3763},{"key":"صححہ_ابن_حبان","label":"صححه ابن حبان","number":7394}]},{"num":16516,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة، أن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال:","((إذا جاء رمضان فتحت أبواب الجنة، وغلقت أبواب النار، وصفدت الشياطين))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (١٨٩٨)، ومسلم (١٠٧٩).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب تفتح أبواب الجنة وتغلق أبواب النار في شهر رمضان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (1898) and Muslim (1079).","chapter_en":"The Gates of Paradise Are Opened and the Gates of the Fire Are Closed During the Month of Ramaḍān","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة والنار معًا","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise and the Fire Together","part_no":66,"group_no":6,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When Ramaḍān comes, the gates of Paradise are opened, the gates of the Fire are closed, and the devils are chained.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":1898},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":1079}]},{"num":16517,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((إذا كان رمضان فتحت أبواب الرحمة، وغلقت أبواب جهنم، وسلسلت الشياطين))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٣٢٧٧)، ومسلم (٢ :١٠٧٩).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب تفتح أبواب الجنة وتغلق أبواب النار في شهر رمضان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3277) and Muslim (2 :1079).","chapter_en":"The Gates of Paradise Are Opened and the Gates of the Fire Are Closed During the Month of Ramaḍān","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة والنار معًا","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise and the Fire Together","part_no":66,"group_no":6,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When Ramaḍān begins, the gates of mercy are opened, the gates of Hell are closed, and the devils are chained.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":3277},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2}]},{"num":16518,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة قال: قال النبي ﷺ:","((لا يدخل أحد الجنة إلا أري مقعده من النار لو أساء، ليزداد شكرًا، ولا يدخل النار أحد إلا أري مقعده من الجنة لو أحسن، ليكون عليه حسرة))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (٦٥٦٩).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أهل الجنة يرون مقاعدهم من النار لو أساؤوا، وأهل النار يرون مقاعدهم من الجنة لو أحسنوا","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6569).","chapter_en":"The People of Paradise Will See Their Places in the Fire Had They Done Evil, and the People of the Fire Will See Their Places in Paradise Had They Done Good","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة والنار معًا","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise and the Fire Together","part_no":66,"group_no":6,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “No one will enter Paradise except that he will be shown the place he would have occupied in the Fire had he done evil, so that he may increase in gratitude. And no one will enter the Fire except that he will be shown the place he would have occupied in Paradise had he done good, so that it may become a source of regret for him.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6569}]},{"num":16519,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((كل أهل النار يرى منزله من الجنة، فيكون له حسرة فيقول: ﴿لَوْ أَنَّ اللَّهَ هَدَانِي لَكُنْتُ مِنَ الْمُتَّقِينَ﴾ [سورة الزمر: ٥٧]، وكل أهل الجنة يرى منزله من النار فيقول: ﴿وَمَا كُنَّا لِنَهْتَدِيَ لَوْلَا أَنْ هَدَانَا اللَّهُ﴾ [سورة الأعراف: ٤٣]، فيكون له شكرًا)).","قال: وقال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((ما من أحد إلا وله منزل في الجنة، ومنزل في النار، فالكافر يرث المؤمن منزله من النار، والمؤمن يرث الكافر منزله من الجنة، وذلك قوله تعالى: ﴿وَتِلْكَ الْجَنَّةُ الَّتِي أُورِثْتُمُوهَا بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُونَ﴾ [الزخرف: ٧٢]))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه ابن أبي حاتم في تفسيره - كما في تفسير ابن كثير - (٢٤٠/٧).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب أهل الجنة يرون مقاعدهم من النار لو أساؤوا، وأهل النار يرون مقاعدهم من الجنة لو أحسنوا","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Ibn Abī Ḥātim in his Tafsīr, as cited in Ibn Kathīr’s Tafsīr (7/240).","chapter_en":"The People of Paradise Will See Their Places in the Fire Had They Done Evil, and the People of the Fire Will See Their Places in Paradise Had They Done Good","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة والنار معًا","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise and the Fire Together","part_no":66,"group_no":6,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Every person from the people of the Fire will see the dwelling that would have been his in Paradise, and it will become a source of regret for him. He will say: ‘If only Allah had guided me, I would have been among the righteous.’ [al-Zumar 39:57] And every person from the people of Paradise will see the dwelling that would have been his in the Fire and will say: ‘We would never have been guided had Allah not guided us.’","[al-Aʿrāf 7:43] So this will increase him in gratitude.” He also said that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no one except that he has a dwelling in Paradise and a dwelling in the Fire. The disbeliever will inherit the believer’s dwelling in the Fire, and the believer will inherit the disbeliever’s dwelling in Paradise. That is the meaning of the statement of Allah, the Exalted: ‘That is the Paradise which you have been made to inherit because of what you used to do.’","[al-Zukhruf 43:72]”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ابن_ابی_حاتم/تفسیرہ_کما_فی_تفسیر_ابن_کثیر","label":"ابن أبي حاتم في تفسيره - كما في تفسير ابن كثير -","number":240}]},{"num":16520,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أنس بن مالك قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((يؤتى بأنعم أهل الدنيا من أهل النار يوم القيامة، فيصبغ في النار صبغة، ثم يقال: يا ابن آدم هل رأيت خيرًا قط؟ هل مر بك نعيم قط؟ فيقول: لا، والله يا رب. ويؤتى بأشد الناس بؤسًا في الدنيا من أهل الجنة، فيصبغ صبغة في الجنة، فيقال له: يا ابن آدم هل رأيت بؤسًا قط؟ هل مر بك شدة قط؟ فيقول: لا، والله يا رب، ما مر بي بؤس قط، ولا رأيت شدة قط))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٢٨٠٧).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب صبغ أنعم أهل الدنيا من أهل النار في النار، وصبغ أشد الناس بؤسًا من أهل الجنة في الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2807).","chapter_en":"The Most Prosperous Person of This World among the People of the Fire Will Be Dipped into the Fire, and the Most Miserable Person of This World among the People of Paradise Will Be Dipped into Paradise","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة والنار معًا","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise and the Fire Together","part_no":66,"group_no":6,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The person who enjoyed the greatest luxury in this world among those destined for the Fire will be brought on the Day of Resurrection and dipped once into the Fire. Then it will be said to him: ‘O son of Ādam, have you ever seen any good? Have you ever experienced any pleasure?’ He will say: ‘No, by Allah, my Lord.’ And the person who suffered the greatest misery in this world among those destined for Paradise will be brought and dipped once into Paradise.","Then it will be said to him: ‘O son of Ādam, have you ever experienced any misery? Have you ever gone through any hardship?’ He will say: ‘No, by Allah, my Lord. No misery ever passed over me, and I never experienced any hardship.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2807}]},{"num":16521,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبد اللّٰه بن مسعود قال: قال النبي ﷺ:","((الجنة أقرب إلى أحدكم من شراك نعله، والنار مثل ذلك))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (٦٤٨٨).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب قرب الجنة والنار من العبد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6488).","chapter_en":"The Nearness of Paradise and the Fire to the Servant","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة والنار معًا","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise and the Fire Together","part_no":66,"group_no":6,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Paradise is closer to each one of you than the strap of his sandal, and the Fire is likewise.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6488}]},{"num":16522,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أنس بن مالك، أن النبي ﷺ خرج حين زاغت الشمس، فصلى الظهر، فلما سلم، قام على المنبر، فذكر الساعة، وذكر أن بين يديها أمورًا عظامًا، ثم قال:","((من أحب أن يسأل عن شيء فليسأل عنه، فوالله لا تسألوني عن شيء إلا أخبرتكم به ما دمت في مقامي هذا)).","قال أنس: فأكثر الناس البكاء، وأكثر رسول اللّٰه ﷺ أن يقول:","((سلوني)).","فقال أنس: فقام إليه رجل، فقال: أين مدخلي يا رسول الله؟ قال:","((النار)).","فقام عبد اللّٰه بن حذافة، فقال: من أبي يا رسول الله؟ قال:","((أبوك حذافة)).","قال: ثم أكثر أن يقول:","((سلوني، سلوني)).","فبرك عمر على ركبتيه، فقال: رضينا بالله ربًا، وبالإسلام دينًا، وبمحمد رسولًا، قال: فسكت رسول اللّٰه ﷺ حين قال عمر ذلك، ثم قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((والذي نفسي بيده لقد عرضت علي الجنة والنار آنفًا في عرض هذا الحائط وأنا أصلي، فلم أر كاليوم في الخير والشر))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٧٢٩٤) واللفظ له، ومسلم (١٣٦ :٢٣٩٥).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب عرض الجنة والنار على النبي ﷺ ورؤيته ما فيها من الخير والشر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (7294), whose wording this is, and Muslim (136 :2395).","chapter_en":"Paradise and the Fire Were Shown to the Prophet ﷺ, and He Saw the Good and Evil Contained in Them","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة والنار معًا","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise and the Fire Together","part_no":66,"group_no":6,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik narrated: The Prophet ﷺ came out after the sun had passed its zenith and prayed Ẓuhr. When he gave the salām, he stood upon the pulpit, mentioned the Hour, and mentioned that tremendous events would occur before it. Then he said: “Whoever wishes to ask about anything, let him ask. By Allah, you will not ask me about anything while I remain standing here except that I will inform you about it.” Anas said: The people began weeping intensely, while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ repeatedly said: “Ask me.”","A man stood and asked: “Where will I enter, O Messenger of Allah?” He replied: “The Fire.” Then ʿAbdullāh ibn Ḥudhāfah stood and asked: “Who is my father, O Messenger of Allah?” He replied: “Your father is Ḥudhāfah.” Then he continued saying: “Ask me, ask me.” ʿUmar fell to his knees and said: “We are pleased with Allah as our Lord, with Islam as our religion, and with Muḥammad as our Messenger.” When ʿUmar said that, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ became silent.","Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, Paradise and the Fire were just now shown to me across this wall while I was praying. I have never seen anything like what I saw today in good and evil.”"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["ولم يعرف اسم الرجل الذي سأله أين مدخله فقال: ((النار)) إما أن يكون هذا الرجل منافقًا، أو فيه إشارة إلى سوء خاتمته، وإلا فالصحابة كلهم في الجنة لقوله تعالى:","﴿وَمَا لَكُمْ أَلَّا تُنْفِقُوا فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ وَلِلَّهِ مِيرَاثُ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضِ لَا يَسْتَوِي مِنْكُمْ مَنْ أَنْفَقَ مِنْ قَبْلِ الْفَتْحِ وَقَاتَلَ أُولَٰئِكَ أَعْظَمُ دَرَجَةً مِنَ الَّذِينَ أَنْفَقُوا مِنْ بَعْدُ وَقَاتَلُوا وَكُلًّا وَعَدَ اللَّهُ الْحُسْنَى وَاللَّهُ بِمَا تَعْمَلُونَ خَبِيرٌ﴾ [الحديد: ١٠].","وقال تعالى:","﴿إِنَّ الَّذِينَ سَبَقَتْ لَهُمْ مِنَّا الْحُسْنَىٰ أُولَٰئِكَ عَنْهَا مُبْعَدُونَ﴾ [الأنبياء: ١٠١]."],"en":["The identity of the man who asked where he would enter and was told “the Fire” is not known.","The author states that either this man was a hypocrite, or the statement indicated that his end would be evil. Otherwise, according to the author, the Companions are all destined for Paradise, based on the statement of Allah, the Exalted:","“Why should you not spend in the cause of Allah when to Allah belongs the inheritance of the heavens and the earth? Those among you who spent and fought before the Conquest are not equal to those who did so afterward. They are greater in rank than those who spent and fought afterward, though Allah has promised the best reward to all. And Allah is fully aware of what you do.”","[al-Ḥadīd 57:10]","And He, the Exalted, says:","“Indeed, those for whom the best reward has already gone forth from Us—they will be kept far away from it.”","[al-Anbiyāʾ 21:101]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":7294},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":136}]},{"num":16523,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أنس بن مالك، عن النبي ﷺ أنه قال:","((لا تزال جهنم يلقى فيها وتقول: هل من مزيد؟ حتى يضع رب العزة فيها قدمه، فينزوي بعضها إلى بعض، وتقول: قط قط، بعزتك وكرمك، ولا يزال في الجنة فضل حتى ينشئ اللّٰه لها خلقًا، فيسكنهم فضل الجنة))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه مسلم (٣٨ :٢٨٤٨) والبخاري (٧٣٨٤).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في سعة الجنة والنار","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by Muslim (38 :2848) and al-Bukhārī (7384).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Vastness of Paradise and the Fire","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة والنار معًا","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise and the Fire Together","part_no":66,"group_no":6,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “People will continue to be cast into Hell while it says: ‘Is there any more?’ until the Lord of Might places His Foot in it. Then its parts will draw together and it will say: ‘Enough, enough, by Your Might and Your Generosity.’ And there will continue to remain extra space in Paradise until Allah creates a creation for it and settles them in the remaining space of Paradise.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":38},{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":7384}]},{"num":16524,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبد الله بن عمر، أن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال:","((إذا صار أهل الجنة إلى الجنة، وصار أهل النار إلى النار، أتي بالموت حتى يجعل بين الجنة والنار، ثم يذبح، ثم ينادي مناد: يا أهل الجنة لا موت، ويا أهل النار لا موت، فيزداد أهل الجنة فرحًا إلى فرحهم، ويزداد أهل النار حزنًا إلى حزنهم))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٦٥٤٨)، ومسلم (٤٣ :٢٨٥٠).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب خلود الجنة والنار","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6548) and Muslim (43 :2850).","chapter_en":"The Eternity of Paradise and the Fire","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة والنار معًا","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise and the Fire Together","part_no":66,"group_no":6,"chapter_no":9,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When the people of Paradise have gone to Paradise and the people of the Fire have gone to the Fire, death will be brought and placed between Paradise and the Fire, then it will be slaughtered. Then a caller will proclaim: ‘O people of Paradise, there is no more death! O people of the Fire, there is no more death!’ The people of Paradise will thereby increase in joy upon their joy, and the people of the Fire will increase in sorrow upon their sorrow.”"]},"intro":{"ar":["قال اللّٰه تعالى:","﴿إِنَّ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَعَمِلُوا الصَّالِحَاتِ كَانَتْ لَهُمْ جَنَّاتُ الْفِرْدَوْسِ نُزُلًا ۝ خَالِدِينَ فِيهَا لَا يَبْغُونَ عَنْهَا حِوَلًا﴾ [الكهف: ١٠٧-١٠٨].","وقال تعالى:","﴿إِنَّ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا وَمَاتُوا وَهُمْ كُفَّارٌ أُولَٰئِكَ عَلَيْهِمْ لَعْنَةُ اللَّهِ وَالْمَلَائِكَةِ وَالنَّاسِ أَجْمَعِينَ ۝ خَالِدِينَ فِيهَا لَا يُخَفَّفُ عَنْهُمُ الْعَذَابُ وَلَا هُمْ يُنْظَرُونَ﴾ [البقرة: ١٦١-١٦٢]."],"en":["Allah, the Exalted, says:","“Indeed, those who believe and perform righteous deeds will have the Gardens of al-Firdaws as their hospitality, remaining therein forever, never desiring any change from it.”","[al-Kahf 18:107-108]","And He, the Exalted, says:","“Indeed, those who disbelieve and die while they are disbelievers—upon them is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all mankind, remaining therein forever. The punishment will not be lightened for them, nor will they be given respite.”","[al-Baqarah 2:161-162]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6548},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":43}]},{"num":16525,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبد اللّٰه بن عمر قال: إن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال:","((يدخل اللّٰه أهل الجنة الجنة، ويدخل أهل النار النار، ثم يقوم مؤذن بينهم فيقول: يا أهل الجنة لا موت، ويا أهل النار لا موت، كل خالد فيما هو فيه))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٦٥٤٤)، ومسلم (٢٨٥٠).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب خلود الجنة والنار","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6544) and Muslim (2850).","chapter_en":"The Eternity of Paradise and the Fire","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة والنار معًا","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise and the Fire Together","part_no":66,"group_no":6,"chapter_no":9,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah will admit the people of Paradise into Paradise and the people of the Fire into the Fire. Then a caller will stand between them and proclaim: ‘O people of Paradise, there is no death! O people of the Fire, there is no death! Everyone will remain forever in the state in which he is.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6544},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2850}]},{"num":16526,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي سعيد الخدري قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((يؤتى بالموت كهيئة كبش أملح، فينادي مناد: يا أهل الجنة، فيشرئبون وينظرون، فيقول: هل تعرفون هذا؟ فيقولون: نعم، هذا الموت، وكلهم قد رآه، ثم ينادي: يا أهل النار، فيشرئبون وينظرون، فيقول: وهل تعرفون هذا؟ فيقولون: نعم، هذا الموت، وكلهم قد رآه، فيذبح، ثم يقول: يا أهل الجنة خلود فلا موت، ويا أهل النار خلود فلا موت)).","ثم قرأ:","﴿وَأَنْذِرْهُمْ يَوْمَ الْحَسْرَةِ إِذْ قُضِيَ الْأَمْرُ وَهُمْ فِي غَفْلَةٍ﴾ [مريم: ٣٩].","وهؤلاء في غفلة أهل الدنيا:","﴿وَهُمْ لَا يُؤْمِنُونَ﴾ [مريم: ٣٩]."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٤٧٣٠)، ومسلم (٢٨٤٩).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب خلود الجنة والنار","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4730) and Muslim (2849).","chapter_en":"The Eternity of Paradise and the Fire","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة والنار معًا","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise and the Fire Together","part_no":66,"group_no":6,"chapter_no":9,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Death will be brought in the form of a black-and-white ram. A caller will proclaim: ‘O people of Paradise!’ They will crane their necks and look. He will ask: ‘Do you recognize this?’ They will reply: ‘Yes. This is death,’ for all of them will have seen it. Then he will call: ‘O people of the Fire!’ They will crane their necks and look. He will ask: ‘Do you recognize this?’","They will reply: ‘Yes. This is death,’ for all of them will have seen it. Then it will be slaughtered, and it will be said: ‘O people of Paradise, everlasting life with no death! O people of the Fire, everlasting life with no death!’” Then he recited: “Warn them of the Day of Regret, when the matter will have been decided while they are in heedlessness.” [Maryam 19:39] These people are presently in the heedlessness of this worldly life: “And they do not believe.”","[Maryam 19:39]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":4730},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2849}]},{"num":16527,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة قال: قال النبي ﷺ:","((يقال لأهل الجنة: خلود لا موت، ولأهل النار: يا أهل النار خلود لا موت))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (٦٥٤٥).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب خلود الجنة والنار","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6545).","chapter_en":"The Eternity of Paradise and the Fire","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة والنار معًا","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise and the Fire Together","part_no":66,"group_no":6,"chapter_no":9,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “It will be said to the people of Paradise: ‘Everlasting life with no death,’ and to the people of the Fire: ‘O people of the Fire, everlasting life with no death.’”"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["ورواه الإمام أحمد (٨٥٣٥) من وجه آخر مرفوعًا ولفظه:","((إذا دخل أهل الجنة الجنة، وأهل النار النار نادى مناد: يا أهل الجنة خلود فلا موت فيه، ويا أهل النار خلود فلا موت فيه))."],"en":["Imām Aḥmad (8535) also narrated it through another route as a Prophetic report with the wording:","“When the people of Paradise have entered Paradise and the people of the Fire have entered the Fire, a caller will proclaim: ‘O people of Paradise, everlasting life with no death therein! O people of the Fire, everlasting life with no death therein!’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6545}]},{"num":16528,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة، أن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال في حديث طويل:","((فإذا أدخل اللّٰه أهل الجنة الجنة وأهل النار النار، قال: أتي بالموت ملببًا فيوقف على السور الذي بين أهل الجنة وأهل النار، ثم يقال: يا أهل الجنة، فيطلعون خائفين، ثم يقال: يا أهل النار، فيطلعون مستبشرين يرجون الشفاعة، فيقال لأهل الجنة وأهل النار: هل تعرفون هذا؟ فيقولون هؤلاء وهؤلاء: قد عرفناه، هو الموت الذي وكل بنا، فيضجع فيذبح ذبحًا على السور الذي بين الجنة والنار، ثم يقال: يا أهل الجنة خلود لا موت، ويا أهل النار خلود لا موت))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (٢٥٥٧)، وابن خزيمة في التوحيد (١٥٠).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب خلود الجنة والنار","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (2557) and Ibn Khuzaymah in al-Tawḥīd (150).","chapter_en":"The Eternity of Paradise and the Fire","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة والنار معًا","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise and the Fire Together","part_no":66,"group_no":6,"chapter_no":9,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said in a lengthy hadith: “When Allah has admitted the people of Paradise into Paradise and the people of the Fire into the Fire, death will be brought restrained and made to stand upon the wall between the people of Paradise and the people of the Fire. Then it will be said: ‘O people of Paradise!’ and they will look out fearfully. Then it will be said: ‘O people of the Fire!’ and they will look out joyfully, hoping for intercession.","Then both the people of Paradise and the people of the Fire will be asked: ‘Do you recognize this?’ Both groups will say: ‘We recognize it. It is death, which had been appointed over us.’ Then it will be laid down and slaughtered upon the wall between Paradise and the Fire. Then it will be said: ‘O people of Paradise, everlasting life with no death! O people of the Fire, everlasting life with no death!’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"tirmidhi","label":"الترمذي","number":2557},{"key":"ابن_خزیمہ/التوحید","label":"ابن خزيمة في التوحيد","number":150}]},{"num":16529,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أنس عن النبي ﷺ قال:","((يؤتى بالموت يوم القيامة فيوقف بين الجنة والنار فيذبح فيقال: يا أهل الجنة خلود لا موت، ويا أهل النار خلود لا موت))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه البزار (٧٢٤٠)، وأبو يعلى (٢٨٩٨)، والطبراني في الأوسط (٣٦٧٢)، والضياء في المختارة (٢٤٤٧).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب خلود الجنة والنار","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Bazzār (7240), Abū Yaʿlā (2898), al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Awsaṭ (3672), and al-Ḍiyāʾ in al-Aḥādīth al-Mukhtārah (2447).","chapter_en":"The Eternity of Paradise and the Fire","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة والنار معًا","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise and the Fire Together","part_no":66,"group_no":6,"chapter_no":9,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Death will be brought on the Day of Resurrection and made to stand between Paradise and the Fire, then it will be slaughtered. It will be said: ‘O people of Paradise, everlasting life with no death! O people of the Fire, everlasting life with no death!’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"البزار","label":"البزار","number":7240},{"key":"ابو_یعلی","label":"أبو يعلى","number":2898},{"key":"الطبرانی/الاوسط","label":"الطبراني في الأوسط","number":3672},{"key":"الضیا/المختارہ","label":"الضياء في المختارة","number":2447},{"key":"sh12862","label":"كشف الأستار عن زوائد البزار","number":3557,"n":3558}]},{"num":16530,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن سعيد بن وهب الهمداني قال: قدم علينا معاذ بن جبل فقال: إني رسول رسول اللّٰه ﷺ إليكم:","((أن تعبدوا الله ولا تشركوا به شيئًا، وأن تطيعوني لا آلوكم خيرًا، وأن المصير إلى اللّٰه تعالى، وإلى الجنة والنار، إقامة بلا ظعن، وخلود بلا موت))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه إسحاق بن راهويه في مسنده كما في إتحاف الخيرة المهرة (٥٨)، والمطالب العالية (٢٨٦٢).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب خلود الجنة والنار","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Isḥāq ibn Rāhawayh in his Musnad, as cited in Itḥāf al-Khiyarah al-Maharah (58) and al-Maṭālib al-ʿĀliyah (2862).","chapter_en":"The Eternity of Paradise and the Fire","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة الجنة والنار معًا","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of Paradise and the Fire Together","part_no":66,"group_no":6,"chapter_no":9,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Saʿīd ibn Wahb al-Hamdānī narrated: Muʿādh ibn Jabal came to us and said: “I am the messenger of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to you, conveying: ‘That you worship Allah and associate nothing with Him; that you obey me, for I will spare no effort in directing you toward good; and that the final return is to Allah, the Exalted, and to Paradise or the Fire—an abiding without departure and an eternity without death.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"اسحاق_بن_راہویہ/مسندہ_کما_فی_اتحاف_الخیرہ_المہرہ","label":"إسحاق بن راهويه في مسنده كما في إتحاف الخيرة المهرة","number":58},{"key":"المطالب_العالیہ","label":"المطالب العالية","number":2862}]},{"num":16531,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر بن عبدالله قال: أتى النبي ﷺ رجل فقال: يا رسول الله، ما الموجبتان؟ قال:","((من مات لا يشرك بالله شيئًا دخل الجنة، ومن مات يشرك بالله شيئًا دخل النار))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٩٣).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب من مات لا يشرك بالله شيئًا دخل الجنة، ومن مات يشرك بالله شيئًا دخل النار","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (93).","chapter_en":"Whoever Dies Without Associating Anything with Allah Will Enter Paradise, and Whoever Dies Associating Anything with Allah Will Enter the Fire","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة وأهل النار معًا","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise and the People of the Fire Together","part_no":66,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked: “O Messenger of Allah, what are the two things that make the outcome certain?” He replied: “Whoever dies without associating anything with Allah will enter Paradise, and whoever dies associating anything with Allah will enter the Fire.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":93}]},{"num":16532,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أسامة بن زيد، عن النبي ﷺ قال:","((قمت على باب الجنة، فكان عامة من دخلها المساكين، وأصحاب الجد محبوسون، غير أن أصحاب النار قد أمر بهم إلى النار، وقمت على باب النار، فإذا عامة من دخلها النساء))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٥١٩٦)، ومسلم (٢٧٣٦).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب أكثر أهل الجنة الفقراء، وأكثر أهل النار النساء","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (5196) and Muslim (2736).","chapter_en":"Most of the People of Paradise Are the Poor, and Most of the People of the Fire Are Women","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة وأهل النار معًا","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise and the People of the Fire Together","part_no":66,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Usāmah ibn Zayd narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “I stood at the gate of Paradise and saw that most of those who entered it were the poor, while the people of wealth and worldly fortune were being detained, except that those destined for the Fire had already been ordered to the Fire. And I stood at the gate of the Fire and saw that most of those who entered it were women.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":5196},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2736}]},{"num":16533,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عمران، عن النبي ﷺ قال:","((اطلعت في الجنة فرأيت أكثر أهلها الفقراء، واطلعت في النار فرأيت أكثر أهلها النساء))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (٦٥٤٦).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أكثر أهل الجنة الفقراء، وأكثر أهل النار النساء","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6546).","chapter_en":"Most of the People of Paradise Are the Poor, and Most of the People of the Fire Are Women","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة وأهل النار معًا","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise and the People of the Fire Together","part_no":66,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿImrān narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “I looked into Paradise and saw that most of its inhabitants were the poor, and I looked into the Fire and saw that most of its inhabitants were women.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6546}]},{"num":16534,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن ابن عباس قال: قال محمد ﷺ:","((اطلعت في الجنة فرأيت أكثر أهلها الفقراء، واطلعت في النار فرأيت أكثر أهلها النساء))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٢٧٣٧).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أكثر أهل الجنة الفقراء، وأكثر أهل النار النساء","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2737).","chapter_en":"Most of the People of Paradise Are the Poor, and Most of the People of the Fire Are Women","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة وأهل النار معًا","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise and the People of the Fire Together","part_no":66,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿAbbās narrated that Muḥammad ﷺ said: “I looked into Paradise and saw that most of its inhabitants were the poor, and I looked into the Fire and saw that most of its inhabitants were women.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2737}]},{"num":16535,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((تحاجت الجنة والنار، فقالت النار: أوثرت بالمتكبرين والمتجبرين، وقالت الجنة: فما لي لا يدخلني إلا ضعفاء الناس وسقطهم وغرتهم؟ قال اللّه للجنة: إنما أنت رحمتي أرحم بك من أشاء من عبادي، وقال للنار: إنما أنت عذابي أعذب بك من أشاء من عبادي، ولكل واحدة منكما ملؤها، فأما النار فلا تمتلئ حتى يضع اللّٰه تبارك وتعالى رجله، تقول: قط قط قط، فهنالك تمتلئ، ويزوى بعضها إلى بعض، ولا يظلم اللّٰه من خلقه أحدًا، وأما الجنة فإن اللّه ينشئ لها خلقًا))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٤٨٥٠)، ومسلم (٣٦/٢٨٤٦).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب يدخل الضعفاء الجنة والجبارون النار","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4850) and Muslim (36/2846).","chapter_en":"The Weak Will Enter Paradise and the Tyrannical Will Enter the Fire","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة وأهل النار معًا","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise and the People of the Fire Together","part_no":66,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Paradise and the Fire disputed with one another. The Fire said: ‘I have been favored with the arrogant and the tyrannical.’ Paradise said: ‘Why is it that none enter me except the weak, insignificant, and simple-minded among the people?’ Allah said to Paradise: ‘You are My mercy; through you I show mercy to whomever I will among My servants.’ And He said to the Fire: ‘You are My punishment; through you I punish whomever I will among My servants. Each of you will have its fill.’","As for the Fire, it will not become full until Allah, Blessed and Exalted, places His Foot in it, and it will say: ‘Enough, enough, enough.’ Then it will become full and its parts will contract together. Allah will not wrong anyone among His creation. As for Paradise, Allah will create a creation for it.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":4850},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":36}]},{"num":16536,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة، عن النبي ﷺ، قال:","((اختصمت الجنة والنار إلى ربهما، فقالت الجنة: يا رب، ما لها لا يدخلها إلا ضعفاء الناس وسقطهم، وقالت النار: - يعني - أوثرت بالمتكبرين، فقال اللّٰه تعالى للجنة: أنت رحمتي، وقال للنار: أنت عذابي، أصيب بك من أشاء، ولكل واحدة منكما ملؤها. قال: فأما الجنة، فإن اللّٰه لا يظلم من خلقه أحدًا، وإنه ينشئ للنار من يشاء، فيلقون فيها، فتقول: هل من مزيد؟ ثلاثًا، حتى يضع فيها قدمه فتمتلئ، ويرد بعضها إلى بعض، وتقول: قط قط قط))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٧٤٤٩) ومسلم (٢٨٤٦).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب يدخل الضعفاء الجنة والجبارون النار","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (7449) and Muslim (2846).","chapter_en":"The Weak Will Enter Paradise and the Tyrannical Will Enter the Fire","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة وأهل النار معًا","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise and the People of the Fire Together","part_no":66,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Paradise and the Fire brought their dispute before their Lord. Paradise said: ‘My Lord, why is it that none enter me except the weak and insignificant among the people?’ The Fire said—meaning—‘I have been favored with the arrogant.’ Allah, the Exalted, said to Paradise: ‘You are My mercy.’ And He said to the Fire: ‘You are My punishment; through you I afflict whomever I will. Each of you will have its fill.’","As for Paradise, Allah does not wrong anyone among His creation. And He creates for the Fire whomever He wills, and they are cast into it. It says three times: ‘Is there any more?’ until He places His Foot in it. Then it becomes full, its parts are drawn together, and it says: ‘Enough, enough, enough.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":7449},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2846}]},{"num":16537,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن حارثة بن وهب الخزاعي، عن النبي ﷺ قال:","((ألا أخبركم بأهل الجنة؟ كل ضعيف متضعف، لو أقسم على اللّٰه لأبره. ألا أخبركم بأهل النار؟ كل عتل جواظ مستكبر))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٦٠٧١)، ومسلم (٢٨٥٣).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب يدخل الضعفاء الجنة والجبارون النار","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6071) and Muslim (2853).","chapter_en":"The Weak Will Enter Paradise and the Tyrannical Will Enter the Fire","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة وأهل النار معًا","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise and the People of the Fire Together","part_no":66,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ḥārithah ibn Wahb al-Khuzāʿī narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Shall I tell you about the people of Paradise? Every weak person who is regarded as weak; if he were to swear an oath by Allah, Allah would fulfill it for him. And shall I tell you about the people of the Fire? Every harsh, coarse, arrogant person.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":6071},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2853}]},{"num":16538,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي سعيد الخدري قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((احتجت الجنة والنار، فقالت النار: في الجبارون والمتكبرون، وقالت الجنة: في ضعفاء الناس ومساكينهم، قال: فقضى بينهما أنك الجنة رحمتي أرحم بك من أشاء، وأنك النار عذابي أعذب بك من أشاء، ولكليكما علي ملؤها))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٢٨٤٧)، والإمام أحمد (١١٧٥٤) واللفظ لأحمد، ومسلم لم يسق لفظه.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب يدخل الضعفاء الجنة والجبارون النار","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2847) and Imām Aḥmad (11754). The wording is Aḥmad’s; Muslim did not quote the full wording.","chapter_en":"The Weak Will Enter Paradise and the Tyrannical Will Enter the Fire","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة وأهل النار معًا","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise and the People of the Fire Together","part_no":66,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Paradise and the Fire disputed. The Fire said: ‘Within me are the tyrants and the arrogant.’ Paradise said: ‘Within me are the weak and poor among the people.’ Allah then judged between them: ‘You, Paradise, are My mercy; through you I show mercy to whomever I will. And you, Fire, are My punishment; through you I punish whomever I will. It is upon Me to fill each of you.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2847},{"key":"الامام_احمد","label":"الإمام أحمد","number":11754},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":11754,"n":11754}]},{"num":16539,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عياض بن حمار المجاشعي، أن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال ذات يوم في خطبته:","((ألا إن ربي أمرني أن أعلمكم ما جهلتم مما علمني يومي هذا، كل مال نحلته عبدًا حلال، وإني خلقت عبادي حنفاء كلهم، وإنهم أتتهم الشياطين فاجتالتهم عن دينهم، وحرمت عليهم ما أحللت لهم، وأمرتهم أن يشركوا بي ما لم أنزل به سلطانًا، وإن اللّٰه نظر إلى أهل الأرض، فمقتهم عربهم وعجمهم إلا بقايا من أهل الكتاب، وقال: إنما بعثتك لأبتليك وأبتلي بك، وأنزلت عليك كتابًا لا يغسله الماء، تقرؤه نائمًا ويقظان، وإن اللّٰه أمرني أن أحرق قريشًا، فقلت: رب إذًا يثلغوا رأسي فيدعوه خبزة، قال: استخرجهم كما استخرجوك، واغزهم نغزك، وأنفق فسننفق عليك، وابعث جيشًا نبعث خمسة مثله، وقاتل بمن أطاعك من عصاك، قال: وأهل الجنة ثلاثة: ذو سلطان مقسط متصدق موفق، ورجل رحيم رقيق القلب لكل ذي قربى ومسلم، وعفيف متعفف ذو عيال، قال: وأهل النار خمسة: ضعيف الذي لا زبر له، الذين هم فيكم تبعًا لا يبتغون أهلًا ولا مالًا، والخائن الذي لا يخفى له طمع وإن دق إلا خانه، ورجل لا يصبح ولا يمسي إلا وهو يخادعك عن أهلك ومالك)).","وذكر:","((البخل أو الكذب والشنظير الفحاش)).","ولم يذكر أبو غسان في حديثه:","((وأنفق فسننفق عليك))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (٢٨٦٥).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب يدخل الضعفاء الجنة والجبارون النار","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2865).","chapter_en":"The Weak Will Enter Paradise and the Tyrannical Will Enter the Fire","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة وأهل النار معًا","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise and the People of the Fire Together","part_no":66,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿIyāḍ ibn Ḥimār al-Mujāshiʿī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said one day in his sermon: “Indeed, my Lord has commanded me to teach you today what you did not know from what He has taught me. Every wealth that I have granted to a servant is lawful. I created all My servants inclining naturally toward the truth, but the devils came to them and turned them away from their religion. They prohibited for them what I had made lawful and commanded them to associate with Me that for which I had sent down no authority.","Allah looked upon the people of the earth and detested them, Arabs and non-Arabs alike, except for remnants among the People of the Book. And He said: ‘I have only sent you in order to test you and test others through you. I have revealed to you a Book that water cannot wash away; you recite it while asleep and awake.’ Allah commanded me to burn Quraysh. I said: ‘My Lord, then they will crush my head and leave it like a loaf of bread.’ He said: ‘Drive them out as they drove you out. Fight them and We will support you. Spend and We will spend upon you. Send an army and We will send five times its number. Fight with those who obey you against those who disobey you.’","The people of Paradise are three: a ruler who is just, charitable, and guided to success; a merciful man whose heart is tender toward every relative and Muslim; and a chaste person who restrains himself despite having dependents. And the people of the Fire are five: the weak person who has no resolve, those who merely follow among you and seek neither family nor wealth; the treacherous person whose greed, however slight, never escapes him without his betraying it; and a man who morning and evening never ceases trying to deceive you regarding your family and wealth.”","He also mentioned: “Miserliness—or lying—and the foul-mouthed, obscene person.” Abū Ghassān did not mention in his narration: “Spend and We will spend upon you.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2865}]},{"num":16540,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبدالله بن عمرو، أن رسول اللّٰه ﷺ قال:","((إن أهل النار كل جعظري جواظ مستكبر، جماع مناع، وأهل الجنة الضعفاء المغلوبون))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (٧٠١٠)، والحاكم (٤٩٩/٢).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب يدخل الضعفاء الجنة والجبارون النار","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (7010) and al-Ḥākim (2/499).","chapter_en":"The Weak Will Enter Paradise and the Tyrannical Will Enter the Fire","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة وأهل النار معًا","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise and the People of the Fire Together","part_no":66,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The people of the Fire are every harsh, coarse, arrogant person, one who amasses wealth and withholds it. And the people of Paradise are the weak and oppressed.”"]},"buhuth":{"ar":["قوله: “جعظري” هو الفظ الغليظ. وقوله: “جواظ” هو المختال في مشيته."],"en":["The author explains that “jaʿẓarī” means a harsh and coarse person.","“Jawwāẓ” means one who walks with arrogance and conceit."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"hakim","label":"الحاكم","number":499},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":7010,"n":7010}]},{"num":16541,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبد اللّٰه بن شقيق، عن رجل من أصحاب النبي ﷺ، عن النبي ﷺ قال:","((ألا أدلكم على أهل الجنة؟)).","قالوا: بلى، قال:","((الضعفاء المتظلمون)).","ثم قال:","((ألا أدلكم على أهل النار؟)).","قالوا: بلى، قال:","((كل شديد جعظري))."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (٢٣١٣١).","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب يدخل الضعفاء الجنة والجبارون النار","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (23131).","chapter_en":"The Weak Will Enter Paradise and the Tyrannical Will Enter the Fire","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة وأهل النار معًا","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise and the People of the Fire Together","part_no":66,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn Shaqīq narrated from a man among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Shall I direct you to the people of Paradise?” They replied: “Yes.” He said: “The weak who are oppressed.” Then he said: “Shall I direct you to the people of the Fire?” They replied: “Yes.” He said: “Every harsh, coarse person.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":23131,"n":23131}]},{"num":16542,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن سراقة بن مالك بن جعشم المدلجي، أن رسول الله ﷺ قال:","((يا سراقة، ألا أخبرك بأهل الجنة وأهل النار؟)).","فقال: بلى يا رسول الله، فقال:","((أما أهل النار فكل جعظري جواظ مستكبر، وأما أهل الجنة فالضعفاء المغلوبون))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الطبراني في الكبير (١٥٢/٧)، والحاكم (٦١٩/٣).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب يدخل الضعفاء الجنة والجبارون النار","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Kabīr (7/152) and al-Ḥākim (3/619).","chapter_en":"The Weak Will Enter Paradise and the Tyrannical Will Enter the Fire","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة وأهل النار معًا","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise and the People of the Fire Together","part_no":66,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Surāqah ibn Mālik ibn Juʿshum al-Mudlijī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Surāqah, shall I tell you about the people of Paradise and the people of the Fire?” He replied: “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “As for the people of the Fire, they are every harsh, coarse, arrogant person. As for the people of Paradise, they are the weak and oppressed.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"الطبرانی/الکبیر","label":"الطبراني في الكبير","number":152},{"key":"hakim","label":"المستدرك على الصحيحين","number":6597,"n":6595}]},{"num":16543,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((ألا أنبئكم بأهل الجنة؟ هم الضعفاء المظلومون، ألا أنبئكم بأهل النار؟ كل شديد جعظري))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (٨٨٢١)، وأبو يعلى (٦١٢٧)، والطبراني في الأوسط (٤٢٧٥)، والبيهقي في شعب الإيمان (٧٨٢٦).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب يدخل الضعفاء الجنة والجبارون النار","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (8821), Abū Yaʿlā (6127), al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Awsaṭ (4275), and al-Bayhaqī in Shuʿab al-Īmān (7826).","chapter_en":"The Weak Will Enter Paradise and the Tyrannical Will Enter the Fire","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة وأهل النار معًا","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise and the People of the Fire Together","part_no":66,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Shall I inform you about the people of Paradise? They are the weak and oppressed. Shall I inform you about the people of the Fire? Every harsh, coarse person.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ابو_یعلی","label":"أبو يعلى","number":6127},{"key":"الطبرانی/الاوسط","label":"الطبراني في الأوسط","number":4275},{"key":"البیہقی/شعب_الایمان","label":"البيهقي في شعب الإيمان","number":7826},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":8821,"n":8821}]},{"num":16544,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أنس بن مالك، عن النبي ﷺ أنه قال:","((ألا أخبركم بأهل النار وأهل الجنة؟ أما أهل الجنة فكل ضعيف متضعف أشعث ذي طمرين، لو أقسم على اللّٰه لأبره، وأما أهل النار، فكل جعظري جواظ، جماع مناع، ذي تبع))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (١٢٤٧٦) وأبو يعلى (٣٩٨٧).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب يدخل الضعفاء الجنة والجبارون النار","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (12476) and Abū Yaʿlā (3987).","chapter_en":"The Weak Will Enter Paradise and the Tyrannical Will Enter the Fire","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة وأهل النار معًا","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise and the People of the Fire Together","part_no":66,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Shall I tell you about the people of the Fire and the people of Paradise? As for the people of Paradise, they are every weak person regarded as weak, disheveled and wearing two worn garments; if he were to swear an oath by Allah, Allah would fulfill it for him. As for the people of the Fire, they are every harsh, coarse person who amasses and withholds wealth and has followers.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"ابو_یعلی","label":"أبو يعلى","number":3987},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":12476,"n":12476}]},{"num":16545,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبد اللّه بن مسعود قال: قال رسول اللّٰه ﷺ:","((ألا أخبركم بمن يحرم على النار أو بمن تحرم عليه النار؟ على كل قريب هين سهل))."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (٢٤٨٨)، وأحمد (٣٩٣٨)، وأبو يعلى (٥٠٥٣)، وابن حبان (٤٧٠، ٤٦٩).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب يدخل الضعفاء الجنة والجبارون النار","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (2488), Aḥmad (3938), Abū Yaʿlā (5053), and Ibn Ḥibbān (470, 469).","chapter_en":"The Weak Will Enter Paradise and the Tyrannical Will Enter the Fire","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة وأهل النار معًا","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise and the People of the Fire Together","part_no":66,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Shall I tell you about the one who will be forbidden to the Fire—or the one upon whom the Fire will be forbidden? It is every person who is approachable, gentle, and easy-going.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"tirmidhi","label":"الترمذي","number":2488},{"key":"ابو_یعلی","label":"أبو يعلى","number":5053},{"key":"ibnhibban","label":"ابن حبان","number":470},{"key":"ahmad","label":"مسند الإمام أحمد","number":3938,"n":3938},{"key":"sh12520","label":"مسند أبي يعلى","number":5053,"n":5058}]},{"num":16546,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة قال: قال النبي ﷺ:","((كلمتان حبيبتان إلى الرحمن، خفيفتان على اللسان، ثقيلتان في الميزان، سبحان اللّٰه وبحمده، سبحان اللّٰه العظيم))."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (٧٥٦٣)، ومسلم (٢٦٩٤).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب في صفة العدل لله تعالى يوم القيامة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب صفة القيامة، وأهوالها","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (7563) and Muslim (2694).","chapter_en":"Concerning the Justice of Allah, the Exalted, on the Day of Resurrection","part_en":"The Description of the Resurrection and Its Terrors","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في صفة أهل الجنة وأهل النار معًا","group_en":"A Collection of What Has Been Narrated Concerning the Description of the People of Paradise and the People of the Fire Together","part_no":66,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Two phrases are beloved to the Most Merciful, light upon the tongue, and heavy upon the Scale: Subḥān Allāhi wa biḥamdih — Glory and praise be to Allah. Subḥān Allāhil-ʿAẓīm — Glory be to Allah, the Magnificent.”"]},"intro":{"ar":["قال تعالى:","﴿وَنَضَعُ الْمَوَازِينَ الْقِسْطَ لِيَوْمِ الْقِيَامَةِ فَلَا تُظْلَمُ نَفْسٌ شَيْئًا وَإِنْ كَانَ مِثْقَالَ حَبَّةٍ مِنْ خَرْدَلٍ أَتَيْنَا بِهَا وَكَفَىٰ بِنَا حَاسِبِينَ﴾ [الأنبياء: ٤٧].","يخبر اللّه تعالى عن عدله، وقضائه القسط بين عباده إذا جمعهم يوم القيامة."],"en":["Allah, the Exalted, says:","“We will set up the scales of justice for the Day of Resurrection, so no soul will be wronged in the least. Even if a deed is the weight of a mustard seed, We will bring it forth. And sufficient are We as Reckoners.”","[al-Anbiyāʾ 21:47]","Allah, the Exalted, informs us of His perfect justice and His judging with equity between His servants when He gathers them on the Day of Resurrection."]}},"tuhfa":{},"refs":[{"key":"bukhari","label":"البخاري","number":7563},{"key":"muslim","label":"مسلم","number":2694}]}]);
